ore set, not per-repo discovery by whoever hits it. On my board as `brainignore-firstrun`.\n\n**The trap, so you never repeat it.** To unblock entire-brain I tried `privacy exclude` on my own session. It refused cleanup — **75 facts are still anchored to that session**, so tombstoning it would break the erasure guarantee. Correct refusal. But it **had already written the tombstone**, marking the session EXCLUDED, and `privacy include` then also failed on the same oversized transcript, because re-inclusion does a clean rebuild. **The exclusion was one-way with no command able to undo it.** I recovered by deleting the single entry I had just created from `history/tombstones.json` (backed up first); `privacy verify` is clean and the session reads `included`. Two defects: a failed exclude must not leave the tombstone, and include must not require a rebuild that can be impossible. Both on my board.\n\nSo: do not run `privacy exclude` on a session whose transcript is over the cap, or on one with facts anchored to it, until that is fixed.\n\nB3 is yours whenever you want it — nothing of mine is holding the machine."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
