{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"02ef096e56aadc31525ba129b55b244d525fc065e034260b2ced38f7ee61fe98","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The Brain session is right, and it measured it. My fixture would never have had a missing blob, so removing the guard would \"change nothing\" for the wrong reason. Both guards also block a fetch independently, so they have to be tested one at a time. Sending the corrected fixture and matrix to the agent now:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YEVQw5G1vKdvLVDSssn7Ku","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","summary":"CORRECTION: B-a fixture inert; use this one","message":"**CORRECTION to my last message. Read this before running the weakening.** The fixture I specified is inert, and the weakening had a confound. This was measured on this machine (git 2.54.0).\n\n## 1. The fixture I specified never has a missing blob\n`git clone --filter=blob:none --no-local file://...src` either warns \"filtering not recognized by server\", or, with `uploadpack.allowFilter=true` set, records promisor=true but STILL sends the blob. In-pack shows 3 objects, `rev-list --objects --all --missing=print | grep -c '^?'` returns 0, and the blob sizes match. So no lazy fetch is ever possible. **Do not use it. Do NOT take the \"stop and report what protects us\" branch on the basis of that fixture.**\n\n## 2. Use this fixture\nClone normally, declare the promisor by hand, then repack without the blob:\n```sh\ngit clone --no-local \"file://$SRC\" cl && cd cl\ngit config remote.origin.promisor true\ngit config remote.origin.partialclonefilter blob:none\nBLOB=$(git rev-parse HEAD:big.txt)\ngit rev-list --objects HEAD | awk -v b=\"$BLOB\" '$1!=b {print $1}' > keep.txt\nrm -f .git/objects/pack/*.pack .git/objects/pack/*.idx\ngit pack-objects --non-empty .git/objects/pack/pack < keep.txt\n```\nVerify before trusting it: in-pack must be 2, and `--missing=print | grep -c '^?'` must be **1**.\n\n**Copy the tree fresh for every probe**, because one successful fetch repairs it and every later probe then measures nothing. Keep `keep.txt` out of the repo, in a temp dir of your own, not shared `/tmp`.\n\n## 3. The matrix. Remove ONE guard at a time, and assert exit code plus stderr, not just \"failed\"\nExpected (measured):\n\n| env | exit | meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` only | 1 | refused silently: **fetch never attempted** |\n| no guards | 0 | fetch succeeded; proves the fixture is live |\n| `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` only | 128 | `fatal: transport 'file' not allowed` / `could not fetch ... from promisor remote`: **attempted, blocked at transport** |\n| both | 1 | the lazy-fetch guard refuses first |\n\nRemoving `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` while `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` is still set stays blocked. That is not evidence that the lazy-fetch guard is inert: both guards protect independently, so test each one in isolation.\n\n## 4. What the fix must rest on\nAdmit promisor repos on the basis of `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` (**never attempted**), and keep `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` as the second layer. \"Attempted but blocked\" is weaker: it is only as good as the protocol allowlist covering every transport git may add. **The PR must say which guard does the work.** The env-enumeration test (fake git asserting both vars at every site) still applies.\n\n## 5. Harness trap\nCapture git's exit code BEFORE any pipe (`git ...; rc=$?`, or `set -o pipefail`). Piping into `head` and reading `$?` reports head's status, and the whole matrix then reads as uniform success."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B3AP9XFpHWUhJ3Ktekg7SJ","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Fixture correction forwarded verbatim to B-a","message":"You're right, and thanks for measuring it rather than arguing it. I've forwarded your correction to the B-a agent:\n- my fixture is marked inert, and the agent is told not to take the \"stop and report\" branch on it;\n- your repack-without-the-blob fixture, with its verification (in-pack 2, missing count 1) and a fresh copy per probe;\n- the one-guard-at-a-time matrix, asserting exit code plus stderr (1 / 0 / 128 / 1);\n- the admission rule rests on `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` (never attempted), with `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` as the second layer, and the PR must name which guard does the work;\n- capture git's exit code before any pipe.\n\nThe \"never attempted\" vs \"attempted but blocked\" distinction is the real result here, and it's sharper than what I'd asked for. I'll hold the entiredb ping until B-a is green on that matrix."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
