n reads the parent's blobs. Real blob:none clones died with \"unable to read <oid>\". Now uses `log -1 --no-walk`.\n  - Docs and changelog updated.\n  - Two cache tests used a promisor remote as their unsafe trigger; switched to `include`. A control proves they still go red.\n  \n  Evidence:\n  - Fixture: repack-without-blob recipe. The plain `--filter=blob:none` recipe is flawed as the coordinator said. Also, deleting the old pack before running pack-objects lazily refetches the blob, so build the new pack first. Verified in-pack=3, missing=1.\n  - Raw one-guard-at-a-time matrix, `cat-file -e` exits: NO_LAZY_FETCH only=1, none=0 (fetched), ALLOW_PROTOCOL only=1 with \"transport 'file' not allowed\", both=1. With `-p` the exits are 128/0/128/128. The coordinator's table had 128 for the ALLOW_PROTOCOL-only row; I measured 1 with -e. stderr is the real signal.\n  - Product-level weakened builds with GIT_TRACE: dropping NO_LAZY_FETCH spawns `git fetch origin --filter=blob:none --stdin`. Dropping only ALLOW_PROTOCOL changes nothing.\n  - So GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH does the work (no fetch is ever attempted). ALLOW_PROTOCOL is only a second layer. The PR states this.\n  - Sites: one env builder, gitSubprocessEnvironment, used by both constructors (newCmd, newGitCmdWithCallerLocale). Callers came from graph neighbors plus grep and are listed in the PR body. No per-site fix needed.\n  \n  Tests, all weakened to red and restored (each restore confirmed with a clean git diff):\n  - (a) Offline index after the remote is deleted. Red when the guard is reverted, and red when `show -s` is restored.\n  - (b) Missing blob gives E_FILE_READ with no child git at all (spy git via GIT_EXEC_PATH, plus a control showing the spy does catch a fetch). Red when noLazyFetchEnv is dropped.\n  - (c) A fake git 2.44 still refuses, with the new text. Red under admit-always, and red with the old message.\n  - (d) The second `query --head` is a cache hit. Red when the guard is reverted.\n  - Env test: a logging git on PATH across 11 CLI commands plus grep; both vars present on every call. Red when either var is dropped, and red when only the grep constructor is unguarded.\n  - Static AST test: no process launch outside the two constructors and the allowlist. Red on an added exec.Command, and red on a non-literal program.\n  - Also: parse threshold, sem gate/diagnosis/probe-cost tests, and a Windows UNC admit test (it only runs on Windows CI).\n  \n  Local: whole gitutil, sem (288s) and cli (282s) packages green, -p 1, under the lock. Focused tests green under -race via mlock. All locked runs used a python fcntl wrapper on measure.lock, the same lock mlock takes. The one `flock` call errored and nothing ran.\n  \n  Live (main checkouts, read-only, fresh cache):\n  - entiredb: base fails with exit 1; new indexes 2542 files / 36068 symbols, completeness ok, 15 partial failures (all parse/minified, none from missing blobs).\n  - cli: base exit 1; new indexes 1427 files / 28619 symbols, ok.\n  - A trace build of cli made 19 git calls and 0 fetches.\n  \n  N2 query --head, base → new medians, 3 interleaved reps, load1 8.6-10.2:\n  - cli: 32.59s → 3.38s\n  - entiredb: 7.96s → 2.37s\n  - Identity: the result lists are identical. Only provenance changes: commit/tree are set and the fallback warnings are gone.\n  - Caveat: on entiredb a query containing \"repository\" takes the slow alias route (review #1) on a cache hit, 15.6s vs 8.8s. That is pre-existing for every non-partial repo and documented in the PR.\n  \n  CI, all pass: build×3, lint, test ubuntu (git 2.55), test macos (git 2.56), test windows + 8 shards, CodeQL, others.\n  CI, failed: Entire Gates, on the Approvals sub-gate only. Findings sub-gate passed (0 findings) and Checks passed.\n  CI, running: none.\n  \n  Not done:\n  - Brain fact not recorded: the protocol forbids touching ~/.local/share/entire. Candidate fact: \"partial clones admitted only with Git ≥2.45; GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH is the load-bearing guard; av