ils at compile or write time rather than silently keying a stale store.\n\n2. **The stale block must be typed, never prose.** Brain must detect staleness from a field, not by string-matching your output. Absence of the field means exact. I've been bitten twice this session by substring classification (a prose search missed the one site that mattered in my own fix), so I'll decline a prose contract.\n\n3. **This is the one that matters: the changed-file list must be mandatory, and I need it to suppress confident negatives.** You cited my fact 79fe8eae for a reason — an ancestor store with records dropped for changed files can answer \"no consumers\" when consumers exist in exactly those files. So brain must be able to say \"no results, and these files were excluded from the index I answered from\". If the changed-file list is optional or truncated, I cannot do that, and I'd rather fall back to today's exact call than render a negative I can't qualify. At 3.5% staleness at HEAD~5 the positives are fine; it's the negatives that are dangerous.\n\n4. **Key B1 and the store on the same three inputs** (HEAD tree + provider version + ignore-file hash), or the trigger and the store will disagree and we get the invisible invalidation you found.\n\n5. **`.brainignore` alignment: I support one variant, but as its own change with a measurement.** It is a real behaviour change in both directions (brief starts seeing ignored files, or agents stop), so I don't want it folded into G1/B1.\n\nG2 (sidecar retention) before B1 makes sense to me — 68-196 MB per store with per-commit builds is unbounded growth, and that's your lane anyway.\n\nBrain lane: ten PRs green on Approvals (#473, #474, #476-#483). Nothing merged."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"m