{"parentUuid":"f34b0034-323d-404b-8f08-bbed9c700e71","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN3Vv3ozoJXQRhbLkTaS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VKCuyCqVPHjfp8X6nYDrXs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-STORE-PER-COMMIT-DESIGN.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Review by the Brain session (2026-10-24) — corrections and G1 interface requirements\n\n**Finding 1 confirmed** against `~/.local/state/entire/logs/watch.log`: 40,499 lines, 0 \"code index\". Count units differ:\nthe Brain session counted raw log lines (`checkpoint_scope_incomplete` 16, `retain transcript` 6, schema 5 loose\nsubstring), the design counted distinct failed refreshes (7 / 3 / 1). Both are right; read the earlier numbers as\nrefreshes. **Attribution limit:** the 7 dirty_worktree entries are the OLD message format (no path list, no\n`.brainignore`), so they are NOT credited to brain #482. The retain failures ARE verbatim the brain #474 defect.\nEither way, B1's point stands: no refresh failure, whatever its cause, should cost the code index.\n**Findings 2 and 3 confirmed** (graph_context.go:75, graph_store.go:54/:297 append `--ignore-file`;\nrefresh.go:738 derives freshness from the `graph store` descriptor).\n\n**G1 interface requirements (consumer: Brain):**\n1. \"`graph store` stays exact\" must be **structural**. An ancestor result carries a type or marker that the store\n   writer and the descriptor path refuse, so it fails at compile or write time instead of keying a stale store.\n2. The stale block is **typed JSON**, never prose. Its absence means exact.\n3. **The changed-file list is mandatory and never truncated.** If it cannot be complete (too many files, a diff\n   failure, renames that cannot be resolved), refuse the ancestor and return today's exact miss. Brain needs it to\n   qualify negatives (\"no results; these files were excluded\").\n4. B1's trigger and the store key use the **same three inputs**: HEAD tree, provider version, ignore-file hash.\n5. `.brainignore` variant alignment is a **separate change with its own measurement**, not folded into G1 or B1.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nif 'G-ancestor' not in T:\n    i=[t['id'] for t in d['tasks']].index('G-Bb')+1\n    d['tasks'].insert(i, dict(id='G-ancestor',lane='graph',title='G1: graph context --allow-ancestor N (typed stale block, mandatory complete changed-file list, store stays exact)',status='doing',owner='claude',source='proactive',note='Interface agreed with brain (5 requirements in the design doc). Brain consumes it in B2.'))\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Record Brain review and interface requirements in the design"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1831,"cache_read_input_tokens":484791,"output_tokens":3843,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":211},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1831,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3843,"cache_read_input_tokens":484791,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1831},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VKCuyCqVPHjfp8X6nYDrXs":{"command":"cat >> /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-STORE-PER-COMMIT-DESIGN.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Review by the Brain session (2026-10-24) — corrections and G1 interface requirements\n\n**Finding 1 confirmed** against `~/.local/state/entire/logs/watch.log`: 40,499 lines, 0 \"code index\". Count units differ:\nthe Brain session counted raw log lines (`checkpoint_scope_incomplete` 16, `retain transcript` 6, schema 5 loose\nsubstring), the design counted distinct failed refreshes (7 / 3 / 1). Both are right; read the earlier numbers as\nrefreshes. **Attribution limit:** the 7 dirty_worktree entries are the OLD message format (no path list, no\n`.brainignore`), so they are NOT credited to brain #482. The retain failures ARE verbatim the brain #474 defect.\nEither way, B1's point stands: no refresh failure, whatever its cause, should cost the code index.\n**Findings 2 and 3 confirmed** (graph_context.go:75, graph_store.go:54/:297 append `--ignore-file`;\nrefresh.go:738 derives freshness from the `graph store` descriptor).\n\n**G1 interface requirements (consumer: Brain):**\n1. \"`graph store` stays exact\" must be **structural**. An ancestor result carries a type or marker that the store\n   writer and the descriptor path refuse, so it fails at compile or write time instead of keying a stale store.\n2. The stale block is **typed JSON**, never prose. Its absence means exact.\n3. **The changed-file list is mandatory and never truncated.** If it cannot be complete (too many files, a diff\n   failure, renames that cannot be resolved), refuse the ancestor and return today's exact miss. Brain needs it to\n   qualify negatives (\"no results; these files were excluded\").\n4. B1's trigger and the store key use the **same three inputs**: HEAD tree, provider version, ignore-file hash.\n5. `.brainignore` variant alignment is a **separate change with its own measurement**, not folded into G1 or B1.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nif 'G-ancestor' not in T:\n    i=[t['id'] for t in d['tasks']].index('G-Bb')+1\n    d['tasks'].insert(i, dict(id='G-ancestor',lane='graph',title='G1: graph context --allow-ancestor N (typed stale block, mandatory complete changed-file list, store stays exact)',status='doing',owner='claude',source='proactive',note='Interface agreed with brain (5 requirements in the design doc). Brain consumes it in B2.'))\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Record Brain review and interface requirements in the design"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"093f2343-6350-4bda-8afc-e0c24fdf7c97","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgN3VuekqLyvHuY2cqc6P","requestRef":"3f519b09-6c70-4c11-be60-a18e0a0ef18f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"102f119e-bbb3-46aa-a2a2-6afaddd56e7c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:55:22.290Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"102f119e-bbb3-46aa-a2a2-6afaddd56e7c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN3Vv3ozoJXQRhbLkTaS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015doR5AmREa1uw7AkYKpheZ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G1: graph context allow-ancestor","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph feature as one open PR. Follow `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, `mlock`, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch in the worktree, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\nBranch `feat/context-allow-ancestor`, worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-allow-ancestor`.\n\n## Item G1: `entire graph context --allow-ancestor N`\nRead `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-STORE-PER-COMMIT-DESIGN.md` in full first, including the final section \"Review by the Brain session\". Those five interface requirements are a CONTRACT with the consumer (Entire Brain's `brief`), not suggestions.\n\n**Problem.**\n- The search store (a sqlite sidecar) is keyed to the exact commit tree. After every new commit, `graph context` returns `store_unavailable` until something rebuilds, so Brain's brief drops code context.\n- Measured staleness of relations touching changed files if an ancestor's store is served: 0.05% at HEAD~1, 3.5% at HEAD~5, 14.6% at HEAD~10.\n\n**Behaviour to build.**\n- `graph context` gains an opt-in `--allow-ancestor N`. On an exact miss, walk back up to N first-parent commits (N capped at 5) for the newest one that has a store, but only if the files changed between it and the requested tree are ≤ 5% of indexed files.\n- Serve from it, DROPPING records whose file is in the changed set.\n- Return a typed `stale` block. Absence of the block means an exact answer.\n\n## The contract (all five are mandatory)\n1. **`graph store` and the store writer stay exact, structurally.** The ancestor-served result must carry a distinct Go type or marker that the store writer and the `graph store` descriptor path REFUSE. A refactor that tries to key or write a stale store must fail to compile, or fail loudly at write time. Add a test proving the refusal, weakened to red.\n2. **The stale block is typed JSON**, e.g. `{\"stale\": {\"ancestor_commit\": ..., \"ancestor_tree\": ..., \"commits_behind\": n, \"changed_files\": [...], \"excluded_records\": k}}`. Choose the names deliberately and document them in the JSON schema/docs the repo already keeps for `graph context`. There is no prose anywhere the consumer must parse.\n3. **`changed_files` is mandatory and complete, never truncated.** If the list cannot be complete, REFUSE the ancestor and return today's exact `store_unavailable`. That covers too many files (over 5%), a diff failure, unresolvable renames, a partial-clone missing blob, and anything else. Include both sides of a rename, and deletions. Use the guarded git constructors, and respect the partial-clone and no-lazy-fetch rules (`--no-renames` or explicit rename handling; think about which is complete).\n4. **Keys.** Document exactly which inputs key the store: tree, provider version, ignore-file hash and anything else, so Brain's trigger (B1) can use the same three. An ancestor is eligible only if its store has the same provider version and ignore policy as the request; only the tree may differ.\n5. **Opt-in only.** Without the flag, behaviour is byte-identical to today. The default stays exact.\n\nBefore editing, run `entire graph impact` on the context and store lookup functions (search_store_context.go:434-501 per the design) and on the store writer.\n\n## Done means\n- **Tests**, each weakened to red and then restored:\n  - an exact hit has no stale block (and stays byte-identical without the flag);\n  - an ancestor at HEAD~1 serves with a correct, complete `changed_files` and drops those files' records;\n  - more than N commits back → miss;\n  - over 5% changed → miss;\n  - a diff failure → miss, never a partial list;\n  - a rename and a deletion appear in `changed_files`;\n  - a provider-version mismatch → miss;\n  - the store writer and descriptor refuse an ancestor-typed result (the structural guarantee).\n- **Live check:** on a scratch clone of entire-graph (under `timing/repos/` or a fresh clone), build a store with `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=1` at HEAD~1. Then query `context --allow-ancestor 3` at HEAD and show the stale block. Use a fresh cache dir and mlock.\n- Coordinate with the parallel G2 agent (branch `fix/search-store-retention`) only by keeping your diff off the eviction code. Don't touch retention.\n- PR open, CI watched, Entire Gates findings checked via the org trail number, and the report per the protocol."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1831,"cache_read_input_tokens":484791,"output_tokens":3843,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":211},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1831,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3843,"cache_read_input_tokens":484791,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1831},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015doR5AmREa1uw7AkYKpheZ":{"description":"G1: graph context allow-ancestor","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph feature as one open PR. Follow `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, `mlock`, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch in the worktree,