e_history_review_test.go:39, provider_git_config_preflight_windows_test.go:28, git_test.go:2394.\n3. **Wording nit:** write the backport list as \"2.39.4+, 2.40.2+, …\" so the versions don't read as exact ones.\n\n## RECOMMENDED. Do these if each stays small, or list them as follow-ups in the PR\n4. **Static launch test hardening.** It still misses: a zero-value `var c exec.Cmd` then `c.Start()`; a struct embedding `exec.Cmd`; a `reflect.New` of `exec.Cmd`; `syscall.Syscall(SYS_EXECVE…)`; cgo `C.system`; and a package under `bin/`, because the walker skips `bin`/`node_modules` at lazy_fetch_guard_test.go:440 even though Go compiles an imported `bin/` package.\n   - Suggested: enumerate files via `go list` (including CgoFiles; flag any `import \"C\"`); flag any `os/exec.Cmd` type reference outside the allowlist; flag `Syscall*` with exec/spawn numbers; stop skipping `bin/`.\n5. **Encoding pin:** pin `-c i18n.logOutputEncoding=UTF-8` on FileCochanges and FindCommitWithCheckpoint too. Today co-change degrades on UTF-16 repos; there's no egress, only degraded output.\n6. **CI coverage for the table:** CI only has Git 2.55/2.56, so the backport table is protected only by local runs with `ENTIRE_GRAPH_TEST_GITS`. Add a CI job that builds Git 2.45.0 plus one backport from source (cached) and runs the two oracle tests, if that's a modest workflow addition. Otherwise list it as a follow-up.\n\n## Same rules as before\nWeakening for every change, focused `-race` under mlock, push with no force, watch CI, update the PR body (add the symlink case to the repro table), and check findings on org trail **2510** with the fresh CLI. Report per the protocol."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"97c66e00-096c-4a8b-8c5b-2165cc450a00","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgN8NHrbGmXWP3boj1xn4","requestRef":"eaf45ebf-b57b-4e30-9bf1-176e5e50aae8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5cbe91db-1ad0-416f-8364-dca12699cd6b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:59:17.856Z","advisorMode