no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>This agent's report was delivered to you as a message from \"aec892fad0f572b1a\" (its SubagentHandback call). Read it there; it is not repeated here.\n</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>289234</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>42</tool_uses><duration_ms>1727408</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"f9925c06fa09d5197fe20fe69df3231cb781c14fd67c3aa7eab2a4b50e0bcd58","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"[#379](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/379), the store cleanup, is done and green, with only Approvals open.\n- **What it keeps:** the 3 newest stores per repo (configurable), up to 1 GB in total. It never deletes the store just written or the one for your current commit.\n- **Live check:** after six commits, the old build held six stores (55 MB) and the new one held two (18 MB).\n- **Safe while Brain reads:** deleting a store Brain has open doesn't break it, and on Windows a locked store is just skipped.\n- **Tests:** all twelve deliberate breakages fail their tests.\n\nIts trail still showed \"reviewing\", so I'll recheck its findings later. Telling the Brain session what the cleanup means for it:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Jr8ZNxN84iXyqXKWMWr5Wt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['G-Bb']['note']='G2 = PR #379 DONE: store retention, newest K=3 per repo+scope, 1 GiB cap; never evicts the just-written or HEAD store; directory-wide lock shared with publish; POSIX readers survive deletion, Windows refusals skipped; ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE_KEEP knob. Live: 6 commits → 2 stores (KEEP=2). 12 mutations red. CI green; only Approvals pending; trail 2525 still \"reviewing\" (0 findings so far; re-check). G1 = PR #380 in CI. B1-B3 brain side.'\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Record PR 379 on the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KFHKtzvhQiawbraXXEkAgs","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"G2 #379 open: retention semantics for brain","message":"G2 is open: **graph #379, search-store retention**. It's green, with only Approvals pending. What it means for your side:\n\n- **Policy:** after a store is published, stores in the same group (repo key + checkout scope) are trimmed to the newest **K=3** by mtime, capped at **1 GiB** total. The newest store is always kept.\n  - **Never evicted:** the store just written, and any store for the writing checkout's current HEAD tree, in any variant (so your `.brainignore` variant at HEAD is safe).\n  - **Group:** deliberately excludes provider version, profile and ignore policy, so old-nightly and old-ignore stores don't strand forever.\n- **For G1/B2:** K=3 leaves up to 2 ancestor stores for `--allow-ancestor`. With commits every ~17 min, older ancestors get evicted, which is fine since N≤5 and the 5% rule bound usefulness anyway. If you want more ancestors, there's a knob: `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE_KEEP` (0 or negative disables retention).\n- **You open the store path directly, so readers take no lock.**\n  - **POSIX:** a store you already have open keeps working after eviction (tested: a delete-by-truncate mutation goes red with \"database disk image is malformed\").\n  - **Windows:** a refused delete is skipped.\n  - **Edge case to handle:** if you resolve a store's path, then open it later after an eviction, the open fails. Treat that as `store_unavailable`, not an error.\n- **Rebuild cost:** gz entries are never touched, so an evicted store is rebuilt from its gz by `index --head`. 0.56 s vs 1.85 s cold on a small repo.\n- Publish and eviction share a new directory-wide lock with a 5 s wait. If it can't get the lock, it publishes and skips eviction.\n\nG1 (#380, allow-ancestor) is in CI now. I'll send you the binary and the exact JSON once it's green."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
