 (wall 379ms).\n- Identity, byte-for-byte except latency_ms:\n  - exact hit, base vs new: same\n  - exact hit, new with vs without flag: same, no stale block\n  - miss, base vs new: same\n  - `graph store` at HEAD, base vs new: same (store_unavailable, so the descriptor never serves the ancestor)\n\nTESTS: 14 weakenings, all red, every restore checked with empty `git diff`\n- HEAD~1 serve (sem + cli): filter off gave \"symbol from changed file served: RenderDoomed\"; relation filter off gave \"relation touching a changed file served\"; relation count dropped gave \"excluded_records = 3, independent count = 7\"; `--find-renames` dropped old_name.go from the list.\n- CLI emission: Stale not copied to the response gave \"emitted JSON has no stale block\".\n- Exact hit byte-identical (sem + cli): attaching a stale block on an exact hit gave red.\n- Refusal byte-identical to the no-flag miss (sem + cli), cases beyond N / >5% / diff failure / provider version / ignore policy, each with a serving control: ignoring N, gate at 10%, diff error ignored, version dropped from the key, and a stale block on refusal each gave red.\n- Structural: a `cacheEntry` field on the ancestor handle was caught by the reflection test. Removing the tree check made a planted mis-keyed store pass the descriptor.\n- gitutil: rename sides, missing-tree-object error with nil list, first-parent-only walk.\n- Flag bounds: removing the check let -1 through.\n- Local: `go test -race -p 1` on the focused regex (gitutil, sem, cli) passed; `go vet` clean.\n\nCI\n- green: all GitHub checks, 34 of 34, including test (ubuntu/macos/windows), every windows shard, lint, CodeQL.\n- failed: Entire Gates, on Approvals only (\"No reviewers have approved\"). Its Checks, Findings and Up-to-date sub-gates passed.\n- running: none.\n- `entire trail finding list 2526 --status any --freshness any`: 0 findings of any kind.\n\nNOTES / NOT DONE\n- Real git (`git show -s`, which HeadCommitAndTree uses) fails when the parent's changed subtree is missing, so the diff-failure fixture puts the ancestor 2 commits back. This is the known partial-clone issue already tracked in PR #372; not changed here.\n- No brain fact recorded: the protocol forbids touching the real store. Facts worth recording: the stale schema and the store key inputs.\n- Scratch is in `.g3/` and `bin/` inside the worktree, excluded from git: mutation runner `.g3/mutate.py`, live outputs `.g3/live/`."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
