ied them, committed before any further weakening, and the script now restores from a byte copy and checks with cmp. Every weakening was re-run after that.\n  \n  Verification\n  - Focused tests in gitutil, sem and cli green under `-race` with mlock.\n  - Whole gitutil (19s) and sem (191s) packages green with `-p 1`.\n  - Live index of entiredb and cli: exit 0, counts unchanged (2542/36068 and 1427/28619).\n  \n  CI on ace66ffc\n  - green: 35 checks, including boundary-gits, test ubuntu, macOS and Windows plus all shards, lint, and build×3\n  - failed: Entire Gates, on Approvals only (Findings and Checks passed)\n  - running: none\n  \n  Findings on org trail 2510, checked with entire CLI nightly 2026-10-24, all statuses: 0.\n  \n  The PR body is updated with the logical-path fix and the case-d before/after table, the motivation, the new test rows, CI matrix evidence, and follow-ups. No Brain fact was recorded, because the protocol forbids touching that store.","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"#372 re-review items are all done. Branch fix/index-partial-clones @ace66ffc, pushed without force; the PR is still open. Commits since 36c0cc41: 1408f2ae (logical-path probe), 69ea1ddf (URL-named promisor test, wording), e35d8caa (scan hardening, encoding pins, CI matrix), f3a584cd and ace66ffc (scan speed, boundary test).\n\nREQUIRED\n1. **Probe and commands now use the same directory string.**\n   - `LazyFetchGuard` runs `git version` at the exact `--repo` string, made absolute by `filepath.Abs` only, which matches the PWD os/exec sets. There is no EvalSymlinks anymore.\n   - In sem, the resolver now carries `commandDir`. If repository discovery swaps to the physical resolver, the probe still runs at the logical path.\n   - One deliberate deviation from your instruction: I did not canonicalize the cache key either. It is keyed by the logical string. A canonical key would let a cached answer for real/repo be reused for evil/link, which is the same hole through the cache. The cost is one extra probe per spelling.\n   - Reviewer's case d on 36c0cc41 (I reproduced it): probe saw 2.54.0, 16 commands ran on 2.44.0, 1 lazy-fetch child.\n   - Case d now: probe sees 2.44.0 at evil/link, the repo is refused, 0 commands, 0 fetches. Cases a, b, c, c2 also have 0 fetches.\n   - Tests:\n     - gitutil: asdf-style fake git that walks up from PWD, run through a symlink.\n     - cli: product-level case d. The shim's \"old git\" reports 2.44.0 and runs real git without GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH; a GIT_EXEC_PATH spy watches for fetches.\n     - sem: the predicate probes the given path.\n   - Weakening: putting EvalSymlinks back turns the gitutil and cli tests red (\"the pinned old Git started a lazy fetch through …/link\"). Probing `baseResolved` turns the sem test red.\n2. Stale \"2.45\" fixed in all 4 test files.\n3. Backport wording is now \"2.39.4+, 2.40.2+, …\" in the message constant, both docs, the changelog and the tests.\n\nCoordinator addition: URL-named checkpoint promisor\n- Fixture: origin is an ordinary remote; the promisor is set on `remote.https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git`.\n- It is refused on a stand-in 2.45.0, and admitted offline on a proven Git with all 3 files indexed and 0 fetches.\n- Weakening: detecting only \"origin\" turns the cli test red (nil error) and the sem test red.\n\nMotivation added to the PR body, with one correction to what you gave me. Measured `entire brain status`:\n- semantic=true: entire-graph and entire-brain\n- semantic=false: cli and entiredb, the two partial clones\n- semantic=false: entire.io, which is not a partial clone, so that cause is unrelated\n- So entire-graph is not the only one with a semantic source; entire-brain has one too. The body states the measured facts.\n\nRECOMMENDED, all done\n4. **Static scan** now also catches:\n   - `exec.Cmd` used as a value type (zero value or embedded; `*exec.Cmd` is allowed)\n   - raw `SYS_EXECVE`, `SYS_FORK`, `SYS_CLONE` and the like\n   - process-creating C functions via `C.system`, a cgo preamble, or `.c/.h/.cc` sources (the vendored grammar C has none)\n   - It now walks `bin/` and `node_modules/`.\n   - Each rule was disabled in turn and the test went red; skipping `bin/` again also goes red.\n   - Speed: the C scan was moved from regexp to bytes.Index because the vendored C is about 216MB; under `-race` it went from 94s to 2s. A unit test pins the identifier boundary, and removing the boundary check turns it red.\n   - Known gaps are listed in the PR as follow-ups: reflect of `(*exec.Cmd)(nil).Elem()`, `plugin.Open`, assembly, computed syscall numbers, third-party dependencies. The suggested fix is `go list -deps` plus an analyzer.\n5. i18n encoding pin added to FileCochanges and FindCommitWithCheckpoint, with a test. Removing either pin turns it red.\n6. **CI matrix**: new path-filtered workflow `lazy-fetch-git-matrix.yml` builds Git 2.45.0 and 2.44.1 from checksummed tarballs and runs both oracle tests, with greps that fail the job if the builds were not exercised. It is **green on CI**. The Linux log independently confirms the reviewer's claim: 2.45.0 starts 1 lazy fetch on log and diff with GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1; 2.44.1 starts 0.\n\nProcess slip (caught and fixed): my mutation script used `git checkout -- file` to restore. That wiped uncommitted edits to provider.go and lazy_fetch_guard.go once. I re-applied them, committed before any further weakening, and the script now restores from a byte copy and checks with cmp. Every weakening was re-run after that.\n\nVerification\n- Focused tests in gitutil, sem and cli green under `-race` with mlock.\n- Whole gitutil (19s) and sem (191s) packages green with `-p 1`.\n- Live index of entiredb and cli: exit 0, counts unchanged (2542/36068 and 1427/28619).\n\nCI on ace66ffc\n- green: 35 checks, including boundary-gits, test ubuntu, macOS and Windows plus all shards, lint, and build×3\n- failed: Entire Gates, on Approvals only (Findings and Checks passed)\n- running: none\n\nFindings on org trail 2510, checked with entire CLI nightly 2026-10-24, all statuses: 0.\n\nThe PR body is updated with the logical-path fix and the case-d before/after table, the motivation, the new test rows, CI matrix evidence, and follow-ups. No Brain fact was recorded, because the protocol forbids touching that store."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
