{"parentUuid":"3b457140-167e-4018-bc59-23dcb835ed90","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNMJwKjwY6NsMrXgqSVX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1518,"cache_read_input_tokens":595164,"output_tokens":1721,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":66},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1518,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1721,"cache_read_input_tokens":595164,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1518,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1518},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":739,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"8d1aa8ce-e5cc-4ee3-be7f-321f544c3824","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNMJvzQPcfpzuwieZ4jp","requestRef":"72a63095-49c1-4f51-9311-f71749a95ba7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cc6d889d-2767-4d0a-934f-5efcae1f025b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:48:45.423Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"cc6d889d-2767-4d0a-934f-5efcae1f025b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNMJwKjwY6NsMrXgqSVX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MzZj4bW8HATtLUC46b6gFP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/HANDOFF-GRAPH.md","content":"# Graph merge handoff (entireio/entire-graph)\n\nAll 12 PRs below are CI-green, with 0 open findings: checked per trail with\n`--trail entire-graph/<n> --status any --freshness any`, and trail.branch matched against the PR head. Each is\nblocked only on the Approvals sub-gate. Draft PR **#381** (DO NOT MERGE) combines all 12 in this order. CI on its\nhead b0a4ba48 is green, and the full local `internal/sem`, `internal/cli` and `internal/gitutil` suites pass, plus\n148 key tests under `-race`.\n\n## Merge order\nMerge with a merge commit. Retarget #377 to `main` once #371 has merged.\n\n| # | PR | What | Measured | Rebase needed? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | #370 | gitignore `.claude/worktrees/` | Brain seed no longer refuses on nested worktrees | no |\n| 2 | #371 | Alias git grep: corpus paths only, `-l` | entire-graph 224 s → 5.1 s; brain 52 → 9.6 s; cli 12 → 4.9 s | no |\n| 3 | #377 | Cold query uses warm preselection (stacked on #371) | cold == warm (before, 20-59 fields differed); first query −2.5 to −3.9 s; eg alias +0.8 s, disclosed | retarget to main |\n| 4 | #373 | Ordered pipeline window ×16 | cold index −28% to −35% on 4 repos, sha-identical | no |\n| 5 | #379 | Search-store retention (K=3, 1 GiB) | 6 commits → 2 stores; HEAD and just-written stores never evicted | no |\n| 6 | #376 | Stop persisting the derived selective view | warm query −0.16 to −0.38 s | no |\n| 7 | #375 | Cache-hit history splice | warm def/neighbors/impact 0.62 → 0.44 s (fixes the regression) | no |\n| 8 | #372 | Index partial clones on Git ≥ 2.45.1 (no network egress) | cli/entiredb index offline; `query --head` cli 34 → 2.5 s. Three adversarial rounds: SAFE TO MERGE | CHANGELOG only |\n| 9 | #380 | `graph context --allow-ancestor N` + capability key | serves HEAD~1 in 350 ms with a typed stale block | CHANGELOG only |\n| 10 | #374 | Tool-handler heuristic reads identifiers only | false tool symbols 84 → 3; cache bump v22/v27 | CHANGELOG only |\n| 11 | #142 | Stop cleanly on cancellation; never cache a truncated snapshot | behaviour fix (time limit dropped) | **yes**: apply `142-x-374.patch`, `142-x-376.patch`, `142-x-378-allowlist.patch` |\n| 12 | #378 | Disclose unmodelled value refs + co-change failure warning; cache bump v23/v28 | silent gaps now warn | **yes**: `375-x-378.patch`, `142-x-378.patch`, `374-x-378-versions.patch`, plus CHANGELOG |\n\nPatches: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-integration/.g3/resolutions/`. They are also embedded in #381's body.\n\n## Combined effect (cli repo, #381 vs main)\n- cold index 11.8 → 7.8 s (−34%)\n- first warm query 11.7 → 3.5 s (−70%)\n- warm def/neighbors/impact 0.62 → 0.44 s\n\n## Your decisions\n- **Approvals** on all 12. You cannot approve your own PRs, so a teammate is needed, or your override.\n- Whether to make the new `lazy-fetch git matrix` CI job (#372) a required check. It is path-filtered.\n- Close #381 after the merges. It exists only for CI.\n- Your two old drafts: #146 (RFD 0005) and #300 (semantic channel). Community #249 is probably superseded by #261.\n\n## Follow-ups noted, not done\n- `--no-renames` in co-change, so it works on blob:none clones.\n- A failing history refresh makes every warm query a cache miss.\n- A faster warm alias route, which would remove #377's +0.8 s.\n- Real C1 fix: Go var symbols plus a REFERENCES relation.\n- Python and TypeScript tool-registration detection.\n- Static launch-scan gaps: reflect, plugin, asm, computed syscalls.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1518,"cache_read_input_tokens":595164,"output_tokens":1721,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":66},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1518,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1721,"cache_read_input_tokens":595164,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1518,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1518},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MzZj4bW8HATtLUC46b6gFP":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/HANDOFF-GRAPH.md","content":"# Graph merge handoff (entireio/entire-graph)\n\nAll 12 PRs below are CI-green, with 0 open findings: checked per trail with\n`--trail entire-graph/<n> --status any --freshness any`, and trail.branch matched against the PR head. Each is\nblocked only on the Approvals sub-gate. Draft PR **#381** (DO NOT MERGE) combines all 12 in this order. CI on its\nhead b0a4ba48 is green, and the full local `internal/sem`, `internal/cli` and `internal/gitutil` suites pass, plus\n148 key tests under `-race`.\n\n## Merge order\nMerge with a merge commit. Retarget #377 to `main` once #371 has merged.\n\n| # | PR | What | Measured | Rebase needed? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | #370 | gitignore `.claude/worktrees/` | Brain seed no longer refuses on nested worktrees | no |\n| 2 | #371 | Alias git grep: corpus paths only, `-l` | entire-graph 224 s → 5.1 s; brain 52 → 9.6 s; cli 12 → 4.9 s | no |\n| 3 | #377 | Cold query uses warm preselection (stacked on #371) | cold == warm (before, 20-59 fields differed); first query −2.5 to −3.9 s; eg alias +0.8 s, disclosed | retarget to main |\n| 4 | #373 | Ordered pipeline window ×16 | cold index −28% to −35% on 4 repos, sha-identical | no |\n| 5 | #379 | Search-store retention (K=3, 1 GiB) | 6 commits → 2 stores; HEAD and just-written stores never evicted | no |\n| 6 | #376 | Stop persisting the derived selective view | warm query −0.16 to −0.38 s | no |\n| 7 | #375 | Cache-hit history splice | warm def/neighbors/impact 0.62 → 0.44 s (fixes the regression) | no |\n| 8 | #372 | Index partial clones on Git ≥ 2.45.1 (no network egress) | cli/entiredb index offline; `query --head` cli 34 → 2.5 s. Three adversarial rounds: SAFE TO MERGE | CHANGELOG only |\n| 9 | #380 | `graph context --allow-ancestor N` + capability key | serves HEAD~1 in 350 ms with a typed stale block | CHANGELOG only |\n| 10 | #374 | Tool-handler heuristic reads identifiers only | false tool symbols 84 → 3; cache bump v22/v27 | CHANGELOG only |\n| 11 | #142 | Stop cleanly on cancellation; never cache a truncated snapshot | behaviour fix (time limit dropped) | **yes**: apply `142-x-374.patch`, `142-x-376.patch`, `142-x-378-allowlist.patch` |\n| 12 | #378 | Disclose unmodelled value refs + co-change failure warning; cache bump v23/v28 | silent gaps now warn | **yes**: `375-x-378.patch`, `142-x-378.patch`, `374-x-378-versions.patch`, plus CHANGELOG |\n\nPatches: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-integration/.g3/resolutions/`. They are also embedded in #381's body.\n\n## Combined effect (cli repo, #381 vs main)\n- cold index 11.8 → 7.8 s (−34%)\n- first warm query 11.7 → 3.5 s (−70%)\n- warm def/neighbors/impact 0.62 → 0.44 s\n\n## Your decisions\n- **Approvals** on all 12. You cannot approve your own PRs, so a teammate is needed, or your override.\n- Whether to make the new `lazy-fetch git matrix` CI job (#372) a required check. It is path-filtered.\n- Close #381 after the merges. It exists only for CI.\n- Your two old drafts: #146 (RFD 0005) and #300 (semantic channel). Community #249 is probably superseded by #261.\n\n## Follow-ups noted, not done\n- `--no-renames` in co-change, so it works on blob:none clones.\n- A failing history refresh makes every warm query a cache miss.\n- A faster warm alias route, which would remove #377's +0.8 s.\n- Real C1 fix: Go var symbols plus a REFERENCES relation.\n- Python and TypeScript tool-registration detection.\n- Static launch-scan gaps: reflect, plugin, asm, computed syscalls.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8d1aa8ce-e5cc-4ee3-be7f-321f544c3824","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNMJvzQPcfpzuwieZ4jp","requestRef":"72a63095-49c1-4f51-9311-f71749a95ba7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d626c0f7-c620-4bf9-87cc-97530824c763","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:48:58.825Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
