{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"75b7d0c4e9730a68b3e975bb9bf9f23e05d1408ca0685e4af2c5ea176a99481d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FmpkSN6sYTaDzgSvdUwdBQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"M=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory; cat > $M/semantic-layer-handoff-state.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: semantic-layer-handoff-state\ndescription: 2026-10-25 RESUME HERE — 25 PRs (graph 12 + brain 13) all green, 0 open findings, awaiting Suhaan's approvals; merge plan page + patches in ~/devenv-worktrees/handoff\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nAs of 2026-10-25 the graph+brain speed/correctness campaign is **finished and handed off**. Nothing is merged; the\nuser said nothing merges until everything is finished, and it now is.\n\n- **Graph** (entireio/entire-graph): #142 and #370-#380, all CI-green.\n  - Findings verified per trail with `--trail entire-graph/<n> --status any --freshness any` plus a branch match: 0 open.\n  - Draft **#381** (DO NOT MERGE) combines all 12 and is green.\n- **Brain** (entireio/entire-brain): #473, #474, #476-#484, #488, #489, all green.\n  - The 4 findings (#477/#483/#484/#489) are fixed.\n  - Draft **#493** combines all 13 and is green.\n- **Merge plan:** the \"Merge plan\" tab of https://claude.ai/artifact/FkY6c5J1XdzaYGM1Q7T9dU.\n  - Rebase patches are in `~/devenv-worktrees/handoff/{graph,brain}-patches`.\n  - Graph detail: `handoff/HANDOFF-GRAPH.md`. Brain decisions: `devenv/DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md`.\n  - **Re-run the merge simulation right before merging**: main drifts, and one brain PR went from clean to\n    conflicting within hours.\n- **Graph merge order:** 370 → 371 → 377 (retarget) → 373 → 379 → 376 → 375 → 372 → 380 → 374 → 142 (3 patches) →\n  378 (3 patches). Graph #380 before brain #484.\n- **Fresh-env adoption on the combined graph build:** main sessions and Explore subagents went graph-first in every\n  searching task, with 0 graph failures. The harness now installs via `entire graph setup`.\n- **User decisions pending:**\n  - approvals on 25 PRs;\n  - the #489 shrinking-export contract;\n  - brain build-then-swap CAS vs the non-interleaving invariant;\n  - the transcript-mode re-distill cost;\n  - making the lazy-fetch CI job required;\n  - the 37 GB brain store delete;\n  - 63 ~/Documents/Coding paths;\n  - 3 cli-lane issues;\n  - old drafts #146/#300 and community #249.\n\nSupersedes [[graph-landing-paused-state]]. Related: [[announce-before-swapping-shared-binaries]],\n[[green-suite-is-not-evidence]], [[mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test]].\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nimport re\nold=[l for l in s.splitlines() if l.startswith('- [Graph landing PAUSED state]')]\nnew='- [Semantic-layer handoff state](semantic-layer-handoff-state.md) — 2026-10-25 RESUME HERE: 25 PRs green, 0 findings, awaiting approvals; merge plan tab + ~/devenv-worktrees/handoff'\nif old: s=s.replace(old[0], new)\nelse: s=s.rstrip('\\n')+'\\n'+new+'\\n'\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('index ok')\nEOF\nf=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/graph-landing-paused-state.md; python3 - \"$f\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('description: PAUSED 2026-10-11','description: SUPERSEDED by semantic-layer-handoff-state (2026-10-25). PAUSED 2026-10-11',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['D4-handoff'].update(status='done', owner='claude', note='DELIVERED: \"Merge plan\" tab on https://claude.ai/artifact/FkY6c5J1XdzaYGM1Q7T9dU; patches + HANDOFF-GRAPH.md in ~/devenv-worktrees/handoff. 25 PRs green, 0 open findings, integration #381 + #493 green.')\nfor k in ('G3','G-Bb','P8','D1'):\n    if k in T: T[k]['status']='done'\nif 'approve-merge' not in T:\n    d['tasks'].insert(0, dict(id='approve-merge',lane='graph',title='Your turn: approve + merge 25 PRs in the order on the Merge plan tab',status='blocked',owner='user',source='proactive',note='Re-run the merge simulation right before merging (main drifts). Graph #380 before brain #484. I apply the rebase patches as each merge lands, if you want.'))\nT['P7'].update(owner='user', status='blocked', note='Now is a good time to /compact: everything is handed off, and the resume note is in memory (semantic-layer-handoff-state).')\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('board ok')\nEOF","description":"Save the handoff state to memory and finalize the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013Ycx7Lm9UsLKyzaSWxW3La","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Handoff delivered: Merge plan tab live","message":"The handoff (D4) is delivered: the \"Merge plan\" tab, now first, on https://claude.ai/artifact/FkY6c5J1XdzaYGM1Q7T9dU. It has all 25 PRs: graph in merge order with the rebase notes, and brain with your two stack rules plus \"#484 after graph #380\". Both integration PRs (#381, #493) are on it, along with D2's adoption result, the \"re-run the simulation right before merging\" step, the `GOFLAGS=-timeout=30m` note, and one combined decisions table. That table covers your §2 (CAS), §3 (transcript mode), §4 (store delete), §7 (#489 shrink contract) and the cli issues, and points at DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md.\n\nI **copied your three patches** (pr473/477/483) out of your session scratchpad into the durable `~/devenv-worktrees/handoff/brain-patches/`, since /private/tmp gets purged. Mine are beside them in `graph-patches/`. Nothing was moved or edited, only copied.\n\nMy lane is done apart from merge-time rebases. I've marked /compact as Suhaan's next step on the board. Thanks: your catches (the fixture, the #372 floor follow-through, the trail addressing, the M1 lock diagnosis, the store data-dir trap) made this materially better."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
