raph impact/neighbors --head` on the touched symbols first (cite results). Read #382's diff and #373's diff fully before resolving; do not drop either side's logic. Watch for --ours/--theirs silently retiring a feature.\n2. Re-prove #373: its tests + weakening (break the window/ordering guard, show red, restore from byte copy, cmp). Output identity: snapshot sha256 or g2-strip.py JSON of base (b31626ea) vs new must be identical on entire-graph + entire-brain repos. Re-measure cold index base vs new, 3 interleaved reps, separate --cache-dir each, under mlock, record load1. #373's old claim (−28 to −35%) was vs d4a0c186; report the honest new delta on top of #382 even if smaller or zero. If zero/negative, say so plainly — do not tune to win.\n3. `go test -race` focused on internal/sem under mlock (GOMAXPROCS=4, env -u FORCE_COLOR). Whole internal/sem package with -p 1 is allowed.\n4. Force-push #373 with `--force-with-lease`. Update the PR body's Measurements section with the new numbers (keep the Entire trail link block at the top). Watch CI to green; check trail findings per protocol (`entire trail finding list --trail entire-graph/<repo#> --status any --freshness any --json`, verify trail.branch == head branch).\n5. Rebuild the integration branch `integration/g3-all` (draft PR #381, DO NOT MERGE) on origin/main with all 12 in order, applying the resolution patches; regenerate any patch that no longer applies and save updated copies to BOTH /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/handoff/graph-patches/ and eg-integration/.g3/resolutions/ (keep old ones as *.pre382). Confirm cache version numbers (#374 v22/search v27, #378 v23/v28) still sit above main's after #382; if #382 bumped any cache version, renumber and say so. Run internal/sem, internal/cli, internal/gitutil suites on the combined tree (under mlock, -p 1) plus the race subset in .g3/race.sh. Push #381 (--force-with-lease), get CI green.\n6. Do NOT touch any other PR branch unless its patch genuinely fails; if one mu