{"parentUuid":"18db8468-1631-4108-a827-fbd36b1ddab6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c5f3cb0c-68b5-4f2c-ac40-0d731c2fd228","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FYoAQFJ72qR4tg5hnZyukU","type":"tool_result","content":"82\t  <section id=\"panel-plan\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-plan\">\n83\t    <div class=\"meta\"><span><b>25 PRs</b> ready: 12 graph, 13 brain</span><span>All CI-green, no open review findings</span><span>Nothing merged</span><span>Updated <b>2026-10-25</b></span></div>\n84\t    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Everything is waiting only on approvals.</b> Each repo also has a combined test PR that merges all its PRs in order and passed CI: graph <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381\">#381</a> and brain <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/493\">#493</a>. They are for testing only; close them after merging. A fresh-environment check on the combined graph build had agents and Claude's Explore helpers reach for the graph first in every task that searched, with no graph errors.</div>\n85\t\n86\t    <h2>Before you merge</h2>\n87\t    <ul class=\"tight\">\n88\t      <li><b>Re-run the merge simulation first.</b> <span class=\"mono\">main</span> keeps moving: a brain PR that merged cleanly at noon conflicted by evening.</li>\n89\t      <li>Use merge commits. Merge graph <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/380\">#380</a> before brain <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/484\">#484</a>.</li>\n90\t      <li>Rebase patches are saved in <span class=\"mono\">~/devenv-worktrees/handoff/</span> (graph-patches, brain-patches). Each was checked by breaking it on purpose.</li>\n91\t      <li>If you run the cli tests locally, set <span class=\"mono\">GOFLAGS=-timeout=30m</span>: under load they exceed Go's 10-minute default and fail on correct code.</li>\n92\t    </ul>\n93\t\n94\t    <h2>Graph, in merge order</h2>\n95\t    <div class=\"tablewrap\"><table>\n96\t      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>PR</th><th>What</th><th>Measured</th><th>When merging</th></tr></thead>\n97\t      <tbody><tr><td class=\"num\">1</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/370\">#370</a></td><td>Ignore nested Claude Code worktrees</td><td>Brain no longer refuses entire-graph on first run</td><td class=\"note\">—</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">2</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/371\">#371</a></td><td>Alias search greps only indexed files</td><td>entire-graph 224 → 5 s; entire-brain 52 → 10 s; cli 12 → 5 s</td><td class=\"note\">—</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">3</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/377\">#377</a></td><td>First query selects files like later ones</td><td>first and later answers identical; first query 2.5–3.9 s faster</td><td class=\"note\">retarget to main after #371</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">4</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/373\">#373</a></td><td>Indexing pipeline runs ahead of slow files</td><td>cold index 28–35% faster, identical output</td><td class=\"note\">—</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">5</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/379\">#379</a></td><td>Old search stores cleaned up (keep 3, 1 GB)</td><td>disk no longer grows per commit</td><td class=\"note\">—</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">6</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/376\">#376</a></td><td>Stop writing a derived file per new question</td><td>warm queries 0.16–0.38 s faster</td><td class=\"note\">—</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">7</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/375\">#375</a></td><td>Splice history into the cache instead of re-sorting</td><td>warm def/neighbors/impact 0.62 → 0.44 s</td><td class=\"note\">—</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">8</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/372\">#372</a></td><td>Index partial clones offline (Git 2.45.1+)</td><td>cli/entiredb index; cli query 34 → 2.5 s; 3 security reviews</td><td class=\"note\">changelog only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">9</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/380\">#380</a></td><td>Answer from a recent commit, opt-in</td><td>Brain keeps code context between re-indexes</td><td class=\"note\">changelog only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">10</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/374\">#374</a></td><td>Tool detection reads names, not text</td><td>false tool symbols 84 → 3</td><td class=\"note\">changelog only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">11</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/142\">#142</a></td><td>Stop cleanly on cancel; never cache partial results</td><td>behaviour fix</td><td class=\"note\">apply 3 patches</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">12</td><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/378\">#378</a></td><td>Say when references or history are missing</td><td>silent gaps now warn</td><td class=\"note\">apply 3 patches</td></tr></tbody>\n98\t    </table></div>\n99\t    <p class=\"note\">Combined on the cli repo: cold index 11.8 → 7.8 s, first warm query 11.7 → 3.5 s, warm lookups 0.62 → 0.44 s.</p>\n100\t\n101\t    <h2>Brain</h2>\n102\t    <div class=\"tablewrap\"><table>\n103\t      <thead><tr><th>PR</th><th>What</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead>\n104\t      <tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/473\">#473</a></td><td>Attribute every daemon log line</td><td class=\"note\">apply pr473 patch (workspace move on main)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/474\">#474</a></td><td>One divergent cached transcript no longer refuses the run</td><td class=\"note\">—</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/476\">#476</a></td><td>Normalize history text once</td><td class=\"note\">history index −40%</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/477\">#477</a></td><td>Doctor proves the MCP tools are reachable</td><td class=\"note\">apply pr477 patch</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/478\">#478</a></td><td>Fact freshness per branch</td><td class=\"note\">—</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/479\">#479</a></td><td>Read checkpoint details concurrently</td><td class=\"note\">before #481 (stacked)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/480\">#480</a></td><td>Ask for all checkpoints in a way the CLI honours (it caps at 100)</td><td class=\"note\">—</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/481\">#481</a></td><td>Take checkpoint metadata from the local store</td><td class=\"note\">cli refresh 2.4 h → 4 min</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/482\">#482</a></td><td>First-run gate ignores every agent's hook config</td><td class=\"note\">—</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/483\">#483</a></td><td>One oversized transcript no longer refuses the index</td><td class=\"note\">apply pr483 patch</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/484\">#484</a></td><td>Brief shows how stale its code context is</td><td class=\"note\">after graph #380</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/488\">#488</a></td><td>An excluded session no longer blocks export</td><td class=\"note\">before #489 (stacked)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/489\">#489</a></td><td>Skip checkpoints whose commit is gone</td><td class=\"note\">on a partial clone, stops instead of dropping sessions (one final commit landing)</td></tr></tbody>\n105\t    </table></div>\n106\t    <p class=\"note\">Only two ordering rules: #479 before #481, and #488 before #489. The rest are independent.</p>\n107\t\n108\t    <h2>Decisions only you can make</h2>\n109\t    <div class=\"tablewrap\"><table>\n110\t      <thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Why it is yours</th></tr></thead>\n111\t      <tbody>\n112\t        <tr><td><b>Approve the 25 PRs</b></td><td>GitHub won't let you approve your own PRs, so a teammate approves or you override.</td></tr>\n113\t        \n114\t        <tr><td><b>Lock rule vs speed</b> (Brain's build-then-swap)</td><td>Faster rebuilds need a compare-and-swap at publish. It keeps \"no deleted data is ever published\" but drops a stricter ordering rule a privacy test pins.</td></tr>\n115\t        <tr><td><b>Transcript mode</b></td><td>Switching to per-session mode means a paid re-distill of every session.</td></tr>\n116\t        <tr><td><b>Make the old-git CI job required</b> (<a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/372\">#372</a>)</td><td>It builds git 2.45.0 and 2.44.1 to prove the no-network rule, but only runs when those files change.</td></tr>\n117\t        <tr><td><b>Delete the 37 GB Brain store</b></td><td>Irreversible. The steps are written down and on hold.</td></tr>\n118\t        <tr><td><b>63 folders under ~/Documents/Coding</b></td><td>On the cleanup list, but three were in use (BFF, tsa, RP) and one is the test harness. List: <span class=\"mono\">cleanup-audit/held-documents-coding.txt</span>.</td></tr>\n119\t        <tr><td><b>Three cli issues to file</b></td><td>Post-commit hook uses 2.8 GB per commit; <span class=\"mono\">checkpoint explain</span> silently caps at 100; it says \"not found\" and exits 0 when data just isn't downloaded.</td></tr>\n120\t        <tr><td><b>Old drafts</b></td><td>Your graph drafts <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/146\">#146</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/300\">#300</a>; community <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/249\">#249</a> looks superseded.</td></tr>\n121\t      </tbody>"}]},"uuid":"37c52955-5fc1-457e-b0bc-54478a45c5a8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:12:31.557Z","