{"parentUuid":"5bc1f588-6dfe-49dd-8d05-e1073c0c08fc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPL2qLn7CNPKE4srGQBi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BgV4tNTrSGwfvZCRFxzdPG","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","old_string":"    <div class=\"meta\"><span><b>25 PRs</b> ready: 12 graph, 13 brain</span><span>All CI-green, no open review findings</span><span>Nothing merged</span><span>Updated <b>2026-10-25</b></span></div>\n    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Everything is waiting only on approvals.</b> Each repo also has a combined test PR that merges all its PRs in order and passed CI: graph <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381\">#381</a> and brain <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/493\">#493</a>. They are for testing only; close them after merging. A fresh-environment check on the combined graph build had agents and Claude's Explore helpers reach for the graph first in every task that searched, with no graph errors.</div>","new_string":"    <div class=\"meta\"><span><b>25 PRs</b>: 12 graph, 13 brain</span><span>Brain final; graph on hold for one rebase</span><span>Nothing merged</span><span>Updated <b>2026-10-25</b></span></div>\n    <div class=\"callout warn\"><b>Graph: hold.</b> A teammate's PR <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/382\">#382</a> merged into graph main overnight (b31626ea), and <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/373\">#373</a> now conflicts with it. It is being rebased, re-tested and re-timed, and the combined PR <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381\">#381</a> is being rebuilt. The other 11 still merge in order. Don't merge graph PRs until this note is gone.</div>\n    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Brain: done, waiting only on approvals.</b> All 13 merge cleanly, in order, onto main a4942dd9. Combined tree 45e7a626: <span class=\"mono\">go test ./...</span> passes on all 25 packages, and CI run <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/actions/runs/40214249807\">40214249807</a> on that exact commit is green on Linux, macOS, Windows and lint. Two expected reds: <span class=\"mono\">benchmark-corpus</span> (see #484 below) and <span class=\"mono\">release-evidence</span>, which only passes on a release tag. Brain's combined PR #493 is closed. A fresh-environment check on the combined graph build had agents and Claude's Explore helpers reach for the graph first in every task that searched, with no graph errors.</div>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4120,"cache_read_input_tokens":153880,"output_tokens":3060,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4120,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3060,"cache_read_input_tokens":153880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4120,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4120},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BgV4tNTrSGwfvZCRFxzdPG":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","old_string":"    <div class=\"meta\"><span><b>25 PRs</b> ready: 12 graph, 13 brain</span><span>All CI-green, no open review findings</span><span>Nothing merged</span><span>Updated <b>2026-10-25</b></span></div>\n    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Everything is waiting only on approvals.</b> Each repo also has a combined test PR that merges all its PRs in order and passed CI: graph <a href=\"https://github.com/e