{"parentUuid":"bf2c7bdb-b362-434e-8546-0d39f8f087c2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c5f3cb0c-68b5-4f2c-ac40-0d731c2fd228","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BgV4tNTrSGwfvZCRFxzdPG","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"1d3fac27-c471-4a3c-8b29-ea07fccc3691","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:12:58.609Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","oldString":"    <div class=\"meta\"><span><b>25 PRs</b> ready: 12 graph, 13 brain</span><span>All CI-green, no open review findings</span><span>Nothing merged</span><span>Updated <b>2026-10-25</b></span></div>\n    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Everything is waiting only on approvals.</b> Each repo also has a combined test PR that merges all its PRs in order and passed CI: graph <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381\">#381</a> and brain <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/493\">#493</a>. They are for testing only; close them after merging. A fresh-environment check on the combined graph build had agents and Claude's Explore helpers reach for the graph first in every task that searched, with no graph errors.</div>","newString":"    <div class=\"meta\"><span><b>25 PRs</b>: 12 graph, 13 brain</span><span>Brain final; graph on hold for one rebase</span><span>Nothing merged</span><span>Updated <b>2026-10-25</b></span></div>\n    <div class=\"callout warn\"><b>Graph: hold.</b> A teammate's PR <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/382\">#382</a> merged into graph main overnight (b31626ea), and <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/373\">#373</a> now conflicts with it. It is being rebased, re-tested and re-timed, and the combined PR <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381\">#381</a> is being rebuilt. The other 11 still merge in order. Don't merge graph PRs until this note is gone.</div>\n    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Brain: done, waiting only on approvals.</b> All 13 merge cleanly, in order, onto main a4942dd9. Combined tree 45e7a626: <span class=\"mono\">go test ./...</span> passes on all 25 packages, and CI run <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/actions/runs/40214249807\">40214249807</a> on that exact commit is green on Linux, macOS, Windows and lint. Two expected reds: <span class=\"mono\">benchmark-corpus</span> (see #484 below) and <span class=\"mono\">release-evidence</span>, which only passes on a release tag. Brain's combined PR #493 is closed. A fresh-environment check on the combined graph build had agents and Claude's Explore helpers reach for the graph first in every task that searched, with no graph errors.</div>","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":80,"oldLines":8,"newStart":80,"newLines":9,"lines":["   </div>"," ","   <section id=\"panel-plan\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-plan\">","-    <div class=\"meta\"><span><b>25 PRs</b> ready: 12 graph, 13 brain</span><span>All CI-green, no open review findings</span><span>Nothing merged</span><span>Updated <b>2026-10-25</b></span></div>","-    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Everything is waiting only on approvals.</b> Each repo also has a combined test PR that merges all its PRs in order and passed CI: graph <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381\">#381</a> and brain <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/493\">#493</a>. They are for testing only; close them after merging. A fresh-environment check on the combined graph build had agents and Claude's Explore helpers reach for the graph first in every task that searched, with no graph errors.</div>","+    <div class=\"meta\"><span><b>25 PRs</b>: 12 graph, 13 brain</span><span>Brain final; graph on hold for one rebase</span><span>Nothing merged</span><span>Updated <b>2026-10-25</b></span></div>","+    <div class=\"callout warn\"><b>Graph: hold.</b> A teammate's PR <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/382\">#382</a> merged into graph main overnight (b31626ea), and <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/373\">#373</a> now conflicts with it. It is being rebased, re-tested and re-timed, and the combined PR <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381\">#381</a> is being rebuilt. The other 11 still merge in order. Don't merge graph PRs until this note is gone.</div>","+    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Brain: done, waiting only on approvals.</b> All 13 merge cleanly, in order, onto main a4942dd9. Combined tree 45e7a626: <span class=\"mono\">go test ./...</span> passes on all 25 packages, and CI run <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/actions/runs/40214249807\">40214249807</a> on that exact commit is green on Linux, macOS, Windows and lint. Two expected reds: <span class=\"mono\">benchmark-corpus</span> (see #484 below) and <span class=\"mono\">release-evidence</span>, which only passes on a release tag. Brain's combined PR #493 is closed. A fresh-environment check on the combined graph build had agents and Claude's Explore helpers reach for the graph first in every task that searched, with no graph errors.</div>"," ","     <h2>Before you merge</h2>","     <ul class=\"tight\">"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"84db9cd1-9308-495a-b946-d0d0d62b42bf","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":255},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.co