{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"93456dd6dfb63465c0a1a3e26c4f1e383f395b7b7972ab20b35309930794ba2d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BgV4tNTrSGwfvZCRFxzdPG","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","old_string":"    <div class=\"meta\"><span><b>25 PRs</b> ready: 12 graph, 13 brain</span><span>All CI-green, no open review findings</span><span>Nothing merged</span><span>Updated <b>2026-10-25</b></span></div>\n    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Everything is waiting only on approvals.</b> Each repo also has a combined test PR that merges all its PRs in order and passed CI: graph <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381\">#381</a> and brain <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/493\">#493</a>. They are for testing only; close them after merging. A fresh-environment check on the combined graph build had agents and Claude's Explore helpers reach for the graph first in every task that searched, with no graph errors.</div>","new_string":"    <div class=\"meta\"><span><b>25 PRs</b>: 12 graph, 13 brain</span><span>Brain final; graph on hold for one rebase</span><span>Nothing merged</span><span>Updated <b>2026-10-25</b></span></div>\n    <div class=\"callout warn\"><b>Graph: hold.</b> A teammate's PR <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/382\">#382</a> merged into graph main overnight (b31626ea), and <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/373\">#373</a> now conflicts with it. It is being rebased, re-tested and re-timed, and the combined PR <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381\">#381</a> is being rebuilt. The other 11 still merge in order. Don't merge graph PRs until this note is gone.</div>\n    <div class=\"callout info\"><b>Brain: done, waiting only on approvals.</b> All 13 merge cleanly, in order, onto main a4942dd9. Combined tree 45e7a626: <span class=\"mono\">go test ./...</span> passes on all 25 packages, and CI run <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/actions/runs/40214249807\">40214249807</a> on that exact commit is green on Linux, macOS, Windows and lint. Two expected reds: <span class=\"mono\">benchmark-corpus</span> (see #484 below) and <span class=\"mono\">release-evidence</span>, which only passes on a release tag. Brain's combined PR #493 is closed. A fresh-environment check on the combined graph build had agents and Claude's Explore helpers reach for the graph first in every task that searched, with no graph errors.</div>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mjum8mqBhvnom5YVnUKQ5u","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","old_string":"      <li>Rebase patches are saved in <span class=\"mono\">~/devenv-worktrees/handoff/</span> (graph-patches, brain-patches). Each was checked by breaking it on purpose.</li>","new_string":"      <li>Graph rebase patches are in <span class=\"mono\">~/devenv-worktrees/handoff/graph-patches/</span>, and each was checked by breaking it on purpose. Brain needs no patches: its conflict fixes are committed on the PR branches, and <span class=\"mono\">brain-patches/</span> is kept only for reference.</li>\n      <li>A closed PR gets no new CI, while <span class=\"mono\">gh pr checks</span> keeps showing the old green. To test a closed branch, run <span class=\"mono\">gh workflow run test.yml --ref &lt;branch&gt;</span> and check that the run's commit is the one you meant.</li>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KdM5EHWFJTFjMGUnDw32k5","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","old_string":"<td>Indexing pipeline runs ahead of slow files</td><td>cold index 28–35% faster, identical output</td><td class=\"note\">—</td>","new_string":"<td>Indexing pipeline runs ahead of slow files</td><td>was 28–35% faster before #382; being re-measured on top of it</td><td class=\"note\"><b>being rebased onto #382</b></td>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019UnwHPXYtg4G6VdWLjADT9","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","old_string":"<td class=\"note\">apply pr473 patch (workspace move on main)</td>","new_string":"<td class=\"note\">—</td>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Bfa5gX6YapgxKGpqVdCTW","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","old_string":"<td>Doctor proves the MCP tools are reachable</td><td class=\"note\">apply pr477 patch</td>","new_string":"<td>Doctor proves the MCP tools are reachable</td><td class=\"note\">independent of #478 (it used to carry #478's files)</td>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DBMYJUzSQa8dnpmXhsZSTP","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","old_string":"<td>One oversized transcript no longer refuses the index</td><td class=\"note\">apply pr483 patch</td>","new_string":"<td>One oversized transcript no longer refuses the index</td><td class=\"note\">—</td>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014DpaenJCeHUTKHWGctrWMh","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","old_string":"<td>Brief shows how stale its code context is</td><td class=\"note\">after graph #380</td>","new_string":"<td>Brief shows how stale its code context is</td><td class=\"note\">after graph #380. Its <span class=\"mono\">benchmark-corpus</span> check is red because two benchmark Python tests still expect the old packet shape. Left that way on purpose, since you said benchmark work can wait.</td>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bds3P4Q5tmbYSVr5k11sDp","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","old_string":"on a partial clone, stops instead of dropping sessions (one final commit landing)","new_string":"on a partial clone, stops instead of dropping sessions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012wV7xjpeUr2uFwjzsuBQsz","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","old_string":"        <tr><td><b>Old drafts</b></td>","new_string":"        <tr><td><b>One unreadable cli checkpoint</b> (<span class=\"mono\">18b787bf552f</span>)</td><td>cli's Brain refresh stops on it. Nothing local refers to it, so fixing it means a cleanup on the shared <span class=\"mono\">cli-checkpoints</span> remote. Details in DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md §6.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Re-add the Linear connector</b></td><td>Its session is dead; remove and re-add it in claude.ai → Connectors. Three tickets are written and waiting.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Old drafts</b></td>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WE2r5Nra5vAbRrejT9mnMy","name":"Artifact","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","url":"https://claude.ai/artifact/FkY6c5J1XdzaYGM1Q7T9dU","label":"Brain final; graph hold for #373"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
