{"parentUuid":"73a71bb2-e511-4e3c-9077-3fa4e9239a5f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPL6eoP9mmqXaAPjK9Yd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Brain is finished. Graph is waiting on one last fix that's still in progress.\n\n**Brain: done.**\n- All 13 PRs merge cleanly, in order, onto today's main.\n- The combined test run passed, and CI on the combined code passed on Linux, macOS, Windows and lint.\n- One CI check stays red on purpose. Brain #484 changed the shape of Brain's output, and two benchmark tests still expect the old shape. You said benchmark work can wait, so they weren't updated.\n\n**Graph: still on hold.** A teammate merged #382 into graph main overnight, and it conflicts with my #373. An agent is rebasing #373, re-testing it and re-timing it. Then it rebuilds the combined test PR #381 and re-checks the conflict-fix patches. #373's \"28–35% faster indexing\" was measured before #382, so the real gain on top of it may be smaller. I'll report whatever number comes out.\n\nThe merge-plan page now has a \"Graph: hold\" note at the top, plus the two new decisions (the unreadable `cli` checkpoint and re-adding the Linear connector): https://claude.ai/artifact/FkY6c5J1XdzaYGM1Q7T9dU\n\nYour to-do list and the improvements are the same as in my last message. When the graph agent reports back, I'll remove the hold note and tell you everything is ready to merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":505,"cache_read_input_tokens":165059,"output_tokens":455,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":505,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":455,"cache_read_input_tokens":165059,"cache_cr