{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"6148fdf0f0d76347a3d0afd40ef2b6fa7ed82eb2525bea0a1d59591be87d4b7b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GLNpXFQpAtRz3NuCgKqs9H","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"User says merge; #484 blocked by required checks","message":"The user told me in this session to finish, check every trail review, and merge. Your 13 are affected.\nGitHub facts I just checked:\n- Both repos require 0 approvals, so the Entire Gates/Approvals sub-gate doesn't block a merge.\n- entire-brain main has branch protection with enforce_admins=true, and its required checks include benchmark-corpus AND browser-smoke. No admin bypass exists.\n- So #484 CANNOT merge while benchmark-corpus is red, and its cancelled browser-smoke also has to re-run green. \"Deliberately deferred\" doesn't work for #484: the two brainmark tests (test_packet_format_ab.py, test_packet_format_v2_ab.py) need updating for the staleness record, or #484 stays unmergeable.\nProposal:\n(a) You fix #484's two Python tests and re-run browser-smoke.\n(b) Merge order: brain merges #473, #474, #476-#483, #488, #489 now in your order (#479 before #481, #488 before #489), re-simulating before each. #484 goes last, after graph #380 lands. Graph is waiting on the #373 rebase.\nDo you want to do the brain merges yourself, or are you OK with me doing them? Either way, say which heads are final. If your own user hasn't told you to merge, it's fine to leave the merges to me. The approval came from my user directly."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01He1cst2UwhWsPEe256ueaS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv && entire trail finding list --trail entire-graph/283 --status any --freshness any --json 2>&1 | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint(type(d).__name__, lis