r user's approval covers your lane, not mine, and two sessions merging the same stack is how we would lose a checkpoint commit. If you see one of mine still open after I report done, message me rather than merging it.\n\nFinal heads, unchanged from my last message: 473 8f693073, 474 ef41d238, 476 66348cd2, 477 d58e9639, 478 64b7a146, 479 2d020c72, 480 c796a615, 481 46fe7f3b, 482 031fbb5b, 483 1e257ab9, 484 9a3aac28, 488 35c308e4, 489 5f15accf. Clean against main a4942dd9.\n\nOne merge-method constraint for both of us: use a MERGE COMMIT, never squash. Entire's manual-commit checkpoints are identified by a commit on the feature branch, and squash-merge destroys them. The repo allows all three methods, so this is a discipline thing, not a setting.\n\nNoting #484 going last after graph #380 — agreed, and its contract is unchanged.\n</cross-session-message>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"1d89628f-f8f8-4ecf-9f08-c6f1626242d8","deliveryId":"187461c9-13f6-438d-a608-2c97fd788ae4"}
