aan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"2609b83d-c474-46a5-92ad-a211e06d221a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01MCNSbSpnDUdiVyhFvDSkaf","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk read /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls.md | head -40\",\"description\":\"Read memory on trail finding sweep silent zeros\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":13},"type":"attachment","uuid":"454092ac-b146-41eb-be6b-5b75f4bf8da4","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:19:40.923Z","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"2609b83d-c474-46a5-92ad-a211e06d221a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f66e26da-3456-4f4a-ac51-861a28ca8ae0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MCNSbSpnDUdiVyhFvDSkaf","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls\ndescription: \"Two ways a finding sweep silently reports zero: scoping to the trails you happen to be working, and grepping ^01M when the CLI indents its IDs — use --json\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37\n  modified: 2026-09-04T06:00:35.108Z\n---\n\nReporting \"0 open findings\" twice in one session when the real count was **142** cost\ncredibility both times. Two independent causes, both silent:\n\n1. **Scope.** I swept only the ~15 trails I had been working. Findings live on *every*\n   trail, including ones whose PRs merged months ago — and those matter more, because they\n   describe defects already on `main`. Sweep the full trail-number range, both repos.\n2. **Parsing.** `entire trail finding list` **indents** its rows, so\n   `grep -cE \"^01M\"` matches nothing and prints a confident `0`. The correct filter is\n   `grep -cE \"^[[:space:]]+01M.*open\"`, and better still `--json` — the human table also\n   wraps long `LOCATION` values, which silently corrupts column-based `awk`.\n\nAlso: `--repo` requires an explicit trail selector, so `finding show <id>` alone fails —\nkeep the trail number paired with every id. Default `--freshness` is `current`; stale\nfindings are hidden unless asked for.\n\n**A third silent zero, found 2026-10-04:** the findings sub-gate can read zero because\n**no agent review has ever run for the current head** — its summary says so in words\n(`No agent review has run for the current head`), but the sub-gate still reads as not-failing,\nso a sweep sees a clean PR that was never reviewed. The driver's `action` field caught it\n(`retrigger_gate`). An empty `chore:` push made the review run; it posted a medium finding\nwithin 20 minutes. The inverse trap fired on the same PR immediately after: the new gate read\n`Findings: passed` while that finding was open, because the review posted *after* the check\ncompleted. **Both gate readings were wrong, in opposite directions, on one PR inside 20\nminutes. Only `trail finding list` was right.**\n\n**A fourth, worse one — stale local worktrees.** Before merging main forward, check the\nworktree against its OWN PR head, not just against main: one worktree here was **76 commits\nbehind `origin/<its-own-branch>`** (0 ahead). Merging main from that tree and pushing would\nhave silently reverted the PR's own work with no conflict and a green build.\n`git merge --ff-only origin/<branch>` first, every time.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ef972216-c613-40b1-a043-460fb735c0f9","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:19:43.365Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls\ndescription: \"Two ways a finding sweep silently reports zero: scoping to the trails you happen to be working, and grepping ^01M when the CLI indents its IDs — use --json\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37\n  modified: 2026-09-04T06:00:35.108Z\n---\n\nReporting \"0 open findings\" twice in one session when the real count was **142** cost\ncredibility both times. Two independent causes, both silent:\n\n1. **Scope.** I swept only the ~15 trails I had been working. Findings live on *every*\n   trail, including ones whose PRs merged months ago — and those matter more, because they\n   describe defects already on `main`. Sweep the full trail-number range, both repos.\n2. **Parsing.** `entire trail finding list` **indents** its rows, so\n   `grep -cE \"^01M\"` matches nothing and prints a confident `0`. The correct filter is\n   `grep -cE \"^[[:space:]]+01M.*open\"`, and better still `--json` — the human table also\n   wraps long `LOCATION` values, which silently corrupts column-based `awk`.\n\nAlso: `--repo` requires an explicit trail selector, so `finding show <id>` alone fails —\nkeep the trail number paired with every id. Default `--freshness` is `current`; stale\nfindings are hidden unless asked for.\n\n**A third silent zero, found 2026-10-04:** the findings sub-gate can read zero because\n**no agent review has ever run for the current head** — its summary says so in words\n(`No agent review has run for the current head`), but the sub-gate still reads as not-failing,\nso a sweep sees a clean PR that was never reviewed. The driver's `action` field caught it\n(`retrigger_gate`). An empty `chore:` push made the review run; it posted a medium finding\nwithin 20 minutes. The inverse trap fired on the same PR immediately after: the new gate read\n`Findings: passed` while that finding was open, because the review posted *after* the check\ncompleted. **Both gate readings were wrong, in opposite directions, on one PR inside 20\nminutes. Only `trail finding list` was right.**\n\n**A fourth, worse one — stale local worktrees.** Before merging main forward, check the\nworktree against its OWN PR head, not just against main: one worktree here was **76 commits\nbehind `origin/<its-own-branch>`** (0 ahead). Merging main from that tree and pushing would\nhave silently reverted the PR's own work with no conflict and a green build.\n`git merge --ff-only origin/<branch>` first, every time.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a2ea5d13-deea-4d53-8062-79607a86253d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":255},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2609b83d-c474-46a5-92ad-a211e06d221a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
