{"parentUuid":"d6de34e0-7f1f-472c-ae1d-5c0cf7c797d9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPLaffFMuwMaCvdNLfzC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CPJ7x4GDncMSaHpYKpAr9i","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"for n in 371 373 375 376 377 372 374; do echo \"== #$n\"; gh pr view $n --repo entireio/entire-graph --json body -q .body | grep -iE 'identical|identity|byte-for-byte|sha256|same output|unchanged|trade|slower|cost' | head -5 | cut -c1-260; done","description":"Pull identity and trade-off claims from graph PR bodies"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1394,"cache_read_input_tokens":183671,"output_tokens":428,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":214},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1394,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":428,"cache_read_input_tokens":183671,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1394,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1394},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CPJ7x4GDncMSaHpYKpAr9i":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv && for n in 371 373 375 376 377 372 374; do echo \"== #$n\"; gh pr view $n --repo entireio/entire-graph --json body -q .body | grep -iE 'identical|identity|byte-for-byte|sha256|same output|unchanged|trade|slower|cost' | head -5 | cut -c1-260; done","description":"Pull identity and trade-off claims from graph PR bodies"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01CPJ7x4GDncMSaHpYKpAr9i":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"64f51493-f692-4881-aab7-791cdf28be43","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPLafKR5QEqAhL1PKFNL","requestRef":"0d798bbf-1d84-483d-9a77-d1879ae55c02","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"309c60fe-c621-4177-9bb4-24856d6df212","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:19:48.707Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"309c60fe-c621-4177-9bb4-24856d6df212","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f66e26da-3456-4f4a-ac51-861a28ca8ae0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CPJ7x4GDncMSaHpYKpAr9i","type":"tool_result","content":"== #371\n2. **`-m 1` does not stop Git early, but `-l` does.** Git now lists files, and each hit is validated with the existing `textMatchesSearchQuery` on its content. The matcher is line-local and monotone, so for a readable file \"the first matching line passes\" impl\nThe expression is unchanged, and so is the `-I` asymmetry with the fixed-string route. There is no `-F -i -l`.\n`GrepTreePatternLines` had one production caller. It is replaced by `GrepTreePatternFiles` and its two tests are ported. `grepPatternLines` (worktree routes) is unchanged in behaviour; it now shares a runner with the new function, with the same argv order.\n- **Output identity:** I byte-compared the JSON after `g2-strip.py` for base vs new on all three repos.\n  - With that field also stripped, all 16 outputs (3 repos × every rep, base and new) are byte-identical per repo. sha256 prefixes: cli `9203298341faaf27`, brain `9ab97eedbe4387c1`, eg `a64130fbe7f3fbd2`.\n== #373\n- **Same output.** Emission and reduction stay in index order, and process closures read only indexes built before the scan, so wider admission cannot change what they see.\n**Output identity:** `snapshot --format ndjson` sha256, base == new on all four repos:\n- The JSON output after stripping latency fields is byte-identical on all 6 base/new pairs.\n- `TestIndexedStreamingPipelineStopsAndJoinsBlockedProducers`: unchanged. It still requires exactly 8 started and all joined.\n== #375\n- the unchanged-history skip fired on both.\n**Output identity.**\n- def/neighbors/impact JSON is byte-identical base vs new on all 18 run pairs (6 verbs × 3 reps) after `g2-strip.py`, which removes the latency fields.\n- `snapshot --format ndjson` sha256 is identical: cli `5bf71305…`, brain `73eaa1f3…`.\n- `TestSpliceFileChangesWithRelationsSkipsUnchangedHistory`: history given in git-log order must return the cached slice itself, not a copy.\n== #376\n- Only a later query with the identical `OnlyFiles` key could read the entry back.\n- The diagnostics header comes from the complete snapshot either way (`searchDiagnosticsHeader`), so the output is unchanged.\n- The write cost more than re-deriving.\n- For each of 5 distinct queries per repo, in this order: novel base/new, then the identical repeat base/new. Order alternates per query.\n| cli | identical repeat | 1.999 | 1.717 | −0.282 (−14%) |\n== #377\nOn a repository within `coldCompleteSnapshotMaxFiles` (3000 files), a cold committed-tree query builds and persists the complete snapshot, then derives its own view from it. Before the build it ran the bounded content scan (`scoreSearchPaths`) to choose that v\nWhen the complete build is going to follow, the cold query now takes the warm route. That means a cache dir is in use, the search is on HEAD, neither `--max-indexed-files` nor `--index-all-files` was given, and the corpus is within the bound. The cold answer i\n- **Unchanged:** `--no-cache`, `--max-indexed-files`, `--index-all-files`, `--deep`, working-tree search, and repositories above the bound. They keep the content scan or the whole-corpus scope they had.\n- **(a) Compute the decision once and pass it down.** It can't be exact before selection. Build failure only happens after selection, and selection has to come first so a 0-hit query builds nothing. So the decision stays in the loader, and the search reacts to\nThe normal path is unchanged. The fixed head's cold output is the same JSON as the previous head's on cli q1 and eg `SearchRepository` (3 reps each). Wall time is within noise: 13.85 vs 14.18 s on cli, 14.29 vs 14.22 s on eg, load1 5.1-6.8.\n== #372\n**Output identity.** Only provenance changes. Comparing base and new JSON, the full ordered result\nlist (`file_path#symbol_name`) is 