{"parentUuid":"17fc02a6-97d5-4c5d-bb96-5e6bd0749934","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPLdaEezgHWTxaeh2QdM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_read_input_tokens":189283,"output_tokens":1759,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":54},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1759,"cache_read_input_tokens":189283,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7772,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"59aad184-82f1-40af-b537-e7258ec8479b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPLdZmd63ho57bgH75Co","requestRef":"c4d25e17-0db6-4752-bcd2-43b4f4864d4a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0585da78-baa8-4162-bdbb-107c68909594","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:20:32.216Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"0585da78-baa8-4162-bdbb-107c68909594","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPLdaEezgHWTxaeh2QdM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's where things stand, then your questions.\n\n**Status**\n- **Merging needs no approvals.** I checked GitHub's settings on both repos. \"Approvals\" is a step the Entire review tool reports, not a GitHub rule. I'll merge the 12 graph PRs myself, in order, using merge commits so Entire's checkpoint history survives.\n- **The Brain session is merging its own 13 PRs.** It asked me not to touch them, to avoid two sessions merging the same stack.\n- **Trail reviews:** an agent review ran on every one of the 25 PRs.\n  - **Graph:** all 12 have 0 open findings.\n  - **Brain:** #477, #483, #484 and #489 still show 9 findings marked open in total. They look like ones already fixed but never closed on the trail. I've asked the Brain session to close each one with evidence before merging.\n- **One blocker on #484.** Brain's GitHub settings require a passing benchmark check, so #484 can't merge while that check is red. Even an admin can't override it. The Brain session is fixing the two outdated benchmark tests. #484 merges last, after graph #380.\n- **Graph waits on #373.** The rebase agent is still running. Graph merging starts when it's done.\n\n## How the speed-ups were found and what changed\nI timed every step of every graph and Brain command and fixed only the biggest delays. None of it came from skipping work or caching wrong answers. Most of it was redundant work being removed.\n\n**Graph**\n| PR | What was wasting time | The change |\n|---|---|---|\n| #371 | Alias search ran `git grep` over the whole repo, including ignored files it never indexes, and read every matching line. | Search only the indexed files, list matching files instead of lines, then check each hit with the existing matcher. **224 → 5 s.** |\n| #373 | The indexer parses files in parallel but must output them in order. Its look-ahead window was small, so one slow file stalled every worker. | A 16× wider window, with the order kept. Cold indexing was 28–35% faster; being re-measured on top of #382. |\n| #375 | Every cached lookup re-sorted the whole history. | New history is spliced into the cached list. **0.62 → 0.44 s.** |\n| #376 | Each new query wrote a derived file to disk that cost more to write than to recompute. | Stopped writing it. |\n| #377 | The first (cold) query picked files differently from later ones, so answers could differ. | It now picks files the same way as later queries. 2.5–3.9 s faster. |\n| #372 | `cli` and `entiredb` couldn't be indexed at all because they're partial clones, so queries rebuilt from scratch. | Indexed safely with network fetching disabled. **`cli` query 34 → 2.5 s.** |\n\n**Brain**\n| PR | What was wasting time | The change |\n|---|---|---|\n| #481 + #479 | One `entire checkpoint explain` subprocess per checkpoint: about 5,700 calls of 2.5–3.6 s each. | Read the metadata from the local checkpoint store, ask Entire only about the rest, and do those several at a time. **5,721 → 134 calls, 2.4 h → 4 min.** |\n| #476 | History text was re-normalized once per keyword, up to 26 times. | Normalize once. **History index −40%.** |\n| #478 | One global freshness fingerprint, so any change invalidated every branch. | One fingerprint per branch. |\n\n## Did quality drop?\nNo. The speed fixes produce the same answers, and the rest made the tools more accurate.\n- **Same output, checked byte for byte.**\n  - #371, #375 and #373: identical JSON and snapshot hashes, base vs new, on 2–4 repos.\n  - #476: identical hash across 157,977 history records.\n  - #372: the identical result list, with commit details added.\n- **Fixes that improve correctness:**\n  - #374: false \"tool\" symbols cut from 84 to 3.\n  - #377: first and later answers now match.\n  - #142: a cancelled run no longer caches half a result.\n  - #378: missing references now produce a warning instead of failing silently.\n  - #480: Brain no longer accepts a list cut off at 100 as complete.\n  - #474, #483, #488 and #489: one bad item no longer blocks or drops everything.\n- **Every new test was checked by breaking the code on purpose** and confirming the test failed. Three adversarial review rounds signed off on #372's safety.\n- **Trade-offs, all stated in the PRs:**\n  - #377 adds about 0.8 s to one kind of search on the entire-graph repo.\n  - #380's older-commit answers are opt-in and labelled as stale.\n  - #379 keeps only the last 3 search stores, so checking out an older commit means a rebuild.\n- **One speed-up was not made, on purpose.** Brain's build-then-swap would have meant loosening a privacy test, so it's waiting for your decision.\n\nWhen the #373 agent reports, I'll check its new review, merge graph #370 → #378 in order, and tell the Brain session when #380 lands so #484 can go."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_read_input_tokens":189283,"output_tokens":1759,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":54},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1759,"cache_read_input_tokens":189283,"cache_creation_input_tokens":635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":635},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"59aad184-82f1-40af-b537-e7258ec8479b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPLdZmd63ho57bgH75Co","requestRef":"c4d25e17-0db6-4752-bcd2-43b4f4864d4a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"01fa71ff-bf13-4c8a-8891-cbae86c24747","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:20:41.489Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
