{"parentUuid":"f0f86331-ce4c-42f3-aa7e-ef93203a48cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPQEYADBEZcFW7Y5GNbM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Graph: **8 of 12 PRs are merged into main.**\n\n| Order | PR | Change | Merge commit |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | #370 | Ignore nested Claude Code worktrees | a12fff59 |\n| 2 | #371 | Alias search only scans indexed files (224 s → 5 s) | 227f7a60 |\n| 3 | #377 | First query gives the same answer as later ones | daa06090 |\n| 4 | #373 | Wider indexing window | 1d1e8394 |\n| 5 | #379 | Old search stores cleaned up | fc71355e |\n| 6 | #376 | Stop writing a derived file per query | 9bad2b4a |\n| 7 | #375 | Faster repeat lookups (0.62 s → 0.44 s) | 57f280bf |\n| 8 | #372 | Partial clones like `cli` and `entiredb` can be indexed, with no network fetches | b8850d68 |\n\nEach one had passing required checks and a trail review with 0 open findings when it merged.\n\n**#373 correction:** measured on top of the teammate's #382, it makes cold indexing only 3–10% faster, not 28–35%. #382 had already captured most of that gain, so the speed-up is shared between the two PRs. The output is still byte-identical on all 4 repos.\n\n**Still to merge:** #380, #374, #142 and #378 each conflict with what's now on main. The agent is applying the saved conflict fixes to each branch and checking that the final code matches the fully tested combined branch exactly. Then it runs CI and waits for a fresh trail review on each. I'll merge them once everything passes.\n\n**Brain:** the Brain session is merging its own 13 PRs, with #484 last. I'll tell it when graph #380 is merged, since #484 depends on it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":612,"cache_read_input_tokens":206707,"output_tokens":606,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests"