{"parentUuid":"93dd50ed-b3be-4dcd-addc-352a8eb6c2dc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPSt3ybxCf2Hw1Xktwjm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011fWgzUqp843tYgq15r7p8i","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map && cp process-map.html .process-map.pre-merge.html && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='process-map.html'; s=open(p).read()\nshas={'370':'a12fff59','371':'227f7a60','377':'daa06090','373':'1d1e8394','379':'fc71355e','376':'9bad2b4a','375':'57f280bf','372':'b8850d68','380':'ebf9a2fa','374':'e514be52','142':'1492feb9','378':'d0475ce8'}\n# meta + callouts\ns=s.replace('<span>Brain final; graph on hold for one rebase</span>','<span><b>Graph: all 12 merged</b>; Brain merging its 13</span>')\ns=re.sub(r'<div class=\"callout warn\"><b>Graph: hold\\.</b>.*?</div>',\n '<div class=\"callout info\"><b>Graph: all 12 merged (2026-10-25).</b> Merged in order with merge commits. Graph main is now d0475ce8, and its tree is byte-identical to the combined test branch <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381\">#381</a> (8b0913a4), which passed CI and has now been closed. Each PR had green required checks and a trail review with 0 open findings on the exact commit merged. <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/373\">#373</a> was rebased onto teammate PR #382 first. On top of #382 it is 3–10% faster at cold indexing, not 28–35%, because #382 had already captured most of that.</div>',s,flags=re.S)\ns=s.replace('<b>Brain: done, waiting only on approvals.</b>','<b>Brain: the Brain session is merging its 13 PRs.</b> #484 goes last, after its two outdated benchmark tests are fixed. That check is required on brain main and admins cannot bypass it.')\ns=s.replace('<h2>Before you merge</h2>','<h2>Merge notes</h2>')\ns=s.replace('<li><b>Re-run the merge simulation first.</b> <span class=\"mono\">main</span> keeps moving: a brain PR that merged cleanly at noon conflicted by evening.</li>','<li><b>Neither repo requires an approval on GitHub.</b> Entire\\'s \"Approvals\" gate is reported, not enforced, so merges went ahead without one.</li>')\n# graph table note cells -> merged SHA\nfor n,sha in shas.items():\n    s=re.sub(r'(pull/%s\">#%s</a></td><td>.*?</td><td>.*?</td><td class=\"note\">).*?(</td></tr>)'%(n,n), r'\\g<1>merged <span class=\"mono\">%s</span>\\g<2>'%sha, s, count=1, flags=re.S)\ns=s.replace('<td>was 28–35% faster before #382; being re-measured on top of it</td>','<td>cold index 3–10% faster on top of #382 (was 28–35% before it); identical output</td>')\ns=s.replace('<th>When merging</th>','<th>Status</th>')\ns=s.replace('<h2>Graph, in merge order</h2>','<h2>Graph, merged in this order</h2>')\ns=s.replace('<tr><td><b>Approve the 25 PRs</b></td><td>GitHub won\\'t let you approve your own PRs, so a teammate approves or you override.</td></tr>','')\ns=s.replace('<p class=\"note\">Combined on the cli repo: cold index 11.8 → 7.8 s, first warm query 11.7 → 3.5 s, warm lookups 0.62 → 0.44 s.</p>','<p class=\"note\">Measured on the cli repo against the old main (before #382): cold index 11.8 → 7.8 s, first warm query 11.7 → 3.5 s, warm lookups 0.62 → 0.44 s. The cold-index figure overlaps with #382\\'s own speed-up. For users to get these changes, a new nightly or release has to be built from main.</p>')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -c 'merged <span class=\"mono\">' process-map.html; grep -o 'Graph: all 12 merged[^<]*' process-map.html | head -2","description":"Update the merge plan page to show all graph PRs merged"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":579,"cache_read_input_tokens":216479,"output_tokens":1840,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":269},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_crea