{"parentUuid":"6142d7e7-ac5b-4d9c-808e-3fe88e4c127f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPSxfXNVwuafzqAU31mq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JV3peCM2tsMuSjVcfzcZr9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='process-map.html'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('<span><b>Graph: all 12 merged</b>; Brain merging its 13</span>','<span><b>All 25 merged</b>: 12 graph, 13 brain</span>')\ns=s.replace('<span>Nothing merged</span>','<span>graph main d0475ce8 · brain main c4c4ae1c</span>')\ns=re.sub(r'<b>Brain: the Brain session is merging its 13 PRs\\.</b>.*?</div>',\n '<b>Brain: all 13 merged (2026-10-25)</b>, by the Brain session, in order with merge commits. #484 went last, after graph #380 and after its two outdated benchmark tests were fixed. Brain main is c4c4ae1c. <b>One follow-up:</b> the final review sweep found an open finding on <a href=\"https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/390\">trail 390</a> in code already merged from #481. The local-metadata shortcut can pre-load sessions that were meant to go down the path that refuses an incomplete export. A fix is being written as a new PR. It isn\\'t settled yet whether this ever shipped smaller data or is only an internal contradiction.</div>',s,flags=re.S)\ns=s.replace('<li>A closed PR gets no new CI,','<li><span class=\"mono\">entire trail finding list</span> hides open findings by default. Always pass <span class=\"mono\">--status any --freshness any</span>: the bare form reported 0 open on trails that had 3, 3, 2 and 1.</li>\\n      <li>A closed PR gets no new CI,')\ns=s.replace('<h2>Brain</h2>','<h2>Brain, merged</h2>')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -o 'All 25 merged\\|Brain: all 13 merged\\|hides open findings' process-map.html | sort | uniq -c","description":"Update the page to show all brain PRs merged plus the follow-up"},"caller":{"type":"direc