{"parentUuid":"a32d6270-e4e8-47a5-93c7-48a74a589a37","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPV3LFNUMu5VE4dkCPkm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RhSDyrBhmFbuf42ejccEb4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='process-map.html'; s=open(p).read()\nold_start=s.index('<b>One follow-up:</b>'); old_end=s.index('</div>',old_start)\ns=s[:old_start]+'<b>One follow-up, a real bug:</b> the final review sweep (<a href=\"https://entire.com/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/390\">trail 390</a>) found that code merged from #481 could produce an incomplete export marked as complete. A checkpoint that was never committed could be skipped while the export still recorded itself as complete. The fix is <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/499\">#499</a>, by the Brain session. <b>It deliberately changes behaviour:</b> an export that used to ship despite an unreadable or undeclared checkpoint may now refuse with <span class=\"mono\">checkpoint_scope_incomplete</span>. That is the intended fail-safe. #499 also carries the same one-line compile fix as evisdren\\'s #497, so whichever lands first turns brain main green again.'+s[old_end:]\ns=s.replace('His fix, <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/497\">#497</a>, is open and is his to merge.','His fix, <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/497\">#497</a>, is open and is his to merge. The Brain session\\'s <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/499\">#499</a> carries the identical line, so main goes green when either one lands.')\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Correct the page on the trail-390 bug and describe #499"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1153,"cache_