 was never committed could be skipped while the export still recorded itself as complete. The fix is <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/499\">#499</a>, by the Brain session. <b>It deliberately changes behaviour:</b> an export that used to ship despite an unreadable or undeclared checkpoint may now refuse with <span class=\"mono\">checkpoint_scope_incomplete</span>. That is the intended fail-safe. #499 also carries the same one-line compile fix as evisdren\\'s #497, so whichever lands first turns brain main green again.'+s[old_end:]\ns=s.replace('His fix, <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/497\">#497</a>, is open and is his to merge.','His fix, <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/497\">#497</a>, is open and is his to merge. The Brain session\\'s <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/499\">#499</a> carries the identical line, so main goes green when either one lands.')\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Correct the page on the trail-390 bug and describe #499"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JZG1YrShZS6pUWLAK5Jhru","name":"Artifact","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","url":"https://claude.ai/artifact/FkY6c5J1XdzaYGM1Q7T9dU","label":"trail-390 settled; #499"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
