{"parentUuid":"ce9d86dc-9ffd-4d79-8f55-c935c1389508","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"075201e8-3156-4e81-a183-2f45bce2878a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TTxYBYyoqiPFpUhWuRRoBD","type":"tool_result","content":"7727 'merged from #481 could produce an incomplete export marked as complete. A checkpoint that was never committed could be skipped while the export still recorded itself as complete. The fix is <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/499\">#499</a>, by the Brain session. <b>It deliberately changes behaviour:</b> an export that used to ship despite an unreadable or undeclared checkpoint may now refuse with <span class=\"mono\">checkpoint_scope_incomplete</span>. That is the intended fail-safe. #499 also carries the same one-line compile fix as evisdren\\'s #497, so whichever lands first t'\n=====\n7983 'a>, by the Brain session. <b>It deliberately changes behaviour:</b> an export that used to ship despite an unreadable or undeclared checkpoint may now refuse with <span class=\"mono\">checkpoint_scope_incomplete</span>. That is the intended fail-safe. #499 also carries the same one-line compile fix as evisdren\\'s #497, so whichever lands first turns brain main green again.</div>\\n\\n    <h2>Merge notes</h2>\\n    <ul class=\"tight\">\\n      <li><b>Neither repo requires an approval on GitHub.</b> Entire\\'s \"Approvals\" gate is reported, not enforced, so merges went ahead without one.</li>\\n      <li>Use merg'\n=====\n8045 ':</b> an export that used to ship despite an unreadable or undeclared checkpoint may now refuse with <span class=\"mono\">checkpoint_scope_incomplete</span>. That is the intended fail-safe. #499 also carries the same one-line compile fix as evisdren\\'s #497, so whichever lands first turns brain main green again.</div>\\n\\n    <h2>Merge notes</h2>\\n    <ul class=\"tight\">\\n      <li><b>Neither repo requires an approval on GitHub.</b> Entire\\'s \"Approvals\" gate is reported, not enforced, so merges went ahead without one.</li>\\n      <li>Use merge commits. Merge graph <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/en'\n=====\n8847 'graph-patches/</span>, and each was checked by breaking it on purpose. Brain needs no patches: its conflict fixes are committed on the PR branches, and <span class=\"mono\">brain-patches/</span> is kept only for reference.</li>\\n      <li><b>Brain main went red after our merges (2026-10-25)</b>, though no PR of ours was broken on its own. evisdren merged his own <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/496\">#496</a> on top of #483, renaming a helper that #483\\'s test calls, so the two don\\'t compile together. His fix, <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/497\">#497</a'\n=====\n9190 'ren merged his own <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/496\">#496</a> on top of #483, renaming a helper that #483\\'s test calls, so the two don\\'t compile together. His fix, <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/497\">#497</a>, is open and is his to merge. The Brain session\\'s <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/499\">#499</a> carries the identical line, so main goes green when either one lands. Lesson: the merge simulation covered only our own batch. It should also cover other open PRs that touch the same packages, or at least list the ones it '\n=====\n9309 'er that #483\\'s test calls, so the two don\\'t compile together. His fix, <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/497\">#497</a>, is open and is his to merge. The Brain session\\'s <a href=\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/499\">#499</a> carries the identical line, so main goes green when either one lands. Lesson: the merge simulation covered only our own batch. It should also cover other open PRs that touch the same packages, or at least list the ones it left out.</li>\\n      <li><span class=\"mono\">entire trail finding list</span> hides open finding