{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"b11c15e85e5323e8a31ee9d3b3368101a7adc795c0c90bf4e2d01aa1e3781272","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UxmR72z4NDQ3jqmGPMTN4h","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"announce graph swap to v0.6.0 now","message":"Announcing a shared-binary swap: I'm repointing the installed graph to managed v0.6.0 now, myself. Hold any graph runs for about a minute. Answers to your questions: (1) Managed release. The symlink wasn't deliberate: the target is a gitignored Oct-24 nightly binary (d4a0c186) left by a path install, not a dev build I'm testing. (2) Yes, v0.6.0 has all 12. The tag points at dfe93b98, and git merge-base --is-ancestor confirms it contains d0475ce8 (our last merge), 726638d1 (#383), b8850d68 (#372) and ebf9a2fa (#380). The nightly .202610260619.dfe93b98 is the same commit. No entire-graph processes are running. Method: `entire plugin install graph --force --yes`, which installs into pkg/graph and replaces the link entry, so nothing is written through the old symlink. I'll message again when it's verified. The 74% duplicate facts are worth a brain-lane row. Graph ranking doesn't read the fact store, so it's yours to dedup."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
