{"parentUuid":"40be38c7-79dd-462c-b6f3-11d180a55cc6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTopWgYuuteyi4fep8Vh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph improvements are now released and installed on your machine, so the graph nightly is off your list. Someone on the team released graph v0.6.0 on Oct 26. It contains all 12 of our merges plus evisdren's #383.\n\n- **Installed:** your machine was still running an Oct 24 build, from before any of the merges. The Brain session noticed and asked me first, since graph is my lane. I told it about the swap, then replaced that build with the official v0.6.0 install. The old build is untouched, and I kept a backup copy.\n- **Checked:** `entire graph version` reports v0.6.0, and the guidance hook for subagents still works. A search on the entire-graph repo took 7.3 s the first time, while the cache rebuilt, then 2.8 s.\n- **Brain is current too:** it's on v0.4.0, upgraded by the Brain session. Brain #484's \"how stale is the code context\" feature now works, because it needed a graph release that included #380.\n\n**One thing for you to decide:** `entire sem` isn't just an old name for the graph on this machine. It runs a separate, outdated build (version \"dev\") from ~/Documents/Coding/entire-sem. Any agent or script that still types `entire sem` gets old behaviour. `entire plugin remove sem` would unregister it without deleting any files. Want me to run that?\n\n**From the Brain session:** 74% of the facts in entire-brain's fact store are exact duplicates (7,526 rows, 1,958 unique). A 10-result recall only returns 3–4 different facts. Fixing that is Brain-lane work.\n\n**Your list now:** the decisions on the page, the `gate-neutral-reads-as-reviewed` request, and /compact.\n\nThe page (https://claude.ai/artifact/FkY6c5J1XdzaYGM1Q7T9dU), the board, the codebase map and memory are all updated."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":668,"cache_read_input_tokens":153746,"output_tokens":649,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":31},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":668,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":153746,"cache_creation_input_tokens":668,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":668},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"77c79b2d-8d56-4a59-b130-63f687be582c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgTopWSfbtPRi2bSP8gkp","requestRef":"0e67b983-2ae5-4029-91cc-05728396d83d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1154824e-0a26-4429-858f-ea64666aede6","timestamp":"2026-10-28T01:59:25.935Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
