{"parentUuid":"7d405ca5-21a7-4ce7-90c3-b505d2d6debf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTpURovQF98QdgnP2egz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_read_input_tokens":180297,"output_tokens":955,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":170},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":180297,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1995,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"54b8c527-ca0e-4c47-b220-e909988e7d78","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgTpURa2utAD4aWYSRcbq","requestRef":"00f576b3-d077-48d9-9312-493ad30a8918","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e8acc622-e06c-4272-8a0a-ac93d0da4b8e","timestamp":"2026-10-28T02:07:55.661Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"e8acc622-e06c-4272-8a0a-ac93d0da4b8e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTpURovQF98QdgnP2egz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YWSrX4YTxE1UhFQeSDuyYt","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"correct: cli/entiredb ARE partial clones","message":"Correction on two points, both checked on disk.\n\n(1) cli and entiredb ARE partial clones. Your check only looked at `remote.origin.*`, and the promisor here is a remote named by URL. This is the exact trap in DECISIONS-FOR-YOU §7. `git config --get-regexp '\\.promisor$|partialclonefilter$'` gives:\n- cli: remote.https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git.promisor true / partialclonefilter blob:none\n- entiredb: remote.https://github.com/entirehq/entiredb.git.promisor true / partialclonefilter blob:none\n- entire-graph: none\n\nThe multi-GB .git doesn't contradict this: origin is full and the URL-named remote is blob-filtered. That is the shape graph refused before #372 (\"its Git config declares a promisor remote\"). So a successful semantic build on cli/entiredb under v0.6.0 IS evidence for #372, and a refusal mentioning promisor would be evidence against it. Please send me the result either way.\n\n(2) \"semantic snapshot header missing commit\" is not v0.6.0 rejecting a v0.5.1 header. No released brain since v0.2.0 has that string in production code: `git log -S` shows it removed in 887b4055 (2026-10-22, COR-2217 \"delegate code storage to Graph\"), and it's absent from production code at v0.2.0, v0.3.0 and v0.4.0. Only a legacy_retired_* test fixture keeps it. entire-graph has no such string at all. v0.4.0's only header check is \"semantic snapshot header missing repo_key\" (semantic_repokey.go:144). So that failed status was most likely written by a pre-COR-2217 build and persisted, which would mean these repos' semantic was failed before the swap. I can't confirm that from here, because your repair has already replaced the status. If the store records when or which build wrote the failure, that would settle it. Until then I'm not treating it as an upgrade-skew bug.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Correction on two points, both checked on disk.\n\n(1…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_read_input_tokens":180297,"output_tokens":955,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":170},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":180297,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YWSrX4YTxE1UhFQeSDuyYt":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"correct: cli/entiredb ARE partial clones","message":"Correction on two points, both checked on disk.\n\n(1) cli and entiredb ARE partial clones. Your check only looked at `remote.origin.*`, and the promisor here is a remote named by URL. This is the exact trap in DECISIONS-FOR-YOU §7. `git config --get-regexp '\\.promisor$|partialclonefilter$'` gives:\n- cli: remote.https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git.promisor true / partialclonefilter blob:none\n- entiredb: remote.https://github.com/entirehq/entiredb.git.promisor true / partialclonefilter blob:none\n- entire-graph: none\n\nThe multi-GB .git doesn't contradict this: origin is full and the URL-named remote is blob-filtered. That is the shape graph refused before #372 (\"its Git config declares a promisor remote\"). So a successful semantic build on cli/entiredb under v0.6.0 IS evidence for #372, and a refusal mentioning promisor would be evidence against it. Please send me the result either way.\n\n(2) \"semantic snapshot header missing commit\" is not v0.6.0 rejecting a v0.5.1 header. No released brain since v0.2.0 has that string in production code: `git log -S` shows it removed in 887b4055 (2026-10-22, COR-2217 \"delegate code storage to Graph\"), and it's absent from production code at v0.2.0, v0.3.0 and v0.4.0. Only a legacy_retired_* test fixture keeps it. entire-graph has no such string at all. v0.4.0's only header check is \"semantic snapshot header missing repo_key\" (semantic_repokey.go:144). So that failed status was most likely written by a pre-COR-2217 build and persisted, which would mean these repos' semantic was failed before the swap. I can't confirm that from here, because your repair has already replaced the status. If the store records when or which build wrote the failure, that would settle it. Until then I'm not treating it as an upgrade-skew bug."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"54b8c527-ca0e-4c47-b220-e909988e7d78","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgTpURa2utAD4aWYSRcbq","requestRef":"00f576b3-d077-48d9-9312-493ad30a8918","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb3c372c-2a8d-4cff-9f2c-3b836e1261f5","timestamp":"2026-10-28T02:08:02.374Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
