{"parentUuid":"1e841891-c7c4-4b7c-84bb-0be0e625f307","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTpVcLTE5rptNuuz3F1K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I corrected two wrong claims from the Brain session, so nothing new needs you. Its index repairs on entire-graph, cli and entiredb are still running.\n\n- **cli and entiredb are partial clones.** The Brain session only checked the remote named `origin`. In both repos the remote that marks the clone as partial (the promisor) is named by its URL. That's the trap its own decisions file warns about. So if the repair builds their code index, that does prove v0.6.0 can index partial clones (#372). Before #372, the graph refused these repos.\n- **The \"header missing commit\" error is not caused by the upgrade.** No Brain release since v0.2.0 contains that message outside tests. It was removed on 2026-10-22, and graph never had it. The likeliest explanation is an old failure record left over from an older build, meaning these repos' index had been broken since before the swap. I can't prove that, because the repair has already overwritten the status. I've asked the Brain session to check, if the store records which build wrote it.\n\nWhen the repairs finish, I'll tell you whether cli and entiredb indexed.\n\nYour four yes/no items are unchanged:\n1. Remove the dead Brain MCP entry from `~/.claude.json`.\n2. Update both CLAUDE.md files.\n3. `entire plugin remove sem`.\n4. A graph PR so \"degraded\" only appears when source code fails to parse."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":440,"cache_read_input_tokens":181940,"output_tokens":476,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":24},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":440,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":476,"cache_read_input_tokens":181940,"cache_creation_input_tokens":440,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":440},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5550ae36-c322-4e90-a60a-7de5bd9e5e68","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgTpVc5KtSxfUzaTgPwzT","requestRef":"1aafec5f-538e-4111-b55d-f87ed231cc84","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2324fe8d-c758-4023-8061-21eac4f95bde","timestamp":"2026-10-28T02:08:14.916Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"2324fe8d-c758-4023-8061-21eac4f95bde","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"stop_hook_summary","hookCount":3,"hookInfos":[{"command":"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code stop'","durationMs":5067},{"command":"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/claude-bridge-wake.py"},{"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/stop-review-gate-hook.mjs\"","durationMs":57}],"hookErrors":[],"hookAdditionalContext":[],"preventedContinuation":false,"stopReason":"","hasOutput":false,"level":"suggestion","timestamp":"2026-10-28T02:08:19.991Z","uuid":"79b115f8-32a0-4e5a-9f85-dcb963a12761","toolUseID":"86f95034-4a32-4062-b658-f71a4bf8a87e","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
