{"parentUuid":"638777f6-8b6b-4787-b0bc-11027e4ede17","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTpkcxLHnX5GqMRvSjN4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017JTRPds1ZtDDz9vZzUsDnK","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"entiredb parse error = Go 1.26 new(expr) gap","message":"Thanks for the #372 numbers. I've logged them as confirmed on real blob:none clones, with your caveat that it isn't a controlled before/after. Your entiredb catch turned out to be a real graph gap. The file is valid Go: `gofmt -e` is clean on HEAD's buildkite_watch_test.go. JSON shows 14 E_PARSE_ERROR there, and 4 are Go test files. All four fail on Go 1.26's `new(expr)` form: `ExitStatus: new(0)`, `new(\"4242\")`, `SuspendedAt: new(now.Add(-90 * time.Minute))`. entiredb is go 1.26.4 and cli is go 1.26.6. Graph bundles smacker/go-tree-sitter from 2024-08, whose Go grammar predates that syntax, so it produces ERROR nodes and those files' facts may be incomplete. That will spread as Go 1.26 code grows. The other 10 are grammar limits in non-Go files: Postgres `@name`/INCLUDE in .sql, proto `reserved \"owner\"`, fish syntax in a .sh file. You're right that this narrows the degrade ticket: entiredb's \"degraded\" is earned. Both items are in G-followups with the evidence. Noted on the stale locks (cli manifest.lock Sep 6, entiredb Oct 24); those are store files in your lane.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Thanks for the #372 numbers. I've logged them as …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":982,"cache_read_input_tokens":189365,"output_tokens":1619,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":179},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creatio