{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"8e6cfa4cc6ba8128e93293b4992d2de5b6621f83a3d8b2f466caade06ab56a96","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GTVechUPcyGEfj35SUVKyU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,fcntl,os,datetime\nlk=open('.claude/todo-board.lock','w'); fcntl.flock(lk,fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='.claude/todo-board.json'; d=json.load(open(p))\nfor r in d['tasks']:\n    if r.get('id')=='G-followups' and 'Go 1.26 new(expr)' not in r['title']:\n        r['title']+=(\" | NEW 2026-10-27 (real parser gap): Go 1.26 `new(expr)` (new(0), new(\\\"4242\\\"), new(now.Add(..))) yields tree-sitter ERROR nodes -> E_PARSE_ERROR on 4 valid entiredb Go test files (gofmt clean); graph bundles smacker/go-tree-sitter 2024-08 grammar. Will spread as Go 1.26 code grows. Also SQL `@name`/INCLUDE, proto reserved names, fish syntax in .sh = grammar limits.\"\n                     \" | #372 CONFIRMED on real blob:none clones: cli 1427 files, entiredb 2542 files indexed under v0.6.0, no promisor refusal (not a controlled before/after).\")\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='seconds')\njson.dump(d,open(p+'.tmp','w'),indent=2); os.replace(p+'.tmp',p)\np='/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/semantic-layer-handoff-state.md'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"- **Open for user:** (nightly done);\"\ns=s.replace(a,\"- **#372 confirmed on real data 2026-10-27:** brain repair under graph v0.6.0 indexed cli (1427 files) + entiredb (2542) with no promisor refusal. **New graph gap:** Go 1.26 `new(expr)` breaks the bundled tree-sitter-go (smacker 2024-08) -> E_PARSE_ERROR on valid Go (4 entiredb test files). Both in G-followups.\\n\"+a)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF","description":"Log Go 1.26 parser gap and #372 confirmation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017JTRPds1ZtDDz9vZzUsDnK","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"entiredb parse error = Go 1.26 new(expr) gap","message":"Thanks for the #372 numbers. I've logged them as confirmed on real blob:none clones, with your caveat that it isn't a controlled before/after. Your entiredb catch turned out to be a real graph gap. The file is valid Go: `gofmt -e` is clean on HEAD's buildkite_watch_test.go. JSON shows 14 E_PARSE_ERROR there, and 4 are Go test files. All four fail on Go 1.26's `new(expr)` form: `ExitStatus: new(0)`, `new(\"4242\")`, `SuspendedAt: new(now.Add(-90 * time.Minute))`. entiredb is go 1.26.4 and cli is go 1.26.6. Graph bundles smacker/go-tree-sitter from 2024-08, whose Go grammar predates that syntax, so it produces ERROR nodes and those files' facts may be incomplete. That will spread as Go 1.26 code grows. The other 10 are grammar limits in non-Go files: Postgres `@name`/INCLUDE in .sql, proto `reserved \"owner\"`, fish syntax in a .sh file. You're right that this narrows the degrade ticket: entiredb's \"degraded\" is earned. Both items are in G-followups with the evidence. Noted on the stale locks (cli manifest.lock Sep 6, entiredb Oct 24); those are store files in your lane."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
