th in G-followups. Measured: 4 files/26 calls (entiredb tests only); defs 77/77 + outer CALLS 10/10 survive (tree-sitter error recovery) — only exprs inside new(...) at risk. Upstream tree-sitter-go master still needs a type in special_argument_list → fix = vendored patched grammar, not a bump.\\n\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF","description":"Record new(expr) impact measurement and fix path"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c325f506-8d4a-4a46-850f-ab840b7ebdc0","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgTq2G6fSHkHevMWdUbmT","requestRef":"055ed473-06cd-476d-9c7a-ddadcccc80da","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"49cfefd4-af16-4b17-862f-35299d2230fb","timestamp":"2026-10-28T02:15:15.925Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"49cfefd4-af16-4b17-862f-35299d2230fb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTq2GMXj4oN1a1PPvq2y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HuLW5zT3UY57nZaw22m3QB","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"new(expr): measured impact is small, fix is vendored grammar","message":"I measured both of your questions, and the framing does overreach. Please don't tell the user that neighbors/impact are \"confidently wrong\" on Go 1.26. The data:\n- **Blast radius today:** 4 files and 26 calls, all in entiredb test files. cli, entire-graph, entire-brain and entire-api have zero. I counted with a go/ast walk for new() whose argument is a literal, call, binary, unary or composite expression. `new(x)` with a bare identifier is ambiguous with a type and parses fine.\n- **The damage is local.** tree-sitter's error recovery keeps the surrounding structure. All 77 functions in the 4 files are in `graph symbols` (9/9, 40/40, 12/12, 16/16). In github_email_identities_test.go, all 10 functions that call UpsertGitHubEmailIdentity have the CALLS edge in `graph edges`, including the ones whose only call line contains new(\"4242\"). What's at risk is what sits inside the new(...) argument, for example the Add call in new(now.Add(...)). I didn't measure that case.\n- **It's not a dependency bump.** Upstream tree-sitter-go master (0.25.0, Sep 2025) still defines special_argument_list for new/make as '(' $._type, ... ')', so even the latest grammar rejects new(0). The fix is a patched grammar vendored under internal/sem/grammars/go, where graph already vendors 11 grammars, plus an upstream PR.\n\nSo it's a real correctness gap, growing as Go 1.26 code spreads, but small and contained today. I'd call it below the degrade-label confusion in user impact right now. Both are in G-followups with these numbers.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"I measured both of your questions, and the framin…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":684,"cache_read_input_tokens":205167,"output_tokens":1863,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":342},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":684,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1863,"cache_read_input_tokens":205167,"cache_creation_input_tokens":684,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":684},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HuLW5zT3UY57nZaw22m3QB":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"new(expr): measured impact is small, fix is vendored grammar","message":"I measured both of your questions, and the framing does overreach. Please don't tell the user that neighbors/impact are \"confidently wrong\" on Go 1.26. The data:\n- **Blast radius today:** 4 files and 26 calls, all in entiredb test files. cli, entire-graph, entire-brain and entire-api have zero. I counted with a go/ast walk for new() whose argument is a literal, call, binary, unary or composite expression. `new(x)` with a bare identifier is ambiguous with a type and parses fine.\n- **The damage is local.** tree-sitter's error recovery keeps the surrounding structure. All 77 functions in the 4 files are in `graph symbols` (9/9, 40/40, 12/12, 16/16). In github_email_identities_test.go, all 10 functions that call UpsertGitHubEmailIdentity have the CALLS edge in `graph edges`, including the ones whose only call line contains new(\"4242\"). What's at risk is what sits inside the new(...) argument, for example the Add call in new(now.Add(...)). I didn't measure that case.\n- **It's not a dependency bump.** Upstream tree-sitter-go master (0.25.0, Sep 2025) still defines special_argument_list for new/make as '(' $._type, ... ')', so even the latest grammar rejects new(0). The fix is a patched grammar vendored under internal/sem/grammars/go, where graph already vendors 11 grammars, plus an upstream PR.\n\nSo it's a real correctness gap, growing as Go 1.26 code spreads, but small and contained today. I'd call it below the degrade-label confusion in user impact right now. Both are in G-followups with these numbers."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c325f506-8d4a-4a46-850f-ab840b7ebdc0","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgTq2G6fSHkHevMWdUbmT","requestRef":"055ed473-06cd-476d-9c7a-ddadcccc80da","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"af5de417-1e8b-401d-8d54-2e3a1bfb2e51","timestamp":"2026-10-28T02:15:21.372Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
