{"parentUuid":"f663eff3-b4ce-4440-a93e-1eca73cad914","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTq3aL3nCi3WVkDEuhgQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Go 1.26 `new(value)` bug is real but small today. The Brain session plans to tell you graph can be \"confidently wrong\" on Go 1.26 code; my measurements don't support that.\n\n- **Where it occurs:** 4 files with 26 uses, all entiredb test files. cli, entire-graph, entire-brain and entire-api have none.\n- **What gets lost:** very little. The parser recovers around the broken spot, so every function in those 4 files is still in graph (77 of 77). Calls on the broken lines also survive: all 10 test functions that call the function on those lines still show the call. Only code inside the `new(...)` brackets is at risk, and I didn't measure that part.\n- **The fix is more than a dependency bump.** Even the newest version of the open-source Go parser graph uses still rejects `new(0)`. Graph would need its own patched copy, as it already keeps for 11 other languages, plus a fix sent upstream. It's not urgent, but it grows as people adopt Go 1.26.\n\nSeparately, the Brain session withdrew its \"stale locks\" warning: those Brain store lock files are working normally, so there's nothing to clean.\n\nEverything is on the board under graph follow-ups with these numbers.\n\n**Still waiting on your yes:**\n1. Remove the dead Brain MCP entry from `~/.claude.json`.\n2. Update both CLAUDE.md files to point at the Brain CLI.\n3. `entire plugin remove sem`.\n4. A graph PR so \"degraded\" only appears when source code fails to parse. This one currently confuses agents more than the parser bug does.\n5. A graph PR with a patched Go parser so Go 1.26 `new(value)` parses."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2152,"cache_read_input_tokens":205851,"output_tokens":563,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2152,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":563,"cache_read_input_tokens":205851,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2152,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2152},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"47a38f76-da24-4a69-9d19-7de981966f86","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgTq3a1hmbLmqwtrrBurM","requestRef":"769a3642-27eb-4a26-9275-685763962c37","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f65fa7e-8329-4cf0-b502-9f967130f8ee","timestamp":"2026-10-28T02:15:28.706Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
