{"parentUuid":"93a11709-ae87-4fbf-8a43-82425554b67a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTqBjWvW5sotRq7hTtTH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The last open question on the Go 1.26 bug is answered: graph loses no information on these files. The parse error is a false alarm whose only real effect is adding to the misleading \"degraded\" label.\n\n**Calls nested inside `new(...)`:** these were the last thing at risk. I tested them in a tiny scratch repo: a function whose only call to `g()` is written as `new(g())`. Graph flags the file as a parse error but still records the call to `g`. The two control functions came out right too.\n\n**Overall:** I found no lost information anywhere, from function definitions to calls on the broken lines to calls nested inside `new(...)`. That merges this bug into the \"degraded\" one.\n\n**Cheaper fix:** for Go files, graph could check Go's own parser before reporting a parse error. Graph already uses Go's parser in three places. A patched copy of the open-source Go parser is still the complete fix, but no longer needed soon.\n\nThe Brain session's extra match in entire-graph is Ruby code inside a Go test string, not Go.\n\n**Still waiting on your yes:**\n1. Remove the dead Brain MCP entry from `~/.claude.json`.\n2. Update both CLAUDE.md files to point at the Brain CLI.\n3. `entire plugin remove sem`.\n4. One graph PR covering both labels: say \"degraded\" only when source code genuinely fails to parse, and check Go's own parser before calling a Go file a parse error."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1753,"cache_read_input_tokens":214106,"output_tokens":469,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1753,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":469,"cache_read_input_tokens":214106,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1753},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b4e28332-d43f-4b2c-ad8c-d66bc11b3b0a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgTqBjG3NTHpkeYYG39B7","requestRef":"37649b48-d679-476e-9e96-89e9fa1f27d3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f6f70fe1-77b5-4649-a992-01c50630d261","timestamp":"2026-10-28T02:17:18.576Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
