{"parentUuid":"8f997464-0760-4e0e-a00a-8d84dbe6ecb5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/semantic-layer-handoff-state.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/semantic-layer-handoff-state.md","content":"---\nname: semantic-layer-handoff-state\ndescription: 2026-10-25 ALL 25 MERGED — graph 12 (main d0475ce8, == #381 tree) + brain 13 (main c4c4ae1c); graph v0.6.0 released+installed; brain mains green\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n**2026-10-25 evening: ALL 25 PRs MERGED on the user's explicit \"merge\".** Neither repo requires approvals on GitHub\n(Entire Gates \"Approvals\" is reported, not enforced); brain main has enforce_admins + required benchmark-corpus /\nbrowser-smoke, so #484 needed its brainmark tests fixed first.\n- **Graph (I merged):** 370 a12fff59, 371 227f7a60, 377 daa06090 (retargeted), 373 1d1e8394, 379 fc71355e,\n  376 9bad2b4a, 375 57f280bf, 372 b8850d68, 380 ebf9a2fa, 374 e514be52, 142 1492feb9, 378 d0475ce8. Final main tree\n  8b0913a4 == #381 tip tree; #381 closed. Last four went in as a fast-forward CHAIN (each merges its predecessor +\n  saved resolution patch) → one CI cycle instead of four.\n- **#373 after #382:** keeps #382's FIFO pool, only lookahead 4→16 / buffers 8→2; −3.4..−9.5% (not −28..−35%).\n- **Brain (brain session merged):** all 13, main c4c4ae1c. Follow-up: open finding trail 390 on merged #481 code\n  (seed copies snapshot.Selected regardless of `covered`); fix PR in progress by brain session.\n- **Brain main red→green same evening:** evisdren #496 broke #483's test (semantic conflict); his #497 merged 19:10 (9f6ab8ec), brain's trail-390 fix #499 merged 19:17 (075a6ea9); main test green through caac7622. #499 got NO agent review: its trail change had branch \"\" so gates were neutral (\"No trail tracks this branch\") and nothing dispatched; brain session hand-reviewed post-merge (2 guards + 108 test lines, code fine). See [[trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls]] #5.\n- **Graph v0.6.0 released 2026-10-26 at dfe93b98** (contains all 12 + #383); installed managed 2026-10-27 replacing a path-install symlink to a gitignored Oct-24 binary in the main checkout. `entire sem` is a SEPARATE stale plugin entry (~/Documents/Coding/entire-sem, version dev), not an alias.\n- **2026-10-27 brain v0.4.0 notes (from brain session):** fact dedup runs inside `entire brain refresh` (entire-brain main 7526 rows/1958 distinct → 1959/1959; `memories gc` is NOT the lever). A graph binary swap invalidates brain's semantic index → `entire brain repair` per repo after any graph upgrade (interrupted refresh also leaves semantic=missing). After my v0.6.0 swap: semantic=true only on entire-brain; false on entire-graph, cli, entiredb, entire.io (entire.io also old-layout). Handed to brain lane. cli+entiredb ARE partial clones (URL-named promisor remote, not origin; brain session missed it checking remote.origin.*), so their repair under v0.6.0 is real evidence for #372. Their earlier 'semantic snapshot header missing commit' failure is NOT v0.6.0 skew: that string left brain prod code in 887b4055 (2026-10-22) and is absent at v0.2.0/v0.3.0/v0.4.0 → a stale pre-COR-2217 record. Graph 'Coverage: degraded' on entire-brain = 47 JSON-only partials (any partial → degraded); in G-followups, user decides.\n- **#372 confirmed on real data 2026-10-27:** brain repair under graph v0.6.0 indexed cli (1427 files) + entiredb (2542) with no promisor refusal. **New graph gap:** Go 1.26 `new(expr)` breaks the bundled tree-sitter-go (smacker 2024-08) -> E_PARSE_ERROR on valid Go (4 entiredb test files). Both in G-followups. Measured: 4 files/26 calls (entiredb tests only); defs 77/77 + outer CALLS 10/10 survive (tree-sitter error recovery) — only exprs inside new(...) at risk. Upstream tree-sitter-go master still needs a type in special_argument_list → fix = vendored patched grammar, not a bump. Synthetic `new(g())` test: E_PARSE_ERROR flagged but CALLS ->g still emitted → no measured loss; effectively a spurious warning feeding 'degraded' (cheap fix: defer to go/parser for Go).\n- **Open for user:** (nightly done); decisions list below still stands (minus approvals).\n\n(History below is the pre-merge state.)\n\nAs of 2026-10-25 the brain half is **final**; the graph half is on **hold for one rebase**. Nothing is merged; the\nuser said nothing merges until everything is finished.\n\n- **Late change (2026-10-25):** evisdren merged graph #382 (shared relation facts, rewrote\n  provider_parallel_stream.go) at b31626ea. #373 now conflicts; a G3 agent is rebasing #373, re-timing it on top of\n  #382 (its old −28–35% was vs d4a0c186), rebuilding #381 and re-checking patches. Board row `G-382-rebase`; page has\n  a \"Graph: hold\" callout to remove when done.\n- **Brain final heads** (clean in order on main a4942dd9; combined 45e7a626, go test 25/25 pkgs, dispatched CI run\n  40214249807 green): 473 8f693073, 474 ef41d238, 476 66348cd2, 477 d58e9639, 478 64b7a146, 479 2d020c72,\n  480 c796a615, 481 46fe7f3b, 482 031fbb5b, 483 1e257ab9, 484 9a3aac28, 488 35c308e4, 489 5f15accf. #493 CLOSED.\n  #484 `benchmark-corpus` red = brainmark Python packet-shape tests, deliberately deferred (user: benchmark work can\n  wait). #477 no longer carries #478's content. Brain patches are reference only.\n- **Closed-PR CI trap:** closing an integration PR stops pull_request CI and `gh pr checks` keeps the old green;\n  use `gh workflow run test.yml --ref <branch>` and verify headSha.\n\n- **Graph** (entireio/entire-graph): #142 and #370-#380, all CI-green.\n  - Findings verified per trail with `--trail entire-graph/<n> --status any --freshness any` plus a branch match: 0 open.\n  - Draft **#381** (DO NOT MERGE) combines all 12 and is green.\n- **Brain** (entireio/entire-brain): #473, #474, #476-#484, #488, #489, all green.\n  - The 4 findings (#477/#483/#484/#489) are fixed.\n  - Draft #493 was the combined PR; now closed (see above).\n- **Merge plan:** the \"Merge plan\" tab of https://claude.ai/artifact/FkY6c5J1XdzaYGM1Q7T9dU.\n  - Rebase patches are in `~/devenv-worktrees/handoff/{graph,brain}-patches`.\n  - Graph detail: `handoff/HANDOFF-GRAPH.md`. Brain decisions: `devenv/DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md`.\n  - **Re-run the merge simulation right before merging**: main drifts, and one brain PR went from clean to\n    conflicting within hours.\n- **Graph merge order:** 370 → 371 → 377 (retarget) → 373 → 379 → 376 → 375 → 372 → 380 → 374 → 142 (3 patches) →\n  378 (3 patches). Graph #380 before brain #484.\n- **Fresh-env adoption on the combined graph build:** main sessions and Explore subagents went graph-first in every\n  searching task, with 0 graph failures. The harness now installs via `entire graph setup`.\n- **User decisions pending:**\n  - approvals on 25 PRs;\n  - brain build-then-swap CAS vs the non-interleaving invariant;\n  - the transcript-mode re-distill cost;\n  - making the lazy-fetch CI job required;\n  - the 37 GB brain store delete;\n  - 63 ~/Documents/Coding paths;\n  - 3 cli-lane issues;\n  - old drafts #146/#300 and community #249;\n  - cli checkpoint 18b787bf552f (shared remote cleanup); Linear connector re-add.\n\nSupersedes [[graph-landing-paused-state]]. Related: [[announce-before-swapping-shared-binaries]],\n[[green-suite-is-not-evidence]], [[mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test]].\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}},"displayPath":"../.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/semantic-layer-handoff-state.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"aa4023d4-d098-4993-85b4-e0ca52c011b4","timestamp":"2026-10-28T03:12:19.063Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/semantic-layer-handoff-state.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t---\n2\tn