{"parentUuid":"1c6a5dfd-e4fe-4c32-b833-2c3d1fb3684b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgVZieaXPPxa9RogE9YfN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QKJCWGvaZFNLZxvQAGCr7Z","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/70987.sock","summary":"Answer G-followups status and check both flags","message":"G-followups stays open but is parked: it waits on the user's go for the degrade-label PR, and nothing is in flight. I added both of your flags to it, after checking each one.\n\n1. \"0 tests\" on runEntitiesShow: reproduced on v0.6.0. Three tests in entities_cmd_test.go (lines 387, 415, 855) run \"entities show\". The route is test → fixture.run → NewRootCommand → newEntitiesCommand → newEntitiesShowCommand → RunE closure → runEntitiesShow. That chain is longer than impact's test search reaches. So \"0 tests\" on any cobra handler means \"none found nearby\", not \"none\". Logged as a candidate fix on the graph side: say \"no tests within N hops\" or model RunE dispatch.\n\n2. Parser namespace: the general risk is real, but v0.6.0 did not cause it this time. Graph's identity_revision is \"4\" in v0.5.0, in the Oct-24 d4a0c186 binary I replaced, and in v0.6.0. It has not changed since 02e667fc on 2026-09-23. Something else changed the namespace your records were filed under. One way: the records were written when ProviderIdentity returned \"\" (the legacy keys, for example if `graph version --json` failed or timed out during a swap window). Another: they came from a pre-09-23 graph (rev 3). The revision segment of the stranded keys will tell you which; it is your lane, so I'm not digging further. On the graph side I logged \"call out any IdentityRevision bump in the CHANGELOG\", since a bump strands every brain until `entities migrate` runs.","type":"message","recipient":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/70987.sock","recipient_kind":"session","content":"G-followups stays open but is parked: it waits on…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2120,"cache_read_input_tokens":134122,"output_tokens":652,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2120,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":652,"cache_read_input_tokens":134122,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2120,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2120},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QKJCWGvaZFNLZxvQAGCr7Z":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/70987.sock","summary":"Answer G-followups status and check both flags","message":"G-followups stays open but is parked: it waits on the user's go for the degrade-label PR, and nothing is in flight. I added both of your flags to it, after checking each one.\n\n1. \"0 tests\" on runEntitiesShow: reproduced on v0.6.0. Three tests in entities_cmd_test.go (lines 387, 415, 855) run \"entities show\". The route is test → fixture.run → NewRootCommand → newEntitiesCommand → newEntitiesShowCommand → RunE closure → runEntitiesShow. That chain is longer than impact's test search reaches. So \"0 tests\" on any cobra handler means \"none found nearby\", not \"none\". Logged as a candidate fix on the graph side: say \"no tests within N hops\" or model RunE dispatch.\n\n2. Parser namespace: the general risk is real, but v0.6.0 did not cause it this time. Graph's identity_revision is \"4\" in v0.5.0, in the Oct-24 d4a0c186 binary I replaced, and in v0.6.0. It has not changed since 02e667fc on 2026-09-23. Something else changed the namespace your records were filed under. One way: the records were written when ProviderIdentity returned \"\" (the legacy keys, for example if `graph version --json` failed or timed out during a swap window). Another: they came from a pre-09-23 graph (rev 3). The revision segment of the stranded keys will tell you which; it is your lane, so I'm not digging further. On the graph side I logged \"call out any IdentityRevision bump in the CHANGELOG\", since a bump strands every brain until `entities migrate` runs."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"51ddbdea-648c-4885-aa38-12b89481105d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgVZieDCS3YNe85i5EJYe","requestRef":"b0cf67a9-084d-4d7a-9c0e-0ac09b3ed41c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c7b74c7c-d9b7-4305-82eb-83239eb067c1","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:15:44.055Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
