{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"e8aad73b5e89839da14cd47b403ff1cc380139b1a5d539e6c5a8d0a9ecf9dd44","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QKJCWGvaZFNLZxvQAGCr7Z","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/70987.sock","summary":"Answer G-followups status and check both flags","message":"G-followups stays open but is parked: it waits on the user's go for the degrade-label PR, and nothing is in flight. I added both of your flags to it, after checking each one.\n\n1. \"0 tests\" on runEntitiesShow: reproduced on v0.6.0. Three tests in entities_cmd_test.go (lines 387, 415, 855) run \"entities show\". The route is test → fixture.run → NewRootCommand → newEntitiesCommand → newEntitiesShowCommand → RunE closure → runEntitiesShow. That chain is longer than impact's test search reaches. So \"0 tests\" on any cobra handler means \"none found nearby\", not \"none\". Logged as a candidate fix on the graph side: say \"no tests within N hops\" or model RunE dispatch.\n\n2. Parser namespace: the general risk is real, but v0.6.0 did not cause it this time. Graph's identity_revision is \"4\" in v0.5.0, in the Oct-24 d4a0c186 binary I replaced, and in v0.6.0. It has not changed since 02e667fc on 2026-09-23. Something else changed the namespace your records were filed under. One way: the records were written when ProviderIdentity returned \"\" (the legacy keys, for example if `graph version --json` failed or timed out during a swap window). Another: they came from a pre-09-23 graph (rev 3). The revision segment of the stranded keys will tell you which; it is your lane, so I'm not digging further. On the graph side I logged \"call out any IdentityRevision bump in the CHANGELOG\", since a bump strands every brain until `entities migrate` runs."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
