{"parentUuid":"aeefe40d-0b72-42ad-9b5c-9458d133dce0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgVZk9vQCKFNekmto7UrH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The brain session asked whether my last open item on the shared todo board, G-followups, can be closed. It stays open, parked. It holds the \"degraded\" label fix, which is waiting on your yes, and nothing is in progress.\n\nThe brain session also flagged two things. I checked both and added them to G-followups:\n\n- **\"0 tests\" in `graph impact`:** the brain session was right. Graph reports 0 tests for the brain command handler behind `entities show`, but three tests do run that command. They go through the CLI's command dispatch, which takes more steps than `impact` searches for tests. So \"0 tests\" on any CLI command handler means \"none found nearby\", not \"none\". A possible graph fix is to say \"no tests within N steps\" instead.\n- **Brain's entity index going empty after the graph upgrade:** the risk is real, but graph v0.6.0 didn't cause it this time. Brain files these records under a parser version number that graph reports. That number was 4 in v0.5.0, in the Oct-24 build I replaced, and in v0.6.0; it hasn't changed since 2026-09-23. Something on the brain side changed which number the records were filed under. That's the brain session's to track down, and I've told it so. On the graph side I noted that any future change to this number belongs in the changelog, because a change empties every brain's entity index until it is migrated.\n\nI recorded the parser-version fact in my memory notes and in brain.\n\n**Still waiting on your yes:**\n1. Remove the dead brain MCP entry from `~/.claude.json`.\n2. Update both CLAUDE.md files to point at the brain CLI instead of the removed `brain_*` MCP tools.\n3. Run `entire plugin remove sem`. It only unregisters the old entry and deletes no files.\n4. Open one graph PR that shows \"degraded\" only when source code genuinely fails to parse, and checks Go's own parser before calling a Go file a parse error."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":905,"cache_read_input_tokens":137061,"output_tokens":636,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":905,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":636,"cache_read_input_tokens":137061,"cache_creation_input_tokens":905,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":905},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"84f7f5ef-5818-42e3-bb10-0ba1d8411262","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgVZk9dnBKPnN3Di6bFf1","requestRef":"8fd18aae-1ec6-4573-b3fe-3452f4786800","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a22db121-bc97-43f1-a4c3-b52a4e665e9d","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:16:01.775Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
