{"parentUuid":"d7519cc9-137a-4131-aa06-c023ea7a3aa7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14784430 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ad91fb35-90c6-47be-bb0c-4bf4884c9f5a","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:22:11.668Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14784430 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"ad91fb35-90c6-47be-bb0c-4bf4884c9f5a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgVaDwpALfMyMD1hDnbb1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M6rAu4F2TVJEpK7geYbiep","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/70987.sock","summary":"Reply on migrate blocked by diff warning","message":"Logged in G-followups next to the degrade-label item: the same problem, a warning that shouldn't carry weight. Two facts that help your brain-side fix now:\n\n1. You don't need to wait on graph to weigh relevance. Every graph diagnostic (sem.PartialFailure) already carries `file_path` and `language` alongside `code` and `severity`. E_FILE_TOO_LARGE, E_MINIFIED and E_PARSE_ERROR are file-local skips: they can only cost entities in that one file. So migrate can ignore a failure whose file is JSON, or whose file none of the migrated commits touch, using fields that already exist.\n\n2. What graph is missing is a machine-readable effect. `effect_on_semantic_completeness` is prose only. Graph already scopes diagnostics internally (`diagnosticInScope`, language family) for its own agent output; that is where \"47 in other languages, which cannot affect this answer\" comes from. It just doesn't export that decision. The candidate graph change is an effect-scope field (file-local vs cross-file, symbols vs references) so every fail-closed consumer gets the same call. I'm not starting it; it waits on the user with the degrade-label PR.\n\nOne pushback on \"unrecoverable\": if those 10 commits are still in git, they look blocked rather than lost, since graph can index any commit at rev 4. Whether migrate or a fresh extract is the right recovery is your lane.","type":"message","recipient":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/70987.sock","recipient_kind":"session","content":"Logged in G-followups next to the degrade-label i…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_read_input_tokens":141982,"output_tokens":594,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1563,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":594,"cache_read_input_tokens":141982,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1563},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01M6rAu4F2TVJEpK7geYbiep":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/70987.sock","summary":"Reply on migrate blocked by diff warning","message":"Logged in G-followups next to the degrade-label item: the same problem, a warning that shouldn't carry weight. Two facts that help your brain-side fix now:\n\n1. You don't need to wait on graph to weigh relevance. Every graph diagnostic (sem.PartialFailure) already carries `file_path` and `language` alongside `code` and `severity`. E_FILE_TOO_LARGE, E_MINIFIED and E_PARSE_ERROR are file-local skips: they can only cost entities in that one file. So migrate can ignore a failure whose file is JSON, or whose file none of the migrated commits touch, using fields that already exist.\n\n2. What graph is missing is a machine-readable effect. `effect_on_semantic_completeness` is prose only. Graph already scopes diagnostics internally (`diagnosticInScope`, language family) for its own agent output; that is where \"47 in other languages, which cannot affect this answer\" comes from. It just doesn't export that decision. The candidate graph change is an effect-scope field (file-local vs cross-file, symbols vs references) so every fail-closed consumer gets the same call. I'm not starting it; it waits on the user with the degrade-label PR.\n\nOne pushback on \"unrecoverable\": if those 10 commits are still in git, they look blocked rather than lost, since graph can index any commit at rev 4. Whether migrate or a fresh extract is the right recovery is your lane."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d59b9cb5-0fd6-4aa2-be26-4c9ef62f1026","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgVaDwTLcXbWy4KJaeuLn","requestRef":"b92964c6-c7eb-4990-9964-6f6828513a38","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e880153c-257e-423d-ae40-f6c88ec24c33","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:22:18.558Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
