{"parentUuid":"9e879fd2-6312-41ce-9510-ea049be3aa4f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgVaF1FZHsekrr9YGRdkL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The brain session pinned down why its entity index went empty, and v0.6.0 wasn't the cause. The missing records were filed under an old parser version number (2) and have been stranded since before 2026-09-23. It has retracted its earlier claim.\n\nIt also hit a new problem that touches graph: brain's `entities migrate` command, the one meant to recover those records, can't run on the entire-brain repo at all. It refuses on any graph warning, and one tracked 16.8 MB JSON benchmark file always triggers a \"file too large\" warning. A JSON file can't affect function or class history, so the refusal blocks recovery of 10 commits for no real reason. It is the third time today that one oversized file has stopped a whole run.\n\nWhat I told the brain session:\n- **It can fix this on its side today.** Every graph warning already names the file and its language, so migrate can ignore a JSON file or a file the migrated commits don't touch.\n- **What graph is missing:** a field saying what each warning can actually affect. Graph already makes that call for its own agent output, which is where \"47 in other languages, which cannot affect this answer\" comes from. It just doesn't include that verdict in its JSON. Adding it belongs with the \"degraded\" label fix, since both are warnings carrying more weight than they should.\n- **\"Unrecoverable\" is too strong.** If those commits are still in git, the records look blocked rather than lost, because graph can index any commit again. Which recovery to use is the brain session's call.\n\nI logged this on the shared todo board and in my memory notes. I haven't started any graph work.\n\n**Still waiting on your yes:**\n1. Remove the dead brain MCP entry from `~/.claude.json`.\n2. Update both CLAUDE.md files to point at the brain CLI.\n3. Run `entire plugin remove sem`. It only unregisters the old entry and deletes no files.\n4. Open one graph PR that:\n   - shows \"degraded\" only when source code genuinely fails to parse;\n   - checks Go's own parser before calling a Go file a parse error;\n   - adds a field to each warning saying what it can affect, so tools like `entities migrate` can tell a harmless one from a real one."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":144307,"output_tokens":716,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":716,"cache_read_input_tokens":144307,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fffe75b2-65f5-4c85-9245-e961010c341c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgVaEzuj2po3hCk49LuUZ","requestRef":"6e2bf08d-9969-4e7a-ae2e-517d32ea132e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e692a7fe-82d7-4abd-a676-9689d8534117","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:22:34.349Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
