{"parentUuid":"501e9fcb-be8d-4504-a50a-0276cd0de987","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6ce88c3e-3159-4e11-8bc8-b684e4fc538f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VPWoMUgA4Y2bNfrQmQ5npq","type":"tool_result","content":"ok","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2ae2cf3a-3983-4a7d-a24f-99b04d46fa19","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:28:31.695Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":1,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {","-  \"updated\": \"2026-10-29T00:27:43Z\",","+  \"updated\": \"2026-10-28T20:28:31-04:00\",","   \"tasks\": [","     {","       \"id\": \"G-382-rebase\","]},{"oldStart":183,"oldLines":7,"newStart":183,"newLines":7,"lines":["     {","       \"id\": \"G-followups\",","       \"lane\": \"graph\",","-      \"title\": \"Graph follow-ups noted by the fix agents (not started) | NEW 2026-10-27: agent 'Coverage: degraded' fires on ANY partial failure (search.go agentSearchDiagnostics); on entire-brain all 47 are data JSON (46 E_MINIFIED benchmark fixtures/.entire/runners, 1 E_FILE_TOO_LARGE), all Go/Python fully covered; same on d4a0c186 (pre-existing). Candidate: degrade only for source-language failures. Also locate miss: 'where does export decide a checkpoint is covered' did not surface covers() (top-2 tied 24.4). | NEW 2026-10-27 (real parser gap): Go 1.26 `new(expr)` (new(0), new(\\\"4242\\\"), new(now.Add(..))) yields tree-sitter ERROR nodes -> E_PARSE_ERROR on 4 valid entiredb Go test files (gofmt clean); graph bundles smacker/go-tree-sitter 2024-08 grammar. Will spread as Go 1.26 code grows. Also SQL `@name`/INCLUDE, proto reserved names, fish syntax in .sh = grammar limits. | #372 CONFIRMED on real blob:none clones: cli 1427 files, entiredb 2542 files indexed under v0.6.0, no promisor refusal (not a controlled before/after). | MEASURED new(expr) impact: blast radius today 4 files/26 calls, all entiredb tests (cli, entire-graph, entire-brain, entire-api: 0, go/ast count). Damage is local: all 77 funcs in the 4 files present in symbols; outer CALLS edges present for 10/10 functions whose call line has new(\\\"..\\\"). Only what is INSIDE the new(...) arg is at risk. Fix is NOT a dep bump: upstream tree-sitter-go master (0.25.0+) special_argument_list still requires a type first; needs a patched grammar vendored under internal/sem/grammars/go (11 grammars already vendored there) + upstream PR. | SYNTHETIC new(g()) test (scratch repo, v0.6.0): file flagged E_PARSE_ERROR yet CALLS onlyInsideNew->g, control->h, afterBroken->h all present. No measured fact loss anywhere => in practice a SPURIOUS warning that feeds 'degraded'. Cheaper fix option: for Go, defer to go/parser's verdict (graph already imports go/parser in 3 files) before emitting E_PARSE_ERROR; vendored grammar still the full fix. | NEW 2026-10-28 (from brain session, verified): impact says runEntitiesShow has '0 tests' though 3 tests in entities_cmd_test.go run 'entities show'. They reach it via fixture.run -> NewRootCommand -> cobra RunE closure, a chain deeper than impact's test search. So '0 tests' on any cobra handler is unreliable; candidate fix: say 'no tests within N hops' or model RunE dispatch. | Parser identity: brain entity records are namespaced by graph version --json identity_revision; a bump strands every brain's entity index until `entities migrate`, and nothing warns outside `entities history`. CHECKED: IdentityRevision is '4' in v0.5.0, d4a0c186 and v0.6.0 (unchanged since 02e667fc, 2026-09-23), so v0.6.0 did NOT move it (brain session confirmed: stranded keys are rev 2, pre-09-23). Candidate: call out any bump in the CHANGELOG. | NEW 2026-10-28 (pairs with degrade-label): `brain entities migrate` refuses on ANY graph diff warning; on entire-brain one tracked 16.8 MB JSON (E_FILE_TOO_LARGE) blocks it. Every PartialFailure already carries file_path + language, and graph scopes them internally (diagnosticInScope, language family) for agent output, but the effect is prose only (effect_on_semantic_completeness). Candidate: a machine-readable effect scope (file-local vs cross-file; symbols vs references) so fail-closed consumers can weigh relevance. Third 'one oversized file aborts a whole pass' instance (see one-file-aborted-the-whole-export).\",","+      \"title\": \"Graph follow-ups noted by the fix agents (not started) | NEW 2026-10-27: agent 'Coverage: degraded' fires on ANY partial failure (search.go agentSearchDiagnostics); on entire-brain all 47 are data JSON (46 E_MINIFIED benchmark fixtures/.entire/runners, 1 E_FILE_TOO_LARGE), all Go/Python fully covered; same on d4a0c186 (pre-existing). Candidate: degrade only for source-language failures. Also locate miss: 'where does export decide a checkpoint is covered' did not surface covers() (top-2 tied 24.4). | NEW 2026-10-27 (real parser gap): Go 1.26 `new(expr)` (new(0), new(\\\"4242\\\"), new(now.Add(..))) yields tree-sitter ERROR nodes -> E_PARSE_ERROR on 4 valid entiredb Go test files (gofmt clean); graph bundles smacker/go-tree-sitter 2024-08 grammar. Will spread as Go 1.26 code grows. Also SQL `@name`/INCLUDE, proto reserved names, fish syntax in .sh = grammar limits. | #372 CONFIRMED on real blob:none clones: cli 1427 files, entiredb 2542 files indexed under v0.6.0, no promisor refusal (not a controlled before/after). | MEASURED new(expr) impact: blast radius today 4 files/26 calls, all entiredb tests (cli, entire-graph, entire-brain, entire-api: 0, go/ast count). Damage is local: all 77 funcs in the 4 files present in symbols; outer CALLS edges present for 10/10 functions whose call line has new(\\\"..\\\"). Only what is INSIDE the new(...) arg is at risk. Fix is NOT a dep bump: upstream tree-sitter-go master (0.25.0+) special_argument_list still requires a type first; needs a patched grammar vendored under internal/sem/grammars/go (11 grammars already vendored there) + upstream PR. | SYNTHETIC new(g()) test (scratch repo, v0.6.0): file flagged E_PARSE_ERROR yet CALLS onlyInsideNew->g, control->h, afterBroken->h all present. No measured fact loss anywhere => in practice a SPURIOUS warning that feeds 'degraded'. Cheaper fix option: for Go, defer to go/parser's verdict (graph already imports go/parser in 3 files) before emitting E_PARSE_ERROR; vendored grammar still the full fix. | NEW 2026-10-28 (from brain session, verified): impact says runEntitiesShow has '0 tests' though 3 tests in entities_cmd_test.go run 'entities show'. They reach it via fixture.run -> NewRootCommand -> cobra RunE closure, a chain deeper than impact's test search. So '0 tests' on any cobra handler is unreliable; candidate fix: say 'no tests within N hops' or model RunE dispatch. | Parser identity: brain entity records are namespaced by graph version --json identity_revision; a bump strands every brain's entity index until `entities migrate`, and nothing warns outside `entities history`. CHECKED: IdentityRevision is '4' in v0.5.0, d4a0c186 and v0.6.0 (unchanged since 02e667fc, 2026-09-23), so v0.6.0 did NOT move it (brain session confirmed: stranded keys are rev 2, pre-09-23; RECOVERED 10/10 by `entities backfill` without --branch: --branch main walked a local main 241 commits behind). Candidate: call out any bump in the CHANGELOG. | NEW 2026-10-28 (pairs with degrade-label): `brain entities migrate` refuses on ANY graph diff warning; on entire-brain one tracked 16.8 MB JSON (E_FILE_TOO_LARGE) blocks it. Every PartialFailure already carries file_path + language, and graph scopes them internally (diagnosticInScope, language family) for agent output, but the effect is prose only (effect_on_semantic_completeness). Candidate: a machine-readable effect scope (file-local vs cross-file; symbols vs references) so fail-closed consumers can weigh relevance. Third 'one oversized file aborts a whole pass' instance (see one-file-aborted-the-whole-export).\",","       \"status\": \"todo\",","       \"owner\": \"claude\",","       \"source\": \"proactive\","]},{"oldStart":1185,"oldLines":4,"newStart":1185,"newLines":4,"lines":["       \"lane\": \"brain\"","     }","   ]","-}","+}"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"75ee6658-44cb-49b1-bdec-2ab417cd7d83","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":260},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire.io","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"501e9fcb-be8d-4504-a50a-0276cd0de987","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
