ARGE JSON data files diagnostics\n- convention | flock(1) is not installed on the shared macOS dev machine; serialize timing runs with a Python fcntl.flock wrapper on the lock file (devenv-worktrees/timing/mlock), which takes the same lock flock(1) would.\n- decision | entire-graph IdentityRevision (internal/sem/provider.go, reported as identity_revision by 'entire graph version --json') is a global parser-identity revision. Brain namespaces entity-index records by it, so any bump strands every brain's entity index until 'en\n- decision | Search cold/warm parity (PR #377, stacked on #371): a cold committed-tree query that will build the complete snapshot (cache dir set, HEAD, no --max-indexed-files/--index-all-files, corpus <= coldCompleteSnapshotMaxFiles) preselects with the warm git-tree-grep\n- decision | Phase-0 offline gate 2026-10-05 FAILED. Built from the first line of a subagent prompt, the graph answer hit (files later Read/Edited) 34.0% [26.9,41.9] on n=150 real prompts, under the 40% gate. Paths named literally in the prompt hit 52%. The query, not retr\n## E_PARSE_ERROR tree-sitter go grammar go/parser\n- decision | entire-graph IdentityRevision (internal/sem/provider.go, reported as identity_revision by 'entire graph version --json') is a global parser-identity revision. Brain namespaces entity-index records by it, so any bump strands every brain's entity index until 'en\n- decision | entire-graph PR #142 was rescoped (2026-10-24): the opt-in --max-seconds wall-clock ceiling on snapshot/symbols/edges (ProviderSnapshotOptions.MaxDuration) and its partial-snapshot path (stream finished with E_ANALYSIS_BUDGET_EXCEEDED) were DROPPED. Reason: a \n- decision | Search cold/warm parity (PR #377, stacked on #371): a cold committed-tree query that will build the complete snapshot (cache dir set, HEAD, no --max-indexed-files/--index-all-files, corpus <= coldCompleteSnapshotMaxFiles) preselects with the warm git-tree-grep\n- decision | entire-graph PR #379 (G2, 202