{"parentUuid":"a7cf3217-1a3c-451b-9988-e12351ef407b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXXau3Df1oRTyUBgMvTT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HSFUr74FNcfaWziPfsvjGD","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Graph PR: degraded label and effect scope","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"You are a G3 fix agent for entireio/entire-graph (Go). FIRST read and follow /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md exactly: fresh worktree off origin/main (main is 28382d8e, newer than v0.6.0), graph/brain preflight, `impact` before editing exported symbols, mlock for long runs, mutation-proven tests, mandatory local -race, PR via gh. The user approved opening this PR. Do NOT merge, approve, request reviewers or hand-create a trail. No AI/Claude attribution lines and no references to people or conversations in commits or the PR body. Output: caveman-ultra compressed report, ≤40 lines. Use RTK for shell.\n\n## Goal: one PR, three commits. Stop warnings that can't affect code facts from carrying weight, and export that verdict in a form machines can read.\n\n### Evidence (measured on v0.6.0)\n- `internal/cli/search.go` `agentSearchDiagnostics` (around line 2182) sets `level = \"degraded\"` whenever `len(response.PartialFailures) > 0`, regardless of language.\n- On the entire-brain repo every query prints \"Coverage: degraded\" with 47 partial failures, and all 47 are JSON:\n  - 46 are E_MINIFIED (benchmark fixtures under `benchmarks/agent-brain/...` and `.entire/runners`);\n  - 1 is E_FILE_TOO_LARGE (a 16.8 MB SNAPSHOT.json).\n  - Go and Python coverage is complete. The old d4a0c186 build behaves the same, so this predates v0.6.0.\n- A downstream consumer (brain `entities migrate`) fails closed on any graph diff warning. That one JSON E_FILE_TOO_LARGE blocks it, because `effect_on_semantic_completeness` is prose only.\n- **Go 1.26 `new(expr)`:** forms like `new(0)`, `new(\"4242\")` and `new(now.Add(...))` are valid, gofmt-clean Go. The bundled smacker go-tree-sitter grammar (2024-08) produces ERROR nodes for them, and upstream tree-sitter-go master still requires a type there, so a dependency bump won't fix it.\n  - Graph emits E_PARSE_ERROR on 4 valid entiredb test files: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entiredb`, a partial clone that graph admits on git ≥ 2.45.1.\n  - A synthetic test showed no fact loss. A file with `func g() int {return 1}`, `func onlyInsideNew() *int { return new(g()) }`, `func control() int { return h() }` and `func afterBroken() int { p := new(0); _ = p; return h() }` was flagged E_PARSE_ERROR, yet the edges onlyInsideNew->g, control->h and afterBroken->h were all present.\n  - Across the 4 real files, 77/77 function definitions and 10/10 outer CALLS edges survived. So in practice this is a spurious warning that feeds \"degraded\".\n  - go/parser accepts `new(expr)` syntactically in any Go version (it is a CallExpr). Graph already imports go/parser (go_route_binding.go, go_signature_evidence.go, search_verify_go_native.go).\n- The existing language-scoping logic is `internal/cli/completeness.go` (`diagnosticInScope`, `sameCompletenessLanguageFamily`, `buildCompletenessScope`).\n- The type is `sem.PartialFailure` (`internal/sem/provider.go:311`): Code, Severity, FilePath, Language, EffectOnCompleteness (prose), Detail.\n- E_PARSE_ERROR has several emission sites: analyze.go:1027, dependents.go:548, groovy.go:78, parser.go:465/487/615/637, provider.go:4879/25480, provider_parallel.go:277.\n\n### Commit A: the degraded label\n- \"Coverage: degraded\" (and the compact `D` marker) should fire only for partial failures that can affect code facts:\n  - any failure that is NOT file-local, such as a repo-ignore shortfall, a missing HEAD, or a budget failure; or\n  - a file-local failure in a SOURCE-code language.\n- File-local failures in data/config formats (JSON, YAML, TOML, XML, CSV, lockfiles and the like) give \"notice\". They are still counted and listed exactly as today; only the level changes.\n- Find an existing language classification first. If none exists, add one helper with a table test. Keep the existing repo-ignore hoisting behaviour intact.\n\n### Commit B: Go grammar gap\n- When the tree-sitter parse of a Go file has errors but `go/parser.ParseFile` (SkipObjectResolution) accepts the same bytes, do not emit the E_PARSE_ERROR partial failure. Emit a WARNING instead, with a new code such as `W_GO_GRAMMAR_GAP`, language go and the file path.\n- Its effect text must say honestly that the file is valid Go the bundled grammar can't fully parse, and that facts inside the unparsed construct may be missing.\n- Truly invalid Go keeps E_PARSE_ERROR.\n- Apply this at ONE chokepoint so every emission site inherits it. Probably the place a Go ParseStatus is computed; verify that with neighbors/impact. Cover at least the snapshot/index path and the `graph diff` path in tests.\n- Completeness and agent output must stay honest. Go coverage can no longer say parse failures exist, but the grammar-gap warning must stay visible in JSON and in agent diagnostics.\n- go/parser runs only on Go files that already errored, so cost should be negligible. Show it: run cold `index --head` on entiredb, base vs new, 3 interleaved reps, mlock, separate cache dirs.\n\n### Commit C: machine-readable effect scope\n- Add an additive JSON field on PartialFailure, `effect_scope`, with values `\"file\"` (only facts from file_path can be missing) or `\"snapshot\"` (anything may be missing). Populate it for every code.\n- Enumerate every code a PartialFailure can carry. Add an exhaustiveness test that fails when a new code appears without a classification.\n- Add a capabilities key, e.g. `partial_failure_effect_scope`, to `entire graph capabilities --json` so consumers can detect support. See how #380 added `context_allow_ancestor`.\n- Follow the repo's AGENTS.md and CHANGELOG conventions for SchemaVersion (currently \"1.4\") and add an Unreleased CHANGELOG entry.\n- Ensure `graph diff` JSON carries the field.\n\n### Hard constraints\n- Do NOT change `IdentityRevision` (provider.go, \"4\"). Brain namespaces entity-index records by it, and a bump strands every user's entity index.\n- Cache invariant (recorded decision): a change that alters what a records-cache or search-snapshot entry CARRIES needs its own `providerRecordsCacheVersion` / `searchSnapshotCacheVersion` bump. Commits B and C change cached diagnostics, so either bump, or derive `effect_scope` at serialization time so old cache entries are correct. Pick one and prove it with a test or a cache-hit check.\n- Every remedy a diagnostic names must actually work in the state that produced it. No \"run X\" where X can't fix that state.\n- Mutation proof for each guard: the data-language exemption, the go/parser deferral (including that invalid Go still gets E_PARSE_ERROR), and the exhaustiveness test.\n\n### Live checks before reporting (use your built binary, never the installed one)\n1. entire-brain: `query --head --format agent` prints \"Coverage: notice\" and still lists the JSON partials.\n2. entiredb: the 4 files no longer carry E_PARSE_ERROR; W_GO_GRAMMAR_GAP is present.\n3. A repo with a genuine Go syntax error still reports E_PARSE_ERROR and \"degraded\".\n4. `capabilities --json` shows the new key.\n5. Snapshot output is identical to base apart from the intended diagnostic changes; diff with g2-strip.py.\n\nReport: PR number and branch, the design choices (language table source, cache strategy, schema decision), live-check results, the mutation proofs, CI state (green/failed/running, enumerated), and anything unfinished.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2874,"cache_read_input_tokens":178482,"output_tokens":3014,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2874,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3014,"cache_read_input_tokens":178482,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2874,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2874},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HSFUr74FNcfaWziPfsvjGD":{"description":"Graph PR: degraded label and effect scope","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"You are a G3 fix agent for entireio/entire-graph (Go). FIRST read and follow /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md exactly: fresh worktree off origin/main (main is 28382d8e, newer than v0.6.0), graph/brain preflight, `impact` before editing exported symbols, mlock for long runs, mutation-proven tests, mandatory local -race, PR via gh. The user approved opening this PR. Do NOT merge, approve, request reviewers or hand-create a trail. No AI/Claude attribution lines and no references to people or conversations in commits or the PR body. Output: caveman-ultra compressed report, ≤40 lines. Use RTK for shell.\n\n## Goal: one PR, three commits. Stop warnings that can't affect code facts from carrying weight, and export that verdict in a form machines can read.\n\n### Evidence (measured on v0.6.0)\n- `internal/cli/search.go` `agentSearchDiagnostics` (around line 2182) sets `level = \"degraded\"` whenever `len(response.PartialFailures) > 0`, regardless of language.\n- On the entire-brain repo every query prints \"Coverage: degraded\" with 47 partial failures, and all 47 are JSON:\n  - 46 are E_MINIFIED (benchmark fixtures under `benchmarks/agent-brain/...` and `.entire/runners`);\n  - 1 is E_FILE_TOO_LARGE (a 16.8 MB SNAPSHOT.json).\n  - Go and Python covera