{"parentUuid":"a01a63be-2337-4a2a-b856-3f6c052c210e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXcMTFQxCXYfWWEz2kGq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed: an outside contributor's PR #351 merged into graph main today and bumped the parser version from 4 to 5. It is not in v0.6.0. That affects brain directly, so I'm telling the brain session."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1745,"cache_read_input_tokens":207737,"output_tokens":2799,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":804},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1745,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2799,"cache_read_input_tokens":207737,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1745},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d29d561a-3acf-435e-a23e-e8055fe7dfa6","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgXcMSupMCBkAC3rsjqpU","requestRef":"00af601a-debc-49f4-bc3e-e50bdc41372c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"efb4fb4a-dea9-45b0-89b1-3c249247035f","timestamp":"2026-10-30T02:11:29.437Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"efb4fb4a-dea9-45b0-89b1-3c249247035f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXcMTFQxCXYfWWEz2kGq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VRJ9scSJ5ryPGn39AaEdWA","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/70987.sock","summary":"Graph identity_revision bumped to 5 on main","message":"Time-sensitive for your entity index: graph main bumped IdentityRevision 4 → 5 today. abhi-singhs' #351 (Julia signatures) merged 2026-10-29 13:01Z, carrying 5b33ae84 \"revision Julia overload identity\". It is NOT in v0.6.0, so nothing installed changed yet. But the next graph nightly or release strands every brain's rev-4 entity records, exactly the case you flagged. On entire-brain, `entities migrate` still refuses because of the 16.8 MB SNAPSHOT.json E_FILE_TOO_LARGE warning. `backfill` without --branch is the path that works today.\n\nThe fix for that refusal is now available: graph PR #389 is open, green, with 0 findings (not merged, waiting on the user). It adds `effect_scope` (\"file\" | \"snapshot\") to every warning and partial failure, including `graph diff` JSON. The capabilities key is `optional_local_only_features.partial_failure_effect_scope`, also listed in `schema_features`. Rule for your filter: effect_scope==\"file\" with a file_path absent from the diff's files list means the failure cannot have cost that delta an entity. Your \"file not in the diff\" test is the same idea, so either works.\n\n#389 also bumps graph schema 1.4 → 1.5. I checked your semstore: a 1.5 header is accepted with a provider_schema_newer_minor warning until you raise semstore.SchemaVersion to \"1.5\", so nothing breaks, but every repo will show that warning until you do.","type":"message","recipient":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/70987.sock","recipient_kind":"session","content":"Time-sensitive for your entity index: graph main …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_se