{"parentUuid":"e41e06b3-5fc1-4291-8dcd-a8aba26f2c8d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14936971 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5500997a-e733-4359-9156-8319bcd35df7","timestamp":"2026-10-30T02:11:54.407Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14936971 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"5500997a-e733-4359-9156-8319bcd35df7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXcQ7JBjksv8AeL95WZp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph PR is open and ready for you to merge: **[#389](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/389)**. CI is green on all 35 checks, and the Entire agent review ran and found nothing. The only red item is Approvals, which isn't enforced on GitHub. I haven't merged it.\n\n**What it changes**\n- **\"Degraded\" label:** it now appears only when a real source-code file fails, or something affects the whole index. JSON and other data-file skips show as \"notice\" and are still listed.\n- **Go parse errors:** when Go's own parser accepts a file that graph's bundled parser can't handle (the Go 1.26 `new(expr)` case), graph now gives a grammar-gap warning instead of a parse error. Genuinely broken Go still gets the parse error and \"degraded\".\n- **Scope field:** every warning now says whether it affects only one file or the whole index, and graph's capabilities output lists the field so brain can detect it. This is what lets brain's `entities migrate` stop refusing on the oversized JSON file.\n\n**What I checked myself**\n- I built the PR branch and ran it. On entire-brain, coverage now reads \"notice\" with all 47 JSON items still listed. On entiredb, the 4 Go test files carry the grammar-gap warning and no Go parse errors.\n- I read the core of the change. Any warning type it doesn't recognise counts as affecting the whole index, and a test fails if a new type is added without being classified.\n- Indexing time is unchanged: 6.38 s before, 6.35 s after (median of 3).\n- It raises graph's data format version from 1.4 to 1.5. Brain still accepts it, but shows a \"newer version\" warning until brain updates its own number.\n\n**One limit:** the rule calls a skipped source file's effect \"one file\". But a call from another file into that skipped file could, in principle, be matched to the wrong function rather than just going missing. This doesn't matter for data files, and a skipped source file still shows \"degraded\".\n\n**Something to know before the next graph release:** an outside contributor's PR #351 merged into graph main today and raised the parser version from 4 to 5. It isn't in v0.6.0, so nothing installed has changed. But the first graph release that includes it will leave brain's existing entity history unreadable in every repo until it's re-indexed. On entire-brain, re-running `entities backfill` works today. `migrate` will keep refusing there until #389 merges and brain builds the filter that uses it. I've told the brain session.\n\n**Other two items, done:**\n- `sem` is unregistered, and its binary is untouched.\n- Both CLAUDE.md files now point at the brain command line. I also fixed one wrong instruction: passing `--branch` to `brief` fails on brain v0.4.0, so it now says `recall` only.\n- The dead brain MCP entry had already been removed by the brain session.\n\nWant me to merge #389?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":538,"cache_read_input_tokens":212511,"output_tokens":956,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":538,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":956,"cache_read_input_tokens":212511,"cache_creation_input_tokens":538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":538},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8aa34779-0c64-4a9f-974f-48226e3a6f12","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgXcQ6vd4sYaPksv8zEo8","requestRef":"84e54c