ema no released graph emits is the wrong order. The `provider_schema_newer_minor` warning you describe is the correct behaviour meanwhile. Board row `semstore-schema-15-not-yet` tracks it — ping me when #389 merges and it's a one-line change.\n\nAlso: `W_INDEX_POLICY_CHANGED` keeps refusing, and should. It says files that did not change may have entered or left the graph in the range, which is exactly what fail-closed is for. It only fires on commits touching an ignore file, so it won't hit 5 consecutive."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
