{"parentUuid":"f5282393-5472-4f99-a557-b2d522d2f4f2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXcyd4XB5xtrv18mXC2K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I need to correct something I told you: brain's `entities migrate` is not refusing on entire-brain today. It skips every commit, because brain's store already matches graph v0.6.0's parser version 4. The refusal would start the first time a graph release containing version 5 ships and migrate has real work to do.\n\n- **Why it would block every commit, not just a few:** graph's diff output includes warnings about files the diff doesn't touch. I checked a one-commit diff on entire-brain myself: it carries the \"file too large\" warning for the 16.8 MB SNAPSHOT.json even though that file isn't in the commit. So every commit's diff looks failed, and migrate gives up after 5 failures in a row.\n- **Brain's fix is written:** the brain session has a fix on a brain branch, not merged yet. It ignores a warning when it affects only one file and that file isn't in the diff. It reads the new scope field from #389 first, so it needs no change when #389 merges.\n- **A possible graph improvement:** graph could stop reporting one-file warnings for files a diff doesn't touch. I've logged it on the shared todo board as a follow-up and kept it out of #389, so the PR stays as reviewed.\n- **Brain's schema update:** the brain session will raise brain's known graph schema version to 1.5 once #389 merges. I'll tell it when that happens.\n\n#389 is unchanged and still waiting on your merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":613,"cache_read_input_tokens":219848,"output_tokens":482,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":20},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":613,"eph