mpact: blast radius today 4 files/26 calls, all entiredb tests (cli, entire-graph, entire-brain, entire-api: 0, go/ast count). Damage is local: all 77 funcs in the 4 files present in symbols; outer CALLS edges present for 10/10 functions whose call line has new(\\\"..\\\"). Only what is INSIDE the new(...) arg is at risk. Fix is NOT a dep bump: upstream tree-sitter-go master (0.25.0+) special_argument_list still requires a type first; needs a patched grammar vendored under internal/sem/grammars/go (11 grammars already vendored there) + upstream PR. | SYNTHETIC new(g()) test (scratch repo, v0.6.0): file flagged E_PARSE_ERROR yet CALLS onlyInsideNew->g, control->h, afterBroken->h all present. No measured fact loss anywhere => in practice a SPURIOUS warning that feeds 'degraded'. Cheaper fix option: for Go, defer to go/parser's verdict (graph already imports go/parser in 3 files) before emitting E_PARSE_ERROR; vendored grammar still the full fix. | NEW 2026-10-28 (from brain session, verified): impact says runEntitiesShow has '0 tests' though 3 tests in entities_cmd_test.go run 'entities show'. They reach it via fixture.run -> NewRootCommand -> cobra RunE closure, a chain deeper than impact's test search. So '0 tests' on any cobra handler is unreliable; candidate fix: say 'no tests within N hops' or model RunE dispatch. | Parser identity: brain entity records are namespaced by graph version --json identity_revision; a bump strands every brain's entity index until `entities migrate`, and nothing warns outside `entities history`. CHECKED: IdentityRevision is '4' in v0.5.0, d4a0c186 and v0.6.0 (unchanged since 02e667fc, 2026-09-23), so v0.6.0 did NOT move it (brain session confirmed: stranded keys are rev 2, pre-09-23; RECOVERED 10/10 by `entities backfill` without --branch: --branch main walked a local main 241 commits behind). Candidate: call out any bump in the CHANGELOG. | NEW 2026-10-28 (pairs with degrade-label): `brain entities migrate` refuses on ANY graph diff warning; on entire-brain one tracked 16.8 MB JSON (E_FILE_TOO_LARGE) blocks it. Every PartialFailure already carries file_path + language, and graph scopes them internally (diagnosticInScope, language family) for agent output, but the effect is prose only (effect_on_semantic_completeness). Candidate: a machine-readable effect scope (file-local vs cross-file; symbols vs references) so fail-closed consumers can weigh relevance. Third 'one oversized file aborts a whole pass' instance (see one-file-aborted-the-whole-export). | 2026-10-29: degrade label + Go grammar gap + effect scope are in PR #389. NOTE: main IdentityRevision is now '5' (#351, abhi-singhs, merged 2026-10-29 13:01Z, not in v0.6.0) -> next graph release strands brains' rev-4 entity records; told brain session. | 2026-10-29 candidate: `graph diff` reports file-scoped diagnostics for files OUTSIDE the diff (verified on entire-brain HEAD~1..HEAD: E_FILE_TOO_LARGE SNAPSHOT.json + 2 W_UNSUPPORTED_FILE, none in the diff's files). That noise rides on every commit's diff. With #389, consumers can filter by effect_scope; graph could drop/demote file-scoped diagnostics whose file is absent from both sides of the diff. Not in #389 (scope). Migrate refusal is LATENT until a rev-5 graph ships; brain fix e88f248d.\",","+      \"title\": \"Graph follow-ups noted by the fix agents (not started) | NEW 2026-10-27: agent 'Coverage: degraded' fires on ANY partial failure (search.go agentSearchDiagnostics); on entire-brain all 47 are data JSON (46 E_MINIFIED benchmark fixtures/.entire/runners, 1 E_FILE_TOO_LARGE), all Go/Python fully covered; same on d4a0c186 (pre-existing). Candidate: degrade only for source-language failures. Also locate miss: 'where does export decide a checkpoint is covered' did not surface covers() (top-2 tied 24.4). | NEW 2026-10-27 (real parser gap): Go 1.26 `new(expr)` (new(0), new(\\\"4242\\\"), new(now.Add(..))) yields tree-sitter ERROR nodes -> E_PARSE_ERROR on 4 valid entiredb Go test files (gofmt 