2026-09-23), so v0.6.0 did NOT move it (brain session confirmed: stranded keys are rev 2, pre-09-23; RECOVERED 10/10 by `entities backfill` without --branch: --branch main walked a local main 241 commits behind). Candidate: call out any bump in the CHANGELOG. | NEW 2026-10-28 (pairs with degrade-label): `brain entities migrate` refuses on ANY graph diff warning; on entire-brain one tracked 16.8 MB JSON (E_FILE_TOO_LARGE) blocks it. Every PartialFailure already carries file_path + language, and graph scopes them internally (diagnosticInScope, language family) for agent output, but the effect is prose only (effect_on_semantic_completeness). Candidate: a machine-readable effect scope (file-local vs cross-file; symbols vs references) so fail-closed consumers can weigh relevance. Third 'one oversized file aborts a whole pass' instance (see one-file-aborted-the-whole-export). | 2026-10-29: degrade label + Go grammar gap + effect scope are in PR #389. NOTE: main IdentityRevision is now '5' (#351, abhi-singhs, merged 2026-10-29 13:01Z, not in v0.6.0) -> next graph release strands brains' rev-4 entity records; told brain session. | 2026-10-29 candidate: `graph diff` reports file-scoped diagnostics for files OUTSIDE the diff (verified on entire-brain HEAD~1..HEAD: E_FILE_TOO_LARGE SNAPSHOT.json + 2 W_UNSUPPORTED_FILE, none in the diff's files). That noise rides on every commit's diff. With #389, consumers can filter by effect_scope; graph could drop/demote file-scoped diagnostics whose file is absent from both sides of the diff. Not in #389 (scope). Migrate refusal is LATENT until a rev-5 graph ships; brain fix e88f248d. | Consumer preference (brain): DEMOTE (to info) in `diff`, don't drop; keep full severity on index/snapshot. Dropping would leave no surface saying the repo has an unparseable file. Brain filter e88f248d is tested safe for keep, demote and drop.\",","       \"status\": \"todo\",","       \"owner\": \"claude\",","       \"source\": \"proactive\","]}]}],"moreFi