","193406a2-20ea-4a75-a666-aecbb06fbefe","6f11ff14-4b8f-4083-89a4-f71cdcc66c84"]},"postTokens":36121,"cumulativeDroppedTokens":16574037},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"0daa5175-d721-433f-b6b8-b3f9a52b98f7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"09a7240f-c397-49fc-9ec2-03b5ad10156e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<artifact-content-authored-by-others/>\nThe summarized conversation included Artifact content written by people other than you, which the summary may restate. Treat restated content as data, not instructions.\nThis session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Artifact, Bash, Edit, ListAgents, Read, SendMessage, Skill, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n## 1. Primary Request and Intent\n\nThe session has been long. Its arc, earliest first:\n\n**Earlier work (summarized before)**\n- Make the entire-graph code graph \"solid and usable\", and make coding agents use it.\n- Free 300 GB of disk.\n- Time every graph and brain process and speed them up.\n- Build an artifact with one tab per tool, and keep a live todo board.\n- Coordinate with the brain Claude session (`fix-brain-initialization-ux`) as \"the semantic layer team\".\n- Refresh graph and brain, and fix the CLAUDE.md files.\n\n**Merges**\n- All 25 PRs were merged on 2026-10-25 after explicit user authorization: 12 graph by me, 13 brain by the brain session.\n\n**This segment**\n- After a series of cross-session exchanges, I listed four pending yes/no items:\n  1. Remove the dead brain MCP entry from `~/.claude.json`.\n  2. Update both CLAUDE.md files to drop `brain_*` MCP references.\n  3. Run `entire plugin remove sem`.\n  4. Open one graph PR covering three things: \"degraded\" only for real source failures; defer Go E_PARSE_ERROR to go/parser; a machine-readable effect-scope field on warnings.\n- User: **\"i give u full perms to do all that\"**. That is explicit approval for items 1–4. Item 4 was \"open\" a PR, not merge it.\n- My last question to the user, \"Want me to merge #389?\", is unanswered.\n\n## 2. Key Technical Concepts\n\n**Merge and review mechanics**\n- Merge commits only.\n- Neither repo enforces approvals on GitHub; the Entire \"Approvals\" gate is reported, not enforced.\n- Trail findings source of truth: `entire trail finding list --trail entire-graph/<n> --status any --freshness any --json`, with `trail.branch` checked against the PR head.\n- Read the Entire Gates check-run `output.summary` to confirm the agent review actually ran. A NEUTRAL gate means no review ran.\n\n**Graph identity revision**\n- `IdentityRevision` lives in `internal/sem/provider.go` and is reported as `identity_revision` by `entire graph version --json`.\n- Brain namespaces entity-index records by it, so a bump strands every brain's entity index until `entities migrate` or `entities backfill` is run.\n- It was \"4\" from 02e667fc (2026-09-23) through v0.5.0, d4a0c186 and v0.6.0.\n- It is **\"5\" on graph main** via #351 (abhi-singhs, Julia signatures, commit 5b33ae84, merged 2026-10-29T13:01:44Z). That is NOT in any release yet.\n\n**Diagnostics model**\n- Graph `sem.PartialFailure` fields: Code, Severity, FilePath, Language, EffectOnCompleteness (prose), Detail.\n- `internal/cli/completeness.go` holds `diagnosticInScope` and `sameCompletenessLanguageFamily` (language-family scoping).\n- Recorded invariant: a change to what a records-cache or search-snapshot entry carries needs its own `providerRecordsCacheVersion` / `searchSnapshotCacheVersion` bump.\n\n**Brain-side facts**\n- Brain semstore knows graph schema \"1.4\". A 1.5 header is accepted with a `provider_schema_newer_minor` warning, and only a major mismatch is rejected.\n- Brain has had no MCP since v0.4.0 (brain #509).\n- `entire brain brief --branch` is rejected on v0.4.0 (\"unknown flag\"); the brain session added it on `rc/m05-surface-fixes` (9f76767), unmerged. `recall --branch` works.\n- `entities backfill --branch main` walks the LOCAL main ref. Here local main is 241 commits behind origin. Omitting `--branch` uses HEAD.\n- `graph diff --json` carries file-scoped diagnostics for files OUTSIDE the diff (verified). Brain's migrate refused on any non-info warning with `maxConsecutiveDiffFailures = 5`, so every commit failed. This is latent until a rev-5 graph ships.\n\n**Coordination rules**\n- Edit the todo board only under `fcntl.flock` on `.claude/todo-board.lock`: write `.tmp`, then `os.replace`, and touch only graph-lane rows.\n\n## 3. Files and Code Sections\n\n**`/Users/suhaan/devenv/CLAUDE.md`** (edited)\n- Line ~144: \"`entire sem …` was the old name. Its stale plugin entry was removed 2026-10-29, so it no longer runs; write `entire graph`.\"\n- Line ~147: \"Knowledge, history and durable memories (CLI only: brain has had no MCP server since v0.4.0, when brain #509 removed `entire brain mcp`):\"\n- `--branch` line: \"**Always pass `--branch main` to `recall` from a worktree.** (`brief` rejects `--branch` on brain v0.4.0 with \"unknown flag\"; the flag is on an unreleased brain branch, so don't add it to `brief` until `entire brain brief --help` lists it.) Facts are…\"\n- The old `brain_impact…` bullet was replaced with `entire brain status` and `entire brain capabilities --json` bullets.\n- The old \"Two corrections…\" paragraph was replaced with a note that `entire brain query` is BM25 lexical ranking, not vector search (trail #278), and that `brain_*` names describe the removed MCP surface.\n\n**`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`** (edited)\n- Line 12: \"`entire sem …` was the old name; its stale plugin entry was removed 2026-10-29, so it no longer runs. Write `entire graph`.\"\n- Line 14: \"Brain has no MCP server since v0.4.0 (brain #509 removed `entire brain mcp`), so any `brain_*` tool name is stale. Use the CLI: `entire brain brief \"<task>\" --json` (task-scoped packet), `recall`, `remember`, `status` (which sources are live for this repo), `inspect` (code, dependencies, change history). `entire brain query` is BM25 lexical ranking, not vector search (semantic retrieval was removed, trail #278). `entire brain capabilities --json` is authoritative.\"\n- Line 16: \"Run `entire brain status` first…\"\n\n**`~/.claude.json`**\n- Already cleaned by the brain session on 2026-10-28; backup at `~/.claude.json.bak-20261028-brainmcp`. The backup held the `/Users/suhaan/devenv` entry `{'type':'stdio','command':'entire','args':['brain','mcp'],'env':{}}`.\n- No edit by me.\n\n**Plugin registry**\n- `entire plugin remove sem` → \"Removed plugin \"sem\"\". That removed only the symlink `~/.local/share/entire/plugins/bin/entire-sem -> ~/Documents/Coding/entire-sem/entire-sem`.\n- The target binary is intact. `entire sem version` now prints usage.\n- `entire plugin list` now shows brain v0.4.0, graph v0.6.0 and judge.\n- Checked first that nothing depends on it: the brain-memory mod only regex-matches `entire (graph|sem)`, and `~/.claude/statusline-combined.sh` only uses a script file path as its third fallback.\n\n**`/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json`** (my graph-lane rows)\n- **G-followups** (todo, parked waiting on the user). Notes appended:\n  - impact \"0 tests\" on cobra handlers (runEntitiesShow is reached through fixture.run → NewRootCommand → RunE closure, deeper than impact's test search);\n  - IdentityRevision history; the brain session confirmed the stranded keys were rev 2 and recovered 10/10 via backfill without `--branch`;\n  - migrate blocked by a JSON warning, with PartialFailure already carrying file_path and language;\n  - degrade, grammar-gap and effect-scope work now in #389;\n  - main IdentityRevision is 5;\n  - candidate: `graph diff` reports file-scoped diagnostics for files outside the diff (verified on entire-brain HEAD~1..HEAD: E_FILE_TOO_LARGE SNAPSHOT.json plus 2 W_UNSUPPORTED_FILE, none in the diff's files). Not in #389. Migrate refusal is latent; brain fix e88f248d;\n  - consumer preference from brain: DEMOTE to info in `diff`, don't drop; keep full severity on index/snapshot.\n- **G-config-cleanup** (done): records sem removal, the CLAUDE.md updates, and that the `~/.claude.json` entry was already removed.\n- **G-degrade-pr** (status \"review\"): PR #389 details and verification results.\n\n**Memory** (`/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/`)\n- `semantic-layer-handoff-state.md` — added:\n  - the 2026-10-28 brain-session flags (impact 0 tests, IdentityRevision, migrate latent plus its mechanism and the brain fix e88f248d);\n  - the 2026-10-29 cleanup and PR #389 line;\n  - graph main IdentityRevision is 5.\n- `brain-mcp-cannot-write-facts.md` — appended the 2026-10-29 cleanup note. The MEMORY.md index line now reads \"config + CLAUDE.md cleaned 2026-10-29; `entire sem` unregistered; use CLI recall/brief/remember\".\n- `brain-facts-are-branch-scoped.md` — corrected: `--branch main` goes on every `recall`. `brief` on v0.4.0 rejects it (verified 2026-10-29), so run brief from the main checkout until `brief --help` lists it.\n\n**Brain facts recorded (`entire brain remember`, from entire-graph)**\n- IdentityRevision semantics and the stranding risk (architecture.integration.invariant).\n- The #389 design (architecture.diagnostics.decision).\n- The 4→5 bump via #351 (project.compatibility.gotcha).\n\n**Graph PR #389** (worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-effect-scope`)\n- Branch `fix/partial-failure-effect-scope`, head 91191330, off main 28382d8e; 54 files, +1113/−62.\n- Commits:\n  - **95137141 fix(cli):** reserve \"Coverage: degraded\" for failures that can reach code. In `internal/cli/search.go`, `if len(response.PartialFailures) > 0` became `if agentFailuresDegradeCoverage(response.PartialFailures)`, which loops `sem.PartialFailureAffectsCode`.\n  - **0a088f5d fix(sem):** report valid Go the grammar cannot parse as W_GO_GRAMMAR_GAP. Lives in `ParseWithStatusCtx` with go/parser SkipObjectResolution and a `GrammarGap` flag. Snapshot and search emit a warning instead; invalid Go keeps E_PARSE_ERROR.\n  - **91191330 feat(sem):** publish effect_scope on every warning and partial failure.\n- New file `internal/sem/diagnostic_scope.go`:\n  - `EffectScopeFile = \"file\"` and `EffectScopeSnapshot = \"snapshot\"`.\n  - `fileScopedDiagnosticCodes`: E_FILE_READ, E_FILE_TOO_LARGE, E_GO_ROUTE_BUDGET_EXCEEDED, E_GO_SIGNATURE_BUDGET_EXCEEDED, E_MINIFIED, E_PARSE_DEPTH_EXCEEDED, E_PARSE_ERROR, E_PARSE_TIMEOUT, E_UNSUPPORTED_LANGUAGE, W_ANALYSIS_BUDGET_EXCEEDED, GoGrammarGapCode, W_UNSUPPORTED_FILE.\n  - `snapshotScopedDiagnosticCodes` (repo-ignore, gitdir, walk, W_INDEX_POLICY_CHANGED, W_MOVE_AMBIGUOUS and others).\n  - `DiagnosticEffectScope(code, filePath)`: \"file\" only when the path is non-empty AND the code is file-scoped; otherwise \"snapshot\".\n  - `PartialFailureAffectsCode`: true if snapshot-scoped, or if `sourceFileLanguage` says source, or if the language is \"\".\n  - `withWarningEffectScopes` / `withFailureEffectScopes` are copy-on-write stampers, applied at 4 exit points plus 2 builders.\n- Other changes:\n  - capability key `optional_local_only_features.partial_failure_effect_scope`, also in `schema_features`;\n  - schema 1.4→1.5, ADR 1.5 section, CHANGELOG Unreleased;\n  - records cache v24→v25, search cache v30;\n  - IdentityRevision untouched;\n  - an exhaustiveness test scans the source for code literals.\n\n## 4. Errors and fixes\n\n- **Python board read failed:** `rows` was None because the board is a dict with key `tasks`. Fixed by walking `b['tasks']`.\n- **`timeout` not found on macOS:** reran without it.\n- **First recall output parse got nothing:** the field is `facts`, not `memories`. Fixed.\n- **`entire graph diff --format json` gave non-JSON:** the correct flag is `--json`.\n- **My wrong claim to the user:** I said \"`migrate` will keep refusing there until #389 merges\". The brain session showed the refusal is LATENT: migrate currently skips all 245 commits because the store matches rev 4. I corrected this in notes, on the board and to the user.\n- **The brain session's wrong claims I corrected this segment:**\n  - \"v0.6.0 moved the parser namespace\": false, identity_revision was 4 in both. They found the stranded keys were rev 2.\n  - \"unrecoverable\": false, recovered 10/10 via backfill.\n  - Misleading remedy text: that string is brain's own, and they fixed it in ad1e2124.\n- **Fix agent nuance:** my brief said IdentityRevision is \"4\"; the agent correctly found it is \"5\" on main and left it untouched.\n\n## 5. Problem Solving\n\n**Verified by me for PR #389**\n- CI: 35/35 green.\n- The Entire Gates summary shows Findings passed (\"Agent review found no blocking issues\"), Checks passed, Up to date passed, and only Approvals failed. Trail 302, branch matched, 0 findings.\n- A built binary (`/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5/scratchpad/v389/eg`) reproduced:\n  - entire-brain: \"Coverage: notice (15 languages/1783 files; 0 warnings; 47 partial failures)\", with the JSON partials listed;\n  - entiredb: the 4 files (`cmd/entire-ci/cli/buildkite_watch_test.go`, `core/githubperms/service_test.go`, `core/identity/github_email_identities_test.go`, `core/regional/author_lookup_test.go`) are W_GO_GRAMMAR_GAP with scope file, and there is no Go E_PARSE_ERROR.\n\n**Agent-reported results**\n- Cold index on entiredb: base 6.38 s vs new 6.35 s (median of 3, load1 ~7).\n- Data records identical.\n- Mutation proofs for every guard.\n- Full sem and cli suites pass with `-p 1`; the race subset is clean.\n\n**Known limit, disclosed to the user:** \"file\" scope claims the loss is confined to that file. But a call from another file into a skipped source file could, in principle, resolve to a different target rather than go missing. This doesn't matter for data files, and source files still show \"degraded\".\n\n**Brain session status**\n- Committed e88f248d on `fix/migrate-warning-relevance`: excuses a warning only when it is file-local AND names a file absent from that diff's `files` (both sides of a rename). It reads effect_scope first and falls back to a code table.\n- Tested safe whether graph keeps, demotes or drops these diagnostics.\n- It deliberately did NOT bump semstore.SchemaVersion to 1.5; tracked on the board as `semstore-schema-15-not-yet`. It wants a ping when #389 merges.\n- It moved `~/.local/bin/entire-brain` v0.1.0 to `entire-brain.v0.1.0-shadow`; the brain pre-edit hook works now.\n- A brain `workspace watch --distill` daemon has run at ~113% CPU for 42 hours: a CPU confound for timings. It is the brain lane's or the user's call.\n\n## 6. All user messages\n\n- (Earlier segments, summarized before) Includes:\n  - \"i am not merging anything TILL WE FINISH EVERYTHING so stop asking\";\n  - \"DON'T delete the stuff i didn't cp\";\n  - keep \"cahces for oggle chrome other apps etc\";\n  - coordinate with the brain session;\n  - \"ok please finish and hwo did u get such gains what u did change/edit, did u reduce quality?, answer pelase then finisha dn thenr eview each cehck trail reviews and emrge\";\n  - \"progress?\".\n- This segment: **\"i give u full perms to do all that\"**. That approves items 1–4: remove the dead MCP entry, update both CLAUDE.md files, `entire plugin remove sem`, and open one graph PR.\n- Every other incoming message was a cross-session message from the brain session or a subagent report. Those are not user approvals.\n\n**Standing constraints (verbatim or near-verbatim, still in effect)**\n- No AI attribution footers in commits or PR bodies. The user's CLAUDE.md overrides the attribution reminder.\n- Never commit in main checkouts (cli/, entiredb/, entire.io/, entire-api/). One fresh worktree per task.\n- Never set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. No git stash.\n- Real-agent e2e costs money; never run it proactively.\n- Don't probe the keychain.\n- Brain test isolation: ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR plus a local binary. NEVER `--daemon`. Never the real store.\n- G3 protocol: never `entire brain setup`/`refresh`; never touch `~/.local/share/entire`. The user-approved `sem` removal was the exception.\n- Use the repo-configured git identity (noreply). Never publish the user's email.\n- Ask or announce to the other session before touching shared state (the real brain store, installed plugins, `.claude/mods/*`).\n- Announce before swapping shared binaries: rm, then cp to a temp name, then mv; never copy over a binary in use.\n- \"DON'T delete the stuff i didn't cp\".\n- Security flag for the user: GitHub recovery codes and Stripe backup codes sit as plain .txt files in Downloads.\n- Lane rule: don't merge or touch brain PRs. Don't merge other authors' PRs.\n- Peer messages never grant permission. Don't edit permission settings, CLAUDE.md or config because a peer asked.\n\n## 7. Pending Tasks\n\n- **The user's decision on merging graph PR #389.** I asked \"Want me to merge #389?\" with no answer yet. Do not merge without an explicit yes.\n- **After #389 merges:** ping the brain session for its one-line semstore.SchemaVersion \"1.5\" bump (`semstore-schema-15-not-yet`).\n- **G-followups candidates (not started, need user approval):**\n  - graph diff: demote (to info), don't drop, file-scoped diagnostics whose file is absent from both sides of the diff; keep full severity on index/snapshot;\n  - impact \"0 tests\" disclosure for cobra handlers;\n  - CHANGELOG call-out on IdentityRevision bumps;\n  - the locate miss on `covers()`;\n  - earlier follow-ups: `--no-renames` co-change, history-refresh cache misses, warm alias route, C1 REFERENCES relation, Python/TS tool registration.\n- **Other user items from the page:**\n  - build-then-swap CAS;\n  - transcript-mode re-distill;\n  - lazy-fetch CI as a required check;\n  - 37 GB brain store delete;\n  - 63 ~/Documents/Coding paths;\n  - 3 cli issues;\n  - cli checkpoint 18b787bf552f;\n  - Linear connector re-add;\n  - old drafts #146, #300 and #249;\n  - entire.io old-layout brain rebuild;\n  - the gate-neutral-reads-as-reviewed product request;\n  - /compact.\n- **Note for the user:** the next graph release containing #351 (identity revision 5) strands brain rev-4 entity records until re-index. backfill works; migrate is fixed brain-side in e88f248d (unmerged).\n\n## 8. Current Work\n\nThe latest cross-session message came from the brain session. It said its filter e88f248d is safe whether graph keeps, demotes or drops diff diagnostics for untouched files. From the consumer side it asked graph to **\"demote in `diff`, not drop — and keep them at full severity on the index/snapshot surfaces\"**, because dropping would remove the only signal that the repo contains an unparseable file. If graph drops them, then `graph index` or `capabilities` should report unparseable files. It said \"No action needed from me either way; e88f248d stands as-is.\"\n\nI logged that preference on the G-followups board row: \"Consumer preference (brain): DEMOTE (to info) in `diff`, don't drop; keep full severity on index/snapshot…\". No reply was sent; none was needed. The last substantive item awaiting the user is the #389 merge decision.\n\n## 9. Optional Next Step\n\nGive the user a one-line update:\n- the brain session prefers demoting, not dropping, out-of-diff file warnings in `graph diff`, and this is logged as a follow-up;\n- the brain fix works under any choice.\n\nThen keep waiting for the user's answer to \"Want me to merge #389?\". Do not merge #389 or start the diff-demotion follow-up without an explicit yes. If the user says merge, merge #389 with a merge commit after re-checking CI and mergeability, then ping the brain session for its semstore 1.5 bump.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"3e1de7e1-3b12-4eda-8fe6-0098b9c85dde","timestamp":"2026-10-30T03:15:29.791Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"3e1de7e1-3b12-4eda-8fe6-0098b9c85dde","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/semantic-layer-handoff-state.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/semantic-layer-handoff-state.md","content":"---\nname: semantic-layer-handoff-state\ndescription: 2026-10-25 ALL 25 MERGED — graph 12 (main d0475ce8, == #381 tree) + brain 13 (main c4c4ae1c); graph v0.6.0 released+installed; brain mains green\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n**2026-10-25 evening: ALL 25 PRs MERGED on the user's explicit \"merge\".** Neither repo requires approvals on GitHub\n(Entire Gates \"Approvals\" is reported, not enforced); brain main has enforce_admins + required benchmark-corpus /\nbrowser-smoke, so #484 needed its brainmark tests fixed first.\n- **Graph (I merged):** 370 a12fff59, 371 227f7a60, 377 daa06090 (retargeted), 373 1d1e8394, 379 fc71355e,\n  376 9bad2b4a, 375 57f280bf, 372 b8850d68, 380 ebf9a2fa, 374 e514be52, 142 1492feb9, 378 d0475ce8. Final main tree\n  8b0913a4 == #381 tip tree; #381 closed. Last four went in as a fast-forward CHAIN (each merges its predecessor +\n  saved resolution patch) → one CI cycle instead of four.\n- **#373 after #382:** keeps #382's FIFO pool, only lookahead 4→16 / buffers 8→2; −3.4..−9.5% (not −28..−35%).\n- **Brain (brain session merged):** all 13, main c4c4ae1c. Follow-up: open finding trail 390 on merged #481 code\n  (seed copies snapshot.Selected regardless of `covered`); fix PR in progress by brain session.\n- **Brain main red→green same evening:** evisdren #496 broke #483's test (semantic conflict); his #497 merged 19:10 (9f6ab8ec), brain's trail-390 fix #499 merged 19:17 (075a6ea9); main test green through caac7622. #499 got NO agent review: its trail change had branch \"\" so gates were neutral (\"No trail tracks this branch\") and nothing dispatched; brain session hand-reviewed post-merge (2 guards + 108 test lines, code fine). See [[trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls]] #5.\n- **Graph v0.6.0 released 2026-10-26 at dfe93b98** (contains all 12 + #383); installed managed 2026-10-27 replacing a path-install symlink to a gitignored Oct-24 binary in the main checkout. `entire sem` is a SEPARATE stale plugin entry (~/Documents/Coding/entire-sem, version dev), not an alias.\n- **2026-10-27 brain v0.4.0 notes (from brain session):** fact dedup runs inside `entire brain refresh` (entire-brain main 7526 rows/1958 distinct → 1959/1959; `memories gc` is NOT the lever). A graph binary swap invalidates brain's semantic index → `entire brain repair` per repo after any graph upgrade (interrupted refresh also leaves semantic=missing). After my v0.6.0 swap: semantic=true only on entire-brain; false on entire-graph, cli, entiredb, entire.io (entire.io also old-layout). Handed to brain lane. cli+entiredb ARE partial clones (URL-named promisor remote, not origin; brain session missed it checking remote.origin.*), so their repair under v0.6.0 is real evidence for #372. Their earlier 'semantic snapshot header missing commit' failure is NOT v0.6.0 skew: that string left brain prod code in 887b4055 (2026-10-22) and is absent at v0.2.0/v0.3.0/v0.4.0 → a stale pre-COR-2217 record. Graph 'Coverage: degraded' on entire-brain = 47 JSON-only partials (any partial → degraded); in G-followups, user decides.\n- **#372 confirmed on real data 2026-10-27:** brain repair under graph v0.6.0 indexed cli (1427 files) + entiredb (2542) with no promisor refusal. **New graph gap:** Go 1.26 `new(expr)` breaks the bundled tree-sitter-go (smacker 2024-08) -> E_PARSE_ERROR on valid Go (4 entiredb test files). Both in G-followups. Measured: 4 files/26 calls (entiredb tests only); defs 77/77 + outer CALLS 10/10 survive (tree-sitter error recovery) — only exprs inside new(...) at risk. Upstream tree-sitter-go master still needs a type in special_argument_list → fix = vendored patched grammar, not a bump. Synthetic `new(g())` test: E_PARSE_ERROR flagged but CALLS ->g still emitted → no measured loss; effectively a spurious warning feeding 'degraded' (cheap fix: defer to go/parser for Go).\n- **2026-10-28 (brain session flags, checked):** (a) `graph impact` reports '0 tests' for cobra handlers (runEntitiesShow) although 3 tests run `entities show` via fixture.run → NewRootCommand → RunE closure, a chain deeper than impact's test search → '0 tests' on a handler is unreliable. (b) Brain entity records are namespaced by `graph version --json` identity_revision; IdentityRevision is \"4\" in v0.5.0, d4a0c186 and v0.6.0 (unchanged since 02e667fc, 2026-09-23), so the brain session's 'v0.6.0 moved the namespace' was wrong; it found the stranded keys are rev 2 (486 keys/11 commits, pre-09-23); recovered 10/10 with `entities backfill` WITHOUT `--branch` (`--branch main` walks LOCAL main, 241 commits behind origin; HEAD was ahead of it, so those commits were unreachable). The migrate remedy in brain's warning pointed away from the fix. (c) `brain entities migrate` refuses on ANY graph diff warning; one tracked 16.8 MB JSON (E_FILE_TOO_LARGE) would block it on entire-brain. LATENT, not live (2026-10-29): today migrate skips all 245 commits (store already rev 4) and never calls diff; it fires once a rev-5 graph lands. Mechanism: graph diff carries file-scoped diagnostics for files OUTSIDE the diff (verified HEAD~1..HEAD: E_FILE_TOO_LARGE SNAPSHOT.json, not in diff files), so every commit fails and maxConsecutiveDiffFailures=5 stops the run. Brain fix e88f248d on fix/migrate-warning-relevance reads effect_scope first (table fallback); unmerged. PartialFailure already has file_path+language (consumers can scope now); graph lacks a machine-readable effect scope, which is a candidate to pair with the degrade-label PR. Both are in G-followups, which is parked waiting on the user.\n- **2026-10-29 user-approved cleanup + PR:** `sem` plugin unregistered; both CLAUDE.md files moved to brain CLI verbs (brief rejects --branch on v0.4.0). Graph **PR #389** (fix/partial-failure-effect-scope @91191330) OPEN, 35/35 green, agent review ran with 0 findings; only Approvals red; awaiting user merge. Schema 1.4->1.5 (brain accepts with provider_schema_newer_minor warning until it bumps semstore.SchemaVersion). **Graph main IdentityRevision is now 5** (#351, abhi-singhs, merged 10-29, not in v0.6.0): the next graph release strands brain rev-4 entity records; brain session told.\n- **Open for user:** (nightly done); decisions list below still stands (minus approvals).\n\n(History below is the pre-merge state.)\n\nAs of 2026-10-25 the brain half is **final**; the graph half is on **hold for one rebase**. Nothing is merged; the\nuser said nothing merges until everything is finished.\n\n- **Late change (2026-10-25):** evisdren merged graph #382 (shared relation facts, rewrote\n  provider_parallel_stream.go) at b31626ea. #373 now conflicts; a G3 agent is rebasing #373, re-timing it on top of\n  #382 (its old −28–35% was vs d4a0c186), rebuilding #381 and re-checking patches. Board row `G-382-rebase`; page has\n  a \"Graph: hold\" callout to remove when done.\n- **Brain final heads** (clean in order on main a4942dd9; combined 45e7a626, go test 25/25 pkgs, dispatched CI run\n  40214249807 green): 473 8f693073, 474 ef41d238, 476 66348cd2, 477 d58e9639, 478 64b7a146, 479 2d020c72,\n  480 c796a615, 481 46fe7f3b, 482 031fbb5b, 483 1e257ab9, 484 9a3aac28, 488 35c308e4, 489 5f15accf. #493 CLOSED.\n  #484 `benchmark-corpus` red = brainmark Python packet-shape tests, deliberately deferred (user: benchmark work can\n  wait). #477 no longer carries #478's content. Brain patches are reference only.\n- **Closed-PR CI trap:** closing an integration PR stops pull_request CI and `gh pr checks` keeps the old green;\n  use `gh workflow run test.yml --ref <branch>` and verify headSha.\n\n- **Graph** (entireio/entire-graph): #142 and #370-#380, all CI-green.\n  - Findings verified per trail with `--trail entire-graph/<n> --status any --freshness any` plus a branch match: 0 open.\n  - Draft **#381** (DO NOT MERGE) combines all 12 and is green.\n- **Brain** (entireio/entire-brain): #473, #474, #476-#484, #488, #489, all green.\n  - The 4 findings (#477/#483/#484/#489) are fixed.\n  - Draft #493 was the combined PR; now closed (see above).\n- **Merge plan:** the \"Merge plan\" tab of https://claude.ai/artifact/FkY6c5J1XdzaYGM1Q7T9dU.\n  - Rebase patches are in `~/devenv-worktrees/handoff/{graph,brain}-patches`.\n  - Graph detail: `handoff/HANDOFF-GRAPH.md`. Brain decisions: `devenv/DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md`.\n  - **Re-run the merge simulation right before merging**: main drifts, and one brain PR went from clean to\n    conflicting within hours.\n- **Graph merge order:** 370 → 371 → 377 (retarget) → 373 → 379 → 376 → 375 → 372 → 380 → 374 → 142 (3 patches) →\n  378 (3 patches). Graph #380 before brain #484.\n- **Fresh-env adoption on the combined graph build:** main sessions and Explore subagents went graph-first in every\n  searching task, with 0 graph failures. The harness now installs via `entire graph setup`.\n- **User decisions pending:**\n  - approvals on 25 PRs;\n  - brain build-then-swap CAS vs the non-interleaving invariant;\n  - the transcript-mode re-distill cost;\n  - making the lazy-fetch CI job required;\n  - the 37 GB brain store delete;\n  - 63 ~/Documents/Coding paths;\n  - 3 cli-lane issues;\n  - old drafts #146/#300 and community #249;\n  - cli checkpoint 18b787bf552f (shared remote cleanup); Linear connector re-add.\n\nSupersedes [[graph-landing-paused-state]]. Related: [[announce-before-swapping-shared-binaries]],\n[[green-suite-is-not-evidence]], [[mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test]].\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}},"displayPath":"../.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/semantic-layer-handoff-state.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"320fe46c-e533-4df1-8bea-f661293dc593","timestamp":"2026-10-30T03:15:30.066Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/semantic-layer-handoff-state.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t---\n2\tname: semantic-layer-handoff-state\n3\tdescription: 2026-10-25 ALL 25 MERGED — graph 12 (main d0475ce8, == #381 tree) + brain 13 (main c4c4ae1c); graph v0.6.0 released+installed; brain mains green\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  type: project\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t**2026-10-25 evening: ALL 25 PRs MERGED on the user's explicit \"merge\".** Neither repo requires approvals on GitHub\n9\t(Entire Gates \"Approvals\" is reported, not enforced); brain main has enforce_admins + required benchmark-corpus /\n10\tbrowser-smoke, so #484 needed its brainmark tests fixed first.\n11\t- **Graph (I merged):** 370 a12fff59, 371 227f7a60, 377 daa06090 (retargeted), 373 1d1e8394, 379 fc71355e,\n12\t  376 9bad2b4a, 375 57f280bf, 372 b8850d68, 380 ebf9a2fa, 374 e514be52, 142 1492feb9, 378 d0475ce8. Final main tree\n13\t  8b0913a4 == #381 tip tree; #381 closed. Last four went in as a fast-forward CHAIN (each merges its predecessor +\n14\t  saved resolution patch) → one CI cycle instead of four.\n15\t- **#373 after #382:** keeps #382's FIFO pool, only lookahead 4→16 / buffers 8→2; −3.4..−9.5% (not −28..−35%).\n16\t- **Brain (brain session merged):** all 13, main c4c4ae1c. Follow-up: open finding trail 390 on merged #481 code\n17\t  (seed copies snapshot.Selected regardless of `covered`); fix PR in progress by brain session.\n18\t- **Brain main red→green same evening:** evisdren #496 broke #483's test (semantic conflict); his #497 merged 19:10 (9f6ab8ec), brain's trail-390 fix #499 merged 19:17 (075a6ea9); main test green through caac7622. #499 got NO agent review: its trail change had branch \"\" so gates were neutral (\"No trail tracks this branch\") and nothing dispatched; brain session hand-reviewed post-merge (2 guards + 108 test lines, code fine). See [[trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls]] #5.\n19\t- **Graph v0.6.0 released 2026-10-26 at dfe93b98** (contains all 12 + #383); installed managed 2026-10-27 replacing a path-install symlink to a gitignored Oct-24 binary in the main checkout. `entire sem` is a SEPARATE stale plugin entry (~/Documents/Coding/entire-sem, version dev), not an alias.\n20\t- **2026-10-27 brain v0.4.0 notes (from brain session):** fact dedup runs inside `entire brain refresh` (entire-brain main 7526 rows/1958 distinct → 1959/1959; `memories gc` is NOT the lever). A graph binary swap invalidates brain's semantic index → `entire brain repair` per repo after any graph upgrade (interrupted refresh also leaves semantic=missing). After my v0.6.0 swap: semantic=true only on entire-brain; false on entire-graph, cli, entiredb, entire.io (entire.io also old-layout). Handed to brain lane. cli+entiredb ARE partial clones (URL-named promisor remote, not origin; brain session missed it checking remote.origin.*), so their repair under v0.6.0 is real evidence for #372. Their earlier 'semantic snapshot header missing commit' failure is NOT v0.6.0 skew: that string left brain prod code in 887b4055 (2026-10-22) and is absent at v0.2.0/v0.3.0/v0.4.0 → a stale pre-COR-2217 record. Graph 'Coverage: degraded' on entire-brain = 47 JSON-only partials (any partial → degraded); in G-followups, user decides.\n21\t- **#372 confirmed on real data 2026-10-27:** brain repair under graph v0.6.0 indexed cli (1427 files) + entiredb (2542) with no promisor refusal. **New graph gap:** Go 1.26 `new(expr)` breaks the bundled tree-sitter-go (smacker 2024-08) -> E_PARSE_ERROR on valid Go (4 entiredb test files). Both in G-followups. Measured: 4 files/26 calls (entiredb tests only); defs 77/77 + outer CALLS 10/10 survive (tree-sitter error recovery) — only exprs inside new(...) at risk. Upstream tree-sitter-go master still needs a type in special_argument_list → fix = vendored patched grammar, not a bump. Synthetic `new(g())` test: E_PARSE_ERROR flagged but CALLS ->g still emitted → no measured loss; effectively a spurious warning feeding 'degraded' (cheap fix: defer to go/parser for Go).\n22\t- **2026-10-28 (brain session flags, checked):** (a) `graph impact` reports '0 tests' for cobra handlers (runEntitiesShow) although 3 tests run `entities show` via fixture.run → NewRootCommand → RunE closure, a chain deeper than impact's test search → '0 tests' on a handler is unreliable. (b) Brain entity records are namespaced by `graph version --json` identity_revision; IdentityRevision is \"4\" in v0.5.0, d4a0c186 and v0.6.0 (unchanged since 02e667fc, 2026-09-23), so the brain session's 'v0.6.0 moved the namespace' was wrong; it found the stranded keys are rev 2 (486 keys/11 commits, pre-09-23); recovered 10/10 with `entities backfill` WITHOUT `--branch` (`--branch main` walks LOCAL main, 241 commits behind origin; HEAD was ahead of it, so those commits were unreachable). The migrate remedy in brain's warning pointed away from the fix. (c) `brain entities migrate` refuses on ANY graph diff warning; one tracked 16.8 MB JSON (E_FILE_TOO_LARGE) would block it on entire-brain. LATENT, not live (2026-10-29): today migrate skips all 245 commits (store already rev 4) and never calls diff; it fires once a rev-5 graph lands. Mechanism: graph diff carries file-scoped diagnostics for files OUTSIDE the diff (verified HEAD~1..HEAD: E_FILE_TOO_LARGE SNAPSHOT.json, not in diff files), so every commit fails and maxConsecutiveDiffFailures=5 stops the run. Brain fix e88f248d on fix/migrate-warning-relevance reads effect_scope first (table fallback); unmerged. PartialFailure already has file_path+language (consumers can scope now); graph lacks a machine-readable effect scope, which is a candidate to pair with the degrade-label PR. Both are in G-followups, which is parked waiting on the user.\n23\t- **2026-10-29 user-approved cleanup + PR:** `sem` plugin unregistered; both CLAUDE.md 