{"parentUuid":"07809a8d-f608-46df-9fad-272cfad844d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cgij3JNiS6y2TVT3jBXy2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FGyb2VKntk6mX2obN81BFo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr checks 357 --repo entireio/entire-graph --json name,state,link --jq 'group_by(.state)|map({state:.[0].state,n:length,names:map(.name)})'; echo \"=== timeline comments:\"; gh pr view 357 --repo entireio/entire-graph --json comments --jq '.comments[]|\"--- \\(.author.login) \\(.createdAt):\\n\\(.body[0:1500])\"'","description":"Checks and comments on PR 357"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1820,"cache_read_input_tokens":149582,"output_tokens":517,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":189},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1820,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":149582,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1820,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1820},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FGyb2VKntk6mX2obN81BFo":{"command":"gh pr checks 357 --repo entireio/entire-graph --json name,state,link --jq 'group_by(.state)|map({state:.[0].state,n:length,names:map(.name)})'; echo \"=== timeline comments:\"; gh pr view 357 --repo entireio/entire-graph --json comments --jq '.comments[]|\"--- \\(.author.login) \\(.createdAt):\\n\\(.body[0:1500])\"'","description":"Checks and comments on PR 357"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"10b26706-978c-4ec2-bd47-98cb27fc8267","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgij3J38CHjkz9Ci7ns4d","requestRef":"19557c14-e63c-4d1c-b199-ed8c2d46bee6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"eb12188a-5727-4487-9271-59f27fab35af","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:05:44.681Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"07809a8d-f608-46df-9fad-272cfad844d1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"98a7f3b5-94c6-4e5c-bf78-00b9da1cb37a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PgqSqn3ct5KNe2QdkqGRae","type":"tool_result","content":"> [!NOTE]\n> This PR was prepared by Claude Code, an AI agent, working under Rod\n> Begbie's direction. Rod reviewed and approved this PR (including this\ndescription before it was posted.)\n\nSwift is parsed by go-tree-sitter's bundled tree-sitter-swift 0.5.0, which\npredates Swift 5.9 macros, so every swift-testing file using `#expect` or\n`#require` is an `E_PARSE_ERROR` partial failure. go-tree-sitter hasn't\nmoved since August 2024, so this vendors tree-sitter-swift 0.7.4 under\n`internal/sem/grammars/swift`, the same way #21 replaced the C# grammar.\nAcross graph-bench's ten Swift repositories, Swift parse failures drop from\n10,928 to 9,964, with a handful of real regressions listed below.\n\nFixes #345.\n\n## Commits\n\n1. **Vendor tree-sitter-swift v0.7.4 at ABI 14** (`ed0b354`). The tag's\n   `src/parser.c` is already ABI 14, so it is copied verbatim with its\n   headers and licence. `IdentityRevision` goes to 6, because previously\n   failing files now yield different declarations and the caches are keyed\n   on the source tree. The 29 golden fixtures change only in that header\n   field.\n1. **Drop the leading-operator continuation mask** (`3b271b4`). It blanked\n   lines starting with `==`, `&&` and friends for the old grammar, and\n   took the line's closing parens with it, so multi-line `#expect(a\\n ==\n   b)` became a \"missing )\" error on 0.7.4.\n1. **Drop masks 0.7.4 makes unnecessary** (`8ef066b`). Each remaining\n   mask was disabled on its own and kept unless that made any repository\n   worse:\n   - Removed: empty attribute calls, which also broke\n     `@autoclosure() -> T?`, and `if let x {` shorthand.\n   - Kept: computed string-property blocks, property-wrapper prefixes,\n     typed throws, multiline strings, and `for try await x in try y`,\n     which 0.7.4 still rejects.\n1. **Record vendored grammar origins and add a refresh tool**\n   (`d683334`). This one is optional: the first three commits stand without\n   it.\n   - `internal/sem/grammars/grammars.json` records each vendored grammar's\n     repository, ref, commit, files and ABI.\n   - `go run ./cmd/grammar-refresh -lang <name> -ref <ref>` re-vendors a\n     grammar verbatim, refusing anything outside ABI 13–14, and always\n     writes the licence as `LICENSE` so `gen-notices.sh` keeps attributing\n     it.\n   - All twelve entries were backfilled from their commit messages and\n     checked by re-vendoring. Every `parser.c` the tool could fetch matches\n     upstream byte-for-byte, and re-running it for Swift or Clojure\n     reproduces the committed files exactly.\n   - The notes record the exceptions:\n     - C# was regenerated from an ABI 15 release, so the tool refuses its ref.\n     - Dart came from an npm tarball whose `parser.c` isn't in git history.\n     - F#'s scanner include was edited by hand.\n     - Julia, Objective-C, R and Zig left out some upstream `tree_sitter/`\n       headers that a refresh would add.\n1. **Changelog entry** (`ad7c49a`).\n\nRevision 5 went to the Julia signature fix on `main` while this was open, so\nthe Swift bump is 6. The refresh tool (commit 4) also adds itself to the\nlazy-fetch guard's allowlist in `internal/gitutil/lazy_fetch_guard_test.go`,\nnext to `cmd/graph-bench`, because it launches `git` directly to fetch an\nupstream grammar into a scratch repository. That keeps commit 4 separable: it\npasses `internal/gitutil` on its own, so it can be dropped or cherry-picked\nwithout the Swift commits.\n\nCommits 2 and 3 ride commit 1's `IdentityRevision` bump. Landed separately,\nthey would need their own.\n\n## Results\n\nSwift-only parse failures and Swift symbols, measured per file over the\nlock-pinned graph-bench clones, `main` → this branch:\n\n| Repository | Failing files | Symbols | Newly failing |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| apple/swift | 10,583 → 9,824 | 180,685 → 181,581 | 69 |\n| swift-composable-architecture | 201 → 54 | 9,861 → 9,866 | 3 |\n| vapor | 53 → 10 | 4,232 → 4,231 | 0 |\n| realm-swift | 30 → 21 | 11,039 → 11,093 | 0 |\n| Alamofire | 10 → 5 | 7,392 → 7,392 | 0 |\n| Kingfisher | 4 → 3 | 4,504 → 4,504 | 0 |\n| lottie-ios | 2 → 2 | 4,758 → 4,758 | 1 |\n| RxSwift, SnapKit, SwiftyJSON | unchanged | unchanged | 0 |\n\nThree repositories outside the benchmark, chosen because they exercise\nnewer Swift:\n\n| Repository | Failing files | Symbols |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| hummingbird 2.28.0 | 42 → 3 | 4,684 → 4,675 |\n| OnionBrowser v3.4.3 | 10 → 0 | 1,562 → 1,566 |\n| firefox-ios v158.0 | 175 → 79 | 82,957 → 82,915 |\n\nSome symbol \"losses\" are fixes:\n\n- firefox-ios: the old grammar turned every `nonisolated(unsafe)` declaration\n  into a phantom `Type.(unsafe)` field.\n- vapor: nine locals of `BaseNTests.check` were filed as fields of the type.\n\n## Regressions\n\nThese are real, and I'd rather list them than mask them:\n\n- **A lone attribute or `#else` branch inside `#if`**, directly above a\n  declaration. This is the big one:\n  - most of apple/swift's 69 newly failing files (stdlib `#if hasFeature`,\n    `_pointerBitWidth`, `#error`)\n  - TCA's three (`#else`)\n  - 19 uniffi-generated firefox-ios files (`@_documentation(visibility:\n    private)`)\n- **`switch consume x`** fails the whole file. In hummingbird's\n  `HTTP2ServerConnectionManager+StateMachine.swift` that is 42 → 23\n  symbols.\n- **A multi-line `where` clause on an `associatedtype`** (lottie-ios's\n  `DiffableSection.swift`).\n- **vapor's `ConditionalResponseCompressionTests.swift`** fails on both\n  grammars, but 0.7.4 loses its top-level struct.\n- **apple/swift has 826 fewer relations (0.07%)** in graph-bench's report,\n  while realm-swift (+157), vapor (+61) and TCA (+29) gain. I haven't traced\n  where the 826 go. My guess is the newly failing `#if` files, but I haven't\n  checked that.\n\nStill unparsed on both grammars: regex literals containing `{n,m}` or\n`\\/`, `any P` inside a tuple type argument, `final` used as an identifier,\nand `while await !x`. These look like upstream tree-sitter-swift issues\nrather than anything for this repo.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go test ./...` passes (10 packages). The race suite was not run:\n  `internal/sem` under `-race` exceeds its 30-minute timeout.\n- `gofmt -s`, `go vet ./...` and `scripts/gen-notices.sh --check` are clean.\n- graph-bench `-languages Swift` (full tier, `repos.lock.json` pins) before\n  and after: the per-repository parse-failure and symbol deltas agree with the\n  table above.\n- On a private macOS app (279 Swift files), after installing this build:\n  `entire brain doctor` goes from 140 partial failures to 9, and its\n  `semantic: degraded` warning goes away.\n\nGetting from roughly 10.9k to 10.0k Swift failures is the headline, but the\n`#if` regression is the thing to weigh before merging.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b8d772af-e328-4241-814b-73f84132e523","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:05:46.611Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"> [!NOTE]\n> This PR was prepared by Claude Code, an AI agent, working under Rod\n> Begbie's direction. Rod reviewed and approved this PR (including this\ndescription before it was posted.)\n\nSwift is parsed by go-tree-sitter's bundled tree-sitter-swift 0.5.0, which\npredates Swift 5.9 macros, so every swift-testing file using `#expect` or\n`#require` is an `E_PARSE_ERROR` partial failure. go-tree-sitter hasn't\nmoved since August 2024, so this vendors tree-sitter-swift 0.7.4 under\n`internal/sem/grammars/swift`, the same way #21 replaced the C# grammar.\nAcross graph-bench's ten Swift repositories, Swift parse failures drop from\n10,928 to 9,964, with a handful of real regressions listed below.\n\nFixes #345.\n\n## Commits\n\n1. **Vendor tree-sitter-swift v0.7.4 at ABI 14** (`ed0b354`). The tag's\n   `src/parser.c` is already ABI 14, so it is copied verbatim with its\n   headers and licence. `IdentityRevision` goes to 6, because previously\n   failing files now yield different declarations and the caches are keyed\n   on the source tree. The 29 golden fixtures change only in that header\n   field.\n1. **Drop the leading-operator continuation mask** (`3b271b4`). It blanked\n   lines starting with `==`, `&&` and friends for the old grammar, and\n   took the line's closing parens with it, so multi-line `#expect(a\\n ==\n   b)` became a \"missing )\" error on 0.7.4.\n1. **Drop masks 0.7.4 makes unnecessary** (`8ef066b`). Each remaining\n   mask was disabled on its own and kept unless that made any repository\n   worse:\n   - Removed: empty attribute calls, which also broke\n     `@autoclosure() -> T?`, and `if let x {` shorthand.\n   - Kept: computed string-property blocks, property-wrapper prefixes,\n     typed throws, multiline strings, and `for try await x in try y`,\n     which 0.7.4 still rejects.\n1. **Record vendored grammar origins and add a refresh tool**\n   (`d683334`). This one is optional: the first three commits stand without\n   it.\n   - `internal/sem/grammars/grammars.json` records each vendored grammar's\n     repository, ref, commit, files and ABI.\n   - `go run ./cmd/grammar-refresh -lang <name> -ref <ref>` re-vendors a\n     grammar verbatim, refusing anything outside ABI 13–14, and always\n     writes the licence as `LICENSE` so `gen-notices.sh` keeps attributing\n     it.\n   - All twelve entries were backfilled from their commit messages and\n     checked by re-vendoring. Every `parser.c` the tool could fetch matches\n     upstream byte-for-byte, and re-running it for Swift or Clojure\n     reproduces the committed files exactly.\n   - The notes record the exceptions:\n     - C# was regenerated from an ABI 15 release, so the tool refuses its ref.\n     - Dart came from an npm tarball whose `parser.c` isn't in git history.\n     - F#'s scanner include was edited by hand.\n     - Julia, Objective-C, R and Zig left out some upstream `tree_sitter/`\n       headers that a refresh would add.\n1. **Changelog entry** (`ad7c49a`).\n\nRevision 5 went to the Julia signature fix on `main` while this was open, so\nthe Swift bump is 6. The refresh tool (commit 4) also adds itself to the\nlazy-fetch guard's allowlist in `internal/gitutil/lazy_fetch_guard_test.go`,\nnext to `cmd/graph-bench`, because it launches `git` directly to fetch an\nupstream grammar into a scratch repository. That keeps commit 4 separable: it\npasses `internal/gitutil` on its own, so it can be dropped or cherry-picked\nwithout the Swift commits.\n\nCommits 2 and 3 ride commit 1's `IdentityRevision` bump. Landed separately,\nthey would need their own.\n\n## Results\n\nSwift-only parse failures and Swift symbols, measured per file over the\nlock-pinned graph-bench clones, `main` → this branch:\n\n| Repository | Failing files | Symbols | Newly failing |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| apple/swift | 10,583 → 9,824 | 180,685 → 181,581 | 69 |\n| swift-composable-architecture | 201 → 54 | 9,861 → 9,866 | 3 |\n| vapor | 53 → 10 | 4,232 → 4,231 | 0 |\n| realm-swift | 30 → 21 | 11,039 → 11,093 | 0 |\n| Alamofire | 10 → 5 | 7,392 → 7,392 | 0 |\n| Kingfisher | 4 → 3 | 4,504 → 4,504 | 0 |\n| lottie-ios | 2 → 2 | 4,758 → 4,758 | 1 |\n| RxSwift, SnapKit, SwiftyJSON | unchanged | unchanged | 0 |\n\nThree repositories outside the benchmark, chosen because they exercise\nnewer Swift:\n\n| Repository | Failing files | Symbols |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| hummingbird 2.28.0 | 42 → 3 | 4,684 → 4,675 |\n| OnionBrowser v3.4.3 | 10 → 0 | 1,562 → 1,566 |\n| firefox-ios v158.0 | 175 → 79 | 82,957 → 82,915 |\n\nSome symbol \"losses\" are fixes:\n\n- firefox-ios: the old grammar turned every `nonisolated(unsafe)` declaration\n  into a phantom `Type.(unsafe)` field.\n- vapor: nine locals of `BaseNTests.check` were filed as fields of the type.\n\n## Regressions\n\nThese are real, and I'd rather list them than mask them:\n\n- **A lone attribute or `#else` branch inside `#if`**, directly above a\n  declaration. This is the big one:\n  - most of apple/swift's 69 newly failing files (stdlib `#if hasFeature`,\n    `_pointerBitWidth`, `#error`)\n  - TCA's three (`#else`)\n  - 19 uniffi-generated firefox-ios files (`@_documentation(visibility:\n    private)`)\n- **`switch consume x`** fails the whole file. In hummingbird's\n  `HTTP2ServerConnectionManager+StateMachine.swift` that is 42 → 23\n  symbols.\n- **A multi-line `where` clause on an `associatedtype`** (lottie-ios's\n  `DiffableSection.swift`).\n- **vapor's `ConditionalResponseCompressionTests.swift`** fails on both\n  grammars, but 0.7.4 loses its top-level struct.\n- **apple/swift has 826 fewer relations (0.07%)** in graph-bench's report,\n  while realm-swift (+157), vapor (+61) and TCA (+29) gain. I haven't traced\n  where the 826 go. My guess is the newly failing `#if` files, but I haven't\n  checked that.\n\nStill unparsed on both grammars: regex literals containing `{n,m}` or\n`\\/`, `any P` inside a tuple type argument, `final` used as an identifier,\nand `while await !x`. These look like upstream tree-sitter-swift issues\nrather than anything for this repo.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go test ./...` passes (10 packages). The race suite was not run:\n  `internal/sem` under `-race` exceeds its 30-minute timeout.\n- `gofmt -s`, `go vet ./...` and `scripts/gen-notices.sh --check` are clean.\n- graph-bench `-languages Swift` (full tier, `repos.lock.json` pins) before\n  and after: the per-repository parse-failure and symbol deltas agree with the\n  table above.\n- On a private macOS app (279 Swift files), after installing this build:\n  `entire brain doctor` goes from 140 partial failures to 9, and its\n  `semantic: degraded` warning goes away.\n\nGetting from roughly 10.9k to 10.0k Swift failures is the headline, but the\n`#if` regression is the thing to weigh before merging.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"10b26706-978c-4ec2-bd47-98cb27fc8267","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":268},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"07809a8d-f608-46df-9fad-272cfad844d1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
