{"parentUuid":"eb12188a-5727-4487-9271-59f27fab35af","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"98a7f3b5-94c6-4e5c-bf78-00b9da1cb37a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FGyb2VKntk6mX2obN81BFo","type":"tool_result","content":"[{\"n\":1,\"names\":[\"Entire Gates\"],\"state\":\"NEUTRAL\"},{\"n\":1,\"names\":[\"publish GitHub release\"],\"state\":\"SKIPPED\"},{\"n\":36,\"names\":[\"test (windows-latest)\",\"test (windows-latest) / coverage and integrity\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 0\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 1\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 2\",\"test (windows-latest) / non-heavy packages\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 3\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 4\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 5\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 6\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 7\",\"test (windows-latest) / vet\",\"build (linux/arm64)\",\"bench-memory-guards\",\"build (darwin/arm64)\",\"build (darwin/amd64)\",\"statusline (macos-latest)\",\"build (windows/amd64)\",\"test (macos-latest)\",\"build (linux/amd64)\",\"kit-reproducibility\",\"prompt-context-hook (macos-latest)\",\"build (windows/arm64)\",\"prompt-context-hook (ubuntu-latest)\",\"statusline (ubuntu-latest)\",\"locomo-summary-gate\",\"bm25-adapter\",\"test (windows-latest) / compile and plan\",\"test (ubuntu-latest)\",\"build (windows-latest)\",\"build (macos-latest)\",\"build (ubuntu-latest)\",\"notices\",\"lint\",\"locate-benchmark-guards\",\"boundary-gits\"],\"state\":\"SUCCESS\"}]\n=== timeline comments:\n--- ashtom 2026-11-04T17:00:45Z:\nPushed `d88b5559` to this branch with fixes from a review of `1c625cdf`. This was prepared by Claude Code for Thomas Dohmke and has not been reviewed by Rod. The PR description is unchanged and is now partly out of date; the notes below supersede it where they differ.\n\n**Parser fixes** (`compatibility.patch`, `scanner.c`, regenerated `parser.c`)\n- A comment no longer ends a statement before a leading `?`, `:`, `<`, `>`, `&`, `|` or `^`. `{` is exempt because a closure can start a statement.\n- `canImport` accepts string versions such as `_version: \"1.2.3\"`.\n- `#warning` and `#error` work before the first `case`.\n- `hasFeature`, `hasAttribute`, `_runtime` and the other predicate names stay usable as plain `-D` flags unless `(` follows.\n- `#elsewhere` and `#endifx` parse as macros, through an identifier-boundary check.\n\n**`grammar-refresh`**\n- New `local_changes` manifest field, set on Swift and F#. The tool refuses those entries unless `-allow-local-changes` is passed.\n- Notes now survive every refresh and are printed afterwards.\n- With the flag, F#'s `scanner.h` is still removed, as the note explains.\n\n**Other changes**\n- Removed `TestSwiftGrammarRefreshIsRevisioned` and `TestSwiftGrammarRecoveryIsRevisioned`, which could not fail.\n- `IdentityRevision` stays at 7, and its comment now covers these fixes.\n\n**Where the description is out of date**\n- The Swift grammar is not verbatim: it is upstream `82bb3a53` plus `compatibility.patch`, regenerated with tree-sitter-cli 0.24.7 `--\n--- rodbegbie 2026-11-04T22:02:31Z:\n@ashtom Thanks for taking this on!\r\n\r\nOne suggestion I might have for a follow-up PR would be to update the grammar-refresh command to apply the patch and call `tree-sitter generate` itself.\r\n\r\nNot only would it help simplify the manual work for cases with a local patch like this, but would also be useful if you were upgrading a grammar that now ships with an ABI 15 interface (e.g. https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust) and would need to be re-generated to work with the go-tree-sitter library.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"aa7ce5a8-f170-43c3-b9f9-69e7bfc95a58","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:05:48.381Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"[{\"n\":1,\"names\":[\"Entire Gates\"],\"state\":\"NEUTRAL\"},{\"n\":1,\"names\":[\"publish GitHub release\"],\"state\":\"SKIPPED\"},{\"n\":36,\"names\":[\"test (windows-latest)\",\"test (windows-latest) / coverage and integrity\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 0\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 1\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 2\",\"test (windows-latest) / non-heavy packages\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 3\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 4\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 5\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 6\",\"test (windows-latest) / shard 7\",\"test (windows-latest) / vet\",\"build (linux/arm64)\",\"bench-memory-guards\",\"build (darwin/arm64)\",\"build (darwin/amd64)\",\"statusline (macos-latest)\",\"build (windows/amd64)\",\"test (macos-latest)\",\"build (linux/amd64)\",\"kit-reproducibility\",\"prompt-context-hook (macos-latest)\",\"build (windows/arm64)\",\"prompt-context-hook (ubuntu-latest)\",\"statusline (ubuntu-latest)\",\"locomo-summary-gate\",\"bm25-adapter\",\"test (windows-latest) / compile and plan\",\"test (ubuntu-latest)\",\"build (windows-latest)\",\"build (macos-latest)\",\"build (ubuntu-latest)\",\"notices\",\"lint\",\"locate-benchmark-guards\",\"boundary-gits\"],\"state\":\"SUCCESS\"}]\n=== timeline comments:\n--- ashtom 2026-11-04T17:00:45Z:\nPushed `d88b5559` to this branch with fixes from a review of `1c625cdf`. This was prepared by Claude Code for Thomas Dohmke and has not been reviewed by Rod. The PR description is unchanged and is now partly out of date; the notes below supersede it where they differ.\n\n**Parser fixes** (`compatibility.patch`, `scanner.c`, regenerated `parser.c`)\n- A comment no longer ends a statement before a leading `?`, `:`, `<`, `>`, `&`, `|` or `^`. `{` is exempt because a closure can start a statement.\n- `canImport` accepts string versions such as `_version: \"1.2.3\"`.\n- `#warning` and `#error` work before the first `case`.\n- `hasFeature`, `hasAttribute`, `_runtime` and the other predicate names stay usable as plain `-D` flags unless `(` follows.\n- `#elsewhere` and `#endifx` parse as macros, through an identifier-boundary check.\n\n**`grammar-refresh`**\n- New `local_changes` manifest field, set on Swift and F#. The tool refuses those entries unless `-allow-local-changes` is passed.\n- Notes now survive every refresh and are printed afterwards.\n- With the flag, F#'s `scanner.h` is still removed, as the note explains.\n\n**Other changes**\n- Removed `TestSwiftGrammarRefreshIsRevisioned` and `TestSwiftGrammarRecoveryIsRevisioned`, which could not fail.\n- `IdentityRevision` stays at 7, and its comment now covers these fixes.\n\n**Where the description is out of date**\n- The Swift grammar is not verbatim: it is upstream `82bb3a53` plus `compatibility.patch`, regenerated with tree-sitter-cli 0.24.7 `--\n--- rodbegbie 2026-11-04T22:02:31Z:\n@ashtom Thanks for taking this on!\r\n\r\nOne suggestion I might have for a follow-up PR would be to update the grammar-refresh command to apply the patch and call `tree-sitter generate` itself.\r\n\r\nNot only would it help simplify the manual work for cases with a local patch like this, but would also be useful if you were upgrading a grammar that now ships with an ABI 15 interface (e.g. https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust) and would need to be re-generated to work with the go-tree-sitter library.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"10b26706-978c-4ec2-bd47-98cb27fc8267","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":268},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sandbox