{"parentUuid":"3965b61f-3415-4f42-8316-320f569986b3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"98a7f3b5-94c6-4e5c-bf78-00b9da1cb37a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R26uuYCKjrU4Ln7EfX3Fom","type":"tool_result","content":"Pushed `d88b5559` to this branch with fixes from a review of `1c625cdf`. This was prepared by Claude Code for Thomas Dohmke and has not been reviewed by Rod. The PR description is unchanged and is now partly out of date; the notes below supersede it where they differ.\n\n**Parser fixes** (`compatibility.patch`, `scanner.c`, regenerated `parser.c`)\n- A comment no longer ends a statement before a leading `?`, `:`, `<`, `>`, `&`, `|` or `^`. `{` is exempt because a closure can start a statement.\n- `canImport` accepts string versions such as `_version: \"1.2.3\"`.\n- `#warning` and `#error` work before the first `case`.\n- `hasFeature`, `hasAttribute`, `_runtime` and the other predicate names stay usable as plain `-D` flags unless `(` follows.\n- `#elsewhere` and `#endifx` parse as macros, through an identifier-boundary check.\n\n**`grammar-refresh`**\n- New `local_changes` manifest field, set on Swift and F#. The tool refuses those entries unless `-allow-local-changes` is passed.\n- Notes now survive every refresh and are printed afterwards.\n- With the flag, F#'s `scanner.h` is still removed, as the note explains.\n\n**Other changes**\n- Removed `TestSwiftGrammarRefreshIsRevisioned` and `TestSwiftGrammarRecoveryIsRevisioned`, which could not fail.\n- `IdentityRevision` stays at 7, and its comment now covers these fixes.\n\n**Where the description is out of date**\n- The Swift grammar is not verbatim: it is upstream `82bb3a53` plus `compatibility.patch`, regenerated with tree-sitter-cli 0.24.7 `--abi 14`.\n- `IdentityRevision` is 7, not 6.\n- Re-running `grammar-refresh` does not reproduce the committed Swift files, and now refuses by default. The steps in `internal/sem/grammars/swift/README.md` do reproduce them.\n- The regressions it lists and its results tables predate the last two commits. Use `internal/sem/grammars/swift/VALIDATION.md` for per-file numbers.\n\n**Verification**\n- `parser.c` and `scanner.c` regenerate byte for byte from the pinned commit plus the patch.\n- `go test -timeout 20m ./...`, race tests for `Swift|IdentityRevision`, `go vet ./...` and `scripts/gen-notices.sh --check` passed on the final grammar. Only comments and `VALIDATION.md` changed afterwards; the targeted Swift and `grammar-refresh` tests were rerun on the final commit, the rest were not.\n- Per-file audit on the ten `bench/repos.lock.json` Swift repositories, `1c625cdf` → this commit: no newly failing files and no symbols lost. Parse errors went from 132 to 132 on the nine application repositories and from 9,739 to 9,736 on `apple/swift`, where symbols went from 181,974 to 181,979.\n\n**Not re-measured on this parser**\n- The whole-repository symbol and relation totals in `VALIDATION.md`, which are marked as predating these fixes.\n- The Hummingbird comparison in `VALIDATION.md` (42 symbols, 113 relations). It is **not** marked in the document and was not rerun, so treat it as unconfirmed for this commit.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2d25806c-8a9b-482e-8d64-58aa33f163f1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:06:03.042Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Pushed `d88b5559` to this branch with fixes from a review of `1c625cdf`. This was prepared by Claude Code for Thomas Dohmke and has not been reviewed by Rod. The PR description is unchanged and is now partly out of date; the notes below supersede it where they differ.\n\n**Parser fixes** (`compatibility.patch`, `scanner.c`, regenerated `parser.c`)\n- A comment no longer ends a statement before a leading `?`, `:`, `<`, `>`, `&`, `|` or `^`. `{` is exempt because a closure can start a statement.\n- `canImport` accepts string versions such as `_version: \"1.2.3\"`.\n- `#warning` and `#error` work before the first `case`.\n- `hasFeature`, `hasAttribute`, `_runtime` and the other predicate names stay usable as plain `-D` flags unless `(` follows.\n- `#elsewhere` and `#endifx` parse as macros, through an identifier-boundary check.\n\n**`grammar-refresh`**\n- New `local_changes` manifest field, set on Swift and F#. The tool refuses those entries unless `-allow-local-changes` is passed.\n- Notes now survive every refresh and are printed afterwards.\n- With the flag, F#'s `scanner.h` is still removed, as the note explains.\n\n**Other changes**\n- Removed `TestSwiftGrammarRefreshIsRevisioned` and `TestSwiftGrammarRecoveryIsRevisioned`, which could not fail.\n- `IdentityRevision` stays at 7, and its comment now covers these fixes.\n\n**Where the description is out of date**\n- The Swift grammar is not verbatim: it is upstream `82bb3a53` plus `compatibility.patch`, regenerated with tree-sitter-cli 0.24.7 `--abi 14`.\n- `IdentityRevision` is 7, not 6.\n- Re-running `grammar-refresh` does not reproduce the committed Swift files, and now refuses by default. The steps in `internal/sem/grammars/swift/README.md` do reproduce them.\n- The regressions it lists and its results tables predate the last two commits. Use `internal/sem/grammars/swift/VALIDATION.md` for per-file numbers.\n\n**Verification**\n- `parser.c` and `scanner.c` regenerate byte for byte from the pinned commit plus the patch.\n- `go test -timeout 20m ./...`, race tests for `Swift|IdentityRevision`, `go vet ./...` and `scripts/gen-notices.sh --check` passed on the final grammar. Only comments and `VALIDATION.md` changed afterwards; the targeted Swift and `grammar-refresh` tests were rerun on the final commit, the rest were not.\n- Per-file audit on the ten `bench/repos.lock.json` Swift repositories, `1c625cdf` → this commit: no newly failing files and no symbols lost. Parse errors went from 132 to 132 on the nine application repositories and from 9,739 to 9,736 on `apple/swift`, where symbols went from 181,974 to 181,979.\n\n**Not re-measured on this parser**\n- The whole-repository symbol and relation totals in `VALIDATION.md`, which are marked as predating these fixes.\n- The Hummingbird comparison in `VALIDATION.md` (42 symbols, 113 relations). It is **not** marked in the document and was not rerun, so treat it as unconfirmed for this commit.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c4eddb9c-93a2-4141-bb80-cabda324142e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":268},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3965b61f-3415-4f42-8316-320f569986b3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
