/... -count=1 -v`\n   - `go test ./internal/gitutil -run 'LazyFetch' -count=1`\n   - `go test ./internal/sem -run 'Fixture|Golden' -count=1`\n5. Then the two packages the diff actually touches, in full, one at a time: `./internal/sem` then `./cmd/grammar-refresh`. If internal/sem exceeds 30 min, say so and report which tests had run.\n6. VERIFY-BY-WEAKENING on the NEW test files `internal/sem/swift_grammar_regression_test.go` and `internal/sem/swift_test.go` and `cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh_test.go`: pick the 6 most load-bearing assertions across them, and for EACH one prove it can fail. Do that by temporarily editing the NON-test code or the test's expected value in your own scratch COPY of the repo (copy the worktree to your scratchpad with `cp -R` and mutate the copy — NEVER mutate /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-357-review), re-running that test, and confirming it goes RED. A test that stays green under a mutation that should break it is a finding — report it with the exact mutation. Known trap: `[build failed]` greps as a pass/fail confusion — grep for `--- FAIL` and check the build actually succeeded.\n7. Report the compiled binary size delta: build `./cmd/entire-graph` (or whatever the main binary is — find it) at HEAD and at origin/main (use `git worktree add` of your own under your scratchpad for main, or `git stash`-free approach: create a second worktree from /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph with `git worktree add --detach <scratchpad>/main-357 origin/main`) and report both `ls -l` sizes.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. No prose padding. Use `rtk` in place of raw git/grep/ls where it works (rtk is a token-saving CLI proxy; `rtk read <file>`, `rtk git status`). Report as:\n- a table of check -> PASS/FAIL -> evidence (1 line)\n- then a numbered list of FINDINGS only (defects, unfailable tests, surprises). Each finding: file:line, what is wrong, the exact command/mutation that proves it.\n- then \"NO OTHER FINDINGS\" if that's the case.\nDo not summarize the PR back to me. I have read it."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2011,"cache_read_input_tokens":185801,"output_tokens":7133,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1457},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2011,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7133,"cache_read_input_tokens":185801,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2011},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01THAAoNwQoPrMZ2rm7KP8i1":{"description":"Build and test PR 357","model":"opus","prompt":"You are verifying entireio/entire-graph PR #357 (vendors tree-sitter-swift 0.7.4 + a compatibility patch, bumps IdentityRevision 5->7, removes 3 Swift source-masking hacks, adds a `cmd/grammar-refresh` tool).\n\nWORKTREE (already created, detached HEAD at the PR head d88b5559, base main = 28382d8e):\n  /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-357-review\nDo NOT create commits, do NOT push, do NOT edit source files. Read-only verification only. You may write scratch output under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5/scratchpad/357-tests/ (mkdir it).\n\nMACHINE CONSTRAINTS (important, violating these invalidates results and annoys the user):\n- load average is ~7 and two `entire-brain` daemons are each burning ~100% CPU. Do NOT run the full repo test suite in parallel.\n- Use `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test -p 1 -parallel 1 -timeout 30m ...` for Go tests. Never use `-race` on internal/sem (it exceeds 30 min).\n- `tree-sitter` CLI is NOT installed. Don't try to regenerate the grammar; anoth