tchpad with `cp -R` and mutate the copy — NEVER mutate /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-357-review), re-running that test, and confirming it goes RED. A test that stays green under a mutation that should break it is a finding — report it with the exact mutation. Known trap: `[build failed]` greps as a pass/fail confusion — grep for `--- FAIL` and check the build actually succeeded.\n7. Report the compiled binary size delta: build `./cmd/entire-graph` (or whatever the main binary is — find it) at HEAD and at origin/main (use `git worktree add` of your own under your scratchpad for main, or `git stash`-free approach: create a second worktree from /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph with `git worktree add --detach <scratchpad>/main-357 origin/main`) and report both `ls -l` sizes.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. No prose padding. Use `rtk` in place of raw git/grep/ls where it works (rtk is a token-saving CLI proxy; `rtk read <file>`, `rtk git status`). Report as:\n- a table of check -> PASS/FAIL -> evidence (1 line)\n- then a numbered list of FINDINGS only (defects, unfailable tests, surprises). Each finding: file:line, what is wrong, the exact command/mutation that proves it.\n- then \"NO OTHER FINDINGS\" if that's the case.\nDo not summarize the PR back to me. I have read it.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d/tasks/a0df3e9f04e5a2ea0.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"85625144-a52b-4639-a2d0-c09bc5cdaf1e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":268},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/deven