w\nREAD-ONLY. Do not edit, commit, or push anything. Scratch files go in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5/scratchpad/357-review/ (mkdir it).\n\nWHAT THE PR DOES: vendors tree-sitter-swift 0.7.4 (upstream commit 82bb3a533e0801fd2bbaa11dc49676e10bf41948) under internal/sem/grammars/swift, NOT verbatim — it is upstream plus `compatibility.patch`, regenerated with tree-sitter-cli 0.24.7 --abi 14. It bumps `IdentityRevision` 5 -> 7 in internal/sem/provider.go, deletes three Swift source-masking hacks from internal/sem/parser.go, and adds `cmd/grammar-refresh` plus a manifest `internal/sem/grammars/grammars.json` describing all 12 vendored grammars.\n\nREVIEW THESE FILES (skip internal/sem/grammars/swift/parser.c — 730k generated lines, do not read it; you may grep it for specific symbols):\n  cmd/grammar-refresh/main.go\n  cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh.go\n  cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh_test.go\n  internal/sem/grammars/swift/compatibility.patch\n  internal/sem/grammars/swift/scanner.c\n  internal/sem/grammars/swift/binding.go\n  internal/sem/grammars/swift/README.md\n  internal/sem/grammars/swift/VALIDATION.md\n  internal/sem/grammars/grammars.json\n  internal/sem/parser.go   (use `git diff origin/main..HEAD -- internal/sem/parser.go`)\n  internal/sem/provider.go (same)\n  internal/sem/swift_grammar_regression_test.go\n  internal/sem/swift_test.go\n  internal/gitutil/lazy_fetch_guard_test.go (one added allowlist entry)\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, CHANGELOG.md\n\nSPECIFIC THINGS TO SETTLE (answer each explicitly, yes/no + evidence):\n1. DEAD CODE: the diff deletes `maskSwiftEmptyAttributeCalls` and `maskSwiftOptionalBindingShorthand` and moves `maskSwiftPropertyWrapperPrefix`. Is every remaining mask function and every remaining regexp var in that `var (...)` block still REACHED from a caller? Grep for each name. Any function or pattern that is now unreferenced is a finding. Also: are the deleted masks' tests also gone, and did any surviving test still assert the deleted behaviour?\n2. The PR author's own comment says two tests were REMOVED because they \"could not fail\": `TestSwiftGrammarRefreshIsRevisioned` and `TestSwiftGrammarRecoveryIsRevisioned`. Find them in `git show 1c625cdf` / the diff history. Was the coverage they claimed to provide replaced by something that CAN fail, or silently lost? Specifically: is there now ANY test that would fail if someone changed the vendored Swift parser.c without bumping IdentityRevision? If not, say so plainly — that is the exact class of bug that this repo has been burned by before.\n3. `cmd/grammar-refresh`: it shells out to `git` to fetch an upstream grammar into a scratch repo. Audit for: unvalidated path joins / directory traversal when writing files named in the manifest (a manifest `files` entry like `../../x` or an absolute path), command injection through `-ref`/`-url`/`-lang` flags, scratch-dir cleanup on error paths, whether it can silently write a partial grammar, whether `-allow-local-changes` correctly gates ONLY the entries whose manifest has `local_changes`, and whether the ABI 13-14 refusal can be bypassed. Does it verify the fetched commit matches the manifest `revision`?\n4. MANIFEST ACCURACY: `grammars.json` claims a url/reference/revision/files/abi for all 12 grammars. Cross-check each entry's `files` list against what is actually committed under `internal/sem/grammars/<lang>/` (`ls`). Any entry whose `files` list disagrees with the directory contents is a finding, because the refresh tool will then add or drop files.\n5. `internal/gitutil/lazy_fetch_guard_test.go` gained ONE allowlist entry for `cmd/grammar-refresh/main.go:`. Read the guard to see what the allowlist actually suppresses and whether the key format (trailing colon, path prefix) matches how the guard builds its keys — a mis-keyed entry would silently suppress nothing (or everything). Does `refresh.go` also launch git? If it does and only `main.go` is allowlisted, the guard either fails or the suppression is in the wrong place.\n6. `compatibility.patch` / `scanner.c`: the scanner \"looks through block comments when deciding whether a newline separates statements\". Read the comment-skipping code in scanner.c. Can it run off the end of input, loop forever on an unterminated `/*`, or mis-handle nested `/* /* */`? Swift block comments DO nest. State a concrete input if you find one.\n7. `IdentityRevision` goes 5 -> 7 in a single PR, with both revision 6 and revision 7 documented in the comment block. Is the constant, the `identity_revision_test.go` expectation, and the two cache-version constants (`providerRecordsCacheVersion`, `searchSnapshotCacheVersion`) mutually consistent? The test asserts the cache versions end in \"-\"+IdentityRevision. Confirm.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. No preamble, no PR summary. Use `rtk` where it works (`rtk read <file>`, `rtk git ...`) to save tokens. Structure:\n- \"SETTLED:\" one line per numbered question above, each starting YES/NO/PARTIAL.\n- \"FINDINGS:\" numbered, severity HIGH/MED/LOW, each exactly: file:line | defect in one sentence | concrete failure scenario (inputs -> wrong result) | how you verified.\n- \"REFUTED:\" anything you suspected and then killed, one line each, so I know it was checked.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d/tasks/a2a219cb3afbbd0da.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"85625144-a52b-4639-a2d0-c09bc5cdaf1e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":268},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/dev