orktree), untouched by #357, so it is not a regression — but if the branch's gate runs `gofmt -l`, it is red for an unrelated reason. Proof: `cd <base worktree> && gofmt -l .` prints the same single path.\n  \n  2. **Unfailable assertion: `cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh_test.go:110-113`** (\"destination changed on refusal\") only guards the *copy* path, not the *destructive stale-removal* path, so half of the contract stated at `refresh.go:45-50` (\"Nothing in destDir changes unless the grammar has a parser.c the go-tree-sitter runtime can load\") is untested. Mutation that stays GREEN: move the `if abi < minABI || abi > maxABI { return ... }` block from `refresh.go:61-63` to immediately before `files := make([]string, 0, len(sources))` (line 99) — i.e. after the `for _, rel := range stale { os.Remove(...) }` loop — then `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./cmd/grammar-refresh -run TestVendorRefusesABI15 -count=1` → `ok ... 0.291s`. It stays green because the test seeds dest with only `parser.c`, which the ABI-15 grammar also provides, so nothing is ever classified stale. Demonstrator proving the destination really is mutated under that same mutation (added as `cmd/grammar-refresh/gap_demo_test.go` in the scratch copy, then removed): seed dest with `parser.c` **and** `scanner.c`, call `vendor(grammarSource(t,\"15\",false), \"\", dest)`, assert `scanner.c` survives → `GAP: scanner.c deleted even though vendor refused the grammar`. Fix: in `TestVendorRefusesABI15` also write a `scanner.c` (or `unicode.h`) into dest and assert it still exists after the refusal. Not a defect at HEAD — the check is correctly ordered there — purely a missing guard.\n  \n  3. **Conditional-compilation directives leak into emitted Swift signatures.** `internal/sem/swift_grammar_regression_test.go:427` asserts only `strings.Contains(advance.Signature, \"@available\")`, and the actual value is `Signature:\"@available(*, deprecated) #endif mutating func advance()\"` — a stray `#endif` in a user-visible symbol signature. Proof: apply M5 above and read the dumped record (`swift_grammar_regression_test.go:428: ... Signature:@available(*, deprecated) #endif mutating func advance() ...`). This is new behavior from this PR's conditional-attribute support and will show up in `graph def` / `--format agent` output for any Swift declaration preceded by an `#if … @attr … #endif` block. Low severity (cosmetic/quality), but the test as written will never notice it.\n  \n  4. **`findLicense` silently keeps only one license file.** `cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh.go:123-135` returns the first `os.ReadDir` entry whose upper-cased name starts with `LICENSE` or `COPYING` and ignores the rest, and `vendor` writes exactly one `sources[\"LICENSE\"]`. A dual-licensed upstream (`LICENSE-APACHE` + `LICENSE-MIT`, common for Rust-adjacent grammars) would be under-attributed in NOTICES with no warning, and `gen-notices.sh --check` cannot catch it because it only looks for files literally named `LICENSE` (`scripts/gen-notices.sh:127`). Not triggered by swift (single `LICENSE`, 1.0K). No test covers multi-license sources. Low.\n  \n  5. **Residual risk the Go suite cannot cover: a verbatim refresh that drops `compatibility.patch`.** Under M2 (grammar reverted to 0.5.0) only 5 of 19 `TestSwiftGrammarRegressionSyntax` subtests go red — `consume_switch_with_later_declarations`, `copy_and_contextual_identifiers`, `conditional_macros_and_literal_lookalikes`, `comments_before_leading_operators`, `closures_after_comments`; the other 14 pass on both grammars. That is expected for preservation cases, but it means the suite's discriminating power against *unpatched 0.7.4* (the realistic regression, since `grammar-refresh` copies upstream verbatim and `grammars.json` marks swift `local_changes: true`) is untested here. `VALIDATION.md`'s load-bearing claims — \"All 296 upstream grammar corpus tests … pass\" and \"generating with tree-sitter-cli 0.24.7 reproduces `parser.c` and `scanner.c` byte for byte\" — are **unverifiable on this machine** (no `tree-sitter` CLI, 0.24.7 not installed). Flagging as a review note, not a defect.\n  \n  6. **The snapshot header does not record which grammar produced Swift.** At HEAD the header still emits `\"language_versions\":{\"go-tree-sitter\":\"github.com/smacker/go-tree-sitter\"}` — identical to main — so no consumer (or cache debugger) can tell Swift records came from a vendored 0.7.4 + `compatibility.patch` rather than go-tree-sitter's bundled 0.5.0. `IdentityRevision` 7 is the only signal. Evidence: `<scratch>/bin/entire-graph-head symbols --repo . --format ndjson` header line. Low observability gap.\n  \n  7. Nit: `cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh.go:159` — the first switch case `name == \"parser.c\" || name == \"scanner.c\"` omits the `!e.IsDir()` guard that the two adjacent cases carry, so a directory so named would be queued for `os.Remove` and fail the whole vendor.\n  \n  POSITIVE EVIDENCE WORTH RELAYING (not findings)\n  - Golden drift is zero: 29 changed golden files, and `grep -E \"^[+-]\" goldens.diff | grep -vE \"^(\\+\\+\\+|---)\" | grep -v identity_revision | wc -l` = **0**. Every changed line is the header's `identity_revision` 5→7. That includes `multilang-relations`, whose fixture contains a real Swift file (`internal/sem/testdata/fixtures/multilang-relations/Ledger.swift`) — so the grammar swap produced byte-identical Swift records for it.\n  - End-to-end smoke on a swift-testing file (`@Test`, `#require`, `#expect`): HEAD binary → `identity_revision:\"7\"`, 3 symbols, 6 relations, `partial_failures:[]`, `completeness_level:\"ok\"`, health `status:\"ok\"`. Main binary → `identity_revision:\"5\"`, same 3 symbols but `E_PARSE_ERROR … near \"#require\" … near \"#expect\"`, `completeness_level:\"unsafe\"`, `flagged_percentage:100`. Real user-visible fix.\n  - Manifest is self-consistent: `grammars.json` swift entry is ABI 14, revision `82bb3a533e…`, `local_changes: true`, note names `swift/compatibility.patch` + tree-sitter-cli 0.24.7, and its 6 `files` exactly match the 6 managed files on disk (`LICENSE`, `parser.c`, `scanner.c`, `tree_sitter/{alloc,array,parser}.h`).\n  - Artifacts kept: `<scratch>/357-tests/bin/entire-graph-{head,main}`, per-check logs (`build.log`, `vet.log`, `notices.log`, `t-*.log`, `full-sem.log`, `goldens.diff`). The temporary base worktree at `<scratch>/357-tests/main-357` was `git worktree remove`d; `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph` worktree list is back to its prior 78 entries.\n  \n  NO OTHER FINDINGS.","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"PR #357 verification — entireio/entire-graph, head d88b5559, base 28382d8e. Review worktree left CLEAN (`git status --porcelain` = 0 lines, HEAD d88b5559). All mutations done in `rsync` copy at `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5/scratchpad/357-tests/mut`.\n\n| # | check | verdict | evidence (1 line) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `GOMAXPROCS=1 go build ./...` | PASS | exit 0. 29s first run in this worktree, 3s warm. Isolated cold cgo: `GOCACHE=<scratch>/cold-cache go build ./internal/sem/grammars/swift` = **8s**, producing a 15 MB object from 730,384-line parser.c. cgo is NOT the bottleneck. |\n| 2a | `gofmt -l .` | **FAIL (pre-existing)** | prints `internal/sem/groovy_test.go`; identical output in a base worktree at 28382d8e. Not touched by #357. |\n| 2b | `go vet ./...` | PASS | exit 0, 39s. Only output: pre-existing cgo `-Wnull-character` warning from `github.com/smacker/go-tree-sitter/lua`. |\n| 3 | `bash scripts/gen-notices.sh --check` | PASS | `NOTICES is up to date` (1s). NOTICES:542 attributes `internal/sem/grammars/swift`; `internal/sem/grammars/swift/LICENSE` + NOTICES both in the diff. |\n| 4a | `go test ./internal/sem -run Swift -count=1 -v` | PASS | 22 top-level / 48 incl. subtests, 0 FAIL, 19s. Names below. |\n| 4b | `-run IdentityRevision` | PASS | `TestParserIdentityRevisionsSnapshotAndCaches` PASS, 2s. |\n| 4c | `go test ./cmd/grammar-refresh/... -v` | PASS | 17 top-level / 21 incl. subtests, 0 FAIL, 0.478s. |\n| 4d | `go test ./internal/gitutil -run LazyFetch` | PASS | 6 tests PASS (`...ProbesTheGitOnPath`, `...InTheRepositoryDirectory`, `...LogicalPathNotTheSymlinkTarget`, `...CachesAFailedProbe`, `...MatchesObservedGitBehaviour`, `TestParseLazyFetchGuardStatus`), 3s. |\n| 4e | `-run 'Fixture\\|Golden'` | PASS | 51 PASS, 0 FAIL, 4s. |\n| 5a | full `./internal/sem` | PASS | `ok github.com/entireio/entire-graph/internal/sem 274.988s`, wall 277s. Did NOT exceed 30m. |\n| 5b | full `./cmd/grammar-refresh` | PASS | `ok ... 0.478s`, all tests. |\n| 6 | verify-by-weakening, 8 mutations / 7 assertions | 7 RED, **1 GREEN = finding 2** | detail below. |\n| 7 | binary size `./cmd/entire-graph` | n/a | main 96,356,226 B → head 97,941,474 B = **+1,585,248 B (+1.51 MiB, +1.65%)**. `go tool nm`: head links `internal/sem/grammars/swift` (2 syms) and **0** `smacker/go-tree-sitter/swift`; main is the exact inverse — clean swap, old grammar not double-linked. |\n\n4a test names (all PASS): TreeSitterParserSwiftMasksModernSyntax, TreeSitterParserSwiftExtensionMembersScopeToExtendedType, BuildProviderSnapshotResolvesSwiftExtensionAndImplicitSelfCalls, BuildProviderSnapshotResolvesSwiftExistentialDelegateAndLabelCalls, SwiftProtocolDeclarationsEmitted, SwiftGrammarRegressionSyntax (19 subtests), SwiftGrammarRegressionKeepsRelations, SwiftGrammarStillReportsMalformedSource, SwiftGrammarConditionalExtensionIsNotAType, SwiftReceiverTypedCallIdioms, SwiftParameterVarTypes, SwiftLocalVarTypes, SwiftFileTypeInfo, SwiftReceiverCallsOperators, SwiftPropertyChainReceiverCalls, SwiftChainedReceiverCalls, SwiftTestingMacrosParse, SwiftLeadingOperatorContinuationParses, SwiftAttributeBeforeEmptyFunctionTypeParses, REDACTED, ObjectiveCPlusPlusSwiftExposureCandidates, SwiftDeclarationVisibleToObjectiveC.\n\nWEAKENING RESULTS (`--- FAIL` grepped, build success confirmed each time — no `[build failed]`):\n- M1 `provider.go:80` `IdentityRevision \"7\"→\"5\"` → **RED**: `identity_revision_test.go:11: identity=\"5\"`; same mutation also reds all 29 `TestProviderGoldenSnapshots/*`.\n- M2 `parser.go:24` import swapped to `swift \"github.com/smacker/go-tree-sitter/swift\"` → **RED**, 9 failures: `SwiftTestingMacrosParse` (`swift_test.go:695` ParseError:true), `SwiftGrammarRegressionKeepsRelations` (`:413` E_PARSE_ERROR), `SwiftGrammarConditionalExtensionIsNotAType` (`:484`), + 5 `SwiftGrammarRegressionSyntax` subtests.\n- M3 re-added `maskSwiftEmptyAttributeCalls` (the removed `@Name()`→`@Name  ` hack) into `maskSwiftUnsupportedSyntax` → **RED**: `swift_test.go:739 ... Code:\"E_PARSE_ERROR\"`.\n- M4 re-added the removed `swiftLeadingOperatorContinuationLinePattern` masking block → **RED**: `swift_test.go:723 ... Detail:\"...missing ) at line 3 column 42 near \\\"#expect(resolve([\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\"], in: paths)\\\"\"` — exactly the failure the test's comment predicts.\n- M5 `swift_grammar_regression_test.go:427` expected `StartLine != 5` → `!= 4` → **RED** at `:428`.\n- M6 fixture mutation: removed `self.after()` and `self.state = .closed` from `KeepsRelations` source → **RED**, reports `missing CALLS:Machine.advance->Machine.after` and `missing WRITES_FIELD:Machine.advance->Machine.state`.\n- M7 `swift_grammar_regression_test.go:450` `\"struct Broken { func missing( }\"` → `\"struct Broken { func missing() {} }\"` → **RED**: `:457: malformed Swift silently accepted`.\n- M8a `refresh.go:86` `sources[\"LICENSE\"] = license` → `sources[filepath.Base(license)] = license` → **RED**: `refresh_test.go:197: files = [COPYING.txt parser.c]`.\n- M8b `refresh.go:17` `maxABI = 14 → 15` → **RED**: `refresh_test.go:103: want error for ABI 15` (t.Fatal, so the `:111` clause never runs).\n- M8c (see finding 2) `refresh.go:61-63` ABI-range check moved to just before `files := make(...)` (after the stale-removal loop) → **GREEN** `ok ... 0.291s`. Same check moved after the copy loop → RED at `:112`.\n\nFINDINGS\n\n1. **`gofmt -l .` is not clean — `internal/sem/groovy_test.go`** (alignment of a `map[string]string` literal around lines 85-115). Pre-existing on `origin/main` 28382d8e (verified in a separate base worktree), untouched by #357, so it is not a regression — but if the branch's gate runs `gofmt -l`, it is red for an unrelated reason. Proof: `cd <base worktree> && gofmt -l .` prints the same single path.\n\n2. **Unfailable assertion: `cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh_test.go:110-113`** (\"destination changed on refusal\") only guards the *copy* path, not the *destructive stale-removal* path, so half of the contract stated at `refresh.go:45-50` (\"Nothing in destDir changes unless the grammar has a parser.c the go-tree-sitter runtime can load\") is untested. Mutation that stays GREEN: move the `if abi < minABI || abi > maxABI { return ... }` block from `refresh.go:61-63` to immediately before `files := make([]string, 0, len(sources))` (line 99) — i.e. after the `for _, rel := range stale { os.Remove(...) }` loop — then `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./cmd/grammar-refresh -run TestVendorRefusesABI15 -count=1` → `ok ... 0.291s`. It stays green because the test seeds dest with only `parser.c`, which the ABI-15 grammar also provides, so nothing is ever classified stale. Demonstrator proving the destination really is mutated under that same mutation (added as `cmd/grammar-refresh/gap_demo_test.go` in the scratch copy, then removed): seed dest with `parser.c` **and** `scanner.c`, call `vendor(grammarSource(t,\"15\",false), \"\", dest)`, assert `scanner.c` survives → `GAP: scanner.c deleted even though vendor refused the grammar`. Fix: in `TestVendorRefusesABI15` also write a `scanner.c` (or `unicode.h`) into dest and assert it still exists after the refusal. Not a defect at HEAD — the check is correctly ordered there — purely a missing guard.\n\n3. **Conditional-compilation directives leak into emitted Swift signatures.** `internal/sem/swift_grammar_regression_test.go:427` asserts only `strings.Contains(advance.Signature, \"@available\")`, and the actual value is `Signature:\"@available(*, deprecated) #endif mutating func advance()\"` — a stray `#endif` in a user-visible symbol signature. Proof: apply M5 above and read the dumped record (`swift_grammar_regression_test.go:428: ... Signature:@available(*, deprecated) #endif mutating func advance() ...`). This is new behavior from this PR's conditional-attribute support and will show up in `graph def` / `--format agent` output for any Swift declaration preceded by an `#if … @attr … #endif` block. Low severity (cosmetic/quality), but the test as written will never notice it.\n\n4. **`findLicense` silently keeps only one license file.** `cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh.go:123-135` returns the first `os.ReadDir` entry whose upper-cased name starts with `LICENSE` or `COPYING` and ignores the rest, and `vendor` writes exactly one `sources[\"LICENSE\"]`. A dual-licensed upstream (`LICENSE-APACHE` + `LICENSE-MIT`, common for Rust-adjacent grammars) would be under-attributed in NOTICES with no warning, and `gen-notices.sh --check` cannot catch it because it only looks for files literally named `LICENSE` (`scripts/gen-notices.sh:127`). Not triggered by swift (single `LICENSE`, 1.0K). No test covers multi-license sources. Low.\n\n5. **Residual risk the Go suite cannot cover: a verbatim refresh that drops `compatibility.patch`.** Under M2 (grammar reverted to 0.5.0) only 5 of 19 `TestSwiftGrammarRegressionSyntax` subtests go red — `consume_switch_with_later_declarations`, `copy_and_contextual_identifiers`, `conditional_macros_and_literal_lookalikes`, `comments_before_leading_operators`, `closures_after_comments`; the other 14 pass on both grammars. That is expected for preservation cases, but it means the suite's discriminating power against *unpatched 0.7.4* (the realistic regression, since `grammar-refresh` copies upstream verbatim and `grammars.json` marks swift `local_changes: true`) is untested here. `VALIDATION.md`'s load-bearing claims — \"All 296 upstream grammar corpus tests … pass\" and \"generating with tree-sitter-cli 0.24.7 reproduces `parser.c` and `scanner.c` byte for byte\" — are **unverifiable on this machine** (no `tree-sitter` CLI, 0.24.7 not installed). Flagging as a review note, not a defect.\n\n6. **The snapshot header does not record which grammar produced Swift.** At HEAD the header still emits `\"language_versions\":{\"go-tree-sitter\":\"github.com/smacker/go-tree-sitter\"}` — identical to main — so no consumer (or cache debugger) can tell Swift records came from a vendored 0.7.4 + `compatibility.patch` rather than go-tree-sitter's bundled 0.5.0. `IdentityRevision` 7 is the only signal. Evidence: `<scratch>/bin/entire-graph-head symbols --repo . --format ndjson` header line. Low observability gap.\n\n7. Nit: `cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh.go:159` — the first switch case `name == \"parser.c\" || name == \"scanner.c\"` omits the `!e.IsDir()` guard that the two adjacent cases carry, so a directory so named would be queued for `os.Remove` and fail the whole vendor.\n\nPOSITIVE EVIDENCE WORTH RELAYING (not findings)\n- Golden drift is zero: 29 changed golden files, and `grep -E \"^[+-]\" goldens.diff | grep -vE \"^(\\+\\+\\+|---)\" | grep -v identity_revision | wc -l` = **0**. Every changed line is the header's `identity_revision` 5→7. That includes `multilang-relations`, whose fixture contains a real Swift file (`internal/sem/testdata/fixtures/multilang-relations/Ledger.swift`) — so the grammar swap produced byte-identical Swift records for it.\n- End-to-end smoke on a swift-testing file (`@Test`, `#require`, `#expect`): HEAD binary → `identity_revision:\"7\"`, 3 symbols, 6 relations, `partial_failures:[]`, `completeness_level:\"ok\"`, health `status:\"ok\"`. Main binary → `identity_revision:\"5\"`, same 3 symbols but `E_PARSE_ERROR … near \"#require\" … near \"#expect\"`, `completeness_level:\"unsafe\"`, `flagged_percentage:100`. Real user-visible fix.\n- Manifest is self-consistent: `grammars.json` swift entry is ABI 14, revision `82bb3a533e…`, `local_changes: true`, note names `swift/compatibility.patch` + tree-sitter-cli 0.24.7, and its 6 `files` exactly match the 6 managed files on disk (`LICENSE`, `parser.c`, `scanner.c`, `tree_sitter/{alloc,array,parser}.h`).\n- Artifacts kept: `<scratch>/357-tests/bin/entire-graph-{head,main}`, per-check logs (`build.log`, `vet.log`, `notices.log`, `t-*.log`, `full-sem.log`, `goldens.diff`). The temporary base worktree at `<scratch>/357-tests/main-357` was `git worktree remove`d; `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph` worktree list is back to its prior 78 entries.\n\nNO OTHER FINDINGS."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
