uct A/B/C` + methods all extracted). The patch does not touch the EOF or nesting path — only the `!semi_is_valid` look-through and the post-comment NON_CONSUMING check. Token wiring is consistent: scanner enum = 35, `TOKEN_COUNT 35`, `EXTERNAL_TOKEN_COUNT 35`, `sym__directive_endif_as_semi = 231` immediately after `sym__fake_try_bang = 230`, matching the grammar.js externals order.\n  7. REVISION/CACHE CONSISTENCY — YES. `IdentityRevision = \"7\"` (provider.go:80); test asserts `\"7\"` (identity_revision_test.go:10); `searchSnapshotCacheVersion = \"search-snapshot-v29-\" + IdentityRevision` (search_cache.go:59) → `…-v29-7`; `providerRecordsCacheVersion = \"provider-records-v24-\" + IdentityRevision` (records_cache.go:54) → `…-v24-7`. Both HasSuffix `-7`. `declaration_name_line_test.go:117` floor (v>=18) satisfied. Revision 6 was never released, so no orphaned \"6\" cache namespace; documenting both 6 and 7 is harmless. Caveat: the HasSuffix assertion is unfalsifiable by construction (both constants are built by concatenating the value being compared) — pre-existing, not PR-introduced.\n  \n  FINDINGS:\n  1. MED | cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh.go:196 (`sort.Search` in `upsert`), with cmd/grammar-refresh/main.go:69-73 | `upsert` binary-searches a manifest it assumes is sorted, but `loadManifest` never sorts and `saveManifest` never sorts, so one out-of-order entry makes it INSERT a duplicate instead of replacing — and main.go's last-match-wins `existing` lookup then reads the duplicate, silently dropping that grammar's `local_changes` guard and `note`. | A maintainer hand-appends a new grammar to the END of grammars.json (the natural edit: `… , {\"language\":\"kotlin\", …}]`). Next `go run ./cmd/grammar-refresh -lang zig -ref v1.1.3` writes a manifest with TWO `zig` entries (`[… swift zig kotlin zig]`); the trailing one has `local_changes:false`, empty `url` and empty `note`. A later `-lang zig` refresh therefore no longer refuses without `-allow-local-changes`, overwri