{"parentUuid":"c34a6f93-4ba5-4211-9728-2416a08db3e9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14826964 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"272c4442-4659-4f9e-9130-5da1488528ed","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:40:40.112Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14826964 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"272c4442-4659-4f9e-9130-5da1488528ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgimihBVG3bY4V8wiRjxr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019w6HVF4rNSjnS3D8QmsL6f","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-357-review && git add cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh.go cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh_test.go && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(grammar-refresh): one entry per language, and never delete before writing\n\nupsert binary-searched a manifest that nothing sorts or validates. Appending a\ngrammar to the end of grammars.json — the natural hand edit — leaves it\nunsorted, and the search then misses a language that is present and inserts a\nsecond entry for it. Measured over every single-entry insertion: all twelve\nlanguages can be duplicated that way. Scan linearly, sort unconditionally, and\nrefuse a manifest that already lists a language twice, because every lookup\nhere resolves a language to exactly one origin.\n\nvendor also removed the files a new grammar lacks before writing the ones it\nhas, so a failure part way through left the directory without a header the\nnewly written parser.c still included: a grammar that no longer compiles,\ndescribed by a manifest that still named the old file set. Write first, then\nsweep, so a failure leaves a superset instead of a hole.\n\nEach guard is mutation-proven: restoring the binary search, dropping the\nduplicate check, moving the ABI gate below the sweep, and restoring the old\ndelete-first order each turn a test red.\nEOF\ngit add internal/sem/vendored_grammars_test.go internal/sem/swift_grammar_regression_test.go internal/sem/grammars/swift/VALIDATION.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ntest(sem): tie the vendored grammar bytes to the identity revision\n\nNothing connected a vendored grammar's contents to IdentityRevision. The\nsnapshot caches are keyed on the indexed repository's git tree, which a parser\nchange does not touch, so the revision is the whole invalidation mechanism —\nand a refresh that changed parse results could land with a stale revision and\nevery test would stay green. The two tests that claimed this ground compared\nIdentityRevision against its previous value, which cannot fail while\nTestParserIdentityRevisionsSnapshotAndCaches pins it exactly; they were\nremoved, correctly, and nothing replaced them.\n\nPin a digest of all 62 managed grammar files instead, with a failure message\nthat says to weigh parse results, bump the revision, then update the digest.\nAlso check grammars.json against the directories it describes: the manifest\ndrives what a refresh adds and deletes, and nothing asserted that its file\nlists and ABI fields match what is committed.\n\nSwift's regression cases reached none of the block-comment path\ncompatibility.patch changed, so add an unterminated comment to the\nmalformed-source set and a nested/multi-line case that must keep the\ndeclarations after it.\n\nVALIDATION.md stated the Hummingbird symbol and relation counts as current;\nthey come from the same run as the whole-repository totals, before the last\nscanner and grammar fixes. Mark them, as those totals already are.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -3 && echo \"=== status:\" && git status --porcelain | head","description":"Commit the two fix sets"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":810,"cache_read_input_tokens":302048,"output_tokens":1099,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":810,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1099,"cache_read_input_tokens":302048,"cache_creation_input_tokens":810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":810},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019w6HVF4rNSjnS3D8QmsL6f":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-357-review && git add cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh.go cmd/grammar-refresh/refresh_test.go && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(grammar-refresh): one entry per language, and never delete before writing\n\nupsert binary-searched a manifest that nothing sorts or validates. Appending a\ngrammar to the end of grammars.json — the natural hand edit — leaves it\nunsorted, and the search then misses a language that is present and inserts a\nsecond entry for it. Measured over every single-entry insertion: all twelve\nlanguages can be duplicated that way. Scan linearly, sort unconditionally, and\nrefuse a manifest that already lists a language twice, because every lookup\nhere resolves a language to exactly one origin.\n\nvendor also removed the files a new grammar lacks before writing the ones it\nhas, so a failure part way through left the directory without a header the\nnewly written parser.c still included: a grammar that no longer compiles,\ndescribed by a manifest that still named the old file set. Write first, then\nsweep, so a failure leaves a superset instead of a hole.\n\nEach guard is mutation-proven: restoring the binary search, dropping the\nduplicate check, moving the ABI gate below the sweep, and restoring the old\ndelete-first order each turn a test red.\nEOF\ngit add internal/sem/vendored_grammars_test.go internal/sem/swift_grammar_regression_test.go internal/sem/grammars/swift/VALIDATION.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ntest(sem): tie the vendored grammar bytes to the identity revision\n\nNothing connected a vendored grammar's contents to IdentityRevision. The\nsnapshot caches are keyed on the indexed repository's git tree, which a parser\nchange does not touch, so the revision is the whole invalidation mechanism —\nand a refresh that changed parse results could land with a stale revision and\nevery test would stay green. The two tests that claimed this ground compared\nIdentityRevision against its previous value, which cannot fail while\nTestParserIdentityRevisionsSnapshotAndCaches pins it exactly; they were\nremoved, correctly, and nothing replaced them.\n\nPin a digest of all 62 managed grammar files instead, with a failure message\nthat says to weigh parse results, bump the revision, then update the digest.\nAlso check grammars.json against the directories it describes: the manifest\ndrives what a refresh adds and deletes, and nothing asserted that its file\nlists and ABI fields match what is committed.\n\nSwift's regression cases reached none of the block-comment path\ncompatibility.patch changed, so add an unterminated comment to the\nmalformed-source set and a nested/multi-line case that must keep the\ndeclarations after it.\n\nVALIDATION.md stated the Hummingbird symbol and relation counts as current;\nthey come from the same run as the whole-repository totals, before the last\nscanner and grammar fixes. Mark them, as those totals already are.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -3 && echo \"=== status:\" && git status --porcelain | head","description":"Commit the two fix sets"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3c2c03ad-ce53-4bd9-8cd5-2b9a740b3721","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgimigstK9coXFbmcdjRb","requestRef":"b0362d2d-23de-41a0-8049-2684b7d49155","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"06bb1300-77cc-45cf-ad6c-9bdb52239b37","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:40:55.360Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
