{"parentUuid":"a394b2b5-4ac4-45ff-8d36-3f22b78c34e4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgimmGpMyXuYNnV4gcvLe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1070,"cache_read_input_tokens":304101,"output_tokens":1443,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":633},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1070,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1443,"cache_read_input_tokens":304101,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1070},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9653,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"155b5ad4-21e8-4c97-a35e-a9814e3f7d0c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgimmGYFCDJ9heNkwUAnk","requestRef":"d4007c2a-b289-49dd-9c66-551918ad1bae","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9dc0a672-e8ec-44ff-82f7-dbf8724073cf","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:41:25.858Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"9dc0a672-e8ec-44ff-82f7-dbf8724073cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgimmGpMyXuYNnV4gcvLe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TpqLsT31WAFxdMVfK7Vo8Q","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/go-overlay-cannot-mutate-data-files.md","content":"---\nname: go-overlay-cannot-mutate-data-files\ndescription: go test -overlay swaps BUILD inputs only, so mutating testdata/vendored files through it silently proves nothing — the test reads the real file at runtime\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\n`go test -overlay=ov.json` replaces files **the compiler reads**. It does not\nintercept `os.ReadFile`, `os.ReadDir` or `filepath.Glob` at runtime. So a\nmutation aimed at a data file — testdata, a vendored `parser.c`, a JSON\nmanifest — is simply ignored, the test reads the real bytes from disk, and the\nrun comes back green.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-04 on entire-graph #357. I wrote two new tests (a digest over\n62 vendored grammar files, and a manifest-vs-disk check), then \"proved\" they\ncould fail by overlaying a mutated `swift/scanner.c` and a mutated\n`grammars.json`. Both mutations came back **ok**. I nearly recorded them as\nmutation-proven. Re-run against the real files — mutate in place, then\n`git checkout -- <path>` — and all three mutations went red immediately.\n\n**Why:** a green run under a mutation reads exactly like a correctly-passing\ntest, which is the failure mode [[green-suite-is-not-evidence]] and\n[[mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test]] are about. Overlay is the right tool\nfor mutating **Go source** (it kept the worktree clean across four tool-code\nmutations in the same session), so the method is sound for half the job and\nsilently useless for the other half.\n\n**How to apply:** mutate Go code with `-overlay`; mutate data files in place\nand restore with `git checkout -- <path>` (verify with `git status --porcelain`\nafter). If a mutation that should break a test does not, suspect the mutation\nreached nothing before suspecting the test — check whether the thing you\nchanged is read at build time or at run time. Related:\n[[verification-harness-false-pass]], [[verified-by-weakening-doctrine]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1070,"cache_read_input_tokens":304101,"output_tokens":1443,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":633},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1070,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1443,"cache_read_input_tokens":304101,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1070},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TpqLsT31WAFxdMVfK7Vo8Q":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/go-overlay-cannot-mutate-data-files.md","content":"---\nname: go-overlay-cannot-mutate-data-files\ndescription: go test -overlay swaps BUILD inputs only, so mutating testdata/vendored files through it silently proves nothing — the test reads the real file at runtime\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\n`go test -overlay=ov.json` replaces files **the compiler reads**. It does not\nintercept `os.ReadFile`, `os.ReadDir` or `filepath.Glob` at runtime. So a\nmutation aimed at a data file — testdata, a vendored `parser.c`, a JSON\nmanifest — is simply ignored, the test reads the real bytes from disk, and the\nrun comes back green.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-04 on entire-graph #357. I wrote two new tests (a digest over\n62 vendored grammar files, and a manifest-vs-disk check), then \"proved\" they\ncould fail by overlaying a mutated `swift/scanner.c` and a mutated\n`grammars.json`. Both mutations came back **ok**. I nearly recorded them as\nmutation-proven. Re-run against the real files — mutate in place, then\n`git checkout -- <path>` — and all three mutations went red immediately.\n\n**Why:** a green run under a mutation reads exactly like a correctly-passing\ntest, which is the failure mode [[green-suite-is-not-evidence]] and\n[[mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test]] are about. Overlay is the right tool\nfor mutating **Go source** (it kept the worktree clean across four tool-code\nmutations in the same session), so the method is sound for half the job and\nsilently useless for the other half.\n\n**How to apply:** mutate Go code with `-overlay`; mutate data files in place\nand restore with `git checkout -- <path>` (verify with `git status --porcelain`\nafter). If a mutation that should break a test does not, suspect the mutation\nreached nothing before suspecting the test — check whether the thing you\nchanged is read at build time or at run time. Related:\n[[verification-harness-false-pass]], [[verified-by-weakening-doctrine]].\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"155b5ad4-21e8-4c97-a35e-a9814e3f7d0c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgimmGYFCDJ9heNkwUAnk","requestRef":"d4007c2a-b289-49dd-9c66-551918ad1bae","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a567cf3e-26fd-42dd-b5a7-4d0bca8438af","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:41:36.540Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
