{"parentUuid":"4b758de0-5b8f-4657-97e6-388349b7295b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14820806 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"bd788c95-3d62-4c53-abe3-72094a6673e4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:42:03.678Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14820806 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"bd788c95-3d62-4c53-abe3-72094a6673e4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgimprVzM6JSL6UULVshH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 178 entries now load, with headroom. Here's the full picture on #357.\n\n## What I verified against upstream\n\nThe provenance is sound. The pinned commit is exactly what the `0.7.4` tag points at; the copied licence and all three headers match upstream byte-for-byte; the parser declares ABI 14 as claimed. The grammar swap is clean — the new binary links the vendored Swift grammar and zero symbols of the old one, costing 1.65% binary size. And the 29 changed test fixtures differ from main by **nothing but the revision number** — zero drift, including the fixture that contains real Swift. End to end, a swift-testing file goes from \"100% of this file is unparseable\" to clean. The headline is real.\n\n## What I fixed\n\nTwo commits on a local branch, all in the PR's own new code:\n\n- **A real bug in the new refresh tool.** It binary-searches a manifest that nothing sorts or validates. Appending a grammar to the end of the JSON file — the obvious hand-edit — leaves it unsorted, and the search then misses a language that *is* present and adds a second entry for it. I checked every single-entry insertion: all twelve languages can be duplicated this way.\n- **The tool deleted files before writing the new ones**, so any mid-write failure left a grammar directory missing a header the new parser still includes — one that no longer compiles, described by a manifest still naming the old files. Now it writes first, then sweeps.\n- **The gap left by two deleted tests.** The author removed two tests as unfailable, and was right — but nothing replaced them, and *nothing in the suite can notice a grammar change at all*. The caches are keyed on the indexed repo's tree, which a parser edit doesn't touch, so the revision number is the entire invalidation mechanism. I pinned a digest over all 62 vendored grammar files, plus a check that the manifest matches what's actually committed. A future refresh that forgets the bump now fails loudly.\n- Swift's tests reached none of the block-comment code the patch changed, so I added an unterminated-comment case and a nested-comment one.\n- The unverified Hummingbird numbers are now marked, like the other stale numbers already were.\n\nEvery guard is mutation-proven. Full runs: 5849 pass in the semantic package, 268 in gitutil, 25 in the tool.\n\n## Two agent findings I threw out\n\n- One agent reported that `#endif` leaking into Swift signatures was new behaviour from this PR. **Main emits byte-identical signatures.** It's a real defect but pre-existing — it belongs in its own PR, and #357 shouldn't be blamed for it.\n- Another reported the tool's `git fetch` as a command-execution hole via `ext::` URLs. **Git 2.54 refuses that transport by default.** My fix for it was a no-op and its test couldn't fail, so I deleted both. I saved the underlying lesson: my mutation-testing method silently proves nothing on data files, which is how I nearly recorded two fake proofs in this session.\n\nOne pre-existing formatting failure in `internal/sem/groovy_test.go` is on main too, not from this PR.\n\n## Three things that need you\n\n1. **Nothing has agent-reviewed this PR.** The gate is neutral because no trail tracks the branch, which displays as *not blocking* rather than *never ran*.\n2. **Merge order matters across repos.** This bumps the parser revision to 7, stranding every Brain's entity index. The Brain-side fix is its PR #592, still open, and it reads a field *your* #389 publishes. So: #389 → Brain #592 → then release this. Wrong order and `migrate` gives up after five commits. The Brain session is offline, so it hasn't been told about revision 7.\n3. **My fixes are committed locally and not pushed** — it's rodbegbie's branch on his fork. I can push there (maintainers are permitted), open a separate PR, or post the findings as a review comment. Which do you want? And do you still want me to run the byte-for-byte grammar regeneration check, which needs the external `tree-sitter-cli`?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":782,"cache_read_input_tokens":308608,"output_tokens":1346,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":782,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1346,"cache_read_input_tokens":308608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":782},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dda5541f-56fe-4325-9c0c-96c4a5d850c5","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgimpr8AS9bwbXBEqBBmx","requestRef":"0ff083b5-24a6-45ba-9152-758bb6c9e9dd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1f1ccf4b-7649-4b9a-98db-995776be4a7d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:42:25.971Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
