{"parentUuid":"8fc9cf31-f4a6-404d-9690-40c8ad6c6f45","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgjjZjpGBvHGLDcxtVEVR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TRFE5FdgLHQBbcNsPXWzCe","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-357-review && git add -A cmd/grammar-refresh && git -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" -c user.email=\"suhaanthayyil@users.noreply.github.com\" commit -q -F - <<'MSG' && git log --oneline -3\nfix(grammar-refresh): refuse to pick between licences, and say when a reference moved\n\nTwo ways the refresh tool loses information without saying so.\n\nfindLicense returned the first LICENSE or COPYING file it found and vendored\nit as the single LICENSE. An upstream offering a choice of grants ships\nLICENSE-MIT beside LICENSE-APACHE, so that silently drops one: scripts/\ngen-notices.sh finds vendored licences by the name LICENSE alone, prints one\nSPDX label per file, and takes the first its grep recognises, which leaves no\nfaithful single-file form. Concatenating would get labelled as whichever text\nclassify_license matched first. So findLicenses now returns every grant and\nvendor refuses more than one, naming them, because which grant we ship is a\ndecision for a person.\n\nThe fetched commit was never compared against the one the manifest records.\nperl's reference is the \"release\" branch, so running the same command a month\napart vendors different bytes, and a review would see \"refreshed perl\" with no\ncommit to look up. Refresh now names both commits when a reference has moved,\nand stays quiet when it has not. shortRevision replaces an unguarded\nrevision[:7] on a value that is read off disk and need not be 40 characters.\n\nEvery guard is mutation-proven in both directions: deleting the warning fails\nthe moved case, warning unconditionally fails the unmoved one.\nMSG","description":"Commit the licence and moving-reference fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":531,"cache_read_input_tokens":168796,"output_tokens":877,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":225},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":531,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":877,"cache_read_input_tokens":168796,"cache_creation_input_tokens":531,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":531},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TRFE5FdgLHQBbcNsPXWzCe":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-357-review && git add -A cmd/grammar-refresh && git -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" -c user.email=\"suhaanthayyil@users.noreply.github.com\" commit -q -F - <<'MSG' && git log --oneline -3\nfix(grammar-refresh): refuse to pick between licences, and say when a reference moved\n\nTwo ways the refresh tool loses information without saying so.\n\nfindLicense returned the first LICENSE or COPYING file it found and vendored\nit as the single LICENSE. An upstream offering a choice of grants ships\nLICENSE-MIT beside LICENSE-APACHE, so that silently drops one: scripts/\ngen-notices.sh finds vendored licences by the name LICENSE alone, prints one\nSPDX label per file, and takes the first its grep recognises, which leaves no\nfaithful single-file form. Concatenating would get labelled as whichever text\nclassify_license matched first. So findLicenses now returns every grant and\nvendor refuses more than one, naming them, because which grant we ship is a\ndecision for a person.\n\nThe fetched commit was never compared against the one the manifest records.\nperl's reference is the \"release\" branch, so running the same command a month\napart vendors different bytes, and a review would see \"refreshed perl\" with no\ncommit to look up. Refresh now names both commits when a reference has moved,\nand stays quiet when it has not. shortRevision replaces an unguarded\nrevision[:7] on a value that is read off disk and need not be 40 characters.\n\nEvery guard is mutation-proven in both directions: deleting the warning fails\nthe moved case, warning unconditionally fails the unmoved one.\nMSG","description":"Commit the licence and moving-reference fixes"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1fe02d15-480f-4dd8-b87b-c3d4774293d3","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgjjZjWAHEzXKtnf7EiDv","requestRef":"1ae61633-cd31-4c97-b3bd-e46178efa2c3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","attributionSkill":"loop","type":"assistant","uuid":"f8b2029b-434f-4a04-b733-93337b88e02e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:53:12.713Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
