{"parentUuid":"3f706b18-b810-402f-a93d-b41c41b0e2b7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14942197 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"59730a6f-5401-4dfe-afb8-1309c27a4fe5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:54:39.334Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14942197 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"59730a6f-5401-4dfe-afb8-1309c27a4fe5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cgjjh1kQryL4yD6dZkitC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Loop ran one tick, then stopped: it's blocked on a permission only you can grant.**\n\n## What the tick got done\n\nFixed two more verified findings in #357's own new code, both mutation-proven:\n\n- **`findLicense` kept one grant.** It returned the first `LICENSE`/`COPYING` it found. An upstream offering a choice ships `LICENSE-MIT` beside `LICENSE-APACHE`, so one gets silently dropped. `gen-notices.sh` finds vendored licences by the name `LICENSE` alone and prints one SPDX label, taking the first its grep matches, so there's no faithful single-file form. It now returns every grant and **refuses** more than one, naming them. Picking a licence is a person's call.\n- **The fetched commit was never checked against the manifest.** `perl`'s reference is the `release` **branch**, so the same command a month apart vendors different bytes and a review sees \"refreshed perl\" with no commit to look up. Refresh now names both commits when a reference moved, and stays quiet when it didn't. Also replaced an unguarded `revision[:7]` on a value read off disk.\n\nProven both directions: deleting the warning fails the moved case, warning unconditionally fails the unmoved case. `cmd/grammar-refresh` 31 pass (was 25), build and vet clean.\n\nThree commits now on `fix/357-followups`.\n\n## Why it stopped\n\nI tried to push them to the PR branch. Denied twice by the permission classifier: first `[Remote Repoint]`, then `[Create Public Surface]`. `maintainerCanModify` is `true` on #357, so GitHub would allow it. I'm not going to keep retrying a denial.\n\nNothing else in the loop can progress without you: the only remaining unverified claim needs the external `tree-sitter-cli`. Restart with `/loop` once the push is cleared.\n\n## Open PRs from external contributors\n\nFork PRs, which is the clean external signal:\n\n**entire-graph — 9 from 7 people**\n\n| PR | Author | Size | State |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #357 | rodbegbie | +734k/-97 | CLEAN, 38 green, gate NEUTRAL |\n| #232 | Shaurya002800 | +20387/-0, 94 files | DIRTY, no CI ever ran |\n| #233 | souzataniya | +3120/-67 | DIRTY, no CI |\n| #235 | Yashwanthk06 | +1016/-1 | DIRTY, no CI |\n| #237 | saranmahadev | +5796/-39 | DIRTY, no CI |\n| #249 | MuskanPaliwal | +708/-138 | DIRTY, no CI |\n| #265 | aniruddhaadak80 | +30/-3 | BLOCKED, gate NEUTRAL |\n| #267 | aniruddhaadak80 | +19/-0 | BLOCKED, gate NEUTRAL |\n| #269 | aniruddhaadak80 | +109/-1 | BLOCKED, gate NEUTRAL |\n\nWorth noting: **five of them have no CI result at all** and are merge-conflicted, the oldest untouched since 6 September. And every one of the nine shows `gate=NEUTRAL` or nothing, so **no external contribution to entire-graph has ever been agent-reviewed.** That's the same gate hole as #357, across the whole external queue.\n\n**entire-brain — 11 forks from 4 people** (Beehtrix 6, garvit-arora 2, tobylo, rennf93). Brain is the other session's lane, so I only listed them.\n\n**cli — 57 forks from 35 people** out of 238 open. Too many to table here; say the word and I'll pull the list with CI and conflict state."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":214,"cache_read_input_tokens":176678,"output_tokens":1255,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":214,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1255,"cache_read_input_tokens":176678,"cache_creation_input_tokens":214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":214},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"aa606e3d-9dd5-46af-875a-f078f1122604","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgjjh1UXwv5LaZdxtMyoJ","requestRef":"c091962c-eaaf-48c6-a0ea-fa84f1ac2c83","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","attributionSkill":"loop","type":"assistant","uuid":"1bd3fc40-e517-4441-93d4-7aeb600441e1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:54:57.542Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
