his repo requires deterministic output and has been bitten by exactly that before.\n4. TESTS: apply verify-by-weakening. For every guard or branch the PR adds, patch it out, re-run the PR's new tests, confirm RED. Report every unfailable test by name. A green suite is not evidence.\n5. Does it build and do the touched packages' tests pass after your conflict resolution?\n\nHARD CONSTRAINTS:\n- Read-only toward GitHub. Do NOT run `gh pr comment`/`review`/`merge` or any push. Never merge anything.\n- CPU discipline: user's laptop, other sessions running. `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test -p 1 -parallel 1` with a NARROW `-run` filter on only the touched packages. NEVER `go test ./...`. NEVER `-race` on internal/sem.\n- Mutate Go source with `go test -overlay` writing the mutated copy to your own temp dir, so the worktree stays clean. -overlay only swaps BUILD inputs: it does NOT intercept runtime os.ReadFile/ReadDir/Glob, so mutate DATA files (testdata, goldens, JSON) in place and restore with `git checkout -- <path>`.\n- Use `entire graph query/def/neighbors/impact --repo . --head` and `entire brain recall \"<q>\" --branch main` instead of grep sweeps for relationships and prior decisions. Preflight both once (`entire graph version --json`, `entire brain version`); report if broken rather than silently grepping.\n- Use `rtk` for shell commands.\n\nREPORT - caveman-ultra compressed. Dense bullets, no prose paragraphs, no preamble, no restating the task. Only this report reaches me.\n  VERDICT: <still-applies | superseded | needs-rework | reject> + one line why\n  WHAT: <2 lines max>\n  SUPERSEDED-BY: <evidence, or \"no\">\n  CONFLICT-RESOLUTION: <what you did to help_test.go>\n  FINDINGS (ranked, worst first): file:line | defect | concrete failure scenario (inputs -> wrong output/panic)\n  TESTS: <n new; guards proven RED; unfailable ones by name>\n  BUILD/TEST: <result>\nEnd with CMDS-RUN. Default every finding to REFUTED unless you reproduced it with a command. \"Could not verify\" beats a guess."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":185032,"output_tokens":7333,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":855},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7333,"cache_read_input_tokens":185032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PkRC4CttZczWShfxiDMzSd":{"description":"Review PR 235 changeset risk","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"You are reviewing external-contributor PR #235 on entireio/entire-graph: \"feat: add graph changeset risk analysis\" by Yashwanthk06 (+1016/-1, 10 files). It is ~1311 commits behind main and has ONE merge conflict onto today's main: internal/cli/help_test.go.\n\nWORKTREE: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-235-review - this is current main with origin/pr-235 merged, left mid-merge with that one conflict UNRESOLVED. Start by looking at the conflict (`git diff --diff-filter=U`), resolve it the way main's current help text wants (the PR is adding a command; main has since changed help output), then proceed.\n\n`git diff origin/main...origin/pr-235` is the PR's own change. `git log origin/main..origin/pr-235` is its 3 commits.\n\nYOUR JOB:\n1. WHAT IS IT: one paragraph max - what feature does this add, what command/flag surface, what does it compute.\n2. DOES IT STILL BELONG: main has moved 1311 commits. Has this capability since been built another way (check `entire graph diff`, `graph impact`, the sear