{"parentUuid":"b40e9bd9-ca1b-4adb-a59d-1335e204d04d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cgkas2yZWDQ8nJsmwy4Jo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RynQpd8diQncyW4AoQLxaE","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PR 249 Gradle ownership","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"You are reviewing external-contributor PR #249 on entireio/entire-graph: \"fix(sem): verify Gradle project ownership before deriving tests\" by MuskanPaliwal (+708/-138, 5 files), referencing issue #219. It is ~914 commits behind main.\n\nCRITICAL CONTEXT, and your first question: it conflicts onto today's main in EXACTLY the two files it changes - internal/sem/search_verify.go and internal/sem/search_verify_test.go. That is the signature of main having already changed the same code. There is a standing suspicion (recorded on our board) that this PR was superseded by PR #261 and its follow-ups. DEFAULT TO SUPERSEDED and disprove it.\n\nWORKTREE: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-249-review - current main with origin/pr-249 merged, left mid-merge with those two files UNRESOLVED.\n\nUseful: `git diff origin/main...origin/pr-249` is the PR's change. `git log origin/main..origin/pr-249` its 13 commits. `git log --oneline origin/pr-249..origin/main -- internal/sem/search_verify.go` shows what main did to the same file since the PR branched - read those commits.\n\nYOUR JOB, in this order:\n1. SUPERSESSION: Does current main already verify Gradle project ownership before deriving tests? Read main's current internal/sem/search_verify.go. Find the commit(s) that changed it (`git log -p` on that file since the PR's merge-base). Check `entire brain recall \"gradle project ownership verify tests\" --branch main` and `--branch main` recall for issue #219. ANSWER: is the bug this PR fixes still present on main, yes or no, with the command output that proves it.\n2. If the bug IS still present on main: reproduce it concretely - construct the Gradle layout that misattributes tests and show the wrong output from main's binary. Then review the PR's fix for correctness and completeness.\n3. If the bug is GONE: say so decisively, name the commit that fixed it, and state whether the PR still contains anything of value main lacks (e.g. a test case main's fix does not cover). That residual value is the only thing worth salvaging.\n4. Either way: review the PR's 5 changed files for defects it would introduce, and apply verify-by-weakening to its new tests - patch out each guard it adds, re-run, confirm RED. Name every unfailable test.\n\nHARD CONSTRAINTS:\n- Read-only toward GitHub. No `gh pr comment`/`review`/`merge`, no push. Never merge anything.\n- CPU discipline: user's laptop, other sessions running. `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test -p 1 -parallel 1` with a NARROW `-run` filter. NEVER `go test ./...`. NEVER `-race` on internal/sem - it exceeds 30 minutes. internal/sem is a huge package: always filter.\n- Mutate Go source via `go test -overlay` with the mutated copy in your own temp dir, keeping the worktree clean. -overlay swaps BUILD inputs ONLY - it does NOT intercept runtime os.ReadFile/ReadDir/Glob, so mutate DATA files (testdata, Gradle fixture files, goldens) in place and restore with `git checkout -- <path>`. An overlay mutation of a data file silently proves nothing - this exact trap produced two fake proofs in an earlier session.\n- Use `entire graph query/def/neighbors/impact --repo . --head` and `entire brain recall --branch main` instead of grep sweeps. Preflight both once; report breakage rather than silently grepping.\n- Use `rtk` for shell commands.\n\nREPORT - caveman-ultra compressed. Dense bullets. No prose paragraphs, no preamble, no restating the task. Only this report reaches me.\n  VERDICT: <superseded | still-applies | partially-superseded> + one line\n  BUG-ON-MAIN: <present y/n> + the command+output that proves it\n  SUPERSEDED-BY: <commit sha + subject, or \"no\">\n  SALVAGEABLE: <what, if anything, main still lacks>\n  FINDINGS: file:line | defect | concrete failure scenario\n  TESTS: <guards proven RED; unfailable by name>\nEnd with CMDS-RUN. Default to REFUTED unless personally reproduced. \"Could not verify\" beats a guess."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":185032,"output_tokens":7333,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":855},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7333,"cache_read_input_tokens":185032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RynQpd8diQncyW4AoQLxaE":{"description":"Review PR 249 Gradle ownership","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"You are reviewing external-contributor PR #249 on entireio/entire-graph: \"fix(sem): verify Gradle project ownership before deriving tests\" by MuskanPaliwal (+708/-138, 5 files), referencing issue #219. It is ~914 commits behind main.\n\nCRITICAL CONTEXT, and your first question: it conflicts onto today's main in EXACTLY the two files it changes - internal/sem/search_verify.go and internal/sem/search_verify_test.go. That is the signature of main having already changed the same code. There is a standing suspicion (recorded on our board) that this PR was superseded by PR #261 and its follow-ups. DEFAULT TO SUPERSEDED and disprove it.\n\nWORKTREE: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-249-review - current main with origin/pr-249 merged, left mid-merge