/eg-265-review\n- #267 \"fix(verify): reject conflicting baseline modes\" (+19/-0, 2 files) -> /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-267-review\n- #269 \"fix(preflight): preserve quoted command arguments\" (+109/-1, 4 files) -> /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-269-review\n\nIn each worktree, `git diff origin/main...HEAD` is exactly what the PR adds on top of current main. `git log origin/main..HEAD` shows its commits.\n\nYOUR JOB, per PR:\n1. Does the bug it claims to fix actually exist on current main? Reproduce it. A PR fixing a bug that no longer exists is the single most likely outcome given the staleness - default to that hypothesis and disprove it.\n2. Is the fix correct and complete, or does it fix one path and leave a sibling path broken?\n3. Are its tests real? Apply the verify-by-weakening method: patch out each guard the PR adds, re-run its new test, and confirm the test goes RED. A test that still passes with the guard removed proves nothing. Report any unfailable test you find.\n4. #265 and #267 both touch baseline handling in verify - check whether they CONFLICT semantically with each other (e.g. one makes the other's check unreachable). This matters because they would land together.\n5. Any correctness defect the PR introduces.\n\nHARD CONSTRAINTS:\n- Read-only toward GitHub. Do NOT run `gh pr comment`, `gh pr review`, `gh pr merge`, or any push. Never merge anything.\n- CPU discipline: this is the user's laptop and other sessions are running. Use `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test -p 1 -parallel 1` and ALWAYS a narrow `-run` filter on only the touched package. NEVER run `go test ./...`. NEVER use `-race` on internal/sem (it exceeds 30 min).\n- Mutate Go source with `go test -overlay` (write the mutated copy to your own temp dir) so the worktree stays clean. NOTE: -overlay only swaps BUILD inputs - it does NOT intercept runtime os.ReadFile/ReadDir/Glob, so for a DATA file (testdata, JSON, vendored .c) you must edit in place and restore with `git checkout -- <path>`. An overlay mutation of a data file silently proves nothing.\n- Use `entire graph query/def/neighbors/impact --repo . --head` and `entire brain recall \"<q>\" --branch main` for code relationships and prior decisions instead of grep sweeps. Run the preflight (`entire graph version --json`, `entire brain version`) once first; if a tool is broken, say so in your report rather than silently grepping.\n- Use `rtk` for shell commands where the hook rewrites them.\n\nREPORT FORMAT - caveman-ultra compressed. No prose paragraphs, no preamble, no restating the task. Dense bullets only. Your tool output does not reach me; only this report does.\nPer PR:\n  #NNN VERDICT: <still-applies | superseded | broken | wrong>\n  BUG-ON-MAIN: <reproduced y/n + the exact command and output that shows it>\n  FINDINGS: file:line | one-line defect | concrete failure scenario (inputs -> wrong output)\n  TESTS: <n new tests; which guards mutation-proven RED; which unfailable>\n  Then: CROSS-PR: does #265 vs #267 interact?\nEnd with: CMDS-RUN (the handful of commands whose output your conclusions rest on).\nDefault every finding to REFUTED unless you personally reproduced it with a command. Say \"could not verify\" rather than guessing.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d/tasks/a1461d77a3551cf48.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b0e9d413-1752-47df-9197-85129c836e91","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"name":