e-<N>).\n\nThe PRs (all target main, all ~1311 commits behind, all with ZERO reviews and ZERO CI runs ever):\n- #232 Shaurya002800 \"feat(pact): add graph-guided verification of confirmed requirements\" +20387/-0, 94 files. Conflicts onto main in only 2 files, both trivial config: .entire/settings.json and .gitignore. So 20k lines of code merge clean.\n- #233 souzataniya \"feat(sem,cli): add evidence state to Graph results\" +3120/-67, 62 files. Conflicts in 119 files including internal/sem/provider.go and dozens of testdata goldens.\n- #237 saranmahadev \"feat(cli): add requirement traceability and review workflows with GPS\" +5796/-39, 85 files, 162 commits. Conflicts in 112 files including go.mod, internal/cli/verify.go, internal/cli/impact.go and dozens of goldens.\n\nRefs are already fetched as origin/pr-232, origin/pr-233, origin/pr-237. `git diff origin/main...origin/pr-NNN` and `git log origin/main..origin/pr-NNN` work from the repo.\n\nANSWER THESE, per PR, with evidence:\n1. WHAT IT ACTUALLY IS: 2-3 lines. What user-visible surface does it add (commands, flags, output fields)? Note especially whether the bulk of those added lines is production code, generated/vendored files, testdata, or docs - a 20k-line PR that is 18k of fixtures is a different proposition from 20k of logic. Give the real production-code line count (`git diff --stat` filtered to non-testdata, non-docs, non-vendor paths).\n2. IS IT ALREADY DONE: has main built this capability in the ~2 months since? Check with `entire graph query --repo . --head --query \"<the feature>\"`, `entire graph def`, and `entire brain recall \"<feature>\" --branch main`. Name the commits/PRs if so. This is the deciding question.\n3. WHY DID CI NEVER RUN: check whether the workflow files require approval for fork PRs, or whether the PR predates the workflows. State which.\n4. COST TO SALVAGE: given the conflict profile, roughly what would a rebase onto main require - mechanical golden regeneration, or genuine re-authoring against a changed provider API? For #233 and #237, say specifically whether the golden conflicts are just the identity_revision/header line (cheap, regenerate) or real content divergence (expensive).\n5. RECOMMENDATION: one of <worth-a-full-review | needs-author-rebase-first | close-as-superseded | close-as-out-of-scope>, with one sentence of why.\n\nHARD CONSTRAINTS:\n- Read-only toward GitHub. No `gh pr comment`/`review`/`merge`, no push, no closing anything. You are gathering evidence for a human decision, not making it.\n- Do not modify /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph. Use your own worktree if needed.\n- CPU discipline: user's laptop, other sessions running. Do NOT run test suites at all for this triage - this is a read-and-reason task. If you must build, `GOMAXPROCS=1 go build` on one package only.\n- Use `entire graph query/def/neighbors --repo . --head` and `entire brain recall --branch main` rather than grep sweeps. Preflight both once (`entire graph version --json`, `entire brain version`); report breakage rather than silently grepping.\n- Use `rtk` for shell commands.\n\nREPORT - caveman-ultra compressed. Dense bullets, no prose paragraphs, no preamble, no restating the task. Only this report reaches me.\nPer PR:\n  #NNN REC: <one of the four> | <one sentence why>\n  WHAT: <2-3 lines>\n  REAL-PROD-LOC: <number> (of <total>) | breakdown: logic/testdata/docs/vendor\n  ALREADY-DONE: <evidence, or \"no\">\n  CI-NEVER-RAN-BECAUSE: <reason>\n  SALVAGE-COST: <mechanical | moderate | re-author> + what specifically\nEnd with CMDS-RUN. Do not speculate - if you could not establish something, write \"could not verify\".","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d/tasks/aa43541a58e2b255f.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b0e9d413-1752-47df-9197-85129c836e91","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","root":"/Users/suhaan