{"parentUuid":"54227ee1-76bb-4d82-b1ba-5917e0d0ec23","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgkcuPAnhxLaiMH1CRfXw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every substantive claim reproduces. Two I corrected. Recording, then here's where all nine stand."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1464,"cache_read_input_tokens":250468,"output_tokens":4030,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1424},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1464,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4030,"cache_read_input_tokens":250468,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1464,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1464},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2ca993ee-9691-46be-aac4-ee92afa88c8a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgkcuNuej35q2k6LwLmw7","requestRef":"f927813a-cc2f-4b33-97e0-723bcb1ad58b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"83baef85-fe24-4527-8e3b-8183f86b6d08","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:06:37.558Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"83baef85-fe24-4527-8e3b-8183f86b6d08","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgkcuPAnhxLaiMH1CRfXw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SUHvkQLz9KaNSXNSrRC5ri","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'PY'\nimport json, os, fcntl, pathlib, datetime\nboard = pathlib.Path(\".claude/todo-board.json\")\nlock = pathlib.Path(\".claude/todo-board.lock\")\nwith open(lock, \"r+\") as lf:\n    fcntl.flock(lf, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n    data = json.loads(board.read_text())\n    row = next(r for r in data[\"tasks\"] if r.get(\"id\") == \"G-external-pr-sweep\")\n    row[\"status\"] = \"blocked\"\n    row[\"owner\"] = \"user\"\n    row[\"notes\"] = (\n        \"ALL 9 REVIEWED. Verdicts (every decisive claim re-verified by me, not relayed): \"\n        \"#357 rodbegbie SOUND + 3 fix commits on fix/357-followups UNPUSHED (see G-357-swift). \"\n        \"#232 Shaurya002800 CLOSE-OUT-OF-SCOPE: 0 Go files, 0 Go lines; a Python FastAPI+databricks-sdk app (btw-pact) + 2.1MB media \"\n        \"+ ~17k lines of JSON evidence dumps vendored into a Go repo; calls `entire graph` as a subprocess. \"\n        \"#233 souzataniya SPLIT-FIRST: majority is a new `graph rank` dev leaderboard (GitHub stars x PR share); internal/rank absent from main. \"\n        \"The ~431-line in-scope evidence-state part was INDEPENDENTLY BUILT on main (neighbors.go Confidence+Resolution, impact.go name_only reasoning). \"\n        \"Goldens header-only (29 files, +29/-29) BUT it sets schema_version 1.4 -> 1.2, a DOWNGRADE. \"\n        \"#235 Yashwanthk06 NEEDS-REWORK: 15 findings. Headline: risk ranks by DependentsCount = len(index[shortEntityName(change)]) \"\n        \"(dependents.go:663 referenceName -> shortEntityName) = a NAME-FREQUENCY count, so live runs put struct fields named err/n and \"\n        \"vendored parser.h fields in the top 5 of 705 entities, 700 silently dropped, recommended_tests empty. overall_risk computed only from \"\n        \"post-cap survivors. Zero-filled graph_evidence serialises identically to '0 callers'. 22 of 43 mutations GREEN. 307 of 1016 lines are \"\n        \"hackathon scaffolding (unvalidated Databricks bundle, BUILDATHON.md). \"\n        \"#237 saranmahadev RE-AUTHOR: GPS, 6 new top-level commands, genuinely unbuilt but never design-accepted. TRAP: merged tree has TWO \"\n        \"`case \\\"context\\\"` at root.go:332+354 in ONE switch = compile error, and git AUTO-MERGES root.go with NO conflict, so nobody resolving its \"\n        \"112 conflicts is ever prompted. 29 goldens carry W_GIT_WORKTREE_FALLBACK ('Git worktree enumeration was unavailable') = author's broken env \"\n        \"baked in, so its own verification ran on a degraded snapshot. \"\n        \"#249 MuskanPaliwal SUPERSEDED: #219 is fixed on main by f22e6c95 'fix(verify): derive only commands the repository can actually run (#261)' \"\n        \"(2026-09-23, ancestor of main, body names #219 AND #203). Bug reproduces at the PR's merge-base, GONE on main. PR would also regress: \"\n        \"picks the NEAREST ancestor gradlew then points it up with -p .., running the root build with a nested wrapper (wrong Gradle version). \"\n        \"Salvage: the name/setName project-rename check (main only checks projectDir). \"\n        \"#265 aniruddhaadak80 REAL BUG, BROKEN AS SUBMITTED: --setup is the one comparability input main never records; fix direction right, but \"\n        \"verifyBaselineFormatVersion 1->2 breaks 3 tests (outputpath_test.go:202/463/1049 - VERIFIED FAILING by me). Write-side guard UNFAILABLE: \"\n        \"deleting `Setup: flags.Setup` keeps the new test green. Precedent 5c3cf40d used omitempty, no version bump, and updated help.go. \"\n        \"#267 aniruddhaadak80 CLEAN - the only one mergeable as-is. Main silently ignores --pre-edit-baseline when --record-baseline is set. \"\n        \"Nits only (no t.Parallel, no CHANGELOG). \"\n        \"#269 aniruddhaadak80 REAL BUG, FIX OVERREACHES. Verified by direct probe of splitPreflightCommandLine: headline fix WORKS \"\n        \"(`--test \\\"go test ./...\\\"` parses), but it adopts POSIX UNQUOTED backslash escaping: `--repo C:\\\\work\\\\repo` -> C:workrepo; \"\n        \"`--repo C:\\\\repo\\\\ --query x` -> [\\\"--repo\\\" \\\"C:repo --query\\\" \\\"x\\\"] with err=nil, so --query is SWALLOWED and doctor records an \"\n        \"`asserted_command_line` it never checked (false approve); `4\\\\096` -> 4096 passes a malformed number main rejects; \"\n        \"`--query don't` now FAILS 'unterminated quote' where main passed. ALSO: #269's parent IS #267's head - merging #269 merges #267. \"\n        \"MY CORRECTIONS TO AGENT CLAIMS: (1) #237's duplicate case is NOT in the PR (PR has 1, main has 1) - the merge creates it silently, which is worse. \"\n        \"(2) 'risk.go is the only emoji producer, 0 hits elsewhere' is WRONG: risk.go is the only PICTOGRAPHIC emoji producer in prod code, but \"\n        \"24 dingbat chars already ship in 5 prod files (verify_parse.go 17x checkmarks, index.go+root.go warning sign, setup_ui.go, impact_progress.go). \"\n        \"CI NEVER RAN on #232/#233/#235/#237/#249/#265/#267/#269 = fork-approval gate, NOT missing workflows (test.yml dates 2026-05-28, triggers on \"\n        \"plain pull_request:; later fork PRs #343/#351/#357 got 30-38 checks once approved). One click fixes it for the ones worth testing. \"\n        \"*** STILL BLOCKING: evisdren's 2026-11-05 proposal to DELETE `graph verify` (~4,960 prod LoC) moots #237/#249/#265/#267/#269 = 5 of the 9. \"\n        \"USER DECISION. *** Nothing pushed, nothing commented, nothing merged, nothing closed.\"\n    )\n    data[\"updated\"] = datetime.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\")\n    tmp = board.with_suffix(\".json.tmp\"); tmp.write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=2) + \"\\n\"); os.replace(tmp, board)\n    print(\"board updated\")\n    fcntl.flock(lf, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\nPY","description":"Record all nine verdicts on the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1464,"cache_read_input_tokens":250468,"output_tokens":4030,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1424},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1464,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4030,"cache_read_input_tokens":250468,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1464,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1464},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SUHvkQLz9KaNSXNSrRC5ri":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv && python3 -I - <<'PY'\nimport json, os, fcntl, pathlib, datetime\nboard = pathlib.Path(\".claude/todo-board.json\")\nlock = pathlib.Path(\".claude/todo-board.lock\")\nwith open(lock, \"r+\") as lf:\n    fcntl.flock(lf, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n    data = json.loads(board.read_text())\n    row = next(r for r in data[\"tasks\"] if r.get(\"id\") == \"G-external-pr-sweep\")\n    row[\"status\"] = \"blocked\"\n    row[\"owner\"] = \"user\"\n    row[\"notes\"] = (\n        \"ALL 9 REVIEWED. Verdicts (every decisive claim re-verified by me, not relayed): \"\n        \"#357 rodbegbie SOUND + 3 fix commits on fix/357-followups UNPUSHED (see G-357-swift). \"\n        \"#232 Shaurya002800 CLOSE-OUT-OF-SCOPE: 0 Go files, 0 Go lines; a Python FastAPI+databricks-sdk app (btw-pact) + 2.1MB media \"\n        \"+ ~17k lines of JSON evidence dumps vendored into a Go repo; calls `entire graph` as a subprocess. \"\n        \"#233 souzataniya SPLIT-FIRST: majority is a new `graph rank` dev leaderboard (GitHub stars x PR share); internal/rank absent from main. \"\n        \"The ~431-line in-scope evidence-state part was INDEPENDENTLY BUILT on main (neighbors.go Confidence+Resolution, impact.go name_only reasoning). \"\n        \"Goldens header-only (29 files, +29/-29) BUT it sets schema_version 1.4 -> 1.2, a DOWNGRADE. \"\n        \"#235 Yashwanthk06 NEEDS-REWORK: 15 findings. Headline: risk ranks by DependentsCount = len(index[shortEntityName(change)]) \"\n        \"(dependents.go:663 referenceName -> shortEntityName) = a NAME-FREQUENCY count, so live runs put struct fields named err/n and \"\n        \"vendored parser.h fields in the top 5 of 705 entities, 700 silently dropped, recommended_tests empty. overall_risk computed only from \"\n        \"post-cap survivors. Zero-filled graph_evidence serialises identically to '0 callers'. 22 of 43 mutations GREEN. 307 of 1016 lines are \"\n        \"hackathon scaffolding (unvalidated Databricks bundle, BUILDATHON.md). \"\n        \"#237 saranmahadev RE-AUTHOR: GPS, 6 new top-level commands, genuinely unbuilt but never design-accepted. TRAP: merged tree has TWO \"\n        \"`case \\\"context\\\"` at root.go:332+354 in ONE switch = compile error, and git AUTO-MERGES root.go with NO conflict, so nobody resolving its \"\n        \"112 conflicts is ever prompted. 29 goldens carry W_GIT_WORKTREE_FALLBACK ('Git worktree enumeration was unavailable') = author's broken env \"\n        \"baked in, so its own verification ran on a degraded snapshot. \"\n        \"#249 MuskanPaliwal SUPERSEDED: #219 is fixed on main by f22e6c95 'fix(verify): derive only commands the repository can actually run (#261)' \"\n        \"(2026-09-23, ancestor of main, body names #219 AND #203). Bug reproduces at the PR's merge-base, GONE on main. PR would also regress: \"\n        \"picks the NEAREST ancestor gradlew then points it up with -p .., running the root build with a nested wrapper (wrong Gradle version). \"\n        \"Salvage: the name/setName project-rename check (main only checks projectDir). \"\n        \"#265 aniruddhaadak80 REAL BUG, BROKEN AS SUBMITTED: --setup is the one comparability input main never records; fix direction right, but \"\n        \"verifyBaselineFormatVersion 1->2 breaks 3 tests (outputpath_test.go:202/463/1049 - VERIFIED FAILING by me). Write-side guard UNFAILABLE: \"\n        \"deleting `Setup: flags.Setup` keeps the new test green. Precedent 5c3cf40d used omitempty, no version bump, and updated help.go. \"\n        \"#267 aniruddhaadak80 CLEAN - the only one mergeable as-is. Main silently ignores --pre-edit-baseline when --record-baseline is set. \"\n        \"Nits only (no t.Parallel, no CHANGELOG). \"\n        \"#269 aniruddhaadak80 REAL BUG, FIX OVERREACHES. Verified by direct probe of splitPreflightCommandLine: headline fix WORKS \"\n        \"(`--test \\\"go test ./...\\\"` parses), but it adopts POSIX UNQUOTED backslash escaping: `--repo C:\\\\work\\\\repo` -> C:workrepo; \"\n        \"`--repo C:\\\\repo\\\\ --query x` -> [\\\"--repo\\\" \\\"C:repo --query\\\" \\\"x\\\"] with err=nil, so --query is SWALLOWED and doctor records an \"\n        \"`asserted_command_line` it never checked (false approve); `4\\\\096` -> 4096 passes a malformed number main rejects; \"\n        \"`--query don't` now FAILS 'unterminated quote' where main passed. ALSO: #269's parent IS #267's head - merging #269 merges #267. \"\n        \"MY CORRECTIONS TO AGENT CLAIMS: (1) #237's duplicate case is NOT in the PR (PR has 1, main has 1) - the merge creates it silently, which is worse. \"\n        \"(2) 'risk.go is the only emoji producer, 0 hits elsewhere' is WRONG: risk.go is the only PICTOGRAPHIC emoji producer in prod code, but \"\n        \"24 dingbat chars already ship in 5 prod files (verify_parse.go 17x checkmarks, index.go+root.go warning sign, setup_ui.go, impact_progress.go). \"\n        \"CI NEVER RAN on #232/#233/#235/#237/#249/#265/#267/#269 = fork-approval gate, NOT missing workflows (test.yml dates 2026-05-28, triggers on \"\n        \"plain pull_request:; later fork PRs #343/#351/#357 got 30-38 checks once approved). One click fixes it for the ones worth testing. \"\n        \"*** STILL BLOCKING: evisdren's 2026-11-05 proposal to DELETE `graph verify` (~4,960 prod LoC) moots #237/#249/#265/#267/#269 = 5 of the 9. \"\n        \"USER DECISION. *** Nothing pushed, nothing commented, nothing merged, nothing closed.\"\n    )\n    data[\"updated\"] = datetime.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\")\n    tmp = board.with_suffix(\".json.tmp\"); tmp.write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=2) + \"\\n\"); os.replace(tmp, board)\n    print(\"board updated\")\n    fcntl.flock(lf, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\nPY","description":"Record all nine verdicts on the board"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01SUHvkQLz9KaNSXNSrRC5ri":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2ca993ee-9691-46be-aac4-ee92afa88c8a","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgkcuNuej35q2k6LwLmw7","requestRef":"f927813a-cc2f-4b33-97e0-723bcb1ad58b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"36b6ad45-cbd0-4335-9d07-b9faa3fe4080","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:07:09.747Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"36b6ad45-cbd0-4335-9d07-b9faa3fe4080","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e00ff51e-71f9-442f-bb3b-e9369b92c0df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SUHvkQLz9KaNSXNSrRC5ri","type":"tool_result","content":"board updated","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c4fc0de8-df60-460b-ba60-77b3acf69aaf","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:07:09.959Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"board updated","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":1,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {","-  \"updated\": \"2026-11-05T17:42:13-05:00\",","+  \"updated\": \"2026-11-05T18:07:09-05:00\",","   \"tasks\": [","     {","       \"id\": \"G-382-rebase\","]},{"oldStart":1600,"oldLines":9,"newStart":1600,"newLines":9,"lines":["       \"id\": \"G-external-pr-sweep\",","       \"lane\": \"graph\",","       \"title\": \"Review all 9 external-contributor PRs on entire-graph (user asked, same process as #357)\",","-      \"status\": \"in-progress\",","-      \"owner\": \"claude\",","-      \"notes\": \"The 9 fork PRs: #232 Shaurya002800, #233 souzataniya, #235 Yashwanthk06, #237 saranmahadev, #249 MuskanPaliwal, #265/#267/#269 aniruddhaadak80, #357 rodbegbie. ALL have maintainerCanModify=true, ALL target main, ALL have ZERO reviews. #357 DONE (see G-357-swift). STALENESS: #232/#233/#235/#237 are 1311 commits behind, #249 914, #265/#267/#269 907. MERGE ONTO TODAY'S MAIN: #265/#267/#269 CLEAN. #232 conflicts in 2 trivial config files only (.entire/settings.json, .gitignore) - its 20k lines of code merge clean. #235 conflicts in 1 file (internal/cli/help_test.go). #249 conflicts in exactly the 2 files it changes (internal/sem/search_verify.go + test) = signature of main having already changed the same code. #233 conflicts in 119 files incl. provider.go + dozens of goldens. #237 in 112 incl. go.mod. *** BLOCKER FOUND 2026-11-05: evisdren proposed on #265 REMOVING the `graph verify` command entirely (~4,960 production LoC: verify.go 900 + search_verify.go 3955 + preflight.go 105; 12,737 lines incl. tests). Evidence cited: 0 invocations across 2,536 local transcripts, nothing org-wide. He asked for concerns and nobody has replied. BLAST RADIUS = 5 OF THE 9: #237, #249, #265, #267, #269 all touch verify/preflight. Only #232, #233, #235 are outside it. search_verify.go opens with the comment 'The verify command', so it is that command's machinery, not the search VERIFY block. If verify goes, reviewing those five is wasted. USER DECISION NEEDED. *** Beehtrix already reviewed #265 (found: bumping verifyBaselineFormatVersion to 2 breaks 3 tests in internal/cli/outputpath_test.go lines 201/462/1048) and #267 (no issues). 4 review agents dispatched: #265+#267+#269, #235, #249, and triage of #232/#233/#237. CONSTRAINTS HELD: no merging anything, no pushes, no PR comments.\"","+      \"status\": \"blocked\",","+      \"owner\": \"user\",","+      \"notes\": \"ALL 9 REVIEWED. Verdicts (every decisive claim re-verified by me, not relayed): #357 rodbegbie SOUND + 3 fix commits on fix/357-followups UNPUSHED (see G-357-swift). #232 Shaurya002800 CLOSE-OUT-OF-SCOPE: 0 Go files, 0 Go lines; a Python FastAPI+databricks-sdk app (btw-pact) + 2.1MB media + ~17k lines of JSON evidence dumps vendored into a Go repo; calls `entire graph` as a subprocess. #233 souzataniya SPLIT-FIRST: majority is a new `graph rank` dev leaderboard (GitHub stars x PR share); internal/rank absent from main. The ~431-line in-scope evidence-state part was INDEPENDENTLY BUILT on main (neighbors.go Confidence+Resolution, impact.go name_only reasoning). Goldens header-only (29 files, +29/-29) BUT it sets schema_version 1.4 -> 1.2, a DOWNGRADE. #235 Yashwanthk06 NEEDS-REWORK: 15 findings. Headline: risk ranks by DependentsCount = len(index[shortEntityName(change)]) (dependents.go:663 referenceName -> shortEntityName) = a NAME-FREQUENCY count, so live runs put struct fields named err/n and vendored parser.h fields in the top 5 of 705 entities, 700 silently dropped, recommended_tests empty. overall_risk computed only from post-cap survivors. Zero-filled graph_evidence serialises identically to '0 callers'. 22 of 43 mutations GREEN. 307 of 1016 lines are hackathon scaffolding (unvalidated Databricks bundle, BUILDATHON.md). #237 saranmahadev RE-AUTHOR: GPS, 6 new top-level commands, genuinely unbuilt but never design-accepted. TRAP: merged tree has TWO `case \\\"context\\\"` at root.go:332+354 in ONE switch = compile error, and git AUTO-MERGES root.go with NO conflict, so nobody resolving its 112 conflicts is ever prompted. 29 goldens carry W_GIT_WORKTREE_FALLBACK ('Git worktree enumeration was unavailable') = author's broken env baked in, so its own verification ran on a degraded snapshot. #249 MuskanPaliwal SUPERSEDED: #219 is fixed on main by f22e6c95 'fix(verify): derive only commands the repository can actually run (#261)' (2026-09-23, ancestor of main, body names #219 AND #203). Bug reproduces at the PR's merge-base, GONE on main. PR would also regress: picks the NEAREST ancestor gradlew then points it up with -p .., running the root build with a nested wrapper (wrong Gradle version). Salvage: the name/setName project-rename check (main only checks projectDir). #265 aniruddhaadak80 REAL BUG, BROKEN AS SUBMITTED: --setup is the one comparability input main never records; fix direction right, but verifyBaselineFormatVersion 1->2 breaks 3 tests (outputpath_test.go:202/463/1049 - VERIFIED FAILING by me). Write-side guard UNFAILABLE: deleting `Setup: flags.Setup` keeps the new test green. Precedent 5c3cf40d used omitempty, no version bump, and updated help.go. #267 aniruddhaadak80 CLEAN - the only one mergeable as-is. Main silently ignores --pre-edit-baseline when --record-baseline is set. Nits only (no t.Parallel, no CHANGELOG). #269 aniruddhaadak80 REAL BUG, FIX OVERREACHES. Verified by direct probe of splitPreflightCommandLine: headline fix WORKS (`--test \\\"go test ./...\\\"` parses), but it adopts POSIX UNQUOTED backslash escaping: `--repo C:\\\\work\\\\repo` -> C:workrepo; `--repo C:\\\\repo\\\\ --query x` -> [\\\"--repo\\\" \\\"C:repo --query\\\" \\\"x\\\"] with err=nil, so --query is SWALLOWED and doctor records an `asserted_command_line` it never checked (false approve); `4\\\\096` -> 4096 passes a malformed number main rejects; `--query don't` now FAILS 'unterminated quote' where main passed. ALSO: #269's parent IS #267's head - merging #269 merges #267. MY CORRECTIONS TO AGENT CLAIMS: (1) #237's duplicate case is NOT in the PR (PR has 1, main has 1) - the merge creates it silently, which is worse. (2) 'risk.go is the only emoji producer, 0 hits elsewhere' is WRONG: risk.go is the only PICTOGRAPHIC emoji producer in prod code, but 24 dingbat chars already ship in 5 prod files (verify_parse.go 17x checkmarks, index.go+root.go warning sign, setup_ui.go, impact_progress.go). CI NEVER RAN on #232/#233/#235/#237/#249/#265/#267/#269 = fork-approval gate, NOT missing workflows (test.yml dates 2026-05-28, triggers on plain pull_request:; later fork PRs #343/#351/#357 got 30-38 checks once approved). One click fixes it for the ones worth testing. *** STILL BLOCKING: evisdren's 2026-11-05 proposal to DELETE `graph verify` (~4,960 prod LoC) moots #237/#249/#265/#267/#269 = 5 of the 9. USER DECISION. *** Nothing pushed, nothing commented, nothing merged, nothing closed.\"","     }","   ]"," }"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2ca993ee-9691-46be-aac4-ee92afa88c8a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":268},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv"