{"parentUuid":"ee75ee5a-9cf2-457f-80c4-70554c85f2d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgnLmwNhDAsYVF3eQp6QY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P1QV6cmfBTFKQFZ1ztZYBc","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Triage cli fork PRs batch A","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","prompt":"Triage 12 external fork PRs on github repo `entireio/cli` (the Go `entire` CLI). Repo checkout: /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli (branch main). READ-ONLY TASK.\n\nPRs: 799, 1210, 1386, 1394, 1396, 1579, 1633, 1643, 1698, 1708, 1803, 1879\n\nHARD RULES (violating these is a failure):\n- NEVER push, comment, close, merge, approve, or review on GitHub. No `gh pr comment/review/merge/close/edit`. Read-only `gh` only.\n- NEVER commit in /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli. It may hold uncommitted work. Do not `git stash`, do not `git checkout` branches there. If you need a build tree, make a worktree under /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/cli-triage-A/ off origin/main.\n- Do NOT run `mise run test:e2e` or `mise run check` (they cost money / run real agents).\n- Use RTK (the hook rewrites git/ls/grep automatically; don't fight it).\n- No full-suite `go test ./...`. If you must run a test, use `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test -p 1 -parallel 1 -count=1 -run '<narrow>' ./internal/<pkg>/`.\n\nPER-PR PROTOCOL (do all five, in order):\n1. `gh pr view N --repo entireio/cli --json title,body,author,createdAt,additions,deletions,changedFiles,mergeable,statusCheckRollup` and `gh pr diff N --repo entireio/cli`. For diffs over ~800 changed lines, do NOT read every line: judge the stated claim + scope, and say you sampled.\n2. **Does the bug still exist on main TODAY?** These PRs are 3-7 months old. Many are already fixed. Find the code it touches on current main and check. Look for a later commit that fixed it: `git log --oneline -20 -- <path>` and `git log --all --grep '<keyword>' --oneline | head`. This is the single most important step — a PR fixing an already-fixed bug is SUPERSEDED, not good.\n3. Is the fix itself correct and minimal? Specifically look for: scope creep (a bug fix carrying an unrelated feature), a guard that cannot fail (delete the fix line, would its own new test still pass?), changed behaviour nobody asked for, and whether it has tests.\n4. CI: how many check runs ran? Zero check runs on a fork PR means nobody clicked \"Approve and run\" — report that as \"CI never ran\", NOT as failing.\n5. Verdict, one of exactly: GOOD / NEEDS-WORK / SUPERSEDED / OUT-OF-SCOPE / TRASH\n   - GOOD = real bug, correct minimal fix, has a test, mergeable as-is\n   - NEEDS-WORK = real bug, fix broken/overreaching/untested\n   - SUPERSEDED = already fixed on main\n   - OUT-OF-SCOPE = works but is an unrequested feature / product decision, not a fix\n   - TRASH = not a real bug, or the fix is wrong, or AI slop with no substance\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT — caveman-ultra compressed, this exact shape, nothing else:\n```\nN | VERDICT | <=22 words why | EVIDENCE: <one command output, commit sha, or file:line that proves it> | CI: <n checks|never ran>\n```\nOne line per PR, 12 lines. Then at most 5 lines under `FLAG:` naming PRs whose verdict would change a merge decision and that you are less than confident about, with the exact thing I should re-verify myself.\n\nNo preamble, no summary paragraph, no markdown headings beyond what is specified. Dense factual lines only."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3988,"cache_read_input_tokens":139749,"output_tokens":10923,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1812},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3988,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10923,"cache_read_input_tokens":13