NTEXT I ALREADY ESTABLISHED (do not redo, do not contradict without evidence):\n- #605 (Beehtrix) is the brain half of entire-graph#392. I verified both halves today: brain main's `factmerge/identity.go:21` has `factPathPattern = ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*(\\.[a-z0-9_]+){2}$`, so the \"lowercase letters, digits, underscores, no hyphens\" rule it documents is REAL, and brain main already says \"code inspection tools\". Its companion graph PR builds clean with a mutation-proven test. So for #605 your job is only: does it break anything else, is the `remember --help` / facts_write_cmd change correct, and does `tools/integration` guide-parity actually run.\n- Brain removed its MCP surface in v0.4.0 (PR #509 removed `entire brain mcp`), so any PR that deletes stale `brain_*` MCP references is factually right to do so.\n- Brain's semantic retrieval was removed (trail #278); `query`/`search` are BM25 lexical, not vector search. #583 claims the agent guide still advertises removed semantic retrieval — verify that against brain main's guide text, and check whether #583 and #605 collide (both edit the agent guide / internal/agentsetup).\n\nPER-PR PROTOCOL:\n1. `gh pr view N --repo entireio/entire-brain --json title,body,author,createdAt,additions,deletions,changedFiles,mergeable,statusCheckRollup` and `gh pr diff N --repo entireio/entire-brain`.\n2. **Does the bug still exist on brain main TODAY?** #367/#368 are from 2026-10-14 and show mergeable=UNKNOWN, which often means a stale/rotten branch. Check `git log --oneline -20 -- <path>` on origin/main for a later fix.\n3. Is the fix correct and minimal? Look for scope creep, a guard that cannot fail, and whether tests exist and actually pin the fix.\n4. CI: count check runs. Zero on a fork PR = nobody clicked \"Approve and run\" (report \"CI never ran\", not failing).\n5. Verdict, exactly one of: GOOD / NEEDS-WORK / SUPERSEDED / OUT-OF-SCOPE / TRASH\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT — caveman-ultra compressed, this exact shape, nothing else:\n```\nN | VERDICT | <=22 words why | EVIDENCE: <one command output, commit sha, or file:line that proves it> | CI: <n checks|never ran>\n```\nOne line per PR, 8 lines. Then at most 4 lines under `FLAG:` for verdicts you are less than confident about, naming the exact thing I should re-verify. Then one line `COLLIDE:` stating whether #583 and #605 edit the same guide text and would conflict.\n\nNo preamble, no summary paragraph. Dense factual lines only."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"fdd8a68a-b0f0-4ea1-bf5a-18af30c46eb1","apiBlockIndex":7,"requestId":"req_011CgnLmvtBw8SGY3BpHM3QU","requestRef":"65e95dd7-b677-4c07-a53d-a9029d207fa7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8e1ffc21-b111-4f26-83ae-2ce63cc4cb4c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T20:57:48.040Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
