ly `gh` only.\n- NEVER commit in /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli. It may hold uncommitted work. Do not `git stash`, do not `git checkout` branches there. If you need a build tree, make a worktree under /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/cli-triage-D/ off origin/main.\n- Do NOT run `mise run test:e2e` or `mise run check` (they cost money / run real agents).\n- Use RTK (the hook rewrites git/ls/grep automatically; don't fight it).\n- No full-suite `go test ./...`. If you must run a test, use `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test -p 1 -parallel 1 -count=1 -run '<narrow>' ./internal/<pkg>/`.\n\nPER-PR PROTOCOL (do all five, in order):\n1. `gh pr view N --repo entireio/cli --json title,body,author,createdAt,additions,deletions,changedFiles,mergeable,statusCheckRollup` and `gh pr diff N --repo entireio/cli`. For diffs over ~800 changed lines, do NOT read every line: judge the stated claim + scope, and say you sampled.\n2. **Does the bug still exist on main TODAY?** These PRs are 1-2 months old. Some are already fixed. Find the code it touches on current main and check. Look for a later commit that fixed it: `git log --oneline -20 -- <path>` and `git log --all --grep '<keyword>' --oneline | head`. This is the single most important step — a PR fixing an already-fixed bug is SUPERSEDED, not good.\n3. Is the fix itself correct and minimal? Specifically look for: scope creep, a guard that cannot fail (delete the fix line, would its own new test still pass?), changed behaviour nobody asked for, and whether it has tests. Several of these are tiny (5-80 lines) — for those, the key question is whether the bug is real at all, and whether the test actually pins the fix.\n4. CI: how many check runs ran? Zero check runs on a fork PR means nobody clicked \"Approve and run\" — report that as \"CI never ran\", NOT as failing.\n5. Verdict, one of exactly: GOOD / NEEDS-WORK / SUPERSEDED / OUT-OF-SCOPE / TRASH\n   - GOOD = real bug, correct minimal fix, has a test, mergeable as-is\n   - NEEDS-WORK = real bug, fix broken/overreaching/untested\n   - SUPERSEDED = already fixed on main\n   - OUT-OF-SCOPE = works but is an unrequested feature / product decision, not a fix\n   - TRASH = not a real bug, or the fix is wrong, or AI slop with no substance\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT — caveman-ultra compressed, this exact shape, nothing else:\n```\nN | VERDICT | <=22 words why | EVIDENCE: <one command output, commit sha, or file:line that proves it> | CI: <n checks|never ran>\n```\nOne line per PR, 12 lines. Then at most 5 lines under `FLAG:` naming PRs whose verdict would change a merge decision and that you are less than confident about, with the exact thing I should re-verify myself.\n\nNo preamble, no summary paragraph, no markdown headings beyond what is specified. Dense factual lines only.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d/tasks/acf26b4426ad9becb.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fdd8a68a-b0f0-4ea1-bf5a-18af30c46eb1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"name":"suhaanthayyil","host":"github.com","remote":"suhaanthayyil/cli","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5