{"parentUuid":"8e1ffc21-b111-4f26-83ae-2ce63cc4cb4c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cc1505eb-cca7-441c-90f1-4bdb109c2f57","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ea4mWUDqYGP4cbPms8vRpp","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a3ef2ef5cdbb15ed7 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a3ef2ef5cdbb15ed7', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d/tasks/a3ef2ef5cdbb15ed7.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"327cbc1a-61d5-4452-9564-d15b1d0c752f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T20:57:49.412Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a3ef2ef5cdbb15ed7","description":"Triage brain fork PRs","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"Triage 8 external fork PRs on github repo `entireio/entire-brain` (the Go `entire-brain` plugin). Repo checkout: /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain. READ-ONLY TASK.\n\nPRs: 367, 368, 554, 581, 583, 601, 605, 606\n\nHARD RULES (violating these is a failure):\n- NEVER push, comment, close, merge, approve, or review on GitHub. No `gh pr comment/review/merge/close/edit`. Read-only `gh` only. Another session owns this repo's lane — do not modify anything in it.\n- NEVER commit in /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain. It is on a detached HEAD at e6bb5c42 and may hold uncommitted work. Do not `git stash`, do not `git checkout`. If you need a build tree, make a worktree under /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/brain-triage/ off origin/main.\n- NEVER run `entire brain setup` or `entire brain refresh`, and never touch ~/.local/share/entire. Brain test isolation requires ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR plus a locally built binary; never `--daemon`, never the real store.\n- Use RTK. No full-suite `go test ./...`. Narrow runs only: `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test -p 1 -parallel 1 -count=1 -run '<narrow>' ./internal/<pkg>/`.\n\nCONTEXT I ALREADY ESTABLISHED (do not redo, do not contradict without evidence):\n- #605 (Beehtrix) is the brain half of entire-graph#392. I verified both halves today: brain main's `factmerge/identity.go:21` has `factPathPattern = ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*(\\.[a-z0-9_]+){2}$`, so the \"lowercase letters, digits, underscores, no hyphens\" rule it documents is REAL, and brain main already says \"code inspection tools\". Its companion graph PR builds clean with a mutation-proven test. So for #605 your job is only: does it break anything else, is the `remember --help` / facts_write_cmd change correct, and does `tools/integration` guide-parity actually run.\n- Brain removed its MCP surface in v0.4.0 (PR #509 removed `entire brain mcp`), so any PR that deletes stale `brain_*` MCP references is factually right to do so.\n- Brain's semantic retrieval was removed (trail #278); `query`/`search` are BM25 lexical, not vector search. #583 claims the agent guide still advertises removed semantic retrieval — verify that against brain main's guide text, and check whether #583 and #605 collide (both edit the agent guide / internal/agentsetup).\n\nPER-PR PROTOCOL:\n1. `gh pr view N --repo entireio/entire-brain --json title,body,author,createdAt,additions,deletions,changedFiles,mergeable,statusCheckRollup` and `gh pr diff N --repo entireio/entire-brain`.\n2. **Does the bug still exist on brain main TODAY?** #367/#368 are from 2026-10-14 and show mergeable=UNKNOWN, which often means a stale/rotten branch. Check `git log --oneline -20 -- <path>` on origin/main for a later fix.\n3. Is the fix correct and minimal? Look for scope creep, a guard that cannot fail, and whether tests exist and actually pin the fix.\n4. CI: count check runs. Zero on a fork PR = nobody clicked \"Approve and run\" (report \"CI never ran\", not failing).\n5. Verdict, exactly one of: GOOD / NEEDS-WORK / SUPERSEDED / OUT-OF-SCOPE / TRASH\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT — caveman-ultra compressed, this exact shape, nothing else:\n```\nN | VERDICT | <=22 words why | EVIDENCE: <one command output, commit sha, or file:line that proves it> | CI: <n checks|never ran>\n```\nOne line per PR, 8 lines. Then at most 4 lines under `FLAG:` for verdicts you are less than confident about, naming the exact thing I should re-verify. Then one line `COLLIDE:` stating whether #583 and #605 edit the same guide text and would conflict.\n\nNo preamble, no summary paragraph. Dense factual lines only.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d/tasks/a3ef2ef5cdbb15ed7.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fdd8a68a-b0f0-4ea1-bf5a-18af30c46eb1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"name":"suhaanthayyil","host":"github.com","remote":"suhaanthayyil/cli","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host