{"parentUuid":"2be52657-c161-4114-bfa7-5864e6f50a8a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgnLvJ9psk6rTpPFCgjSa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`#357 got merged yesterday` — 2026-11-05 12:44, without my three fix commits. Those are still sitting unpushed on `fix/357-followups`.\n\nAnd the real scope is much bigger than the graph nine:\n\n- **entire-graph**: 9 open fork PRs\n- **entire-brain**: 8 open fork PRs\n- **cli**: **61** open fork PRs (out of 240 open total)\n\n78 external PRs. I've launched triage on the cli 61 and brain 8. Here's the graph set, which is fully verified.\n\n## entire-graph — 9 open, external\n\n| PR | Author | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| **#392** | Beehtrix | **GOOD** (new today, verified below) |\n| **#267** | aniruddhaadak80 | **GOOD** |\n| #265 | aniruddhaadak80 | Real bug, broken as submitted |\n| #269 | aniruddhaadak80 | Real bug, fix overreaches |\n| #249 | MuskanPaliwal | Superseded, fixed on main in September |\n| #235 | Yashwanthk06 | Needs rework, ranking is inverted |\n| #233 | souzataniya | Split first, in-scope part already built |\n| #237 | saranmahadev | Re-author, compile trap + polluted fixtures |\n| #232 | Shaurya002800 | Close, zero Go lines |\n\n## #392 is the best external PR I've seen on this repo\n\nFixes real cross-repo guide drift. I verified every claim:\n\n- **The `--path` rule is real.** `factmerge/identity.go:21` on brain main: `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*(\\.[a-z0-9_]+){2}$`. Hyphens are rejected and the guide never said so. rodbegbie filed brain issue #588 about exactly this.\n- **The MCP sentence was stale.** Brain removed `entire brain mcp` in v0.4.0, so telling agents `brain_remember` exists was wrong.\n- **\"semantic inspection tools\" → \"code inspection tools\"** matches brain main, which already says \"code\" at `guide.go:306`. Graph was the drifted side.\n- **The stale script reference is right too.** `scripts/test-agent-coordination.py` is gone from brain main; `tools/integration` exists.\n- Builds clean, `internal/agentsetup` green, and **I mutation-proved the new test in both directions** (strip the rule from `guide.go` → red; strip it from `strict.go` → red).\n- `TestCheckedInGuideMatchesInstallerPreview` passes, so the checked-in `.entire/agent-guide.md` matches the renderer.\n- Zero leftover `brain_remember` strings except the CHANGELOG entry describing the removal.\n\nTwo notes, neither blocking:\n- The guide prose drops part of the rule. Brain's own `PathRule` constant also says three segments and \"the first starting with a letter\". The prose is byte-identical to brain #605's prose, so parity holds, but `9x.foo.bar` would still surprise someone.\n- It pairs with **brain #605**, which is open, not merged. The CHANGELOG hedges this correctly (\"a Brain that includes #605\"), so the \"same text either way\" goal isn't reached until #605 lands.\n\n## Still true across every fork PR\n\n**Nobody has ever clicked \"Approve and run\".** #392 has zero check runs, same as the other eight. One click each.\n\ncli and brain triage is running. I'll report those when they land. Nothing pushed, commented, closed or merged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13320,"cache_read_input_tokens":143737,"output_tokens":1649,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":463},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13320,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1649,"cache_read_input_tokens":143737,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13320},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassif