{"parentUuid":"c3ac6fbd-8a88-4f5a-a0a9-65a00e72d37e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14802441 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"aedde064-d553-44b4-a8a8-221c6814b315","timestamp":"2026-11-06T21:14:28.749Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14802441 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"aedde064-d553-44b4-a8a8-221c6814b315","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01Jn2NDYYKMQXrsaoSoUkZGg","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"33ceb58d-adc7-4d66-aacf-7f1dbbdb73e4","timestamp":"2026-11-06T21:14:49.554Z","session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"33ceb58d-adc7-4d66-aacf-7f1dbbdb73e4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgnNBxAc6nkkXDnfxKYep","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**78 open external PRs**, not nine. Here's the sort.\n\n| | count |\n|---|---|\n| **Actually good** | **13** |\n| Real bug, broken fix | 35 |\n| Out of scope (unrequested features) | 16 |\n| Already fixed on main | 10 |\n| Trash | 4 |\n\nSplit: graph 9, brain 8, **cli 61**.\n\n## The 13 worth your time\n\n**I mutation-proved six of these myself.** Patched out the fix, watched the test go red.\n\n| PR | Repo | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| **#2611** | cli | `CheckoutBranch` lacks `--no-overwrite-ignore`, so resume **overwrites your ignored untracked files**. One line. Test red without it. |\n| **#3040** | cli | `setup` hangs forever when a hook opens a git pager. One line (`GIT_PAGER=cat`). The mutated test **hangs 15s then fails**, so the repro is real. Still a DRAFT. |\n| **#2331** | cli | Lefthook silently overwrites Entire's hooks, never flagged. Red in two separate places when mutated. |\n| **#2479** | cli | Two doctor tests fail under ambient `ENTIRE_TEST_TTY=1`. Confirmed: main fails, PR passes. Same class as the `FORCE_COLOR` trap. |\n| **#392** | graph | Guide drift vs brain. Verified across both repos, mutation-proven. |\n| **#267** | graph | `--pre-edit-baseline` silently ignored. |\n\nPlus seven I have not personally run: cli **#2285** (18 green checks already), **#2911**, **#2950**, **#3005**, and brain **#554**, **#605**, **#606**.\n\n## Two corrections to my agents\n\n**brain #605's pinned sha is not orphaned.** The agent said `56f1de69` exists only locally and would break required CI. It's actually **graph #392's own head commit**, fetchable from the base repo as `refs/pull/392/head`. The recommendation still holds for a different reason: it pins brain's required CI to an *unmerged fork PR*. Merge graph #392, then repin to main.\n\n**cli #3005 is bigger than billed.** Sold as one focused fix for the sibling-worktree bug. It's **674 lines across 10 commits, and nine of them are self-corrections** about amend and reflog detection. `withoutIdleSessions` is there and the tests pass, but I'd call it real-and-sprawling, not clean.\n\n## The pattern in the 35 \"real bug, broken fix\"\n\nAlmost all fail the same two ways:\n\n- **Months behind main, conflicting.** The bug is genuine, the patch no longer applies.\n- **Scope creep.** #2996 fixes dropped review findings and **deletes 529 lines** of diagnostics on the way. #2966 bundles an unrelated Windows fix. #799 is seven unrelated changes with zero tests.\n\nAnd four separate stacks, where merging one silently merges others: `2959 → 3003 → 3046`, `3005 → 3034`, `2285 → 2305 → 2320`, and graph `#267 → #269`.\n\n## The 16 out-of-scope ones aren't bad code\n\nThey're product decisions nobody made: #1633 is a 3,600-line Linear integration, #2077 adds Goose and Qwen (**its own issue was closed NOT_PLANNED by the author**), #2161 wires in a vendor's API. #2131/#2190/#2320 are 1,800-3,900 line refactors of shared git code with 30+ conflicts each.\n\n## Two things I need\n\n**1. CI has never been approved on a single fork PR.** Not one of the 78. That's one click each and it would turn 78 unknowns into 78 signals.\n\n**2. Permission to keep running fork tests.** The classifier blocked `go test` on external PR code mid-sweep (`[Code from External]`). It's a fair guard. I got six proven before it fired; #2911 and #2950 are merged clean in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/cli-verify` and ready to verify the moment you say go.\n\nAlso: **graph #357 merged yesterday without my three fix commits.** Still unpushed on `fix/357-followups`. Pushing those needs your go-ahead too.\n\nI pushed nothing, commented nowhere, merged nothing, closed nothing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3289,"cache_read_input_tokens":194307,"output_tokens":1469,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3289,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1469,"cache_read_input_tokens":194307,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3289},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c094e4bf-822d-4f10-9492-2f6eccd1c15f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgnNBwsVqRMXgh6B5LyAJ","requestRef":"e918b88c-d24a-49d7-91e0-302e2f88644f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2d370a62-ad09-4993-a164-78da12a0dc96","timestamp":"2026-11-06T21:14:49.553Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
