{"parentUuid":"a1219ce6-ce05-4e17-a197-fff75858d94c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgnPpLzusH7cz658xX5g8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":929,"cache_read_input_tokens":206329,"output_tokens":4001,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2019},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":929,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4001,"cache_read_input_tokens":206329,"cache_creation_input_tokens":929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":929},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":29712,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"98dadb36-9014-4dcd-9705-8b986e7b2a98","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgnPpLdaiHj4ReVKJzoKg","requestRef":"9c52d7da-0022-46e9-891a-e24cc414a970","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a6c364c1-ca1d-40c2-acd0-2a54d5786ab1","timestamp":"2026-11-06T21:36:20.608Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"a6c364c1-ca1d-40c2-acd0-2a54d5786ab1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgnPpLzusH7cz658xX5g8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Got it. Sorting by whether the **problem** deserves solving, patch quality aside. The hard evidence: whether a maintainer already filed that exact issue.\n\n## Tier 1: the maintainers' own open issues, fixed by outsiders\n\nThese aren't opinions. Someone on the team filed the issue, an outside contributor went and solved it.\n\n| PR | Targets | Filed by | The problem |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| graph **#265** | issue #222 | **you** | `--setup` is the one comparability input a baseline never records, so you adjudicate against a different setup and never know |\n| cli **#2713** | #2637 (**assigned**) | peyton-alt | `commit --amend -m` drops the Entire-Checkpoint trailer, no link repair |\n| cli **#2199** / **#2277** | #2197 | Soph | persistent-ref lock files accumulate one per checkpoint and nothing ever reaps them |\n| cli **#2099** | #2091 | Soph | hook latency, the remaining work after #2002 |\n| cli **#2385** | #2378 | MuskanPaliwal | cleanup can make uncondensed checkpoint commits unreachable |\n| graph **#233** | #273 | **you** | confidence and resolution are never surfaced, so an agent can't tell \"no consumers\" from \"unresolved\" |\n\ngraph #265 is the standout. You filed #222, aniruddhaadak80 found it and fixed it. The patch is broken, the idea is yours.\n\n## Tier 2: silent data loss\n\nConcept value is highest here because the failure is invisible.\n\n- **cli #2611** — `checkout` overwrites your ignored untracked files. Already good code too.\n- **cli #2358** — post-push cleanup deletes an uncondensed shadow ref when its state is malformed. Live data, gone.\n- **cli #3015** — checkpoint replay **reports success after dropping another clone's session.** Success plus data loss is the worst combination in the list.\n- **cli #2395** — git-refs writes return success without durable push bookkeeping.\n- **graph #269** — doctor records an `asserted_command_line` it never actually checked. A preflight that quietly approves.\n- **cli #2103** — transcript images capped before externalization, so content is lost.\n\n## Tier 3: capture gaps, which is the product's one job\n\n- **cli #2911** — `git commit -q` makes import anchor the turn to the tip instead of the real commit\n- **cli #3005** — a sibling worktree's session idle for days gets linked to every commit, 5GB condense\n- **cli #2027** — OpenCode user prompts lost when message events arrive in the wrong order\n- **cli #3034** — commit keeps a trailer naming a checkpoint that was never written\n- **cli #2996** — `entire review` silently drops findings when session matching fails\n- **brain #581** — history rebuild races checkpoint finalize\n\n## Tier 4: one architectural problem, three PRs circling it\n\n**cli #2959, #3003, #3046, plus #2966.** Entire and entire-brain both wrap the same git hook and rotate each other out of the chain. Doctor miscounts, uninstall leaves a hook behind, re-wrapping drops the user's own pre-push.\n\nThe concept is clearly real and nobody owns it. Every one of these patches has the CLI pattern-match brain's exact wrapper text, which is the wrong layer. The right fix is probably a marker brain writes. **Worth a design decision, not three merges.**\n\n## Tier 5: trust and expectation bugs\n\n- **brain #606** → issue #570, \"Global memories never reach a second machine.\" Users believe global memories sync. They don't.\n- **cli #2684** — keep prompts out of checkpoints. Filed as a feature, but it's really a privacy question some customers will force. Worth a decision either way.\n- **brain #583**, graph **#392**, brain **#605** — the guide tells agents to use features that were deleted, and omits the `--path` rule, so agents burn turns on retries. Cheap, real.\n\n## Worth having but narrow\n\n#1708 (WSL can't open a browser to log in), #2552 (resume fails on NFC/NFD branch names), #3040 (setup hangs on a pager), #2275 (`disable` never reaches linked worktrees), #2621 (commit linking grabs an unrelated session), #1579, #2585, #1879, #2331.\n\n## Ideas not worth having\n\n- **cli #1633** Linear ticket integration, 3,600 lines, nobody asked\n- **cli #2077** Goose and Qwen support. **The author closed their own issue NOT_PLANNED.**\n- **cli #2161** OrcaRouter, a vendor wiring their API in\n- **cli #1993** flutter-doctor-style sweep\n- **graph #237** GPS, six new top-level commands\n- **graph #232** a Python FastAPI app with zero Go\n- **cli #799**, **#2501**, **#2724**, **#2479**. #2479's code is correct and I proved it works, but conceptually it's pure test hygiene.\n- The refactor pile (#2131, #2190, #2320, #2053, #2285, #2305). No user-visible problem at all.\n\n## Two things that reframe this\n\n**Most of these people filed the issue themselves, then fixed it.** Beehtrix, aniruddhaadak80, ChetanReddyC, KC1706, Puneet-Pal-Singh, sidsharma96, hummbl-dev, levelorbit. That's a user hitting a real bug and reporting it, which is the opposite of a drive-by PR. The three I'd actually close (#232, #233's leaderboard half, #237) are all Bengaluru Tech Week Buildathon submissions filed within an hour of each other.\n\n**MuskanPaliwal is an org member**, just submitting from a fork. So they aren't an external contributor, which means several of those big refactors are internal work I mislabeled as external in the previous list."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":929,"cache_read_input_tokens":206329,"output_tokens":4001,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2019},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":929,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4001,"cache_read_input_tokens":206329,"cache_creation_input_tokens":929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":929},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"98dadb36-9014-4dcd-9705-8b986e7b2a98","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgnPpLdaiHj4ReVKJzoKg","requestRef":"9c52d7da-0022-46e9-891a-e24cc414a970","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4d8e42f2-36f6-4dd8-802f-c96cfcc026ae","timestamp":"2026-11-06T21:36:44.024Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
