{"parentUuid":"9369065a-a5b9-4754-95a6-3b835f8e75c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgpgYWEagTLHJGCxaxhEV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1786,"cache_read_input_tokens":119190,"output_tokens":2002,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":960},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1786,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2002,"cache_read_input_tokens":119190,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1786},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":14197,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"18ab9150-360a-4b17-976e-64f54bfc0bda","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgpgYW1Se9GgAYr2bz6Us","requestRef":"86b7fa6d-a346-4f93-bbbd-35d14ef095a4","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c79f4e45-569e-48af-8766-01a8267abfee","timestamp":"2026-11-08T02:36:36.970Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"c79f4e45-569e-48af-8766-01a8267abfee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgpgYWEagTLHJGCxaxhEV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed: `peyton-alt` and `Soph` (Stefan Haubold) are both org members. Neither authored any of these, so the list doesn't change. One new one landed an hour ago though: **#394 by rodbegbie**, external.\n\n## External-contributor PRs on entire-graph, ranked by concept\n\n| PR | Author | Size | What it's actually trying to fix | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **#265** | aniruddhaadak80 | +30 | Baseline records every comparability input **except `--setup`**, so verify adjudicates two runs that aren't comparable and says nothing. **Your issue #222.** | **good** |\n| **#394** | rodbegbie | +561 | `grammar-refresh` can only copy upstream's generated files, so #357's hand-applied Swift patch is unreproducible and dies on the next refresh. Makes the tool do the patch + regen. | **good** |\n| **#269** | aniruddhaadak80 | +109 | `doctor --assert` splits quoted args, so it can't parse its own help-text examples. Writes an `asserted_command_line` it never checked. | **good** |\n| **#267** | aniruddhaadak80 | +19 | `--record-baseline` silently ignores `--pre-edit-baseline`. You ask for a delta, you get \"BASELINE RECORDED\" and exit 0. | **good** |\n| **#392** | Beehtrix | +71 | Agent guide says `remember --path` without the lowercase/underscore rule, and advertises `brain_remember`, deleted in brain 0.4.0. Agents burn turns guessing. | **good**, small |\n| **#235** | Yashwanthk06 | +1016 | Rank what a changeset puts at risk. Real gap, nothing on main does it. | **concept yes, patch no** — ranks by short-name frequency, so `err` and `n` top the list, 700/705 entities dropped |\n| **#233** | souzataniya | +3120 | Two things in one PR. Evidence state on results = **your issue #273**. The rest is a `graph rank` dev leaderboard. | **half** — split it |\n| **#237** | saranmahadev | +5796 | Six new top-level commands for requirement traceability. | **no** — product decision nobody made |\n| **#232** | Shaurya002800 | +20387 | Python FastAPI app, 2.1 MB media, **0 Go lines**. | **no** |\n\n**Excluded as internal:** #249 (MuskanPaliwal), #152/#391 (ashtom), #388 (prichodko), plus dependabot. All org members, even the fork ones.\n\n**The read:** aniruddhaadak80 is your best outside bug-finder on this repo. Three PRs, three silent-wrong-answer bugs in `verify`/`doctor`, two with their own issues filed first. rodbegbie is your best outside engineer. #394 is the only external PR here that picks up someone else's merged work and closes the gap it left.\n\n#232, #233, #237 are all Bengaluru Tech Week Buildathon submissions from the same hour on 6 Sept."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1786,"cache_read_input_tokens":119190,"output_tokens":2002,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":960},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1786,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2002,"cache_read_input_tokens":119190,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1786},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"18ab9150-360a-4b17-976e-64f54bfc0bda","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgpgYW1Se9GgAYr2bz6Us","requestRef":"86b7fa6d-a346-4f93-bbbd-35d14ef095a4","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3788ab43-ce2a-4db1-b34b-c0bce641b818","timestamp":"2026-11-08T02:36:48.605Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-