{"parentUuid":"49ba1df4-a888-4cc6-b724-e76da1143e0b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgphBDR5RWVoAfDo5byET","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Green: 17/17, and `verify.go` is back to the PR's own state (diff shows only my two test files)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":875,"cache_read_input_tokens":148019,"output_tokens":1209,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":591},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":875,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1209,"cache_read_input_tokens":148019,"cache_creation_input_tokens":875,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":875},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"388ca65f-371b-4661-a88f-2fd37b4f9f84","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgphBD4VfNFmNMHrp6zQq","requestRef":"10ef9ef7-63cb-4362-bbcb-f7836383eea1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e517cf60-9622-40b2-83f5-3ce3547c166f","timestamp":"2026-11-08T02:44:50.654Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"e517cf60-9622-40b2-83f5-3ce3547c166f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgphBDR5RWVoAfDo5byET","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018cZiAB6oeRoWKBJ4UDerjG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-265-fix && git config user.name && git config user.email && git add -A internal/cli && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest(verify): cover the setup baseline on both sides\n\n#265's concept is right: a baseline records every comparability input except\nthe setup command, so verify adjudicates two runs that were prepared by\ndifferent commands and reports a delta that means nothing (issue #222).\n\nTwo things kept it from landing.\n\nThe bump of verifyBaselineFormatVersion to 2 is correct — a v1 baseline has\nno setup field, so it reads as \"\" and mismatches any real --setup — but three\ntests in outputpath_test.go asserted the literal `\"format_version\": 1` and\nwent red. They assert \"this file is the recorded JSON\", not \"the format is\nversion 1\", so they now read the constant through one derived variable.\n\nThe write side was unfailable. TestVerifyRefusesBaselineWithDifferentSetup\nrecords with one --setup and reruns with another, so it passes even when\nwriteVerifyBaseline stops recording Setup at all: the recorded \"\" mismatches\nthe rerun either way. Removing the assignment leaves that test green, which\nis how this was found. The new round-trip test covers that direction — same\n--setup must be accepted, and the recorded JSON must name the command.\n\nMutation-proven in both directions: dropping the write assignment reds only\nthe new test, dropping the read comparison reds only the original.\nMSG\necho \"=== committed ===\"; git log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the 265 fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":875,"cache_read_input_tokens":148019,"output_tokens":1209,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":591},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":875,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1209,"cache_read_input_tokens":148019,"cache_creation_input_tokens":875,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":875},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018cZiAB6oeRoWKBJ4UDerjG":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-265-fix && git config user.name && git config user.email && git add -A internal/cli && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest(verify): cover the setup baseline on both sides\n\n#265's concept is right: a baseline records every comparability input except\nthe setup command, so verify adjudicates two runs that were prepared by\ndifferent commands and reports a delta that means nothing (issue #222).\n\nTwo things kept it from landing.\n\nThe bump of verifyBaselineFormatVersion to 2 is correct — a v1 baseline has\nno setup field, so it reads as \"\" and mismatches any real --setup — but three\ntests in outputpath_test.go asserted the literal `\"format_version\": 1` and\nwent red. They assert \"this file is the recorded JSON\", not \"the format is\nversion 1\", so they now read the constant through one derived variable.\n\nThe write side was unfailable. TestVerifyRefusesBaselineWithDifferentSetup\nrecords with one --setup and reruns with another, so it passes even when\nwriteVerifyBaseline stops recording Setup at all: the recorded \"\" mismatches\nthe rerun either way. Removing the assignment leaves that test green, which\nis how this was found. The new round-trip test covers that direction — same\n--setup must be accepted, and the recorded JSON must name the command.\n\nMutation-proven in both directions: dropping the write assignment reds only\nthe new test, dropping the read comparison reds only the original.\nMSG\necho \"=== committed ===\"; git log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the 265 fix"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"388ca65f-371b-4661-a88f-2fd37b4f9f84","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgphBD4VfNFmNMHrp6zQq","requestRef":"10ef9ef7-63cb-4362-bbcb-f7836383eea1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"31119cb6-feca-4b3b-82e8-ebba9552e019","timestamp":"2026-11-08T02:44:55.810Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
