{"parentUuid":"5a0a9734-0325-4d08-8525-2eb20fd2b454","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgphEkBqmrHWsLRBYsXXx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#265 fixed.** Nothing merged, nothing pushed. Branch `fix/265-setup-baseline` in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-265-fix`, aniruddhaadak80's commit kept with their authorship, my fix on top.\n\nTwo things were wrong, both now proven:\n\n- **3 tests asserted the literal `\"format_version\": 1`.** The bump to 2 is *correct* (a v1 baseline has no `setup` field, so it reads as `\"\"` and mismatches any real `--setup`). The tests were checking \"this file is the recorded JSON\", not \"the version is 1\" — they now read the constant. I reverted my change and ran them to confirm all 3 really did go red on the PR as submitted.\n- **The write side was unfailable.** The PR's own test records with one `--setup` and reruns with another, so it passes even if `writeVerifyBaseline` stops recording `Setup` entirely — `\"\"` mismatches either way. Added a round-trip test for that direction.\n\nMutation-proven both ways:\n- drop the write assignment → only my new test reds, PR's test **stays green**\n- drop the read comparison → only the PR's test reds\n\n17/17 focused tests pass, `go vet` clean, no mutation residue in the worktree.\n\n**Loop armed, self-paced.** Next tick (~25 min) is **#269** — its fix overreaches into POSIX unquoted-backslash escaping and mangles Windows paths (`--repo C:\\work\\repo` → `C:workrepo`), so the concept is right but the splitter needs narrowing. Then #235's ranking, then splitting #233.\n\nOne thing I'll need you for: a classifier denial blocked a compound test command mid-run (no reason given, same as the earlier `[Code from External]` block). Single commands work, so I'm unblocked for now — but if it starts refusing plain `go test` on fork code, I'll stop and hand it back rather than work around it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"