{"parentUuid":"f4b76d2c-ec17-447d-a076-7e4f0dacf3d9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgpjT1eaiU6bRwXCfZXBc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SgpW16vdM6yMdGyt42rRBu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-269-fix && git add -A internal/cli && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(preflight): a backslash outside quotes is an ordinary character\n\n#269's concept is right: doctor --assert split on strings.Fields, so it could\nnot parse the quoted examples in its own help text, and it recorded an\nasserted_command_line it had never actually checked (issue #268).\n\nThe splitter it added reaches too far. Outside quotes it treats a backslash as\na POSIX escape, and --assert carries a command line, not a shell line, so an\nunquoted Windows path is a normal input. Measured on the submitted patch:\n\n  search --repo C:\\work\\repo        -> [\"search\" \"--repo\" \"C:workrepo\"]\n  search --repo C:\\repo\\ --query x  -> [\"search\" \"--repo\" \"C:repo --query\" \"x\"]\n\nThe first silently rewrites the path. The second is worse: the escaped space\nmerges two arguments into one, returns no error, and the preflight then\napproves a command line the caller never wrote, which is the same class of\nsilent false approval the PR set out to fix.\n\nDropping that one branch fixes both. Quoting still works, which is the part\nstrings.Fields could not express, and inside double quotes a backslash still\nescapes \", \\, $ and ` while anything else is kept verbatim, so quoted paths\nsurvive too. The PR's trailing-backslash test case asserted the broken\nbehaviour and is replaced by the round-trip it should have pinned.\n\nMutation-proven in three directions: restoring the unquoted escape reds only\nthe new test, treating quotes as ordinary characters reds both tests, and\nremoving the unterminated-quote refusal reds the original.\nMSG\necho \"=== stack ===\"; git log --oneline -4","description":"Commit the 269 fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1000,"cache_read_input_tokens":169293,"output_tokens":781,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":106},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1000,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":781,"cache_read_input_tokens":169293,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1000},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SgpW16vdM6yMdGyt42rRBu":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-269-fix && git add -A internal/cli && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(preflight): a backslash outside quotes is an ordinary character\n\n#269's concept is right: doctor --assert split on strings.Fields, so it could\nnot parse the quoted examples in its own help text, and it recorded an\nasserted_command_line it had never actually checked (issue #268).\n\nThe splitter it added reaches too far. Outside quotes it treats a backslash as\na POSIX escape, and --assert carries a command line, not a shell line, so an\nunquoted Windows path is a normal input. Measured on the submitted patch:\n\n  search --repo C:\\work\\repo        -> [\"search\" \"--repo\" \"C:workrepo\"]\n  search --repo C:\\repo\\ --query x  -> [\"search\" \"--repo\" \"C:repo --query\" \"x\"]\n\nThe first silently rewrites the path. The second is worse: the escaped space\nmerges two arguments into one, returns no error, and the preflight then\napproves a command line the caller never wrote, which is the same class of\nsilent false approval the PR set out to fix.\n\nDropping that one branch fixes both. Quoting still works, which is the part\nstrings.Fields could not express, and inside double quotes a backslash still\nescapes \", \\, $ and ` while anything else is kept verbatim, so quoted paths\nsurvive too. The PR's trailing-backslash test case asserted the broken\nbehaviour and is replaced by the round-trip it should have pinned.\n\nMutation-proven in three directions: restoring the unquoted escape reds only\nthe new test, treating quotes as ordinary characters reds both tests, and\nremoving the unterminated-quote refusal reds the original.\nMSG\necho \"=== stack ===\"; git log --oneline -4","description":"Commit the 269 fix"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5faaaeb8-9844-43be-8141-3c402705c4b0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgpjT1BJoPeiTq5hMEhWh","requestRef":"a6d6ee35-4a4d-4eac-855f-9c2dcc3664f8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","attributionSkill":"loop","type":"assistant","uuid":"be9a8080-7439-4c02-bd77-1f45ea52bd0c","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:14:37.983Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
