{"parentUuid":"27b7750e-f400-4773-ad0f-c75929f881b1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgpjVufF8wLDVVdSF9yvf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#269 fixed.** Branch `fix/269-preflight-quoting` in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-269-fix`. Nothing merged, nothing pushed.\n\nUseful discovery: **#269 already contains #267** (it's stacked on it), so #267 needs no separate fix — both commits cherry-picked onto the branch with authorship preserved.\n\nI reproduced the overreach live before touching it, rather than trusting my earlier read:\n\n```\nsearch --repo C:\\work\\repo        -> [\"search\" \"--repo\" \"C:workrepo\"]\nsearch --repo C:\\repo\\ --query x  -> [\"search\" \"--repo\" \"C:repo --query\" \"x\"]\n```\n\nThe second is the bad one: the escaped space merges two arguments, returns **no error**, and the preflight then approves a command line nobody wrote. Same silent-false-approval class the PR set out to fix.\n\nFix is one deleted branch — a backslash outside quotes is an ordinary character. Quoting still works (the part `strings.Fields` couldn't do), and inside double quotes `\\\"`, `\\\\`, `\\$`, `` \\` `` still escape while everything else stays verbatim, so quoted paths survive too. The PR's trailing-backslash test case asserted the broken behaviour, so it's replaced by the round-trip it should have pinned.\n\nThree mutations, three directions:\n- restore the unquoted escape → only my test reds\n- quotes become ordinary chars → **both** tests red (quoting genuinely held)\n- drop the unterminated-quote refusal → the PR's test reds\n\n26 pass / 1 skip, and static count 27 matches, so the `-run` filter isn't hiding anything. `go vet` clean.\n\n**Next tick (~25 min): #235.** That one's different in kind — not a small correction but replacing the ranking signal, since `DependentsCount = len(index[shortEntityName(change)])` is a name-frequency count that put `err` and `n` in the top 5 of 705 entities and dropped 700. I'll treat it as a rewrite behind the PR's concept, and if the honest answer is \"the patch can't be salvaged, only the idea\", I'll say that instead of forcing it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":424,"cache_read_input_tokens":171980,"output_tokens":733,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":424,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":733,"cache_read_input_tokens":171980,"cache_creation_input_tokens":424,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":424},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"cff79dd4-9a71-417b-92c7-8360afdc996d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgpjVuMtz4zAMSSyFBZe6","requestRef":"798d3e1a-9548-4efe-9f9f-3ec168eba027","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","attributionSkill":"loop","type":"assistant","uuid":"14da269e-8f7b-4fc0-adf8-401889b07b43","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:15:16.394Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
