{"parentUuid":"c2f471f7-9879-49b8-bf0e-e0ef1af30992","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14909163 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6c8eb243-b7e7-4660-95c5-60e9d2908edd","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:46:18.856Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14909163 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"6c8eb243-b7e7-4660-95c5-60e9d2908edd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgpmstrUxL5Dd5RnWgtYe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C6agzwEcsWVJ93MH8iRQGQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-235-fix && git add -A internal/cli && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(risk): preselect by change type, not by a short-name reference count\n\n#235's concept holds up: nothing on main answers \"what does this changeset put\nat risk\", and the report it builds — per-entity callers, type consumers and\nsuggested tests, with an overall verdict — is the right shape for it.\n\nThe preselection inverted it. --max-entities bounds the expensive step, the\nper-entity impact evidence, so whatever orders the candidates decides which\nentities ever get measured. That ordering led with DependentsCount, which is\nsem's SHORT-NAME reference count (internal/sem/dependents.go: referenceName ->\nshortEntityName): a field named err keys the same bucket as every other err in\nthe repository and scores in the hundreds, while a distinctively named exported\nfunction with real callers scores low. So the cheap collision-prone signal\nchose the subjects for the accurate one. Reproduced at the default cap of 5 on\na 705-entity changeset: the survivors were fields named err and n plus vendored\nparser.h members, and every removal and signature change was dropped unmeasured.\n\nChange type leads instead. It is exact, free and causal: removing or re-signing\nan entity breaks a caller, a body change can change behaviour for existing\ncallers, and an addition cannot break what already compiles. DependentsCount\nstays as a tiebreak within one severity band, where a collision can no longer\nevict a whole class of change, and the cap's limitation line now says which\naxis it ordered on instead of claiming \"lower-priority\".\n\nTwo notes for review. The count itself is main's, not this PR's — the PR is the\nfirst thing to lean on it hard enough for the collisions to show, and fixing\nreferenceName would change diff/analyze output and the frozen 1.x schema, so it\nbelongs in its own change. classifyEntityRisk still reads DependentsCount for\nremovals, where the current snapshot genuinely cannot supply evidence because\nthe entity is gone; that path can still over-rate a removed err and is left\nas-is deliberately.\n\nThis branch carries only the risk-analysis commit. The PR's other two commits,\na Databricks ingestion bundle and a buildathon submission guide, are out of\nscope for this repository and are not here.\n\nMutation-proven in both directions: flattening the severity bands reds only the\npreselection test, and deleting the tiebreak reds only the within-band test.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -3","description":"Commit the 235 fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":991,"cache_read_input_tokens":213004,"output_tokens":912,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":991,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":912,"cache_read_input_tokens":213004,"cache_creation_input_tokens":991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":991},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01C6agzwEcsWVJ93MH8iRQGQ":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-235-fix && git add -A internal/cli && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(risk): preselect by change type, not by a short-name reference count\n\n#235's concept holds up: nothing on main answers \"what does this changeset put\nat risk\", and the report it builds — per-entity callers, type consumers and\nsuggested tests, with an overall verdict — is the right shape for it.\n\nThe preselection inverted it. --max-entities bounds the expensive step, the\nper-entity impact evidence, so whatever orders the candidates decides which\nentities ever get measured. That ordering led with DependentsCount, which is\nsem's SHORT-NAME reference count (internal/sem/dependents.go: referenceName ->\nshortEntityName): a field named err keys the same bucket as every other err in\nthe repository and scores in the hundreds, while a distinctively named exported\nfunction with real callers scores low. So the cheap collision-prone signal\nchose the subjects for the accurate one. Reproduced at the default cap of 5 on\na 705-entity changeset: the survivors were fields named err and n plus vendored\nparser.h members, and every removal and signature change was dropped unmeasured.\n\nChange type leads instead. It is exact, free and causal: removing or re-signing\nan entity breaks a caller, a body change can change behaviour for existing\ncallers, and an addition cannot break what already compiles. DependentsCount\nstays as a tiebreak within one severity band, where a collision can no longer\nevict a whole class of change, and the cap's limitation line now says which\naxis it ordered on instead of claiming \"lower-priority\".\n\nTwo notes for review. The count itself is main's, not this PR's — the PR is the\nfirst thing to lean on it hard enough for the collisions to show, and fixing\nreferenceName would change diff/analyze output and the frozen 1.x schema, so it\nbelongs in its own change. classifyEntityRisk still reads DependentsCount for\nremovals, where the current snapshot genuinely cannot supply evidence because\nthe entity is gone; that path can still over-rate a removed err and is left\nas-is deliberately.\n\nThis branch carries only the risk-analysis commit. The PR's other two commits,\na Databricks ingestion bundle and a buildathon submission guide, are out of\nscope for this repository and are not here.\n\nMutation-proven in both directions: flattening the severity bands reds only the\npreselection test, and deleting the tiebreak reds only the within-band test.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -3","description":"Commit the 235 fix"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3c7c50ba-49a4-4326-95ff-c1e681fbeecd","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgpmstZsAC1KbkfKGzyZx","requestRef":"60633af6-f80a-4a56-a702-d37b3246dee6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","attributionSkill":"loop","type":"assistant","uuid":"e784f5df-e86d-4747-a555-92244d15a930","timestamp":"2026-11-08T03:46:32.404Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
