{"parentUuid":"64dc71c3-b092-4ad9-847c-4686cc52766e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14860679 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"acd0d6ca-2a0d-46be-ab69-7f55c78daaac","timestamp":"2026-11-08T04:22:16.949Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14860679 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"acd0d6ca-2a0d-46be-ab69-7f55c78daaac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgppcyjM55RzK2tsQGM2T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01REtEMrebT5SdDG57Eyvpkm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-233-fix && git -c core.editor=true cherry-pick --continue 2>&1 | tail -2 && git commit -q --amend -F - <<'MSG'\nfeat(sem,cli): carry an explicit evidence state on Graph results\n\nRebase of the evidence-state half of #233 onto current main, with the schema\nbump and the stale golden headers redone.\n\nThe concept answers issue #273. An empty or tiny Graph answer currently reads\nexactly like a resolved \"nothing depends on this\", and those are different\nfacts: dynamic dispatch past its fan-out limit, an inventory-only language, and\na weak-pattern match all produce a confident-looking zero. This carries the\ndistinction on the response — confirmed vs requires_verification, with a note\nnaming a concrete way to check — computed once on the finished response so the\ntext and JSON surfaces cannot disagree.\n\nOnly the evidence-state commit is here. The PR's other four commits are the\n`graph rank` developer/commit leaderboard, its relation-graph cache, its\n--profile flag and a README demo section; that is an unrelated feature and\nbelongs in its own pull request.\n\nWhat the rebase changed, all because the PR is six weeks stale:\n\n- Schema goes to 1.5, not 1.2. Main moved 1.1 -> 1.4 meanwhile, so the PR's\n  constant would have been a silent DOWNGRADE. ADR 0001 makes this a minor bump\n  since the field is optional and additive, and the shape-contract test agrees.\n  pinnedShapeDigest is recomputed to a58a947cb2c21535; the old pin described a\n  wire shape that no longer exists.\n- The 29 golden headers are REGENERATED with -update, not hand-edited. The PR's\n  versions predate identity_revision on the header, so resolving them by hand\n  would have reintroduced a stale field set.\n- neighbors.go keeps BOTH main's value-reference disclosure and the new evidence\n  verdict. They are complementary: one appends a warning, the other sets the\n  state.\n- impact.go follows main's refactor. The overview moved to impact_text.go and\n  prints a bulleted summary rather than a \"Blast radius:\" line, so the note is a\n  sibling bullet of the value-reference note for the same documented reason\n  (above every section, so the bounded renderer's caps reach it last). The\n  verdict is still computed after impactDegenerateReason, which escalates it,\n  and the note is emitted on the degenerate path too, since that path never\n  reaches the overview and is where a reader is most likely to misread a zero.\n\nMutation-proven in three directions: making WorstEvidenceState always return\nconfirmed reds the three requires_verification tests while the \"is confirmed\"\ntest correctly stays green; dropping the note from the degenerate path reds the\nimpact test (this is how the missing emit was caught); and reverting the schema\nconstant to 1.4 reds the shape contract.\n\nCo-authored-by: Taniya Souza <souzataniya@users.noreply.github.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the rebased evidence-state work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":969,"cache_read_input_tokens":261530,"output_tokens":1112,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":969,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1112,"cache_read_input_tokens":261530,"cache_creation_input_tokens":969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":969},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01REtEMrebT5SdDG57Eyvpkm":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-233-fix && git -c core.editor=true cherry-pick --continue 2>&1 | tail -2 && git commit -q --amend -F - <<'MSG'\nfeat(sem,cli): carry an explicit evidence state on Graph results\n\nRebase of the evidence-state half of #233 onto current main, with the schema\nbump and the stale golden headers redone.\n\nThe concept answers issue #273. An empty or tiny Graph answer currently reads\nexactly like a resolved \"nothing depends on this\", and those are different\nfacts: dynamic dispatch past its fan-out limit, an inventory-only language, and\na weak-pattern match all produce a confident-looking zero. This carries the\ndistinction on the response — confirmed vs requires_verification, with a note\nnaming a concrete way to check — computed once on the finished response so the\ntext and JSON surfaces cannot disagree.\n\nOnly the evidence-state commit is here. The PR's other four commits are the\n`graph rank` developer/commit leaderboard, its relation-graph cache, its\n--profile flag and a README demo section; that is an unrelated feature and\nbelongs in its own pull request.\n\nWhat the rebase changed, all because the PR is six weeks stale:\n\n- Schema goes to 1.5, not 1.2. Main moved 1.1 -> 1.4 meanwhile, so the PR's\n  constant would have been a silent DOWNGRADE. ADR 0001 makes this a minor bump\n  since the field is optional and additive, and the shape-contract test agrees.\n  pinnedShapeDigest is recomputed to a58a947cb2c21535; the old pin described a\n  wire shape that no longer exists.\n- The 29 golden headers are REGENERATED with -update, not hand-edited. The PR's\n  versions predate identity_revision on the header, so resolving them by hand\n  would have reintroduced a stale field set.\n- neighbors.go keeps BOTH main's value-reference disclosure and the new evidence\n  verdict. They are complementary: one appends a warning, the other sets the\n  state.\n- impact.go follows main's refactor. The overview moved to impact_text.go and\n  prints a bulleted summary rather than a \"Blast radius:\" line, so the note is a\n  sibling bullet of the value-reference note for the same documented reason\n  (above every section, so the bounded renderer's caps reach it last). The\n  verdict is still computed after impactDegenerateReason, which escalates it,\n  and the note is emitted on the degenerate path too, since that path never\n  reaches the overview and is where a reader is most likely to misread a zero.\n\nMutation-proven in three directions: making WorstEvidenceState always return\nconfirmed reds the three requires_verification tests while the \"is confirmed\"\ntest correctly stays green; dropping the note from the degenerate path reds the\nimpact test (this is how the missing emit was caught); and reverting the schema\nconstant to 1.4 reds the shape contract.\n\nCo-authored-by: Taniya Souza <souzataniya@users.noreply.github.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the rebased evidence-state work"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"58b8e658-9f1f-4f40-b5c9-2779c440918b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgppcyD6Pz7x7tCSogdns","requestRef":"1b808985-f4bc-48f8-a6f9-fb6fa07a1f5a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","attributionSkill":"loop","type":"assistant","uuid":"73e2e2a8-392a-4c38-ac37-eb183b68c985","timestamp":"2026-11-08T04:22:32.964Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
