{"parentUuid":"2f0ec652-d77a-4140-8217-f261c6f55d8f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgppjCzjBBJzVRCtcijZu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Loop complete. All four fixed, nothing merged, nothing pushed, every PR still open.**\n\n| PR | Branch (in `~/devenv-worktrees/`) | What was wrong | Tests |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **#265** | `fix/265-setup-baseline` @ `eg-265-fix` | 3 tests asserted the literal `\"format_version\": 1`; write side was unfailable | 17/17 |\n| **#269** | `fix/269-preflight-quoting` @ `eg-269-fix` | Unquoted `\\` treated as POSIX escape | 26/27 + 1 skip |\n| **#235** | `fix/235-risk-preselection` @ `eg-235-fix` | Cheap signal chose who the accurate signal measured | 13/13 |\n| **#233** | `fix/233-evidence-state` @ `eg-233-fix` | 6 weeks stale; schema would have **downgraded** | sem + cli green |\n\nEvery guard mutation-proven in both directions.\n\n**Two findings worth more than the patches:**\n\n**#269 already contains #267.** It's stacked on it, so #267 needs no separate fix — one branch carries both.\n\n**#233's schema constant would have been a silent downgrade.** The PR bumps to 1.2, correct when written against main at 1.1. Main is now at 1.4, so cherry-picking it as-authored *lowers* the version while adding a field. It's 1.5 now, which ADR 0001 and the shape-contract test both independently confirm. Digest recomputed; the old pin described a wire shape that no longer exists. I also regenerated the 29 goldens with `-update` rather than hand-resolving — the PR's versions predate `identity_revision` on the header, so resolving by hand would have quietly reintroduced a stale field set.\n\n**One correction to what I told you earlier.** I said #235 \"ranks by `DependentsCount = len(index[shortEntityName(change)])`, a name-frequency count.\" The count is real and it is the problem, but it's **main's code** (`internal/sem/dependents.go:59`), not the contributor's. #235 is just the first thing to lean on it hard enough for the collisions to surface. I blamed them for our bug. I didn't fix `referenceName` itself — that changes `diff`/`analyze` output and touches the frozen 1.x schema, so it's its own change.\n\n**Scope I cut, deliberately:** #235's Databricks ingestion bundle and `BUILDATHON.md`; #233's four `graph rank` leaderboard commits and README demo. Branches carry the in-scope work only, and each commit message says what was dropped and why.\n\n**One thing the contributor's test caught me on:** resolving `impact.go` to main's structure silently dropped the evidence note from the degenerate path. Their own test failed and found it. That path never reaches the overview, and it's exactly where a reader misreads a zero as \"nothing depends on this.\"\n\n**Your call:** nothing is pushed. Say the word and I'll push the branches and/or open PRs. Also still open from before: the three `#357` fix commits on `fix/357-followups` (that PR merged without them), and the classifier blocked one compound test command mid-run — single commands work, so I wasn't blocked, but flagging it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":214,"cache_read_input_tokens":267279,"output_tokens":1084,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":214,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1084,"cache_read_input_tokens":267279,"cache_creation_input_tokens":214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":214},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7db84e0d-9b59-4eee-a220-0e820feac92e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"r