{"parentUuid":"66065e49-099c-44d9-9ebd-eec776614eb4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgqdzP9Ks64r1DnQxYyrX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2450,"cache_read_input_tokens":125659,"output_tokens":1147,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":438},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2450,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1147,"cache_read_input_tokens":125659,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2450},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6073,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"f435e09d-0a20-45c8-aa4b-312168b55154","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgqdzNugGdPKyrLTwsaxg","requestRef":"0dd3e700-743c-4e4f-b467-c2de3dd7121f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"25d721ec-9f64-4bd6-9457-2f5a428f8a8c","timestamp":"2026-11-08T14:43:35.134Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"25d721ec-9f64-4bd6-9457-2f5a428f8a8c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgqdzP9Ks64r1DnQxYyrX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No. Two of the four remaining are good, I just haven't gotten to them.\n\n**Not useless, genuinely worth landing:**\n\n- **#394** (rodbegbie, +561/-38, 12 files) — makes `grammar-refresh` patch *and regenerate* grammars. This closes the exact gap #357 left: the Swift patch was hand-applied, so the \"byte-for-byte reproducible with tree-sitter-cli 0.24.7\" claim in `VALIDATION.md:50-52` was never reproducible by anyone else. Best concept of anything still open. Unreviewed.\n- **#392** (Beehtrix, +71/-20, 6 files) — deletes the `brain_remember` / \"over MCP\" sentence from the agent guide and adds the `--path` segment rule. The MCP deletion is **correct**: brain #509 removed `entire brain mcp` in v0.4.0, so the guide has been telling agents to use a tool that doesn't exist. Smallest, truest PR in the set. May need nothing but a check of two cross-repo claims (the lowercase/underscore rule it attributes to brain #605, and that brain's `tools/integration` Go tests replaced `test-agent-coordination.py`).\n\n**These two are where the concept itself is the problem:**\n\n- **#232** (Shaurya002800) — **+20,387 lines, 94 files**. \"pact: graph-guided verification of confirmed requirements.\"\n- **#237** (saranmahadev) — **+5,796 lines, 85 files**. \"requirement traceability and review workflows with GPS.\"\n\nBoth build a whole new requirements/traceability subsystem *on top of* the graph. That's not a fix to entire-graph, it's a second product arriving as a PR. 26k lines of someone else's design, no design discussion first. Fixing them isn't fixing, it's adopting. That's a product call, not a code-review call, which is why I didn't touch them.\n\nNot useless as effort. Just not mergeable in the shape they arrived in, and nobody can review 26k lines of new subsystem off a cold start.\n\nWant me to review #394 next? It's the one with real value sitting unread."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2450,"cache_read_input_tokens":125659,"output_tokens":1147,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":438},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2450,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1147,"cache_read_input_tokens":125659,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2450},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f435e09d-0a20-45c8-aa4b-312168b55154","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgqdzNugGdPKyrLTwsaxg","requestRef":"0dd3e700-743c-4e4f-b467-c2de3dd7121f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cfba7f6c-db67-4edb-9b9f-f026f567260c","timestamp":"2026-11-08T14:43:45.894Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
