{"parentUuid":"a27714f3-68b0-43ca-9a13-bdbda9777f36","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"28398f49-5ade-4a59-9174-f5364aaf08a6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EkYdUuE2SUU8RwBNWmXV7z","type":"tool_result","content":"base=main head=feature/grammar-refresh-local-build oid=63ab18576a9390d51d50ac344ea30de407269402 mergeable=MERGEABLE\n--commits--\n1d39f2ad sem(grammars): apply manifest patches in grammar-refresh\n2920a799 sem(grammars): regenerate grammars with a pinned or latest tree-sitte…\n5d69ba68 docs(grammars): record local builds for Swift and C#\n3cef0d10 fix(grammar-refresh): resolve review findings on local builds\n8400a210 refactor(grammar-refresh): derive the ABI from one constant\n63ab1857 sem(swift): vendor the generator's tree_sitter headers\n--body--\n> Written by Claude Code (an AI agent) working under Rod's direction; Rod has reviewed the code, and edited this description, before anything was posted upstream. \n\nFollow-up to [entireio/entire-graph#357](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/357), which added `grammar-refresh` and vendored Swift 0.7.4 with Tom's compatibility patch. That patch was applied by hand; this makes the tool do it.\n\n`grammar-refresh` can now build a grammar instead of only copying upstream's generated files. That covers Tom's Swift compatibility patch, and the growing list of grammars whose releases ship only ABI 15 (C# v0.23.5, Rust v0.24.2).\n\nThis is the first of three stacked changes. The other two are previewed as PRs in my fork with the intention to follow once this one lands:\n\n- [rodbegbie/entire-graph#3](https://github.com/rodbegbie/entire-graph/pull/3) moves F# onto a patch and removes `local_changes`.\n- [rodbegbie/entire-graph#4](https://github.com/rodbegbie/entire-graph/pull/4) uses the tool to vendor Rust v0.24.2, which fixes the `&raw const` parse errors @thomaseleff reported in [a comment](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/345#issuecomment-6532737539) on #345.\n\n## What changes\n\n- A manifest entry can carry a `local_build` block:\n\n  ```json\n  \"local_build\": {\n    \"patch\": \"swift/compatibility.patch\",\n    \"tree_sitter_cli\": \"0.24.7\",\n    \"generate_args\": [\"--abi\", \"14\"]\n  }\n  ```\n\n- The tool applies `patch` to the fetched checkout with `git apply`, then runs `npx --yes tree-sitter-cli@<version> generate <args>`, then vendors as before. A failure at any step leaves the vendored folder and manifest untouched.\n- Regenerating the recorded revision reuses the recorded CLI version, so it is reproducible. A new revision uses `@latest`, resolved once to an exact version, which is recorded. `-generate` adds the block to a new grammar, and `-tree-sitter-cli` pins a version.\n- The ABI comes from one constant (`maxABI`), and a test fails if go-tree-sitter's `api.h` range ever stops matching it, so a runtime upgrade changes one value.\n- Swift and C# now use `local_build`. Swift also picks up 0.24.7's generated `alloc.h` and `array.h` in place of upstream's committed copies (parameter names and MSVC pragma push/pop only; no parse change).\n\n## Validation\n\n- Regenerating Swift and C# at their recorded revisions with the real tool reproduces the vendored folders byte for byte.\n- `mise run check`: everything passes except the known `internal/cli` exact-name search tests, which time out at 30 minutes under `-race` on `main` too. `internal/cli` passes in full without `-race` (319s).\n- This is the first CI run on Windows for the new tests (the fork cannot use the Depot runners). They replace the `npx` runner in-process rather than relying on `PATH`, so they should not need Node or a shell there.\n\n## Worth knowing\n\n- Generating needs Node.js (`npx`). Building or running Graph still never downloads or generates anything.\n- tree-sitter can still generate ABI 14 today, but a future release may drop it. The error then suggests `-tree-sitter-cli <older version>`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6df95063-7b72-4fea-a673-f3d99ca08138","timestamp":"2026-11-08T14:53:56.874Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"base=main head=feature/grammar-refresh-local-build oid=63ab18576a9390d51d50ac344ea30de407269402 mergeable=MERGEABLE\n--commits--\n1d39f2ad sem(grammars): apply manifest patches in grammar-refresh\n2920a799 sem(grammars): regenerate grammars with a pinned or latest tree-sitte…\n5d69ba68 docs(grammars): record local builds for Swift and C#\n3cef0d10 fix(grammar-refresh): resolve review findings on local builds\n8400a210 refactor(grammar-refresh): derive the ABI from one constant\n63ab1857 sem(swift): vendor the generator's tree_sitter headers\n--body--\n> Written by Claude Code (an AI agent) working under Rod's direction; Rod has reviewed the code, and edited this description, before anything was posted upstream. \n\nFollow-up to [entireio/entire-graph#357](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/357), which added `grammar-refresh` and vendored Swift 0.7.4 with Tom's compatibility patch. That patch was applied by hand; this makes the tool do it.\n\n`grammar-refresh` can now build a grammar instead of only copying upstream's generated files. That covers Tom's Swift compatibility patch, and the growing list of grammars whose releases ship only ABI 15 (C# v0.23.5, Rust v0.24.2).\n\nThis is the first of three stacked changes. The other two are previewed as PRs in my fork with the intention to follow once this one lands:\n\n- [rodbegbie/entire-graph#3](https://github.com/rodbegbie/entire-graph/pull/3) moves F# onto a patch and removes `local_changes`.\n- [rodbegbie/entire-graph#4](https://github.com/rodbegbie/entire-graph/pull/4) uses the tool to vendor Rust v0.24.2, which fixes the `&raw const` parse errors @thomaseleff reported in [a comment](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/345#issuecomment-6532737539) on #345.\n\n## What changes\n\n- A manifest entry can carry a `local_build` block:\n\n  ```json\n  \"local_build\": {\n    \"patch\": \"swift/compatibility.patch\",\n    \"tree_sitter_cli\": \"0.24.7\",\n    \"generate_args\": [\"--abi\", \"14\"]\n  }\n  ```\n\n- The tool applies `patch` to the fetched checkout with `git apply`, then runs `npx --yes tree-sitter-cli@<version> generate <args>`, then vendors as before. A failure at any step leaves the vendored folder and manifest untouched.\n- Regenerating the recorded revision reuses the recorded CLI version, so it is reproducible. A new revision uses `@latest`, resolved once to an exact version, which is recorded. `-generate` adds the block to a new grammar, and `-tree-sitter-cli` pins a version.\n- The ABI comes from one constant (`maxABI`), and a test fails if go-tree-sitter's `api.h` range ever stops matching it, so a runtime upgrade changes one value.\n- Swift and C# now use `local_build`. Swift also picks up 0.24.7's generated `alloc.h` and `array.h` in place of upstream's committed copies (parameter names and MSVC pragma push/pop only; no parse change).\n\n## Validation\n\n- Regenerating Swift and C# at their recorded revisions with the real tool reproduces the vendored folders byte for byte.\n- `mise run check`: everything passes except the known `internal/cli` exact-name search tests, which time out at 30 minutes under `-race` on `main` too. `internal/cli` passes in full without `-race` (319s).\n- This is the first CI run on Windows for the new tests (the fork cannot use the Depot runners). They replace the `npx` runner in-process rather than relying on `PATH`, so they should not need Node or a shell there.\n\n## Worth knowing\n\n- Generating needs Node.js (`npx`). Building or running Graph still never downloads or generates anything.\n- tree-sitter can still generate ABI 14 today, but a future release may drop it. The error then suggests `-tree-sitter-cli <older version>`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a27714f3-68b0-43ca-9a13-bdbda9777f36","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"subcommandResults"},"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
