{"parentUuid":"e1a317ee-c66c-45ec-9b51-be4c0beb4d02","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14864784 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d7294781-f55f-4579-aca5-dd8640426f65","timestamp":"2026-11-08T16:51:30.708Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14864784 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"d7294781-f55f-4579-aca5-dd8640426f65","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgqokiJXTwDKdEM8WCHxg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H1a3zAexTYfVQbZnDBtkZd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-394-fix && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(grammar-refresh): keep the ABI derived, the generator exact, and the patch honest\n\nThe feature is the right one. #357 vendored a Swift parser built from a\nhand-applied grammar.js patch and nothing in the tree tied the two together;\nthis makes the tool do it. Three things undercut that.\n\nThe ABI was pinned, not derived. refresh wrote the resolved default back into\nthe manifest, and both entries carried \"generate_args\": [\"--abi\", \"14\"]. When\nmaxABI becomes 15, TestABIRangeMatchesRuntime forces the one constant to be\nedited and every grammar goes on generating ABI 14 off its recorded pin, which\nvendor accepts for as long as 14 is inside the range. Nothing fails. The\ndecision now lives in recordedLocalBuild, which records the version and\nnothing else new, and the two derived pins are out of grammars.json. Explicit\nargs stay the maintainer's and are kept verbatim.\n\nA prerelease generator was recorded as a different generator. The version\npattern was \\b\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+\\b, so \"tree-sitter 0.25.0-rc.1\" recorded as\n0.25.0. The whole local_build design rests on regenerating the recorded\nrevision with the recorded version, and the pin would have fetched a build\nthat never produced those bytes. The pattern now takes the whole version,\nprerelease and build metadata included.\n\nA patch that edits grammar.js with no generator was a silent no-op. The patch\nis applied whatever wantsGeneration says, so patching the grammar and then\ncopying upstream's committed parser.c discards the patch and prints \"next:\nbump IdentityRevision\". That is #357's original sin reproduced by the tool\nbuilt to prevent it. refresh now refuses before the fetch, naming the paths\nwhose effect needs generation. A patch confined to vendored files is still a\ncomplete change on its own: the real compatibility.patch resolves to\ngrammar.js plus src/scanner.c, and Swift records a generator, so it passes.\n\nAlso removed the PR's assertion that the resolved default is recorded.\n\nProof, five mutations, each red, no two caught by the same test: the old\nversion pattern; recording the default args; every path counted as vendored;\nreading only the new side of a diff; unwiring the guard from refresh. The\nunwired run exits 0 and reports success, which is the defect. Both\ndirections: a vendored-file-only patch is still accepted, and explicit args\nare still honoured.\n\nNot run: the eleven tests whose path reaches `npx tree-sitter-cli`, which\nthis machine refuses to execute from a fork checkout. Their guards are proven\nthrough the pure functions instead (recordedLocalBuild, cliVersionPattern,\npatchPathsNeedingGeneration); the twenty-one tests that touch no npx pass\nindividually.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -8 | cat && git status --short && echo \"(clean)\"","description":"Commit the 394 fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":992,"cache_read_input_tokens":263633,"output_tokens":1090,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":992,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1090,"cache_read_input_tokens":263633,"cache_creation_input_tokens":992,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":992},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01H1a3zAexTYfVQbZnDBtkZd":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-394-fix && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(grammar-refresh): keep the ABI derived, the generator exact, and the patch honest\n\nThe feature is the right one. #357 vendored a Swift parser built from a\nhand-applied grammar.js patch and nothing in the tree tied the two together;\nthis makes the tool do it. Three things undercut that.\n\nThe ABI was pinned, not derived. refresh wrote the resolved default back into\nthe manifest, and both entries carried \"generate_args\": [\"--abi\", \"14\"]. When\nmaxABI becomes 15, TestABIRangeMatchesRuntime forces the one constant to be\nedited and every grammar goes on generating ABI 14 off its recorded pin, which\nvendor accepts for as long as 14 is inside the range. Nothing fails. The\ndecision now lives in recordedLocalBuild, which records the version and\nnothing else new, and the two derived pins are out of grammars.json. Explicit\nargs stay the maintainer's and are kept verbatim.\n\nA prerelease generator was recorded as a different generator. The version\npattern was \\b\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+\\b, so \"tree-sitter 0.25.0-rc.1\" recorded as\n0.25.0. The whole local_build design rests on regenerating the recorded\nrevision with the recorded version, and the pin would have fetched a build\nthat never produced those bytes. The pattern now takes the whole version,\nprerelease and build metadata included.\n\nA patch that edits grammar.js with no generator was a silent no-op. The patch\nis applied whatever wantsGeneration says, so patching the grammar and then\ncopying upstream's committed parser.c discards the patch and prints \"next:\nbump IdentityRevision\". That is #357's original sin reproduced by the tool\nbuilt to prevent it. refresh now refuses before the fetch, naming the paths\nwhose effect needs generation. A patch confined to vendored files is still a\ncomplete change on its own: the real compatibility.patch resolves to\ngrammar.js plus src/scanner.c, and Swift records a generator, so it passes.\n\nAlso removed the PR's assertion that the resolved default is recorded.\n\nProof, five mutations, each red, no two caught by the same test: the old\nversion pattern; recording the default args; every path counted as vendored;\nreading only the new side of a diff; unwiring the guard from refresh. The\nunwired run exits 0 and reports success, which is the defect. Both\ndirections: a vendored-file-only patch is still accepted, and explicit args\nare still honoured.\n\nNot run: the eleven tests whose path reaches `npx tree-sitter-cli`, which\nthis machine refuses to execute from a fork checkout. Their guards are proven\nthrough the pure functions instead (recordedLocalBuild, cliVersionPattern,\npatchPathsNeedingGeneration); the twenty-one tests that touch no npx pass\nindividually.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -8 | cat && git status --short && echo \"(clean)\"","description":"Commit the 394 fix"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"45b1014c-53a2-47b0-bbb2-b48b8f068995","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgqokhzQn56RnaZSj57h9","requestRef":"9ef960c0-00b5-4e38-8571-bf999448b466","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a1f777d0-0f31-4f8f-9f62-de0b23c84565","timestamp":"2026-11-08T16:51:45.459Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"323e0f71-94c9-40df-877e-b0c11113f22d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
